window.TWG_K1C={"level":1,"track":"sake","exam":{"questions":30,"minutes":45,"pass":70,"written":false,"tasting":false},"ch":{"k01":{"it":"Che cos'è il sake","fr":"Qu'est-ce que le saké ?","en":"What sake is"},"k02":{"it":"Le tappe della produzione","fr":"Les étapes de l'élaboration","en":"The brewing steps"},"k03":{"it":"Dal riso integrale al riso cotto a vapore","fr":"Du riz brun au riz cuit à la vapeur","en":"From brown rice to steamed rice"},"k04":{"it":"Come si fa il kōji","fr":"Comment on fait le kōji","en":"Making kōji"},"k05":{"it":"Fermentazione e stile","fr":"Fermentation et style","en":"Fermentation and style"},"k06":{"it":"Sake base e sake premium","fr":"Saké de base et saké premium","en":"Basic and premium sake"},"k07":{"it":"Leggere un'etichetta giapponese","fr":"Lire une étiquette japonaise","en":"Reading a Japanese label"},"k08":{"it":"Gli stili speciali","fr":"Les styles spéciaux","en":"Speciality styles"},"k09":{"it":"Degustare il sake","fr":"Déguster le saké","en":"Tasting sake"},"k10":{"it":"Conservazione e difetti","fr":"Conservation et défauts","en":"Storage and faults"},"k11":{"it":"Servire il sake","fr":"Servir le saké","en":"Serving sake"},"k12":{"it":"Sake e cibo","fr":"Saké et mets","en":"Sake and food"}},"groups":[{"k":"p","w":10,"n":{"it":"Ingredienti e produzione","fr":"Ingrédients et élaboration","en":"Ingredients and brewing"},"c":["k01","k02","k03","k04","k05"]},{"k":"s","w":15,"n":{"it":"Categorie e stili","fr":"Catégories et styles","en":"Categories and styles"},"c":["k06","k07","k08"]},{"k":"t","w":5,"n":{"it":"Degustare, conservare, servire","fr":"Déguster, conserver, servir","en":"Tasting, storage and service"},"c":["k09","k10","k11","k12"]}],"bank":[{"id":"k177b2fe2","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Da quale materia prima si ottiene il sake?","À partir de quelle matière première élabore-t-on le saké ?","What is sake made from?"],"o":[["Riso","Riz","Rice"],["Orzo maltato","Orge maltée","Malted barley"],["Patate dolci","Patates douces","Sweet potatoes"],["Uva bianca","Raisin blanc","White grapes"]],"e":["Il sake è una bevanda alcolica giapponese fatta con il riso.","Le saké est une boisson alcoolisée japonaise faite à partir de riz.","Sake is a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice."],"d":["L'orzo maltato è la base della birra, l'uva quella del vino. Le patate dolci si usano per altre bevande, non per il sake.","L'orge maltée sert à la bière, le raisin au vin. Les patates douces servent à d'autres boissons, pas au saké.","Malted barley is the base of beer and grapes of wine. Sweet potatoes are used for other drinks, not sake."]},{"id":"k18948e84","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa alla lettera nihon-shu, uno dei nomi ufficiali del sake?","Que signifie littéralement nihon-shu, l'un des noms officiels du saké ?","What does nihon-shu, one of sake's official names, literally mean?"],"o":[["Bevanda alcolica del Giappone","Boisson alcoolisée du Japon","Japanese alcoholic drink"],["Vino di riso pregiato","Vin de riz de prestige","Fine rice wine"],["Riso puro","Riz pur","Pure rice"],["Grande sake","Grand saké","Big sake"]],"e":["Nihon-shu vuol dire «bevanda alcolica giapponese»: il nome lega il sake al suo Paese.","Nihon-shu veut dire « boisson alcoolisée japonaise » : le nom lie le saké à son pays.","Nihon-shu means 'Japanese alcoholic drink': the name ties sake to its country."],"d":["«Riso puro» è il significato di junmai, un termine di etichetta. «Grande» richiama dai di daiginjō. Nessun nome ufficiale significa «vino di riso pregiato».","« Riz pur » est le sens de junmai, un terme d'étiquette. « Grand » rappelle le dai de daiginjō. Aucun nom officiel ne veut dire « vin de riz de prestige ».","'Pure rice' is the meaning of junmai, a label term. 'Big' recalls the dai in daiginjō. No official name means 'fine rice wine'."]},{"id":"k1231f01f","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Qual è il grado alcolico tipico di un sake in bottiglia?","Quel est le degré d'alcool typique d'un saké en bouteille ?","What is the typical alcohol level of a bottled sake?"],"o":[["15–17% vol.","15–17 % vol.","15–17% abv"],["4–6% vol.","4–6 % vol.","4–6% abv"],["9–11% vol.","9–11 % vol.","9–11% abv"],["38–40% vol.","38–40 % vol.","38–40% abv"]],"e":["La maggior parte dei sake ha tra il 15 e il 17% di alcol.","La plupart des sakés titrent entre 15 et 17 %.","Most sakes are between 15 and 17% abv."],"d":["4–6% è il grado di molte birre, 38–40% quello di un distillato. 9–11% è troppo basso per un sake tipico, anche se alcuni sake frizzanti sono leggeri.","4–6 % correspond à beaucoup de bières, 38–40 % à un spiritueux. 9–11 % est trop bas pour un saké typique, même si certains sakés pétillants sont légers.","4–6% is the level of many beers and 38–40% that of a spirit. 9–11% is too low for a typical sake, although some sparkling sakes are light."]},{"id":"k180499e3","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde a un sake tipico?","Quelle description correspond à un saké typique ?","Which description fits a typical sake?"],"o":[["Limpido e incolore, leggermente dolce, poco acido","Limpide et incolore, légèrement sucré, peu acide","Clear and colourless, slightly sweet, lightly acidic"],["Ambrato, molto amaro, frizzante","Ambré, très amer, pétillant","Amber, very bitter, fizzy"],["Torbido, secco, molto tannico","Trouble, sec, très tannique","Cloudy, dry, very tannic"],["Rosso rubino, acidulo, fruttato","Rouge rubis, acidulé, fruité","Ruby red, tart, fruity"]],"e":["Il sake tipico è limpido e incolore, appena dolce e poco acido, con aromi delicati.","Le saké typique est limpide et incolore, légèrement sucré et peu acide, avec des arômes délicats.","Typical sake is clear and colourless, slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with delicate flavours."],"d":["Torbido è il nigori, ambrato è spesso il koshu: sono stili speciali, non il sake tipico. Il sake non è rosso e non ha tannini, e l'amaro marcato appartiene piuttosto alla birra.","Trouble, c'est le nigori ; ambré, c'est souvent le koshu : ce sont des styles spéciaux, pas le saké typique. Le saké n'est ni rouge ni tannique, et l'amertume marquée appartient plutôt à la bière.","Cloudy describes nigori and amber is often koshu: these are speciality styles, not typical sake. Sake is never red or tannic, and marked bitterness belongs to beer rather than sake."]},{"id":"k18ad9685","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi NON è uno dei quattro ingredienti principali del sake?","Lequel de ces éléments n'est PAS l'un des quatre ingrédients principaux du saké ?","Which of these is NOT one of the four main ingredients of sake?"],"o":[["Alcol distillato ad alta gradazione","Alcool distillé à haut degré","High-strength distilled alcohol"],["Kōji","Kōji","Kōji"],["Acqua","Eau","Water"],["Lievito","Levure","Yeast"]],"e":["L'alcol distillato è un ingrediente facoltativo, non uno dei quattro principali.","L'alcool distillé est un ingrédient facultatif, pas l'un des quatre principaux.","Distilled alcohol is an optional extra, not one of the four main ingredients."],"d":["Riso bianco cotto a vapore, kōji, acqua e lievito si trovano in ogni sake. L'alcol distillato si aggiunge solo in alcuni casi, prima della filtrazione.","Riz blanc cuit à la vapeur, kōji, eau et levure se trouvent dans tout saké. L'alcool distillé n'est ajouté que dans certains cas, avant la filtration.","Steamed white rice, kōji, water and yeast are in every sake. Distilled alcohol is added only in some cases, before filtration."]},{"id":"k1201cd5c","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["In che stato arriva di solito il riso in una cantina di sake?","Dans quel état le riz arrive-t-il généralement dans une brasserie de saké ?","In what state does rice usually arrive at a sake brewery?"],"o":[["Crudo, duro e polveroso","Cru, dur et poussiéreux","Raw, hard and dusty"],["Già cotto a vapore","Déjà cuit à la vapeur","Already steamed"],["Già trasformato in kōji","Déjà transformé en kōji","Already turned into kōji"],["Macinato in farina","Moulu en farine","Ground into flour"]],"e":["Il riso viene comprato crudo; la cottura a vapore si fa in cantina.","Le riz est acheté cru ; la cuisson à la vapeur se fait à la brasserie.","Rice is bought raw; steaming is done in the brewery."],"d":["Il kōji si prepara in cantina partendo dal riso cotto. Il riso non viene ridotto in farina: si leviga, si lava, si ammolla e si cuoce a vapore.","Le kōji est préparé sur place à partir du riz cuit. Le riz n'est pas réduit en farine : on le polit, le lave, le fait tremper et le cuit à la vapeur.","Kōji is made in the brewery from steamed rice. Rice is not ground into flour: it is polished, washed, soaked and steamed."]},{"id":"k155cacf2","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Perché il riso viene cotto a vapore?","Pourquoi cuit-on le riz à la vapeur ?","Why is the rice steamed?"],"o":[["Per ammorbidirlo, così che si sciolga nell'acqua","Pour l'attendrir afin qu'il se défasse dans l'eau","To soften it so it can break up in the water"],["Per trasformare l'amido in alcol","Pour transformer l'amidon en alcool","To turn its starch into alcohol"],["Per dargli un colore ambrato","Pour lui donner une couleur ambrée","To give it an amber colour"],["Per eliminare gli strati esterni","Pour éliminer les couches extérieures","To remove the outer layers"]],"e":["Il vapore ammorbidisce il riso duro, che poi si disgrega nell'acqua durante la fermentazione.","La vapeur attendrit le riz dur, qui se désagrège ensuite dans l'eau pendant la fermentation.","Steam softens the hard rice, which can then break up in the water during fermentation."],"d":["Gli strati esterni si tolgono con la levigatura, non con il vapore. L'amido diventa zucchero grazie agli enzimi del kōji e poi alcol grazie ai lieviti. Il vapore non colora il riso.","Les couches extérieures s'enlèvent au polissage, pas à la vapeur. L'amidon devient sucre grâce aux enzymes du kōji, puis alcool grâce aux levures. La vapeur ne colore pas le riz.","The outer layers are removed by polishing, not steaming. Starch becomes sugar thanks to kōji enzymes, then alcohol thanks to yeast. Steaming does not colour the rice."]},{"id":"k165e0f34","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è il kōji?","Qu'est-ce que le kōji ?","What is kōji?"],"o":[["Riso cotto su cui è stata fatta crescere una muffa speciale","Du riz cuit sur lequel on a fait pousser une moisissure spéciale","Steamed rice on which a special mould has been grown"],["Un lievito selezionato comprato da un fornitore","Une levure sélectionnée achetée à un fournisseur","A selected yeast bought from a supplier"],["Un alcol neutro aggiunto prima della filtrazione","Un alcool neutre ajouté avant la filtration","A neutral alcohol added before filtration"],["La polvere di riso tolta durante la levigatura","La poussière de riz retirée au polissage","The rice dust removed during polishing"]],"e":["Il kōji è riso cotto a vapore coperto da una muffa speciale che produce enzimi.","Le kōji est du riz cuit à la vapeur couvert d'une moisissure spéciale qui produit des enzymes.","Kōji is steamed rice covered in a special mould that produces enzymes."],"d":["Il lievito è un ingrediente diverso, che trasforma lo zucchero in alcol. L'alcol neutro è l'ingrediente facoltativo. La polvere di levigatura viene lavata via e non serve.","La levure est un autre ingrédient, qui transforme le sucre en alcool. L'alcool neutre est l'ingrédient facultatif. La poussière de polissage est lavée et ne sert pas.","Yeast is a separate ingredient that turns sugar into alcohol. Neutral alcohol is the optional ingredient. Polishing dust is washed off and not used."]},{"id":"k14da22af","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Quale parte del riso viene usata per fare il kōji?","Quelle part du riz sert à faire le kōji ?","How much of the rice is used to make kōji?"],"o":[["Una piccola parte del riso cotto a vapore","Une petite partie du riz cuit à la vapeur","A small proportion of the steamed rice"],["Tutto il riso cotto a vapore","Tout le riz cuit à la vapeur","All of the steamed rice"],["Solo gli strati esterni marroni","Seulement les couches extérieures brunes","Only the brown outer layers"],["Il riso crudo non levigato","Le riz cru non poli","Unpolished raw rice"]],"e":["Si prende solo una piccola parte del riso cotto per farci crescere la muffa.","On ne prélève qu'une petite partie du riz cuit pour y faire pousser la moisissure.","Only a small proportion of the steamed rice is taken to grow the mould on."],"d":["Il resto del riso cotto serve come fonte di amido nella fermentazione. Il kōji si fa su riso levigato e cotto, non su riso crudo o sugli strati esterni.","Le reste du riz cuit sert de source d'amidon pendant la fermentation. Le kōji se fait sur du riz poli et cuit, pas sur du riz cru ni sur les couches extérieures.","The rest of the steamed rice is the starch source in fermentation. Kōji is made from polished, steamed rice, not raw rice or the outer layers."]},{"id":"k1eac4580","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Quale acqua usano di solito le cantine di sake?","Quelle eau les brasseries de saké utilisent-elles en général ?","What water do sake breweries usually use?"],"o":[["Acqua locale: quasi qualsiasi acqua, purché pulita","De l'eau locale : presque n'importe laquelle, pourvu qu'elle soit propre","Local water: almost any, as long as it is clean"],["Solo acqua di mare desalinizzata","Uniquement de l'eau de mer dessalée","Only desalinated seawater"],["Solo acqua distillata comprata in fabbrica","Uniquement de l'eau distillée achetée en usine","Only factory-bought distilled water"],["Acqua importata da una sola sorgente del Giappone","De l'eau importée d'une seule source au Japon","Water imported from a single Japanese spring"]],"e":["Si usa acqua del posto; quasi ogni acqua va bene se è pulita.","On utilise l'eau locale ; presque toute eau convient si elle est propre.","Local supplies are used; almost any water works if it is clean."],"d":["Non esiste un obbligo di acqua distillata, di mare o di una sorgente unica. La regola semplice da ricordare è: acqua locale e pulita.","Il n'y a aucune obligation d'eau distillée, de mer ou d'une source unique. La règle simple à retenir : eau locale et propre.","There is no rule requiring distilled water, seawater or a single spring. The simple rule to remember: local, clean water."]},{"id":"k1129cffb","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Da dove provengono di solito i lieviti usati per il sake?","D'où viennent généralement les levures utilisées pour le saké ?","Where do the yeasts used for sake usually come from?"],"o":[["Da fornitori specializzati che vendono varietà precise","De fournisseurs spécialisés qui vendent des variétés précises","From specialist suppliers selling specific varieties"],["Dalla muffa del kōji","De la moisissure du kōji","From the kōji mould"],["Dalla buccia del riso integrale","De l'enveloppe du riz brun","From the husk of brown rice"],["Dall'alcol distillato aggiunto","De l'alcool distillé ajouté","From the added distilled alcohol"]],"e":["Le cantine comprano varietà specifiche di lievito da fornitori specializzati.","Les brasseries achètent des variétés précises de levure à des fournisseurs spécialisés.","Breweries buy specific yeast varieties from specialist suppliers."],"d":["La muffa del kōji produce enzimi, non è il lievito. L'alcol distillato non contiene lieviti vivi, e i lieviti non vengono presi dal riso.","La moisissure du kōji produit des enzymes, ce n'est pas la levure. L'alcool distillé ne contient pas de levures vivantes, et on ne prend pas les levures sur le riz.","The kōji mould produces enzymes; it is not the yeast. Distilled alcohol contains no live yeast, and yeasts are not taken from the rice."]},{"id":"k1b8e32d4","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Durante la fermentazione alcolica, il lievito trasforma lo zucchero in…","Pendant la fermentation alcoolique, la levure transforme le sucre en…","During alcoholic fermentation, yeast turns sugar into…"],"o":[["alcol e anidride carbonica","alcool et dioxyde de carbone","alcohol and carbon dioxide"],["amido e acqua","amidon et eau","starch and water"],["enzimi e ossigeno","enzymes et oxygène","enzymes and oxygen"],["kōji e alcol","kōji et alcool","kōji and alcohol"]],"e":["Il lievito mangia lo zucchero e produce alcol, liberando anidride carbonica.","La levure consomme le sucre et produit de l'alcool en libérant du dioxyde de carbone.","Yeast eats sugar and makes alcohol, releasing carbon dioxide."],"d":["L'amido è il punto di partenza, non il risultato. Gli enzimi vengono dal kōji, che si prepara prima della fermentazione: il lievito non li crea dallo zucchero.","L'amidon est le point de départ, pas le résultat. Les enzymes viennent du kōji, préparé avant la fermentation : la levure ne les crée pas à partir du sucre.","Starch is the starting point, not the product. Enzymes come from kōji, which is made before fermentation: yeast does not make them from sugar."]},{"id":"k17295a4b","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Perché il lievito da solo non potrebbe trasformare il riso in alcol?","Pourquoi la levure seule ne pourrait-elle pas transformer le riz en alcool ?","Why could yeast alone not turn rice into alcohol?"],"o":[["Perché il riso contiene amido e il lievito non sa mangiarlo","Parce que le riz contient de l'amidon et que la levure ne peut pas le consommer","Because rice contains starch and yeast cannot eat starch"],["Perché il riso contiene troppo zucchero","Parce que le riz contient trop de sucre","Because rice contains too much sugar"],["Perché il lievito ha bisogno di uva","Parce que la levure a besoin de raisin","Because yeast needs grapes"],["Perché il riso è troppo acido","Parce que le riz est trop acide","Because rice is too acidic"]],"e":["Il riso non ha zucchero ma amido: senza gli enzimi del kōji il lievito non ha nulla da mangiare.","Le riz n'a pas de sucre mais de l'amidon : sans les enzymes du kōji, la levure n'a rien à consommer.","Rice has no sugar, only starch: without kōji enzymes the yeast has nothing to eat."],"d":["Il riso non contiene zucchero, quindi non può averne troppo. Il lievito non ha bisogno di uva: gli basta zucchero sciolto in acqua. L'acidità del riso non è il problema.","Le riz ne contient pas de sucre, il ne peut donc pas en avoir trop. La levure n'a pas besoin de raisin : du sucre dissous dans l'eau lui suffit. L'acidité du riz n'est pas en cause.","Rice contains no sugar, so it cannot have too much. Yeast does not need grapes: sugar dissolved in water is enough. Acidity is not the issue."]},{"id":"k19f54cda","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Che cosa fanno gli enzimi durante la conversione dell'amido?","Que font les enzymes pendant la conversion de l'amidon ?","What do enzymes do during starch conversion?"],"o":[["Spezzano le catene di amido in singoli zuccheri","Ils découpent les chaînes d'amidon en sucres simples","They break starch chains into individual sugars"],["Trasformano l'alcol in zucchero","Ils transforment l'alcool en sucre","They turn alcohol back into sugar"],["Uniscono gli zuccheri in amido","Ils assemblent les sucres en amidon","They join sugars together into starch"],["Eliminano l'anidride carbonica","Ils éliminent le dioxyde de carbone","They remove the carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Gli enzimi sciolgono i legami tra le molecole di zucchero dell'amido, liberando zuccheri che il lievito può mangiare.","Les enzymes coupent les liaisons entre les molécules de sucre de l'amidon et libèrent des sucres que la levure peut consommer.","Enzymes unlock the bonds between the sugar molecules in starch, freeing sugars the yeast can eat."],"d":["Unire gli zuccheri in amido è il contrario di ciò che serve. Gli enzimi non agiscono sull'alcol né sull'anidride carbonica, che sono prodotti dal lievito.","Assembler les sucres en amidon est l'inverse de ce qu'il faut. Les enzymes n'agissent ni sur l'alcool ni sur le dioxyde de carbone, produits par la levure.","Joining sugars into starch is the opposite of what is needed. Enzymes do not act on alcohol or carbon dioxide, which are made by the yeast."]},{"id":"k1fc9b3aa","c":"k01","p":0,"q":["Da dove vengono gli enzimi che trasformano l'amido del riso in zucchero?","D'où viennent les enzymes qui transforment l'amidon du riz en sucre ?","Where do the enzymes that turn rice starch into sugar come from?"],"o":[["Dalla muffa coltivata sul kōji","De la moisissure cultivée sur le kōji","From the mould grown to make kōji"],["Dal lievito","De la levure","From the yeast"],["Dall'acqua della sorgente","De l'eau de source","From the spring water"],["Dall'alcol distillato","De l'alcool distillé","From the distilled alcohol"]],"e":["È la muffa del kōji a produrre gli enzimi: per questo il kōji è indispensabile.","C'est la moisissure du kōji qui produit les enzymes : voilà pourquoi le kōji est indispensable.","The kōji mould produces the enzymes: that is why kōji is essential."],"d":["Il lievito trasforma lo zucchero in alcol ma non sa scomporre l'amido. L'acqua e l'alcol distillato non portano enzimi utili alla conversione.","La levure transforme le sucre en alcool mais ne sait pas décomposer l'amidon. L'eau et l'alcool distillé n'apportent pas d'enzymes utiles à la conversion.","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol but cannot break down starch. Water and distilled alcohol bring no enzymes for conversion."]},{"id":"k19d3b011","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le tre tappe che avvengono SEMPRE nella produzione del sake?","Quelles sont les trois étapes qui ont TOUJOURS lieu dans l'élaboration du saké ?","Which three steps ALWAYS happen when sake is made?"],"o":[["Fermentazione, filtrazione, imbottigliamento","Fermentation, filtration, mise en bouteille","Fermentation, filtration, bottling"],["Fermentazione, pastorizzazione, aggiunta di acqua","Fermentation, pasteurisation, ajout d'eau","Fermentation, pasteurisation, adding water"],["Aggiunta di alcol, filtrazione, invecchiamento","Ajout d'alcool, filtration, vieillissement","Adding alcohol, filtration, ageing"],["Distillazione, filtrazione, imbottigliamento","Distillation, filtration, mise en bouteille","Distillation, filtration, bottling"]],"e":["Fermentazione, filtrazione e imbottigliamento ci sono in ogni sake.","Fermentation, filtration et mise en bouteille ont lieu pour tout saké.","Fermentation, filtration and bottling happen for every sake."],"d":["Pastorizzazione, aggiunta di acqua e aggiunta di alcol sono facoltative. Il sake non si distilla, e l'invecchiamento riguarda solo uno stile speciale, il koshu.","Pasteurisation, ajout d'eau et ajout d'alcool sont facultatifs. Le saké n'est pas distillé, et le vieillissement ne concerne qu'un style spécial, le koshu.","Pasteurisation, adding water and adding alcohol are optional. Sake is not distilled, and ageing applies only to one speciality style, koshu."]},{"id":"k1d528dc7","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Quale di queste tappe è FACOLTATIVA?","Laquelle de ces étapes est FACULTATIVE ?","Which of these steps is OPTIONAL?"],"o":[["Pastorizzazione","Pasteurisation","Pasteurisation"],["Filtrazione","Filtration","Filtration"],["Fermentazione","Fermentation","Fermentation"],["Imbottigliamento","Mise en bouteille","Bottling"]],"e":["La pastorizzazione è molto diffusa ma non obbligatoria: i sake che la saltano si chiamano nama.","La pasteurisation est très répandue mais pas obligatoire : les sakés qui s'en passent s'appellent nama.","Pasteurisation is very common but not compulsory: sakes that skip it are called nama."],"d":["Filtrazione, fermentazione e imbottigliamento avvengono sempre; la filtrazione è anzi richiesta dalla legge.","Filtration, fermentation et mise en bouteille ont toujours lieu ; la filtration est même exigée par la loi.","Filtration, fermentation and bottling always happen; filtration is even required by law."]},{"id":"k12b6777d","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["A che cosa serve l'avviamento della fermentazione?","À quoi sert le levain de fermentation ?","What is the fermentation starter for?"],"o":[["A creare una popolazione di lieviti sana e attiva","À créer une population de levures saine et active","To build a healthy, active yeast population"],["A togliere i residui solidi di riso","À retirer les résidus solides de riz","To remove the rice solids"],["A ridurre il grado alcolico","À réduire le degré d'alcool","To lower the alcohol level"],["A pastorizzare il sake","À pasteuriser le saké","To pasteurise the sake"]],"e":["Con pochi ingredienti si moltiplicano i lieviti, poi l'avviamento passa alla fermentazione principale.","Avec peu d'ingrédients, on multiplie les levures, puis le levain passe à la fermentation principale.","A little of the ingredients is used to multiply the yeast; the starter then goes into the main fermentation."],"d":["I residui si tolgono con la filtrazione, il grado si abbassa con l'acqua, la pastorizzazione è un trattamento con il calore: tutte tappe successive.","Les résidus s'enlèvent par filtration, le degré baisse avec l'eau, la pasteurisation est un traitement thermique : ce sont des étapes ultérieures.","Solids are removed by filtration, alcohol is lowered with water, and pasteurisation is a heat treatment: all later steps."]},{"id":"k119725e9","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si intende per «fermentazione parallela» nel sake?","Qu'entend-on par « fermentation parallèle » dans le saké ?","What is meant by 'parallel fermentation' in sake?"],"o":[["Gli enzimi producono zucchero mentre il lievito lo trasforma in alcol","Les enzymes produisent du sucre pendant que la levure le transforme en alcool","Enzymes make sugar while yeast turns it into alcohol"],["Due vasche fermentano lo stesso sake una accanto all'altra","Deux cuves fermentent le même saké côte à côte","Two tanks ferment the same sake side by side"],["Si fanno fermentare insieme riso e uva","On fait fermenter ensemble riz et raisin","Rice and grapes are fermented together"],["Il sake fermenta una seconda volta in bottiglia","Le saké fermente une seconde fois en bouteille","The sake ferments a second time in the bottle"]],"e":["Conversione dell'amido e fermentazione alcolica avvengono nello stesso momento: è unico del sake.","Conversion de l'amidon et fermentation alcoolique ont lieu en même temps : c'est propre au saké.","Starch conversion and alcoholic fermentation happen at the same time: this is unique to sake."],"d":["«Parallela» si riferisce alle due reazioni simultanee, non a due vasche. Nel sake non c'è uva, e la seconda fermentazione in bottiglia non definisce questo termine.","« Parallèle » désigne les deux réactions simultanées, pas deux cuves. Il n'y a pas de raisin dans le saké, et une seconde fermentation en bouteille ne définit pas ce terme.","'Parallel' refers to the two simultaneous reactions, not two tanks. There are no grapes in sake, and a second fermentation in bottle is not what the term means."]},{"id":"k180b5e5d","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Quanto alcol ha di solito il sake alla fine della fermentazione?","Quel degré d'alcool le saké atteint-il généralement en fin de fermentation ?","How much alcohol does sake usually have at the end of fermentation?"],"o":[["Circa 20% vol.","Environ 20 % vol.","About 20% abv"],["Circa 5% vol.","Environ 5 % vol.","About 5% abv"],["Circa 12% vol.","Environ 12 % vol.","About 12% abv"],["Circa 40% vol.","Environ 40 % vol.","About 40% abv"]],"e":["A fine fermentazione il sake arriva in genere intorno al 20%; poi l'acqua lo riporta a 15–17%.","En fin de fermentation, le saké atteint en général environ 20 % ; l'eau le ramène ensuite à 15–17 %.","At the end of fermentation sake is usually around 20%; water then brings it down to 15–17%."],"d":["5% è un grado da birra e 12% da vino leggero. 40% è un grado da distillato, impossibile da raggiungere con la sola fermentazione.","5 % est un degré de bière et 12 % de vin léger. 40 % est un degré de spiritueux, impossible à atteindre par la seule fermentation.","5% is beer strength and 12% light-wine strength. 40% is spirit strength, impossible to reach by fermentation alone."]},{"id":"k17d15e43","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Perché il liquido in fermentazione è bianco e torbido?","Pourquoi le liquide en fermentation est-il blanc et trouble ?","Why is the fermenting liquid white and cloudy?"],"o":[["Per il riso presente nella vasca","À cause du riz présent dans la cuve","Because of the rice in the tank"],["Per l'alcol distillato aggiunto","À cause de l'alcool distillé ajouté","Because of the added distilled alcohol"],["Per il latte aggiunto alla ricetta","À cause du lait ajouté à la recette","Because milk is added to the recipe"],["Per la pastorizzazione","À cause de la pasteurisation","Because of pasteurisation"]],"e":["Il colore bianco viene dal riso: i residui solidi si tolgono poi con la filtrazione.","La couleur blanche vient du riz : les résidus solides sont ensuite retirés par filtration.","The white colour comes from the rice: the solids are removed later by filtration."],"d":["L'alcol neutro è limpido. Nel sake non si aggiunge latte: gli aromi «lattici» vengono dalla fermentazione. La pastorizzazione avviene dopo, sul sake già filtrato.","L'alcool neutre est limpide. On n'ajoute pas de lait au saké : les arômes « lactés » viennent de la fermentation. La pasteurisation a lieu après, sur le saké déjà filtré.","Neutral alcohol is clear. No milk is added to sake: 'lactic' aromas come from fermentation. Pasteurisation happens later, on filtered sake."]},{"id":"k1bf34bec","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Che cosa dice la legge sulla filtrazione del sake?","Que dit la loi sur la filtration du saké ?","What does the law say about filtering sake?"],"o":[["Ogni sake deve essere filtrato","Tout saké doit être filtré","Every sake must be filtered"],["La filtrazione è vietata per i sake premium","La filtration est interdite pour les sakés premium","Filtration is banned for premium sakes"],["Si filtra solo il sake da esportazione","On ne filtre que le saké d'exportation","Only export sake is filtered"],["La legge non ne parla","La loi n'en dit rien","The law says nothing about it"]],"e":["Per legge tutti i sake vanno filtrati dopo la fermentazione.","Selon la loi, tous les sakés doivent être filtrés après la fermentation.","By law, all sake must be filtered after fermentation."],"d":["Anche il nigori, torbido, è filtrato: solo in modo grossolano. Non esiste una regola che esenti i premium o riguardi solo l'esportazione.","Même le nigori, trouble, est filtré : simplement de façon grossière. Aucune règle n'exempte les premium ni ne vise seulement l'export.","Even cloudy nigori is filtered, just roughly. No rule exempts premium sake or applies only to exports."]},{"id":"k1415f25a","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Che cosa elimina la filtrazione?","Qu'élimine la filtration ?","What does filtration remove?"],"o":[["I residui solidi di riso","Les résidus solides de riz","The rice solids"],["L'alcol in eccesso","L'excès d'alcool","Excess alcohol"],["L'anidride carbonica","Le dioxyde de carbone","The carbon dioxide"],["La dolcezza","La douceur","The sweetness"]],"e":["Filtrando si separano i solidi di riso e si ottiene di solito un liquido limpido.","La filtration sépare les solides de riz et donne généralement un liquide limpide.","Filtering separates out the rice solids and usually leaves a clear liquid."],"d":["L'alcol si abbassa aggiungendo acqua, non filtrando. La filtrazione non toglie né gas né dolcezza.","On abaisse l'alcool en ajoutant de l'eau, pas en filtrant. La filtration n'enlève ni le gaz ni la douceur.","Alcohol is lowered by adding water, not by filtering. Filtration removes neither gas nor sweetness."]},{"id":"k157a801d","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["In quale contenitore viene confezionato quasi tutto il sake?","Dans quel contenant presque tout le saké est-il conditionné ?","What container is nearly all sake packed in?"],"o":[["Bottiglie di vetro","Bouteilles en verre","Glass bottles"],["Lattine","Canettes","Cans"],["Fusti di legno","Fûts en bois","Wooden casks"],["Cartoni","Briques en carton","Cartons"]],"e":["Quasi tutti i sake vanno in bottiglie di vetro di varie misure.","Presque tous les sakés sont mis en bouteilles de verre de tailles variées.","Nearly all sake goes into glass bottles of various sizes."],"d":["Lattine e cartoni esistono, ma sono rari. Il legno, e soprattutto la quercia, si usa molto raramente anche solo per l'invecchiamento.","Canettes et briques existent mais sont rares. Le bois, surtout le chêne, est très rarement utilisé, même pour le vieillissement.","Cans and cartons exist but are rare. Wood, and oak especially, is very rarely used, even for ageing."]},{"id":"k15f228d2","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Perché un birraio aggiunge alcol distillato neutro prima della filtrazione?","Pourquoi un brasseur ajoute-t-il de l'alcool distillé neutre avant la filtration ?","Why does a brewer add neutral distilled alcohol before filtration?"],"o":[["Per estrarre gli aromi intrappolati nei solidi di riso","Pour extraire les arômes piégés dans les solides de riz","To extract flavours trapped in the rice solids"],["Per trasformare il sake in un distillato","Pour transformer le saké en spiritueux","To turn the sake into a spirit"],["Per far ripartire la fermentazione","Pour relancer la fermentation","To restart fermentation"],["Per dare colore al sake","Pour donner de la couleur au saké","To give the sake colour"]],"e":["L'alcol neutro aiuta a tirare fuori gli aromi rimasti nei residui solidi.","L'alcool neutre aide à extraire les arômes restés dans les résidus solides.","The neutral alcohol helps draw out flavours left in the solids."],"d":["Il sake resta una bevanda fermentata e poi viene diluito con acqua. L'alcol non fa ripartire la fermentazione, e non colora: è neutro.","Le saké reste une boisson fermentée, ensuite allongée d'eau. L'alcool ne relance pas la fermentation et ne colore pas : il est neutre.","Sake stays a fermented drink and is later diluted with water. The alcohol does not restart fermentation and adds no colour: it is neutral."]},{"id":"k1fc0667c","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["In quale momento si aggiunge l'alcol distillato, quando viene usato?","À quel moment ajoute-t-on l'alcool distillé, lorsqu'on l'utilise ?","At what point is distilled alcohol added, when it is used?"],"o":[["Prima della filtrazione","Avant la filtration","Before filtration"],["Prima di cuocere il riso","Avant de cuire le riz","Before steaming the rice"],["Dopo l'imbottigliamento","Après la mise en bouteille","After bottling"],["Durante la preparazione del kōji","Pendant la fabrication du kōji","While making kōji"]],"e":["L'alcol si aggiunge a fine fermentazione, prima di filtrare, quando ci sono ancora i solidi di riso.","L'alcool est ajouté en fin de fermentation, avant la filtration, quand les solides de riz sont encore là.","It is added at the end of fermentation, before filtering, while the rice solids are still present."],"d":["Il suo scopo è estrarre aromi dai solidi: dopo la filtrazione o l'imbottigliamento i solidi non ci sono più. Non ha alcun ruolo nel kōji o nella cottura.","Son but est d'extraire les arômes des solides : après filtration ou mise en bouteille, il n'y en a plus. Il ne joue aucun rôle dans le kōji ni la cuisson.","Its job is to extract flavour from the solids: after filtration or bottling there are none left. It has no role in kōji or steaming."]},{"id":"k1e7c7c82","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Perché quasi sempre si aggiunge acqua al sake prima dell'imbottigliamento?","Pourquoi ajoute-t-on presque toujours de l'eau au saké avant la mise en bouteille ?","Why is water nearly always added to sake before bottling?"],"o":[["Per abbassare l'alcol da circa 20% a 15–17%","Pour abaisser l'alcool d'environ 20 % à 15–17 %","To lower the alcohol from about 20% to 15–17%"],["Per renderlo torbido","Pour le rendre trouble","To make it cloudy"],["Per pastorizzarlo","Pour le pasteuriser","To pasteurise it"],["Per farlo diventare frizzante","Pour le rendre pétillant","To make it sparkling"]],"e":["L'acqua porta il sake dal grado di fine fermentazione (circa 20%) a quello abituale (15–17%).","L'eau fait passer le saké du degré de fin de fermentation (environ 20 %) au degré habituel (15–17 %).","Water takes sake from its end-of-fermentation strength (about 20%) to the usual 15–17%."],"d":["La torbidità viene dai solidi di riso lasciati dal nigori, le bollicine dall'anidride carbonica, la pastorizzazione dal calore: l'acqua non fa nessuna di queste cose.","Le trouble vient des solides de riz laissés dans le nigori, les bulles du dioxyde de carbone, la pasteurisation de la chaleur : l'eau ne fait rien de tout cela.","Cloudiness comes from rice solids left in nigori, bubbles from carbon dioxide and pasteurisation from heat: water does none of these."]},{"id":"k1bc764c5","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la pastorizzazione del sake?","Qu'est-ce que la pasteurisation du saké ?","What is pasteurisation of sake?"],"o":[["Un trattamento con il calore prima della vendita","Un traitement par la chaleur avant la vente","A heat treatment before the sake goes on sale"],["Un invecchiamento in botti di cedro","Un vieillissement en fûts de cèdre","Ageing in cedar casks"],["Un'aggiunta di zucchero","Un ajout de sucre","An addition of sugar"],["Una seconda filtrazione con carbone","Une seconde filtration au charbon","A second filtration through charcoal"]],"e":["Pastorizzare significa scaldare il sake prima di metterlo in vendita.","Pasteuriser, c'est chauffer le saké avant de le mettre en vente.","Pasteurising means heating the sake before it is sold."],"d":["La pastorizzazione non ha nulla a che vedere con il legno, lo zucchero o il carbone: è solo una questione di calore.","La pasteurisation n'a rien à voir avec le bois, le sucre ou le charbon : c'est uniquement une question de chaleur.","Pasteurisation has nothing to do with wood, sugar or charcoal: it is purely about heat."]},{"id":"k183c8d9e","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Quale effetto ha la pastorizzazione?","Quel est l'effet de la pasteurisation ?","What does pasteurisation achieve?"],"o":[["Impedisce lo sviluppo di aromi difettosi","Elle empêche le développement d'arômes défectueux","It prevents faulty aromas from developing"],["Aumenta il grado alcolico","Elle augmente le degré d'alcool","It raises the alcohol level"],["Dà aromi di frutta e fiori","Elle donne des arômes de fruits et de fleurs","It adds fruity and floral aromas"],["Rende il sake torbido","Elle rend le saké trouble","It makes the sake cloudy"]],"e":["Il calore stabilizza il sake ed evita la comparsa di aromi difettosi.","La chaleur stabilise le saké et évite l'apparition d'arômes défectueux.","Heat stabilises the sake and stops faulty aromas from appearing."],"d":["Gli aromi di frutta e fiori vengono da riso molto levigato, lieviti speciali e fermentazione fresca. La pastorizzazione non cambia il grado né la limpidezza.","Les arômes de fruits et de fleurs viennent d'un riz très poli, de levures spéciales et d'une fermentation fraîche. La pasteurisation ne change ni le degré ni la limpidité.","Fruity, floral aromas come from highly polished rice, special yeasts and cool fermentation. Pasteurisation changes neither strength nor clarity."]},{"id":"k171d5022","c":"k02","p":0,"q":["Un sake è appena uscito dalla fermentazione: quale sequenza delle tappe successive è corretta?","Un saké sort de fermentation : quel ordre des étapes suivantes est correct ?","A sake has just finished fermenting: which order of the next steps is correct?"],"o":[["Eventuale alcol → filtrazione → acqua → imbottigliamento","Alcool éventuel → filtration → eau → mise en bouteille","Optional alcohol → filtration → water → bottling"],["Filtrazione → alcol → imbottigliamento → acqua","Filtration → alcool → mise en bouteille → eau","Filtration → alcohol → bottling → water"],["Imbottigliamento → filtrazione → alcol → acqua","Mise en bouteille → filtration → alcool → eau","Bottling → filtration → alcohol → water"],["Acqua → imbottigliamento → alcol → filtrazione","Eau → mise en bouteille → alcool → filtration","Water → bottling → alcohol → filtration"]],"e":["L'alcol va prima della filtrazione (servono i solidi), l'acqua prima dell'imbottigliamento.","L'alcool précède la filtration (il faut les solides), l'eau précède la mise en bouteille.","Alcohol comes before filtration (it needs the solids) and water before bottling."],"d":["Aggiungere alcol dopo la filtrazione non avrebbe senso, perché non ci sarebbero più solidi da cui estrarre aromi. L'acqua serve a regolare il grado prima che il sake finisca in bottiglia.","Ajouter l'alcool après la filtration n'aurait pas de sens : il n'y aurait plus de solides dont extraire les arômes. L'eau ajuste le degré avant la mise en bouteille.","Adding alcohol after filtration would be pointless: there would be no solids left to extract flavour from. Water adjusts the strength before the sake is bottled."]},{"id":"k170923f2","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le quattro fasi che trasformano il riso integrale in riso bianco cotto a vapore?","Quelles sont les quatre étapes qui transforment le riz brun en riz blanc cuit à la vapeur ?","Which four stages turn brown rice into steamed white rice?"],"o":[["Levigatura, lavaggio, ammollo, cottura a vapore","Polissage, lavage, trempage, cuisson à la vapeur","Polishing, washing, soaking, steaming"],["Maltazione, macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura","Maltage, concassage, brassage, ébullition","Malting, milling, mashing, boiling"],["Lavaggio, essiccazione, tostatura, macinatura","Lavage, séchage, torréfaction, mouture","Washing, drying, roasting, grinding"],["Ammollo, germinazione, essiccazione, levigatura","Trempage, germination, séchage, polissage","Soaking, germination, drying, polishing"]],"e":["Il riso integrale viene levigato, lavato, messo in ammollo e cotto a vapore.","Le riz brun est poli, lavé, mis à tremper puis cuit à la vapeur.","Brown rice is polished, washed, soaked and steamed."],"d":["Maltazione, macinatura e ammostamento appartengono alla birra. Il riso del sake non viene fatto germinare né tostato.","Maltage, concassage et brassage appartiennent à la bière. Le riz du saké n'est ni germé ni torréfié.","Malting, milling and mashing belong to beer. Sake rice is neither germinated nor roasted."]},{"id":"k10dd7037","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Come avviene la levigatura del riso?","Comment se fait le polissage du riz ?","How is rice polished?"],"o":[["I chicchi passano per alcune ore tra due superfici ruvide","Les grains passent quelques heures entre deux surfaces rugueuses","Grains pass between two rough surfaces for a few hours"],["I chicchi vengono sciolti in acqua bollente","Les grains sont dissous dans l'eau bouillante","Grains are dissolved in boiling water"],["Una muffa consuma gli strati esterni","Une moisissure dévore les couches extérieures","A mould eats away the outer layers"],["I chicchi vengono tostati finché la buccia cade","Les grains sont torréfiés jusqu'à ce que l'enveloppe tombe","Grains are roasted until the husk falls off"]],"e":["Due superfici ruvide consumano lentamente, nel giro di alcune ore, gli strati esterni e parte di quelli intermedi.","Deux surfaces rugueuses usent lentement, en quelques heures, les couches extérieures et une partie des intermédiaires.","Two rough surfaces slowly wear away the outer and some middle layers over a few hours."],"d":["La muffa interviene dopo, sul riso cotto, per fare il kōji. Il riso non viene sciolto né tostato.","La moisissure intervient plus tard, sur le riz cuit, pour faire le kōji. Le riz n'est ni dissous ni torréfié.","The mould comes later, on steamed rice, to make kōji. The rice is neither dissolved nor roasted."]},{"id":"k1c5404c2","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Di che colore sono gli strati intermedi del chicco di riso?","De quelle couleur sont les couches intermédiaires du grain de riz ?","What colour are the middle layers of a rice grain?"],"o":[["Bianchi","Blanches","White"],["Marroni","Brunes","Brown"],["Verdi","Vertes","Green"],["Neri","Noires","Black"]],"e":["Gli strati esterni sono marroni, quelli intermedi e il nucleo sono bianchi.","Les couches extérieures sont brunes, les intermédiaires et le cœur sont blancs.","The outer layers are brown; the middle layers and core are white."],"d":["Il marrone è il colore degli strati esterni, che si tolgono quasi sempre. Verde e nero non descrivono nessuna parte del chicco.","Le brun est la couleur des couches extérieures, presque toujours retirées. Ni vert ni noir ne décrivent une partie du grain.","Brown is the colour of the outer layers, which are nearly always removed. Neither green nor black describes any part of the grain."]},{"id":"k1d89e068","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Di che cosa è fatto quasi interamente il nucleo del chicco di riso?","De quoi est presque entièrement fait le cœur du grain de riz ?","What is the core of a rice grain made of, almost entirely?"],"o":[["Amido","Amidon","Starch"],["Zucchero","Sucre","Sugar"],["Grassi e proteine","Graisses et protéines","Fats and proteins"],["Acqua","Eau","Water"]],"e":["Il nucleo è quasi amido puro: per questo levigare molto dà sake più puri.","Le cœur est presque de l'amidon pur : c'est pourquoi un polissage poussé donne des sakés plus purs.","The core is almost pure starch: that is why heavy polishing gives purer sakes."],"d":["Il riso non contiene zucchero, e le «altre sostanze» che danno acidità e umami stanno soprattutto negli strati esterni e intermedi.","Le riz ne contient pas de sucre, et les « autres substances » qui donnent acidité et umami se trouvent surtout dans les couches extérieures et intermédiaires.","Rice contains no sugar, and the 'other components' that give acidity and umami sit mainly in the outer and middle layers."]},{"id":"k1d85c97c","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa portano al sake gli strati esterni e intermedi del chicco?","Qu'apportent au saké les couches extérieures et intermédiaires du grain ?","What do the outer and middle layers of the grain bring to sake?"],"o":[["Più acidità e umami, con aromi di cereali e latticini","Plus d'acidité et d'umami, avec des arômes de céréales et lactés","More acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas"],["Aromi puri di frutta e fiori","Des arômes purs de fruits et de fleurs","Pure fruity and floral aromas"],["Bollicine naturali","Des bulles naturelles","Natural bubbles"],["Un colore ambrato e aromi di frutta secca","Une couleur ambrée et des arômes de fruits secs","An amber colour and dried-fruit aromas"]],"e":["Oltre all'amido contengono altre sostanze che danno acidità, umami e note cerealicole e lattiche.","En plus de l'amidon, elles contiennent d'autres substances qui donnent acidité, umami et notes céréalières et lactées.","Besides starch they contain other components that give acidity, umami and cereal, lactic notes."],"d":["Frutta e fiori arrivano quando questi strati vengono tolti quasi del tutto. Ambra e frutta secca sono tipiche del koshu invecchiato; le bollicine vengono dall'anidride carbonica.","Fruits et fleurs apparaissent quand ces couches sont presque entièrement retirées. Ambre et fruits secs sont typiques du koshu vieilli ; les bulles viennent du dioxyde de carbone.","Fruit and flowers come when these layers are almost entirely removed. Amber and dried fruit belong to aged koshu; bubbles come from carbon dioxide."]},{"id":"k1028c7a0","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Un birraio elimina quasi tutti gli strati intermedi, lasciando soprattutto il nucleo. Che stile otterrà di solito?","Un brasseur retire presque toutes les couches intermédiaires pour garder surtout le cœur. Quel style obtiendra-t-il en général ?","A brewer removes almost all the middle layers, leaving mainly the core. What style will usually result?"],"o":[["Meno acidità e umami, più aromi fruttati e floreali","Moins d'acidité et d'umami, plus d'arômes fruités et floraux","Less acidity and umami, more fruity and floral aromas"],["Più acidità e umami, aromi di cereali","Plus d'acidité et d'umami, arômes de céréales","More acidity and umami, cereal aromas"],["Un sake torbido con pezzetti di riso","Un saké trouble avec des fragments de riz","A cloudy sake with rice fragments"],["Un sake più alcolico, oltre il 25%","Un saké plus alcoolisé, au-delà de 25 %","A stronger sake, above 25% abv"]],"e":["Lasciando quasi solo amido si perdono le sostanze che danno acidità e umami, e prevalgono frutta e fiori.","En ne gardant presque que de l'amidon, on perd les substances qui donnent acidité et umami ; fruits et fleurs dominent.","Keeping almost pure starch removes the components behind acidity and umami, so fruit and flowers take over."],"d":["Più acidità e note di cereali vengono da una levigatura leggera. La torbidità dipende dalla filtrazione grossolana, non dalla levigatura, che non cambia nemmeno il grado alcolico finale.","Plus d'acidité et des notes céréalières viennent d'un polissage léger. Le trouble dépend d'une filtration grossière, pas du polissage, qui ne change pas non plus le degré final.","More acidity and cereal notes come from light polishing. Cloudiness depends on rough filtration, not polishing, which does not change the final strength either."]},{"id":"k17c2aa45","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Chi stabilisce il grado di levigatura minimo per le categorie premium?","Qui fixe le taux de polissage minimum des catégories premium ?","Who sets the minimum polishing for the premium grades?"],"o":[["La legge giapponese","La loi japonaise","Japanese law"],["Ogni cantina, liberamente","Chaque brasserie, librement","Each brewery, freely"],["I fornitori di riso","Les fournisseurs de riz","The rice suppliers"],["Gli importatori di ogni Paese","Les importateurs de chaque pays","The importers in each country"]],"e":["Il grado di levigatura richiesto per ogni categoria premium è fissato dalla legge giapponese.","Le taux de polissage exigé pour chaque catégorie premium est fixé par la loi japonaise.","The polishing ratio required for each premium grade is defined in Japanese law."],"d":["Proprio perché è una legge e non una scelta libera, i termini in etichetta sono una guida affidabile allo stile.","C'est justement parce qu'il s'agit d'une loi et non d'un libre choix que les termes d'étiquette sont un guide fiable du style.","Precisely because it is law rather than free choice, the label terms are a reliable guide to style."]},{"id":"k160f12c1","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta si legge «grado di levigatura 60%». Che cosa significa?","Sur une étiquette, on lit « taux de polissage 60 % ». Qu'est-ce que cela signifie ?","A label says 'polishing ratio 60%'. What does this mean?"],"o":[["È rimasto il 60% del chicco: il 40% è stato tolto","Il reste 60 % du grain : 40 % ont été retirés","60% of the grain remains: 40% has been removed"],["È stato tolto il 60% del chicco","On a retiré 60 % du grain","60% of the grain has been removed"],["Il sake contiene il 60% di riso e il 40% di acqua","Le saké contient 60 % de riz et 40 % d'eau","The sake contains 60% rice and 40% water"],["Il 60% del riso è diventato kōji","60 % du riz est devenu du kōji","60% of the rice became kōji"]],"e":["Il grado di levigatura indica la parte di chicco che resta dopo la levigatura.","Le taux de polissage indique la part du grain qui reste après le polissage.","The polishing ratio shows the part of the grain left after polishing."],"d":["È l'errore più comune: il numero non indica quanto si toglie, ma quanto rimane. Non ha nulla a che vedere con l'acqua o con la quantità di kōji.","C'est l'erreur la plus fréquente : le chiffre n'indique pas ce qu'on enlève, mais ce qui reste. Il n'a rien à voir avec l'eau ni avec la quantité de kōji.","This is the most common mistake: the number shows what remains, not what is removed. It has nothing to do with water or the amount of kōji."]},{"id":"k1f613098","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Quale riso è stato levigato DI PIÙ?","Quel riz a été le PLUS poli ?","Which rice has been polished the MOST?"],"o":[["Grado di levigatura 45%","Taux de polissage 45 %","Polishing ratio 45%"],["Grado di levigatura 60%","Taux de polissage 60 %","Polishing ratio 60%"],["Grado di levigatura 70%","Taux de polissage 70 %","Polishing ratio 70%"],["Grado di levigatura 90%","Taux de polissage 90 %","Polishing ratio 90%"]],"e":["Al 45% resta meno chicco di tutti: è il riso più levigato.","À 45 %, c'est là qu'il reste le moins de grain : c'est le riz le plus poli.","At 45% the least grain remains: this is the most polished rice."],"d":["Più il numero è alto, più chicco resta e meno il riso è stato levigato: il 90% è il meno levigato dei quattro.","Plus le chiffre est élevé, plus il reste de grain et moins le riz a été poli : 90 % est le moins poli des quatre.","The higher the number, the more grain remains and the less polishing: 90% is the least polished of the four."]},{"id":"k179e5d4a","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Qual è il grado di levigatura massimo consentito per daiginjō e junmai daiginjō?","Quel est le taux de polissage maximal autorisé pour daiginjō et junmai daiginjō ?","What is the maximum polishing ratio allowed for daiginjō and junmai daiginjō?"],"o":[["50%","50 %","50%"],["60%","60 %","60%"],["70%","70 %","70%"],["80%","80 %","80%"]],"e":["Per i daiginjō deve restare il 50% del chicco o meno.","Pour les daiginjō, il doit rester 50 % du grain ou moins.","For daiginjō, 50% or less of the grain must remain."],"d":["Il 60% è la soglia di ginjō e junmai ginjō, il 70% quella di honjōzō e della maggior parte dei junmai. L'80% non corrisponde a nessuna categoria premium.","60 % est le seuil des ginjō et junmai ginjō, 70 % celui des honjōzō et de la plupart des junmai. 80 % ne correspond à aucune catégorie premium.","60% is the limit for ginjō and junmai ginjō, 70% for honjōzō and most junmai. 80% matches no premium grade."]},{"id":"k1f87d333","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Quale categoria richiede un grado di levigatura del 60% o meno?","Quelle catégorie exige un taux de polissage de 60 % ou moins ?","Which grade requires a polishing ratio of 60% or less?"],"o":[["Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu"],["Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō"]],"e":["Ginjō e junmai ginjō: 60% o meno.","Ginjō et junmai ginjō : 60 % ou moins.","Ginjō and junmai ginjō: 60% or less."],"d":["Honjōzō si ferma al 70%, junmai daiginjō scende al 50%. Il futsū-shu è il sake di base e non ha soglie premium.","Le honjōzō s'arrête à 70 %, le junmai daiginjō descend à 50 %. Le futsū-shu est le saké de base, sans seuil premium.","Honjōzō stops at 70% and junmai daiginjō goes down to 50%. Futsū-shu is basic sake with no premium threshold."]},{"id":"k1c0df721","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa vale per il grado di levigatura del junmai?","Qu'en est-il du taux de polissage du junmai ?","What is true of the polishing ratio for junmai?"],"o":[["Di solito 70%; si può usare riso fino al 100%, ma è molto raro","Généralement 70 % ; on peut aller jusqu'à 100 %, mais c'est très rare","Usually 70%; rice up to 100% may be used, but this is very rare"],["Deve essere sempre del 50% o meno","Il doit toujours être de 50 % ou moins","It must always be 50% or less"],["È vietato scendere sotto il 70%","Il est interdit de descendre sous 70 %","It may never go below 70%"],["Il junmai non usa riso levigato","Le junmai n'utilise pas de riz poli","Junmai does not use polished rice"]],"e":["Il junmai si fa di solito con riso levigato al 70%; tra 100% e 70% è permesso ma molto raro.","Le junmai se fait généralement avec du riz poli à 70 % ; entre 100 % et 70 %, c'est permis mais très rare.","Junmai is usually made with rice polished to 70%; 100–70% is allowed but very rare."],"d":["Il 50% riguarda i daiginjō. Un junmai può essere più levigato del 70% (anche i junmai ginjō sono junmai), quindi non c'è divieto di scendere sotto.","Les 50 % concernent les daiginjō. Un junmai peut être plus poli que 70 % (les junmai ginjō sont aussi des junmai) : aucune interdiction de descendre.","50% applies to daiginjō. A junmai may be polished further than 70% (junmai ginjō is also junmai), so there is no ban on going lower."]},{"id":"k191281ca","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["Perché il riso va lavato dopo la levigatura?","Pourquoi faut-il laver le riz après le polissage ?","Why must rice be washed after polishing?"],"o":[["Per togliere la polvere degli strati appena eliminati","Pour enlever la poussière des couches qu'on vient d'éliminer","To remove the dust from the layers just polished away"],["Per dare al riso un aroma floreale","Pour donner au riz un arôme floral","To give the rice a floral aroma"],["Per avviare la fermentazione","Pour lancer la fermentation","To start fermentation"],["Per togliere l'amido dal nucleo","Pour enlever l'amidon du cœur","To remove the starch from the core"]],"e":["La polvere è fatta degli strati esterni e intermedi che il birraio voleva togliere.","La poussière est faite des couches extérieures et intermédiaires que le brasseur voulait retirer.","The dust is made of the outer and middle layers the brewer wanted to remove."],"d":["L'amido del nucleo è proprio ciò che serve per fare alcol, quindi non va tolto. Il lavaggio non dà aromi e non avvia la fermentazione.","L'amidon du cœur est justement ce qu'il faut pour faire de l'alcool : on ne l'enlève pas. Le lavage n'apporte pas d'arômes et ne lance pas la fermentation.","The starch in the core is exactly what is needed to make alcohol, so it stays. Washing adds no aroma and does not start fermentation."]},{"id":"k19ffe3da","c":"k03","p":0,"q":["A che cosa servono l'ammollo e la cottura a vapore?","À quoi servent le trempage et la cuisson à la vapeur ?","What are soaking and steaming for?"],"o":[["A dare al chicco consistenza e umidità giuste per sciogliersi nella fermentazione","À donner au grain la texture et l'humidité justes pour se défaire pendant la fermentation","To give the grain the right texture and moisture to break up during fermentation"],["A levigare il chicco più in profondità","À polir le grain plus en profondeur","To polish the grain more deeply"],["A trasformare l'amido in zucchero","À transformer l'amidon en sucre","To turn the starch into sugar"],["A sterilizzare il sake finito","À stériliser le saké fini","To sterilise the finished sake"]],"e":["Ammollo e vapore ammorbidiscono il chicco e gli danno la giusta umidità.","Trempage et vapeur attendrissent le grain et lui donnent la bonne humidité.","Soaking and steaming soften the grain and give it the right moisture."],"d":["L'amido diventa zucchero grazie agli enzimi del kōji. La levigatura avviene prima, e la pastorizzazione del sake finito è un'altra tappa.","L'amidon devient sucre grâce aux enzymes du kōji. Le polissage a lieu avant, et la pasteurisation du saké fini est une autre étape.","Starch becomes sugar thanks to kōji enzymes. Polishing comes first, and pasteurising the finished sake is a different step."]},{"id":"k1eff3ad1","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Che cosa permette di controllare la stanza del kōji?","Que permet de contrôler la salle du kōji ?","What does the kōji room allow the brewer to control?"],"o":[["Temperatura e umidità, con grande precisione","La température et l'humidité, très précisément","Temperature and humidity, very precisely"],["La pressione dell'anidride carbonica","La pression du dioxyde de carbone","Carbon dioxide pressure"],["Il grado alcolico del sake","Le degré d'alcool du saké","The alcohol level of the sake"],["La luce e il rumore","La lumière et le bruit","Light and noise"]],"e":["Le stanze del kōji servono a regolare con precisione caldo e umidità, che decidono la crescita della muffa.","Les salles du kōji servent à régler précisément chaleur et humidité, qui commandent la croissance de la moisissure.","Kōji rooms let the brewer fine-tune warmth and humidity, which drive mould growth."],"d":["Nel kōji non c'è ancora alcol né gas di fermentazione: si tratta solo di far crescere una muffa nelle condizioni giuste.","Dans le kōji, il n'y a encore ni alcool ni gaz de fermentation : il s'agit seulement de faire pousser une moisissure dans de bonnes conditions.","There is no alcohol or fermentation gas yet in kōji making: it is just about growing a mould under the right conditions."]},{"id":"k12954b84","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Qual è la PRIMA fase della preparazione del kōji?","Quelle est la PREMIÈRE étape de la fabrication du kōji ?","What is the FIRST stage of making kōji?"],"o":[["Raffreddare il riso cotto a vapore","Refroidir le riz cuit à la vapeur","Cooling the steamed rice"],["Spargere le spore della muffa","Répandre les spores de la moisissure","Spreading the mould spores"],["Girare il riso a mano","Retourner le riz à la main","Turning the rice by hand"],["Portare il riso nella zona più fresca","Porter le riz dans la zone la plus fraîche","Moving the rice to the coolest zone"]],"e":["Appena uscito dal vapore il riso è troppo caldo: prima di tutto va raffreddato.","À la sortie de la vapeur, le riz est trop chaud : il faut d'abord le refroidir.","Fresh from the steamer the rice is too hot: it must be cooled first."],"d":["Spargere le spore è la seconda fase, girare il riso fa parte della terza, portarlo nella zona più fresca serve a fermare la crescita, alla fine.","Répandre les spores est la deuxième étape, retourner le riz fait partie de la troisième, l'amener dans la zone la plus fraîche sert à arrêter la croissance, à la fin.","Spreading spores is stage two, turning the rice belongs to stage three, and moving it to the coolest zone stops growth at the end."]},{"id":"k18e0e486","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Come si raffredda il riso destinato al kōji?","Comment refroidit-on le riz destiné au kōji ?","How is the rice for kōji cooled?"],"o":[["Steso su stuoie, si raffredda naturalmente","Étalé sur des nattes, il refroidit naturellement","Spread on mats, it cools naturally"],["Immerso in acqua ghiacciata","Plongé dans l'eau glacée","Plunged into iced water"],["Messo in congelatore","Mis au congélateur","Put in a freezer"],["Mescolato con alcol distillato","Mélangé à de l'alcool distillé","Mixed with distilled alcohol"]],"e":["Il riso viene steso su stuoie e lasciato raffreddare da solo.","Le riz est étalé sur des nattes et laissé refroidir seul.","The rice is spread on mats and left to cool by itself."],"d":["L'acqua ghiacciata lo renderebbe troppo bagnato, il congelatore troppo freddo per la muffa. L'alcol distillato non ha nulla a che vedere con il kōji.","L'eau glacée le mouillerait trop, le congélateur le rendrait trop froid pour la moisissure. L'alcool distillé n'a rien à voir avec le kōji.","Iced water would make it too wet and a freezer too cold for the mould. Distilled alcohol has nothing to do with kōji."]},{"id":"k128a396c","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["In quale zona della stanza si spargono le spore della muffa?","Dans quelle zone de la salle répand-on les spores de la moisissure ?","In which part of the room are the mould spores spread?"],"o":[["Nella zona più calda e umida","Dans la zone la plus chaude et la plus humide","The warmest, most humid part"],["Nella zona più fresca e asciutta","Dans la zone la plus fraîche et la plus sèche","The coolest, driest part"],["All'aperto, al sole","Dehors, au soleil","Outdoors, in the sun"],["Nella vasca di fermentazione","Dans la cuve de fermentation","In the fermentation tank"]],"e":["Caldo e umidità fanno partire in fretta la muffa.","Chaleur et humidité font démarrer vite la moisissure.","Warmth and humidity get the mould growing quickly."],"d":["La zona più fresca serve alla fine, per fermare la crescita. Il kōji si fa nelle sue stanze, non all'aperto né in vasca.","La zone la plus fraîche sert à la fin, pour arrêter la croissance. Le kōji se fait dans ses salles, ni dehors ni en cuve.","The coolest zone is used at the end, to stop growth. Kōji is made in its own rooms, not outdoors or in the tank."]},{"id":"k17b49aca","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Perché il riso viene girato regolarmente a mano durante la prima crescita della muffa?","Pourquoi retourne-t-on régulièrement le riz à la main pendant la première croissance de la moisissure ?","Why is the rice turned regularly by hand during the initial mould growth?"],"o":[["Perché la muffa cresca in modo uniforme","Pour que la moisissure pousse de façon homogène","So that the mould grows evenly"],["Per togliere la muffa","Pour retirer la moisissure","To remove the mould"],["Per raffreddarlo sotto zero","Pour le refroidir sous zéro","To cool it below freezing"],["Per aggiungere il lievito","Pour ajouter la levure","To add the yeast"]],"e":["Girare il riso distribuisce caldo e umidità e rende la crescita omogenea.","Retourner le riz répartit chaleur et humidité et rend la croissance homogène.","Turning spreads warmth and moisture so the growth is even."],"d":["La muffa è voluta, non va tolta. Il lievito entra in gioco nella fermentazione, e nel kōji non si scende sotto zero.","La moisissure est voulue, on ne l'enlève pas. La levure intervient à la fermentation, et on ne descend pas sous zéro pour le kōji.","The mould is wanted, not removed. Yeast comes in at fermentation, and kōji is never taken below freezing."]},{"id":"k1808887a","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Come si rallenta e poi si ferma la crescita della muffa?","Comment ralentit-on puis arrête-t-on la croissance de la moisissure ?","How is mould growth slowed and then stopped?"],"o":[["Spostando il riso in zone più fresche, fino alla più fresca","En déplaçant le riz vers des zones plus fraîches, jusqu'à la plus fraîche","By moving the rice to cooler zones, finally the coolest"],["Aggiungendo molta acqua calda","En ajoutant beaucoup d'eau chaude","By adding lots of hot water"],["Cuocendo di nuovo il riso a vapore","En recuisant le riz à la vapeur","By steaming the rice again"],["Mettendo il riso al buio","En plaçant le riz dans l'obscurité","By putting the rice in the dark"]],"e":["Meno caldo e meno umidità rallentano la muffa; la zona più fresca la ferma.","Moins de chaleur et d'humidité ralentissent la moisissure ; la zone la plus fraîche l'arrête.","Less warmth and humidity slow the mould; the coolest zone stops it."],"d":["Acqua calda e vapore aumenterebbero caldo e umidità, cioè il contrario. La luce non è la leva usata: lo sono temperatura e umidità.","Eau chaude et vapeur augmenteraient chaleur et humidité, c'est-à-dire l'inverse. La lumière n'est pas le levier utilisé : ce sont la température et l'humidité.","Hot water and steam would add warmth and moisture, the opposite of what is needed. Light is not the lever: temperature and humidity are."]},{"id":"k164fdbbf","c":"k04","p":0,"q":["Perché il birraio rallenta la muffa invece di lasciarla crescere liberamente?","Pourquoi le brasseur ralentit-il la moisissure au lieu de la laisser pousser librement ?","Why does the brewer slow the mould instead of letting it grow freely?"],"o":[["Per ottenere esattamente la quantità di muffa desiderata","Pour obtenir exactement la quantité de moisissure voulue","To get exactly the right amount of mould"],["Perché la muffa è un difetto","Parce que la moisissure est un défaut","Because mould is a fault"],["Per rendere il sake frizzante","Pour rendre le saké pétillant","To make the sake sparkling"],["Per alzare il grado di levigatura","Pour augmenter le taux de polissage","To raise the polishing ratio"]],"e":["L'obiettivo è una crescita misurata: né troppa né troppo poca muffa.","L'objectif est une croissance mesurée : ni trop ni trop peu de moisissure.","The goal is measured growth: neither too much nor too little mould."],"d":["La muffa del kōji è indispensabile, non un difetto. Le bollicine e il grado di levigatura non dipendono da questa fase.","La moisissure du kōji est indispensable, ce n'est pas un défaut. Les bulles et le taux de polissage ne dépendent pas de cette étape.","The kōji mould is essential, not a fault. Bubbles and the polishing ratio do not depend on this stage."]},{"id":"k16f6d778","c":"k05","p":0,"q":["In quasi tutti gli stili di sake, quale ingrediente contribuisce di più agli aromi?","Dans presque tous les styles de saké, quel ingrédient contribue le plus aux arômes ?","In nearly all sake styles, which ingredient contributes most to the aromas?"],"o":[["Il lievito","La levure","Yeast"],["L'acqua","L'eau","Water"],["Il kōji","Le kōji","Kōji"],["L'alcol distillato","L'alcool distillé","Distilled alcohol"]],"e":["Il lievito dà una parte importante degli aromi in quasi tutti gli stili.","La levure apporte une part importante des arômes dans presque tous les styles.","Yeast contributes a large share of the aromas in nearly all styles."],"d":["In molti stili riso, kōji e acqua danno relativamente poco gusto. L'alcol aggiunto è neutro: aiuta a estrarre aromi, ma non ne porta di suoi.","Dans beaucoup de styles, riz, kōji et eau donnent relativement peu de goût. L'alcool ajouté est neutre : il aide à extraire les arômes, sans en apporter.","In many styles rice, kōji and water give relatively little flavour. Added alcohol is neutral: it helps extract flavour but brings none of its own."]},{"id":"k16cffdd6","c":"k05","p":0,"q":["Che cosa serve per ottenere gli aromi fruttati e floreali tipici degli stili ginjō?","Que faut-il pour obtenir les arômes fruités et floraux typiques des styles ginjō ?","What is needed for the fruity, floral aromas typical of ginjō styles?"],"o":[["Lieviti speciali e temperature di fermentazione più basse","Des levures spéciales et des températures de fermentation plus basses","Special yeast strains and lower fermentation temperatures"],["Lieviti qualsiasi e temperature più alte","N'importe quelle levure et des températures plus hautes","Any yeast and higher temperatures"],["Molta acqua e una lunga pastorizzazione","Beaucoup d'eau et une longue pasteurisation","Lots of water and a long pasteurisation"],["Invecchiamento in rovere","Un vieillissement en fût de chêne","Ageing in oak"]],"e":["Gli aromi ginjō richiedono ceppi di lievito speciali e una fermentazione fresca.","Les arômes ginjō exigent des souches de levure spéciales et une fermentation fraîche.","Ginjō aromas require special yeast strains and a cool fermentation."],"d":["Le temperature calde portano aromi di cereali e latticini. Acqua e pastorizzazione non creano profumi fruttati, e il rovere si usa pochissimo nel sake.","Les températures chaudes donnent des arômes de céréales et lactés. L'eau et la pasteurisation ne créent pas de parfums fruités, et le chêne est très peu utilisé pour le saké.","Warm temperatures give cereal and lactic aromas. Water and pasteurisation do not create fruity scents, and oak is very rarely used in sake."]},{"id":"k148027a0","c":"k05","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi tende a dare una fermentazione più calda?","Quels arômes une fermentation plus chaude tend-elle à donner ?","What aromas does a warmer fermentation tend to give?"],"o":[["Cereali e latticini","Céréales et produits laitiers","Cereal and lactic"],["Fiori bianchi e frutta delicata","Fleurs blanches et fruits délicats","White flowers and delicate fruit"],["Frutta secca e carne","Fruits secs et viande","Dried fruit and meat"],["Caramello e toffee","Caramel et caramel au beurre","Caramel and toffee"]],"e":["Più calore in fermentazione = aromi di cereali e lattici.","Plus de chaleur en fermentation = arômes de céréales et lactés.","More warmth in fermentation = cereal and lactic aromas."],"d":["Fiori e frutta delicata vengono dalla fermentazione fresca. Frutta secca e carne sono tipiche del koshu; caramello e toffee indicano spesso un sake ossidato o vecchio.","Fleurs et fruits délicats viennent de la fermentation fraîche. Fruits secs et viande sont typiques du koshu ; caramel et caramel au beurre signalent souvent un saké oxydé ou trop vieux.","Flowers and delicate fruit come from cool fermentation. Dried fruit and meat belong to koshu; caramel and toffee often signal an oxidised or old sake."]},{"id":"k17a223e3","c":"k05","p":0,"q":["Quale combinazione produce di solito un sake fruttato e floreale, con poca acidità e umami?","Quelle combinaison donne généralement un saké fruité et floral, avec peu d'acidité et d'umami ?","Which combination usually produces a fruity, floral sake with little acidity and umami?"],"o":[["Riso molto levigato, lieviti speciali, fermentazione fresca","Riz très poli, levures spéciales, fermentation fraîche","Highly polished rice, special yeasts, cool fermentation"],["Riso poco levigato, fermentazione calda","Riz peu poli, fermentation chaude","Lightly polished rice, warm fermentation"],["Riso poco levigato, lieviti speciali, invecchiamento","Riz peu poli, levures spéciales, vieillissement","Lightly polished rice, special yeasts, ageing"],["Riso molto levigato, fermentazione calda, niente filtrazione","Riz très poli, fermentation chaude, pas de filtration","Highly polished rice, warm fermentation, no filtration"]],"e":["Sono i tre fattori dello stile ginjō: levigatura spinta, lieviti speciali, temperatura bassa.","Ce sont les trois facteurs du style ginjō : polissage poussé, levures spéciales, température basse.","These are the three factors of the ginjō style: heavy polishing, special yeasts, low temperature."],"d":["Riso poco levigato e fermentazione calda danno note di cereali, latticini, più acidità e umami. La filtrazione è comunque obbligatoria per legge.","Riz peu poli et fermentation chaude donnent des notes céréalières et lactées, plus d'acidité et d'umami. La filtration est de toute façon obligatoire.","Lightly polished rice and warm fermentation give cereal, lactic notes with more acidity and umami. Filtration is required by law anyway."]},{"id":"k168b4c64","c":"k05","p":0,"q":["Durante la fermentazione, quali sono le due leve con cui il birraio orienta lo stile?","Pendant la fermentation, quels sont les deux leviers avec lesquels le brasseur oriente le style ?","During fermentation, which two levers does the brewer use to steer style?"],"o":[["La scelta del lievito e la temperatura","Le choix de la levure et la température","Choice of yeast and temperature"],["La scelta della bottiglia e la luce","Le choix de la bouteille et la lumière","Choice of bottle and light"],["Il tipo di legno e il tempo in botte","Le type de bois et le temps en fût","Type of wood and time in cask"],["La quantità di zucchero aggiunto e il gas","La quantité de sucre ajouté et le gaz","Amount of added sugar and gas"]],"e":["Lievito e temperatura di fermentazione cambiano molto il profilo aromatico.","Levure et température de fermentation changent beaucoup le profil aromatique.","Yeast and fermentation temperature change the aroma profile a great deal."],"d":["Bottiglia e luce riguardano la conservazione, non la fermentazione. Il legno è raro nel sake, e lo zucchero non viene aggiunto per orientare lo stile.","Bouteille et lumière concernent la conservation, pas la fermentation. Le bois est rare pour le saké, et l'on n'ajoute pas de sucre pour orienter le style.","Bottle and light concern storage, not fermentation. Wood is rare in sake, and sugar is not added to steer the style."]},{"id":"k13fade1d","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Come si chiama in giapponese il sake di base?","Comment appelle-t-on en japonais le saké de base ?","What is basic sake called in Japanese?"],"o":[["Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu"],["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],["Koshu","Koshu","Koshu"],["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"]],"e":["Futsū-shu è il nome del sake di base, semplice.","Futsū-shu est le nom du saké de base, simple.","Futsū-shu is the name for simple, basic sake."],"d":["Junmai e daiginjō sono gradi premium; koshu è lo stile speciale dei sake invecchiati.","Junmai et daiginjō sont des grades premium ; koshu est le style spécial des sakés vieillis.","Junmai and daiginjō are premium grades; koshu is the speciality style for aged sake."]},{"id":"k1e8d6b1c","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Qual è la divisione principale delle categorie di sake?","Quelle est la grande division des catégories de saké ?","What is the main division of sake categories?"],"o":[["Sake di base e sake premium","Saké de base et saké premium","Basic sake and premium sake"],["Sake bianco e sake rosso","Saké blanc et saké rouge","White sake and red sake"],["Sake secco e sake dolce","Saké sec et saké doux","Dry sake and sweet sake"],["Sake giapponese e sake estero","Saké japonais et saké étranger","Japanese and foreign sake"]],"e":["Prima si distingue tra base (futsū-shu) e premium, poi il premium si divide in gradi.","On distingue d'abord base (futsū-shu) et premium, puis le premium se divise en grades.","First comes basic (futsū-shu) versus premium, then premium splits into grades."],"d":["Il sake non è rosso. Dolcezza e origine non sono il criterio principale delle categorie.","Le saké n'est pas rouge. La douceur et l'origine ne sont pas le critère principal des catégories.","Sake is not red. Sweetness and origin are not the main basis of the categories."]},{"id":"k1353d36e","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Che cosa hanno in comune quasi tutti i sake premium con il sake di base?","Qu'ont en commun presque tous les sakés premium avec le saké de base ?","What do nearly all premium sakes share with basic sake?"],"o":[["Lo stesso grado alcolico e lo stesso colore","Le même degré d'alcool et la même couleur","The same alcohol level and colour"],["Lo stesso grado di levigatura","Le même taux de polissage","The same polishing ratio"],["Gli stessi aromi fruttati","Les mêmes arômes fruités","The same fruity aromas"],["Lo stesso prezzo","Le même prix","The same price"]],"e":["La maggior parte dei premium ha grado e colore simili al futsū-shu; cambiano gli aromi e lo stile.","La plupart des premium ont un degré et une couleur proches du futsū-shu ; ce sont les arômes et le style qui changent.","Most premium sakes have similar strength and colour to futsū-shu; aromas and style change."],"d":["La levigatura è proprio ciò che distingue i gradi premium. Gli aromi variano tra le due famiglie di stile.","Le polissage est justement ce qui distingue les grades premium. Les arômes varient entre les deux familles de style.","Polishing is exactly what sets the premium grades apart. Aromas differ between the two style families."]},{"id":"k19789174","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quale parola indica in etichetta lo stile con aromi puri di fiori e frutta?","Quel mot indique sur l'étiquette le style aux arômes purs de fleurs et de fruits ?","Which label word indicates the style with pure floral and fruity aromas?"],"o":[["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Nama","Nama","Nama"],["Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu"]],"e":["Ginjō è la parola chiave dello stile fruttato e floreale.","Ginjō est le mot clé du style fruité et floral.","Ginjō is the key word for the fruity, floral style."],"d":["Honjōzō sta nello stile cerealicolo e lattico. Nama indica solo l'assenza di pastorizzazione, futsū-shu il sake di base.","Le honjōzō appartient au style céréalier et lacté. Nama indique seulement l'absence de pasteurisation, futsū-shu le saké de base.","Honjōzō belongs to the cereal, lactic style. Nama only means unpasteurised, and futsū-shu is basic sake."]},{"id":"k1bf8e9e8","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa letteralmente daiginjō?","Que signifie littéralement daiginjō ?","What does daiginjō literally mean?"],"o":[["Grande ginjō","Grand ginjō","Big ginjō"],["Riso puro","Riz pur","Pure rice"],["Sake invecchiato","Saké vieilli","Aged sake"],["Sake crudo","Saké cru","Raw sake"]],"e":["Dai significa «grande»: daiginjō è il «grande ginjō», con gli aromi più puri.","Dai signifie « grand » : daiginjō est le « grand ginjō », aux arômes les plus purs.","Dai means 'big': daiginjō is the 'big ginjō', with the purest aromas."],"d":["«Riso puro» è junmai, «sake invecchiato» è koshu. Nama (non pastorizzato) è a volte descritto come «crudo», ma non è daiginjō.","« Riz pur » est junmai, « saké vieilli » est koshu. Nama (non pasteurisé) est parfois décrit comme « cru », mais ce n'est pas daiginjō.","'Pure rice' is junmai and 'aged sake' is koshu. Nama (unpasteurised) is sometimes described as 'raw', but that is not daiginjō."]},{"id":"k165e007b","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quali sake hanno di solito aromi di cereali e latticini, con più acidità e umami?","Quels sakés ont généralement des arômes de céréales et lactés, avec plus d'acidité et d'umami ?","Which sakes usually have cereal and lactic aromas with more acidity and umami?"],"o":[["Junmai e honjōzō","Junmai et honjōzō","Junmai and honjōzō"],["Ginjō e daiginjō","Ginjō et daiginjō","Ginjō and daiginjō"],["Junmai ginjō e junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō et junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō"],["Daiginjō e junmai daiginjō","Daiginjō et junmai daiginjō","Daiginjō and junmai daiginjō"]],"e":["Junmai e honjōzō formano la famiglia cerealicola e lattica.","Junmai et honjōzō forment la famille céréalière et lactée.","Junmai and honjōzō make up the cereal, lactic family."],"d":["Tutti gli altri gradi contengono la parola ginjō: appartengono allo stile fruttato e floreale, con meno acidità e umami.","Tous les autres grades contiennent le mot ginjō : ils appartiennent au style fruité et floral, avec moins d'acidité et d'umami.","All the other options contain the word ginjō: they belong to the fruity, floral style with less acidity and umami."]},{"id":"k19ff78a1","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa junmai?","Que signifie junmai ?","What does junmai mean?"],"o":[["Riso puro: nessun alcol distillato aggiunto","Riz pur : aucun alcool distillé ajouté","Pure rice: no distilled alcohol added"],["Riso levigato al 50%","Riz poli à 50 %","Rice polished to 50%"],["Sake non filtrato","Saké non filtré","Unfiltered sake"],["Sake non pastorizzato","Saké non pasteurisé","Unpasteurised sake"]],"e":["Junmai significa «riso puro»: prima della filtrazione non è stato aggiunto alcol distillato.","Junmai signifie « riz pur » : aucun alcool distillé n'a été ajouté avant la filtration.","Junmai means 'pure rice': no distilled alcohol was added before filtration."],"d":["Il 50% è la soglia dei daiginjō. Ogni sake è filtrato per legge; il sake non pastorizzato si chiama nama.","Les 50 % sont le seuil des daiginjō. Tout saké est filtré par la loi ; le saké non pasteurisé s'appelle nama.","50% is the daiginjō threshold. All sake is filtered by law; unpasteurised sake is called nama."]},{"id":"k1dd79ae3","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'UNICA differenza tra un ginjō e un junmai ginjō?","Quelle est la SEULE différence entre un ginjō et un junmai ginjō ?","What is the ONLY difference between a ginjō and a junmai ginjō?"],"o":[["Il junmai ginjō non ha alcol distillato aggiunto","Le junmai ginjō n'a pas d'alcool distillé ajouté","The junmai ginjō has no added distilled alcohol"],["Il junmai ginjō è levigato al 70%","Le junmai ginjō est poli à 70 %","The junmai ginjō is polished to 70%"],["Il junmai ginjō è torbido","Le junmai ginjō est trouble","The junmai ginjō is cloudy"],["Il junmai ginjō è invecchiato","Le junmai ginjō est vieilli","The junmai ginjō is aged"]],"e":["Lo stile è simile; cambia solo l'alcol aggiunto, assente nel junmai ginjō.","Le style est proche ; seul change l'alcool ajouté, absent du junmai ginjō.","The style is similar; only the added alcohol differs, absent in junmai ginjō."],"d":["Entrambi richiedono riso levigato al 60% o meno. Torbidità (nigori) e invecchiamento (koshu) sono stili speciali, non la differenza tra questi due gradi.","Les deux exigent un riz poli à 60 % ou moins. Le trouble (nigori) et le vieillissement (koshu) sont des styles spéciaux, pas la différence entre ces deux grades.","Both require rice polished to 60% or less. Cloudiness (nigori) and ageing (koshu) are speciality styles, not the difference between these grades."]},{"id":"k14fd18fa","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Un sake è levigato al 65% e ha ricevuto alcol distillato prima della filtrazione. Quale grado può portare?","Un saké est poli à 65 % et a reçu de l'alcool distillé avant filtration. Quel grade peut-il porter ?","A sake is polished to 65% and had distilled alcohol added before filtration. Which grade can it carry?"],"o":[["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],["Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō"]],"e":["Con alcol aggiunto e levigatura al 70% o meno (ma sopra il 60%), il grado è honjōzō.","Avec alcool ajouté et un polissage de 70 % ou moins (mais au-dessus de 60 %), le grade est honjōzō.","With added alcohol and polishing of 70% or less (but above 60%), the grade is honjōzō."],"d":["Per il ginjō servirebbe il 60% o meno. Junmai e junmai ginjō escludono l'alcol aggiunto.","Pour le ginjō, il faudrait 60 % ou moins. Junmai et junmai ginjō excluent l'alcool ajouté.","Ginjō would need 60% or less. Junmai and junmai ginjō rule out added alcohol."]},{"id":"k189a2c89","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Un sake è levigato al 45% e non ha alcol aggiunto. Quale grado più alto può portare?","Un saké est poli à 45 % sans alcool ajouté. Quel grade le plus élevé peut-il porter ?","A sake is polished to 45% with no added alcohol. What is the highest grade it can carry?"],"o":[["Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō"],["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"],["Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō","Junmai ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"]],"e":["Riso al 50% o meno e nessun alcol aggiunto: junmai daiginjō.","Riz à 50 % ou moins et aucun alcool ajouté : junmai daiginjō.","Rice at 50% or less and no added alcohol: junmai daiginjō."],"d":["Daiginjō e honjōzō indicano alcol aggiunto. Junmai ginjō sarebbe possibile, ma non è il grado più alto per un riso al 45%.","Daiginjō et honjōzō indiquent un alcool ajouté. Junmai ginjō serait possible, mais ce n'est pas le grade le plus élevé pour un riz à 45 %.","Daiginjō and honjōzō mean added alcohol. Junmai ginjō would be possible, but it is not the highest grade for rice at 45%."]},{"id":"k1d7ec4eb","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quanti dei sei principali gradi premium contengono la parola junmai?","Combien des six principaux grades premium contiennent le mot junmai ?","How many of the six main premium grades contain the word junmai?"],"o":[["Tre","Trois","Three"],["Due","Deux","Two"],["Quattro","Quatre","Four"],["Sei","Six","Six"]],"e":["Junmai, junmai ginjō e junmai daiginjō: tre gradi senza alcol aggiunto.","Junmai, junmai ginjō et junmai daiginjō : trois grades sans alcool ajouté.","Junmai, junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō: three grades with no added alcohol."],"d":["Gli altri tre (honjōzō, ginjō, daiginjō) hanno alcol distillato aggiunto prima della filtrazione.","Les trois autres (honjōzō, ginjō, daiginjō) ont un alcool distillé ajouté avant filtration.","The other three (honjōzō, ginjō, daiginjō) have distilled alcohol added before filtration."]},{"id":"k127051f1","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Un cliente cerca un sake premium con aromi puri di frutta e fiori, fatto solo di riso, senza alcol aggiunto. Che cosa proporre?","Un client cherche un saké premium aux arômes purs de fruits et de fleurs, fait uniquement de riz, sans alcool ajouté. Que proposer ?","A customer wants a premium sake with pure fruity, floral aromas, made from rice only with no added alcohol. What do you suggest?"],"o":[["Junmai ginjō o junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō ou junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō or junmai daiginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Ginjō o daiginjō","Ginjō ou daiginjō","Ginjō or daiginjō"],["Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu"]],"e":["Ginjō = frutta e fiori; junmai = niente alcol aggiunto: servono entrambe le parole.","Ginjō = fruits et fleurs ; junmai = pas d'alcool ajouté : il faut les deux mots.","Ginjō = fruit and flowers; junmai = no added alcohol: both words are needed."],"d":["Ginjō e daiginjō senza junmai hanno alcol aggiunto. Honjōzō ha alcol aggiunto e stile cerealicolo; il futsū-shu non è premium.","Ginjō et daiginjō sans junmai ont de l'alcool ajouté. Le honjōzō a de l'alcool ajouté et un style céréalier ; le futsū-shu n'est pas premium.","Ginjō and daiginjō without junmai have added alcohol. Honjōzō has added alcohol and a cereal style; futsū-shu is not premium."]},{"id":"k18213cba","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quale combinazione di fattori dà lo stile di junmai e honjōzō?","Quelle combinaison de facteurs donne le style du junmai et du honjōzō ?","Which combination of factors gives the junmai and honjōzō style?"],"o":[["Riso poco levigato e fermentazione più calda","Riz peu poli et fermentation plus chaude","Lightly polished rice and warmer fermentation"],["Riso molto levigato e fermentazione fresca","Riz très poli et fermentation fraîche","Highly polished rice and cool fermentation"],["Invecchiamento lungo e filtrazione grossolana","Long vieillissement et filtration grossière","Long ageing and rough filtration"],["Niente pastorizzazione e anidride carbonica","Pas de pasteurisation et dioxyde de carbone","No pasteurisation and carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Poca levigatura e temperatura più alta danno cereali, latticini, acidità e umami.","Peu de polissage et une température plus élevée donnent céréales, notes lactées, acidité et umami.","Light polishing and warmer temperature give cereal, lactic notes, acidity and umami."],"d":["Riso molto levigato e fermentazione fresca sono la ricetta ginjō. Le altre opzioni descrivono stili speciali (koshu, nigori, nama, sparkling).","Riz très poli et fermentation fraîche sont la recette ginjō. Les autres options décrivent des styles spéciaux (koshu, nigori, nama, pétillant).","Highly polished rice and cool fermentation are the ginjō recipe. The other options describe speciality styles (koshu, nigori, nama, sparkling)."]},{"id":"k12cae20e","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quale passaggio di produzione è controllato dalla legge per il junmai?","Quelle étape d'élaboration est contrôlée par la loi pour le junmai ?","Which production step is legally controlled for junmai?"],"o":[["Nessuna aggiunta di alcol distillato","Aucun ajout d'alcool distillé","No addition of distilled alcohol"],["Nessuna pastorizzazione","Aucune pasteurisation","No pasteurisation"],["Un invecchiamento obbligatorio","Un vieillissement obligatoire","Compulsory ageing"],["Una filtrazione grossolana","Une filtration grossière","Rough filtration"]],"e":["Per legge il junmai non può ricevere alcol distillato ad alta gradazione.","Selon la loi, le junmai ne peut pas recevoir d'alcool distillé à haut degré.","By law, junmai may not have high-strength distilled alcohol added."],"d":["Niente pastorizzazione definisce il nama, l'invecchiamento il koshu, la filtrazione grossolana il nigori.","L'absence de pasteurisation définit le nama, le vieillissement le koshu, la filtration grossière le nigori.","No pasteurisation defines nama, ageing defines koshu, and rough filtration defines nigori."]},{"id":"k1f8662ae","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quale passaggio di produzione definisce il koshu?","Quelle étape d'élaboration définit le koshu ?","Which production step defines koshu?"],"o":[["L'invecchiamento","Le vieillissement","Maturation (ageing)"],["L'assenza di pastorizzazione","L'absence de pasteurisation","No pasteurisation"],["L'aggiunta di anidride carbonica","L'ajout de dioxyde de carbone","Adding carbon dioxide"],["Una levigatura al 50%","Un polissage à 50 %","Polishing to 50%"]],"e":["Il koshu è il sake invecchiato: il passaggio che lo definisce è la maturazione.","Le koshu est le saké vieilli : l'étape qui le définit est la maturation.","Koshu is aged sake: maturation is the step that defines it."],"d":["Niente pastorizzazione = nama; anidride carbonica = sparkling; levigatura al 50% = daiginjō.","Pas de pasteurisation = nama ; dioxyde de carbone = pétillant ; polissage à 50 % = daiginjō.","No pasteurisation = nama; carbon dioxide = sparkling; 50% polishing = daiginjō."]},{"id":"k1da4a6b6","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Qual è il grado di levigatura massimo per un honjōzō?","Quel est le taux de polissage maximal pour un honjōzō ?","What is the maximum polishing ratio for honjōzō?"],"o":[["70%","70 %","70%"],["50%","50 %","50%"],["60%","60 %","60%"],["100%","100 %","100%"]],"e":["Per l'honjōzō deve restare il 70% del chicco o meno.","Pour le honjōzō, il doit rester 70 % du grain ou moins.","For honjōzō, 70% or less of the grain must remain."],"d":["50% e 60% sono le soglie di daiginjō e ginjō. Il 100% è ammesso solo per il junmai, e anche lì è raro.","50 % et 60 % sont les seuils des daiginjō et ginjō. 100 % n'est admis que pour le junmai, et c'est rare.","50% and 60% are the daiginjō and ginjō limits. 100% is allowed only for junmai, and even there it is rare."]},{"id":"k12c8809a","c":"k06","p":0,"q":["Quale tra questi sake è del tutto privo di alcol distillato aggiunto?","Lequel de ces sakés est totalement sans alcool distillé ajouté ?","Which of these sakes has no added distilled alcohol at all?"],"o":[["Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō","Junmai daiginjō"],["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"]],"e":["La parola junmai garantisce che non c'è alcol distillato aggiunto.","Le mot junmai garantit l'absence d'alcool distillé ajouté.","The word junmai guarantees no added distilled alcohol."],"d":["Daiginjō, ginjō e honjōzō senza la parola junmai indicano sake con alcol aggiunto prima della filtrazione.","Daiginjō, ginjō et honjōzō sans le mot junmai désignent des sakés avec alcool ajouté avant filtration.","Daiginjō, ginjō and honjōzō without the word junmai are sakes with alcohol added before filtration."]},{"id":"k19e8178d","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Quanti kanji bisogna imparare per riconoscere i quattro termini chiave dell'etichetta?","Combien de kanji faut-il apprendre pour reconnaître les quatre termes clés de l'étiquette ?","How many kanji must you learn to recognise the four key label terms?"],"o":[["Sette","Sept","Seven"],["Nove","Neuf","Nine"],["Quattro","Quatre","Four"],["Dodici","Douze","Twelve"]],"e":["Sono sette, perché gin 吟 e jō 醸 compaiono in più termini.","Il y en a sept, car gin 吟 et jō 醸 apparaissent dans plusieurs termes.","There are seven, because gin 吟 and jō 醸 appear in more than one term."],"d":["Contando i suoni di tutti i termini senza ripetizioni si arriva a nove; togliendo i doppioni di gin e jō restano sette simboli diversi.","En comptant tous les sons avec les répétitions, on arrive à neuf ; sans les doublons de gin et jō, il reste sept symboles différents.","Counting every sound including repeats gives nine; removing the duplicate gin and jō leaves seven different symbols."]},{"id":"k196ded2b","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Quale termine si scrive 純米?","Quel terme s'écrit 純米 ?","Which term is written 純米?"],"o":[["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"]],"e":["純 (jun) + 米 (mai) = junmai, «riso puro».","純 (jun) + 米 (mai) = junmai, « riz pur ».","純 (jun) + 米 (mai) = junmai, 'pure rice'."],"d":["Ginjō è 吟醸, honjōzō è 本醸造, daiginjō è 大吟醸.","Ginjō s'écrit 吟醸, honjōzō 本醸造, daiginjō 大吟醸.","Ginjō is 吟醸, honjōzō is 本醸造, daiginjō is 大吟醸."]},{"id":"k1bd45fe4","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta compare 大吟醸. Di quale grado si tratta?","Une étiquette porte 大吟醸. De quel grade s'agit-il ?","A label shows 大吟醸. Which grade is it?"],"o":[["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"]],"e":["大 (dai) + 吟 (gin) + 醸 (jō) = daiginjō.","大 (dai) + 吟 (gin) + 醸 (jō) = daiginjō.","大 (dai) + 吟 (gin) + 醸 (jō) = daiginjō."],"d":["Il ginjō sarebbe solo 吟醸, senza 大. Junmai è 純米 e honjōzō 本醸造.","Le ginjō serait seulement 吟醸, sans 大. Junmai s'écrit 純米 et honjōzō 本醸造.","Ginjō would be just 吟醸, without 大. Junmai is 純米 and honjōzō 本醸造."]},{"id":"k15c5f712","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Quale kanji compare sia in ginjō sia in honjōzō?","Quel kanji apparaît à la fois dans ginjō et dans honjōzō ?","Which kanji appears in both ginjō and honjōzō?"],"o":[["醸 (jō)","醸 (jō)","醸 (jō)"],["吟 (gin)","吟 (gin)","吟 (gin)"],["米 (mai)","米 (mai)","米 (mai)"],["大 (dai)","大 (dai)","大 (dai)"]],"e":["Il suono jō, 醸, sta in ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) e daiginjō (大吟醸).","Le son jō, 醸, se trouve dans ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) et daiginjō (大吟醸).","The sound jō, 醸, is in ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) and daiginjō (大吟醸)."],"d":["吟 (gin) è in ginjō e daiginjō ma non in honjōzō. 米 è solo in junmai, 大 solo in daiginjō.","吟 (gin) est dans ginjō et daiginjō mais pas dans honjōzō. 米 n'est que dans junmai, 大 que dans daiginjō.","吟 (gin) is in ginjō and daiginjō but not honjōzō. 米 is only in junmai and 大 only in daiginjō."]},{"id":"k1cec5fb8","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Un'etichetta mostra 純米吟醸. Che cosa indica?","Une étiquette affiche 純米吟醸. Qu'indique-t-elle ?","A label shows 純米吟醸. What does it indicate?"],"o":[["Junmai ginjō: stile fruttato, senza alcol aggiunto","Junmai ginjō : style fruité, sans alcool ajouté","Junmai ginjō: fruity style, no added alcohol"],["Honjōzō: stile cerealicolo, con alcol aggiunto","Honjōzō : style céréalier, avec alcool ajouté","Honjōzō: cereal style, with added alcohol"],["Daiginjō: con alcol aggiunto, riso al 50%","Daiginjō : avec alcool ajouté, riz à 50 %","Daiginjō: with added alcohol, rice at 50%"],["Futsū-shu: sake di base","Futsū-shu : saké de base","Futsū-shu: basic sake"]],"e":["純米 (junmai) + 吟醸 (ginjō): fruttato e floreale, senza alcol distillato aggiunto.","純米 (junmai) + 吟醸 (ginjō) : fruité et floral, sans alcool distillé ajouté.","純米 (junmai) + 吟醸 (ginjō): fruity and floral, with no added distilled alcohol."],"d":["Non c'è 本醸造 (honjōzō) né 大 (dai). Il futsū-shu non porta questi termini premium.","Il n'y a ni 本醸造 (honjōzō) ni 大 (dai). Le futsū-shu ne porte pas ces termes premium.","There is no 本醸造 (honjōzō) and no 大 (dai). Futsū-shu does not carry these premium terms."]},{"id":"k1d9cf708","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa 純米?","Que signifie 純米 ?","What does 純米 mean?"],"o":[["Junmai (riso puro)","Junmai (riz pur)","Junmai (pure rice)"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Nama","Nama","Nama"],["Koshu","Koshu","Koshu"]],"e":["純米 si legge junmai e significa «riso puro».","純米 se lit junmai et signifie « riz pur ».","純米 reads junmai and means 'pure rice'."],"d":["Ginjō si scrive 吟醸. Nama e koshu non fanno parte dei quattro termini kanji da conoscere a questo livello.","Ginjō s'écrit 吟醸. Nama et koshu ne font pas partie des quatre termes en kanji à connaître à ce niveau.","Ginjō is written 吟醸. Nama and koshu are not among the four kanji terms at this level."]},{"id":"k10c2739e","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta compare 本醸造. Che cosa sai di questo sake?","Une étiquette porte 本醸造. Que sait-on de ce saké ?","A label shows 本醸造. What do you know about this sake?"],"o":[["È un honjōzō: alcol aggiunto, riso ≤70%, stile cerealicolo","C'est un honjōzō : alcool ajouté, riz ≤70 %, style céréalier","It is honjōzō: added alcohol, rice ≤70%, cereal style"],["È un junmai: senza alcol aggiunto","C'est un junmai : sans alcool ajouté","It is junmai: no added alcohol"],["È un daiginjō: riso ≤50%","C'est un daiginjō : riz ≤50 %","It is daiginjō: rice ≤50%"],["È un sake non pastorizzato","C'est un saké non pasteurisé","It is an unpasteurised sake"]],"e":["本醸造 = honjōzō: alcol aggiunto, levigatura al 70% o meno, note di cereali e latticini.","本醸造 = honjōzō : alcool ajouté, polissage à 70 % ou moins, notes céréalières et lactées.","本醸造 = honjōzō: added alcohol, polished to 70% or less, cereal and lactic notes."],"d":["Junmai si scrive 純米, daiginjō 大吟醸. Il termine per il sake non pastorizzato è nama.","Junmai s'écrit 純米, daiginjō 大吟醸. Le saké non pasteurisé se dit nama.","Junmai is 純米 and daiginjō 大吟醸. Unpasteurised sake is called nama."]},{"id":"k1ca4d4a6","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["In quale termine compare il kanji 米 (mai)?","Dans quel terme apparaît le kanji 米 (mai) ?","In which term does the kanji 米 (mai) appear?"],"o":[["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"]],"e":["米 è il «mai» di junmai (純米).","米 est le « mai » de junmai (純米).","米 is the 'mai' in junmai (純米)."],"d":["Ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) e daiginjō (大吟醸) non contengono 米.","Ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) et daiginjō (大吟醸) ne contiennent pas 米.","Ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) and daiginjō (大吟醸) do not contain 米."]},{"id":"k12e536af","c":"k07","p":0,"q":["Perché è utile riconoscere i kanji dei quattro termini chiave?","Pourquoi est-il utile de reconnaître les kanji des quatre termes clés ?","Why is it useful to recognise the kanji of the four key terms?"],"o":[["Le etichette sono quasi tutte in giapponese, con poche parole in alfabeto latino","Les étiquettes sont presque toutes en japonais, avec peu de mots en alphabet latin","Labels are mostly in Japanese, with few words in the Latin alphabet"],["I kanji indicano il prezzo del sake","Les kanji indiquent le prix du saké","The kanji show the sake's price"],["I kanji indicano l'anno di produzione","Les kanji indiquent l'année de production","The kanji show the production year"],["La legge vieta l'alfabeto latino","La loi interdit l'alphabet latin","The law bans the Latin alphabet"]],"e":["Riconoscere pochi kanji permette di capire il grado anche su un'etichetta tutta in giapponese.","Reconnaître quelques kanji permet de comprendre le grade même sur une étiquette entièrement en japonais.","Recognising a few kanji lets you read the grade even on an all-Japanese label."],"d":["Questi kanji indicano il grado, non il prezzo né l'anno; l'alfabeto latino non è vietato, è solo poco usato.","Ces kanji indiquent le grade, pas le prix ni l'année ; l'alphabet latin n'est pas interdit, juste peu utilisé.","These kanji show the grade, not price or year; the Latin alphabet is not banned, just little used."]},{"id":"k117ea205","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Che cosa indica il termine nama?","Qu'indique le terme nama ?","What does the term nama indicate?"],"o":[["Un sake non pastorizzato","Un saké non pasteurisé","An unpasteurised sake"],["Un sake torbido","Un saké trouble","A cloudy sake"],["Un sake invecchiato","Un saké vieilli","An aged sake"],["Un sake senza alcol aggiunto","Un saké sans alcool ajouté","A sake with no added alcohol"]],"e":["Nama significa che il sake ha saltato la pastorizzazione.","Nama signifie que le saké n'a pas été pasteurisé.","Nama means the sake has skipped pasteurisation."],"d":["Torbido è nigori, invecchiato è koshu, senza alcol aggiunto è junmai.","Trouble, c'est nigori ; vieilli, koshu ; sans alcool ajouté, junmai.","Cloudy is nigori, aged is koshu, no added alcohol is junmai."]},{"id":"k16da0590","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Come va conservato un nama-zake?","Comment conserver un nama-zake ?","How should a nama-zake be stored?"],"o":[["Sempre in frigorifero, da bere poco dopo l'uscita","Toujours au réfrigérateur, à boire peu après sa sortie","Always refrigerated, drunk soon after release"],["A temperatura ambiente per qualche anno","À température ambiante pendant quelques années","At room temperature for a few years"],["Coricato, alla luce del sole","Couché, à la lumière du soleil","Lying down, in sunlight"],["In una botte di rovere","Dans un fût de chêne","In an oak cask"]],"e":["Senza pastorizzazione il nama è meno stabile: freddo costante e consumo rapido.","Sans pasteurisation, le nama est moins stable : froid constant et consommation rapide.","Without pasteurisation nama is less stable: constant cold and quick drinking."],"d":["Il caldo e il tempo lo rovinano, e la luce forte danneggia ogni sake. Le bottiglie di sake si conservano in piedi, e il rovere non c'entra.","La chaleur et le temps l'abîment, et la lumière forte nuit à tout saké. Les bouteilles de saké se gardent debout, et le chêne n'a rien à voir.","Heat and time spoil it, and strong light harms any sake. Sake bottles are stored upright, and oak has nothing to do with it."]},{"id":"k11e22f92","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi può sviluppare in fretta un nama?","Quels arômes un nama peut-il développer rapidement ?","What aromas can a nama quickly develop?"],"o":[["Speziati e maltati","Épicés et maltés","Spicy and malty"],["Fiori bianchi e pera","Fleurs blanches et poire","White flowers and pear"],["Agrumi e menta","Agrumes et menthe","Citrus and mint"],["Vaniglia e cocco","Vanille et noix de coco","Vanilla and coconut"]],"e":["Appena uscito è fresco e vivace, ma può diventare presto speziato e maltato.","À sa sortie il est frais et vif, mais il peut vite devenir épicé et malté.","On release it is fresh and lively, but it can soon turn spicy and malty."],"d":["Fiori e pera sono note ginjō, non legate al nama. Vaniglia e cocco vengono dal rovere, che nel sake si usa pochissimo.","Fleurs et poire sont des notes ginjō, pas liées au nama. Vanille et coco viennent du chêne, très peu utilisé pour le saké.","Flowers and pear are ginjō notes, not linked to nama. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, which is hardly used for sake."]},{"id":"k16bc4708","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Perché un nigori è torbido?","Pourquoi un nigori est-il trouble ?","Why is a nigori cloudy?"],"o":[["È filtrato in modo grossolano e contiene particelle di riso","Il est filtré grossièrement et contient des particules de riz","It is roughly filtered and contains rice particles"],["Non è mai stato filtrato","Il n'a jamais été filtré","It has never been filtered"],["Gli si aggiunge latte","On y ajoute du lait","Milk is added to it"],["È invecchiato in terracotta","Il est vieilli en terre cuite","It is aged in terracotta"]],"e":["La filtrazione grossolana lascia nel sake particelle di riso in sospensione.","La filtration grossière laisse des particules de riz en suspension dans le saké.","Rough filtration leaves suspended rice particles in the sake."],"d":["La filtrazione è obbligatoria per legge: il nigori è filtrato, ma poco. Il latte non si usa, e la terracotta riguarda alcuni koshu.","La filtration est obligatoire : le nigori est filtré, mais peu. On n'utilise pas de lait, et la terre cuite concerne certains koshu.","Filtration is legally required: nigori is filtered, just lightly. No milk is used, and terracotta relates to some koshu."]},{"id":"k1976da6d","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sul nigori è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur le nigori est correcte ?","Which statement about nigori is correct?"],"o":[["Può essere appena velato oppure denso con pezzetti di riso","Il peut être à peine voilé ou épais avec des fragments de riz","It can be lightly cloudy or thick with rice fragments"],["È sempre limpido dopo qualche giorno","Il devient toujours limpide après quelques jours","It always turns clear after a few days"],["È sempre frizzante","Il est toujours pétillant","It is always sparkling"],["È sempre un futsū-shu","C'est toujours un futsū-shu","It is always a futsū-shu"]],"e":["Lo stile varia con la quantità di solidi lasciati: da leggermente torbido a molto denso.","Le style varie selon la quantité de solides conservée : de légèrement trouble à très épais.","The style varies with how much solid matter is kept: from slightly cloudy to very thick."],"d":["Un nigori può essere frizzante, ma non per forza. Gli stili speciali si combinano con qualunque grado, quindi non solo con il futsū-shu.","Un nigori peut être pétillant, mais pas forcément. Les styles spéciaux se combinent avec tous les grades, pas seulement le futsū-shu.","A nigori can be sparkling, but need not be. Speciality styles combine with any grade, not just futsū-shu."]},{"id":"k15409c46","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Da dove vengono le bollicine del sake frizzante?","D'où viennent les bulles du saké pétillant ?","Where do the bubbles in sparkling sake come from?"],"o":[["Da anidride carbonica disciolta nel liquido","Du dioxyde de carbone dissous dans le liquide","Carbon dioxide dissolved in the liquid"],["Dall'ossigeno dell'aria","De l'oxygène de l'air","Oxygen from the air"],["Dall'alcol distillato aggiunto","De l'alcool distillé ajouté","The added distilled alcohol"],["Dalle particelle di riso","Des particules de riz","The rice particles"]],"e":["Come in ogni bevanda frizzante, sono anidride carbonica disciolta.","Comme dans toute boisson pétillante, il s'agit de dioxyde de carbone dissous.","As in any sparkling drink, they are dissolved carbon dioxide."],"d":["L'ossigeno rovina il sake invece di dargli bollicine. Le particelle di riso rendono torbido (nigori), non frizzante.","L'oxygène abîme le saké au lieu de lui donner des bulles. Les particules de riz rendent trouble (nigori), pas pétillant.","Oxygen spoils sake rather than making it fizzy. Rice particles make it cloudy (nigori), not sparkling."]},{"id":"k1b181e56","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione del sake frizzante è corretta?","Quelle description du saké pétillant est correcte ?","Which description of sparkling sake is correct?"],"o":[["Va da leggero e poco alcolico a ricco e complesso, e può essere nigori","Il va de léger et peu alcoolisé à riche et complexe, et peut être nigori","It ranges from light and low-alcohol to rich and complex, and can be nigori"],["È sempre al 20% di alcol","Il titre toujours 20 %","It is always 20% abv"],["Si fa con un'unica tecnica","Il est fait avec une seule technique","It is made with a single technique"],["Non può mai essere torbido","Il ne peut jamais être trouble","It can never be cloudy"]],"e":["Gli stili sono vari: alcuni leggeri e poco alcolici, altri più ricchi, anche torbidi.","Les styles sont variés : certains légers et peu alcoolisés, d'autres plus riches, voire troubles.","Styles vary: some light and low in alcohol, others richer, even cloudy."],"d":["Esistono diverse tecniche per sciogliere l'anidride carbonica. Molti sake frizzanti sono più leggeri, non al 20%, e alcuni sono anche nigori.","Il existe plusieurs techniques pour dissoudre le dioxyde de carbone. Beaucoup de sakés pétillants sont plus légers, pas à 20 %, et certains sont aussi nigori.","Several techniques exist for dissolving carbon dioxide. Many sparkling sakes are lighter, not 20%, and some are also nigori."]},{"id":"k124e4cbd","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un koshu?","Qu'est-ce qu'un koshu ?","What is a koshu?"],"o":[["Un sake invecchiato","Un saké vieilli","An aged sake"],["Un sake frizzante","Un saké pétillant","A sparkling sake"],["Un sake non pastorizzato","Un saké non pasteurisé","An unpasteurised sake"],["Un sake di base","Un saké de base","A basic sake"]],"e":["Koshu è il nome dei sake invecchiati.","Koshu est le nom des sakés vieillis.","Koshu is the name for aged sakes."],"d":["Frizzante, non pastorizzato (nama) e di base (futsū-shu) sono altre categorie.","Pétillant, non pasteurisé (nama) et de base (futsū-shu) sont d'autres catégories.","Sparkling, unpasteurised (nama) and basic (futsū-shu) are other categories."]},{"id":"k119e4f86","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Quale recipiente si usa MOLTO RARAMENTE per invecchiare il sake?","Quel contenant est TRÈS RAREMENT utilisé pour vieillir le saké ?","Which vessel is VERY RARELY used to age sake?"],"o":[["La botte di rovere","Le fût de chêne","The oak cask"],["La vasca di stoccaggio","La cuve de stockage","The storage tank"],["La bottiglia di vetro","La bouteille en verre","The glass bottle"],["La terracotta","La terre cuite","Terracotta"]],"e":["Il legno si può usare, ma il rovere è molto raro nel sake.","Le bois peut être utilisé, mais le chêne est très rare pour le saké.","Wood can be used, but oak is very rare for sake."],"d":["Vasche, vetro e terracotta sono tutti recipienti usati per invecchiare il koshu.","Cuves, verre et terre cuite sont tous des contenants utilisés pour le koshu.","Tanks, glass and terracotta are all used for ageing koshu."]},{"id":"k15d10bf4","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Come si presenta di solito un koshu?","À quoi ressemble généralement un koshu ?","What is a typical koshu like?"],"o":[["Ambrato o marrone, ricco, dolce, con note di frutta secca e noci","Ambré ou brun, riche, sucré, avec des notes de fruits secs et de noix","Amber or brown, rich, sweet, with dried fruit and nut notes"],["Incolore, leggerissimo, con note di mela verde","Incolore, très léger, avec des notes de pomme verte","Colourless, very light, with green apple notes"],["Torbido, con pezzetti di riso","Trouble, avec des fragments de riz","Cloudy, with rice fragments"],["Frizzante e poco alcolico","Pétillant et peu alcoolisé","Sparkling and low in alcohol"]],"e":["La maggior parte dei koshu è ambrata o marrone, ricca, dolce e molto aromatica.","La plupart des koshu sont ambrés ou bruns, riches, sucrés et très aromatiques.","Most koshu is amber or brown, rich, sweet and highly aromatic."],"d":["Esistono koshu più chiari e delicati, ma non sono la norma. Torbido indica nigori, frizzante indica sparkling.","Il existe des koshu plus pâles et délicats, mais ce n'est pas la norme. Trouble évoque le nigori, pétillant le saké pétillant.","Paler, more delicate koshu exist, but they are not the norm. Cloudy suggests nigori and fizzy suggests sparkling sake."]},{"id":"k1a4093f5","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Perché i koshu sono così diversi tra loro?","Pourquoi les koshu sont-ils si différents les uns des autres ?","Why do koshu vary so much?"],"o":[["Si invecchiano in recipienti diversi e a temperature diverse, anche sotto zero","On les vieillit dans des contenants et à des températures variés, parfois sous zéro","They are aged in different vessels and at different temperatures, even below freezing"],["Si fanno con uva di varietà diverse","On les fait avec différents cépages","They are made from different grape varieties"],["Si distillano più volte","On les distille plusieurs fois","They are distilled several times"],["Contengono quantità diverse di luppolo","Ils contiennent des quantités différentes de houblon","They contain different amounts of hops"]],"e":["Recipienti (vasche, terracotta, vetro, legno) e temperature (ambiente o basse) creano molti stili.","Contenants (cuves, terre cuite, verre, bois) et températures (ambiante ou basses) créent de nombreux styles.","Vessels (tanks, terracotta, glass, wood) and temperatures (room or low) create many styles."],"d":["Il sake si fa con riso, non con uva o luppolo, e non si distilla.","Le saké se fait avec du riz, pas avec du raisin ni du houblon, et il n'est pas distillé.","Sake is made from rice, not grapes or hops, and is not distilled."]},{"id":"k190e8bd9","c":"k08","p":0,"q":["Un junmai ginjō può essere anche nama e nigori?","Un junmai ginjō peut-il aussi être nama et nigori ?","Can a junmai ginjō also be nama and nigori?"],"o":[["Sì: gli stili speciali si combinano con qualunque grado","Oui : les styles spéciaux se combinent avec tous les grades","Yes: speciality styles combine with any grade"],["No: gli stili speciali valgono solo per il futsū-shu","Non : les styles spéciaux ne valent que pour le futsū-shu","No: speciality styles apply only to futsū-shu"],["No: un sake può avere un solo stile speciale","Non : un saké ne peut avoir qu'un seul style spécial","No: a sake can have only one speciality style"],["Solo se è anche invecchiato","Seulement s'il est aussi vieilli","Only if it is also aged"]],"e":["Un sake premium può essere nama, nigori, frizzante o koshu, anche combinando più stili.","Un saké premium peut être nama, nigori, pétillant ou koshu, en combinant même plusieurs styles.","A premium sake can be nama, nigori, sparkling or koshu, even combining several."],"d":["Gli stili speciali non sono riservati al futsū-shu e non si escludono a vicenda; l'invecchiamento non è una condizione.","Les styles spéciaux ne sont pas réservés au futsū-shu et ne s'excluent pas ; le vieillissement n'est pas une condition.","Speciality styles are not reserved for futsū-shu and do not exclude each other; ageing is not a condition."]},{"id":"k19a65b8a","c":"k09","p":0,"q":["Quale bicchiere è più adatto per degustare il sake?","Quel verre convient le mieux pour déguster le saké ?","Which glass is best for tasting sake?"],"o":[["Coppa ampia che si stringe verso l'alto","Calice large qui se resserre vers le haut","A wide bowl that narrows towards the top"],["Bicchiere dritto e stretto, tipo flûte","Verre droit et étroit, type flûte","A straight, narrow flute"],["Coppa larga e bassa, aperta in alto","Coupe large et basse, ouverte en haut","A wide, shallow, open coupe"],["Una scatola di legno di cedro","Une boîte en bois de cèdre","A cedar wood box"]],"e":["La forma che si stringe in alto concentra gli aromi.","La forme qui se resserre en haut concentre les arômes.","A shape that narrows at the top concentrates the aromas."],"d":["Una coppa aperta disperde gli aromi. Il masu di cedro dà sapore di legno e non è adatto alla degustazione.","Une coupe ouverte disperse les arômes. Le masu en cèdre donne un goût de bois et ne convient pas à la dégustation.","An open coupe lets aromas escape. A cedar masu adds wood flavour and is unsuitable for tasting."]},{"id":"k1265f964","c":"k09","p":0,"q":["Perché serve una superficie bianca durante la degustazione?","Pourquoi faut-il une surface blanche pendant la dégustation ?","Why is a white surface needed when tasting?"],"o":[["Per valutare l'aspetto del sake","Pour évaluer l'aspect du saké","To assess the sake's appearance"],["Per raffreddare il bicchiere","Pour refroidir le verre","To cool the glass"],["Per assorbire gli odori","Pour absorber les odeurs","To absorb smells"],["Per scaldare il sake","Pour réchauffer le saké","To warm the sake"]],"e":["Sul bianco si vedono meglio limpidezza, colore e bollicine.","Sur fond blanc, on voit mieux la limpidité, la couleur et les bulles.","Clarity, colour and bubbles show up best against white."],"d":["La superficie non cambia temperatura né odori: serve solo a guardare.","La surface ne change ni la température ni les odeurs : elle sert seulement à regarder.","The surface changes neither temperature nor smells: it is only for looking."]},{"id":"k1cf978db","c":"k09","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si valuta nella fase «aspetto» della degustazione?","Qu'évalue-t-on dans la partie « aspect » de la dégustation ?","What is assessed under 'appearance' when tasting?"],"o":[["Limpidezza (limpido–torbido), bollicine, colore","Limpidité (limpide–trouble), bulles, couleur","Clarity (clear–cloudy), bubbles, colour"],["Dolcezza e acidità","Douceur et acidité","Sweetness and acidity"],["Umami e persistenza","Umami et longueur","Umami and finish"],["Famiglie di aromi","Familles d'arômes","Aroma families"]],"e":["L'aspetto riguarda ciò che si vede: limpidezza, bollicine e colore.","L'aspect concerne ce que l'on voit : limpidité, bulles et couleur.","Appearance covers what you see: clarity, bubbles and colour."],"d":["Dolcezza, acidità, umami e persistenza si valutano in bocca; le famiglie di aromi al naso (e in bocca).","Douceur, acidité, umami et longueur s'évaluent en bouche ; les familles d'arômes au nez (et en bouche).","Sweetness, acidity, umami and finish are judged on the palate; aroma families on the nose (and palate)."]},{"id":"k18a86b64","c":"k09","p":0,"q":["Quale di queste famiglie di aromi NON fa parte della griglia per il sake?","Laquelle de ces familles d'arômes NE fait PAS partie de la grille du saké ?","Which of these aroma families is NOT part of the sake tasting grid?"],"o":[["Rovere e vaniglia","Chêne et vanille","Oak and vanilla"],["Fruttato/floreale","Fruité/floral","Fruity/floral"],["Cereali/chicco/frutta a guscio","Céréales/grain/fruits à coque","Cereal/grain/nut"],["Latticini","Lacté","Lactic/dairy"]],"e":["La griglia usa fruttato/floreale, cereali/frutta a guscio, latticini e «altro»; il rovere non è tra le famiglie.","La grille utilise fruité/floral, céréales/fruits à coque, lacté et « autre » ; le chêne n'en fait pas partie.","The grid uses fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy and 'other'; oak is not one of the families."],"d":["Il rovere si usa pochissimo nel sake, quindi non ha una famiglia propria; le altre tre opzioni sono famiglie della griglia.","Le chêne est très peu utilisé pour le saké : il n'a donc pas de famille propre ; les trois autres options sont des familles de la grille.","Oak is hardly used for sake, so it has no family of its own; the other three options are grid families."]},{"id":"k14290c30","c":"k09","p":0,"q":["Prima di una degustazione, che cosa conviene evitare subito prima?","Avant une dégustation, qu'est-il préférable d'éviter juste avant ?","Before a tasting, what should you avoid just beforehand?"],"o":[["Lavarsi i denti o bere caffè","Se brosser les dents ou boire un café","Brushing your teeth or drinking coffee"],["Bere un bicchiere d'acqua","Boire un verre d'eau","Drinking a glass of water"],["Accendere una luce","Allumer une lumière","Switching on a light"],["Sedersi a un tavolo bianco","S'asseoir à une table blanche","Sitting at a white table"]],"e":["Dentifricio e caffè lasciano sapori in bocca che falsano l'assaggio.","Le dentifrice et le café laissent des goûts qui faussent la dégustation.","Toothpaste and coffee leave lingering flavours that distort tasting."],"d":["L'acqua non lascia sapori, la luce aiuta a vedere e il tavolo bianco è proprio consigliato.","L'eau ne laisse pas de goût, la lumière aide à voir et la table blanche est justement conseillée.","Water leaves no taste, light helps you see, and a white table is actually recommended."]},{"id":"k1f9089c4","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le quattro regole per conservare il sake?","Quelles sont les quatre règles pour conserver le saké ?","What are the four rules for storing sake?"],"o":[["Al fresco, bere giovane, bottiglia in piedi, lontano dalla luce forte","Au frais, boire jeune, bouteille debout, loin de la lumière forte","Keep cool, drink young, store upright, avoid bright light"],["Al caldo, invecchiare, bottiglia coricata, alla luce","Au chaud, vieillir, bouteille couchée, à la lumière","Keep warm, age it, lie it down, keep in light"],["Al fresco, invecchiare, bottiglia coricata, al buio","Au frais, vieillir, bouteille couchée, dans le noir","Keep cool, age it, lie it down, keep dark"],["Temperatura ambiente, bere giovane, bottiglia coricata, alla luce","Température ambiante, boire jeune, bouteille couchée, à la lumière","Room temperature, drink young, lie it down, keep in light"]],"e":["Fresco, giovane, in piedi, al riparo dalla luce forte.","Frais, jeune, debout, à l'abri de la lumière forte.","Cool, young, upright, away from bright light."],"d":["Il sake non si conserva coricato e, salvo il koshu, non è fatto per invecchiare; caldo e luce forte lo rovinano.","Le saké ne se garde pas couché et, sauf le koshu, il n'est pas fait pour vieillir ; chaleur et lumière forte l'abîment.","Sake is not stored lying down and, apart from koshu, is not made for ageing; heat and bright light spoil it."]},{"id":"k14f3eb37","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Entro quanto tempo si dovrebbe bere la maggior parte dei sake dopo la messa in vendita?","Dans quel délai faut-il boire la plupart des sakés après leur mise en vente ?","Within what time should most sake be drunk after going on sale?"],"o":[["Circa un anno","Environ un an","About a year"],["Circa una settimana","Environ une semaine","About a week"],["Circa cinque anni","Environ cinq ans","About five years"],["Non ci sono limiti","Il n'y a pas de limite","There is no limit"]],"e":["Quasi tutti i sake vanno bevuti entro circa un anno, poi perdono freschezza.","Presque tous les sakés se boivent dans l'année environ, puis perdent leur fraîcheur.","Most sake should be drunk within about a year, after which it loses freshness."],"d":["Una settimana è il tempo di un ginjō già aperto. I nama durano solo pochi mesi; solo il koshu è pensato per invecchiare.","Une semaine, c'est la durée d'un ginjō déjà ouvert. Les nama ne tiennent que quelques mois ; seul le koshu est fait pour vieillir.","A week is how long an opened ginjō lasts. Nama lasts only a few months; only koshu is meant for ageing."]},{"id":"k10566797","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Quanto resta fresco di solito un ginjō dopo l'apertura, in frigorifero?","Combien de temps un ginjō reste-t-il frais en général après ouverture, au réfrigérateur ?","How long does a ginjō usually stay fresh once opened, in the fridge?"],"o":[["Circa una settimana","Environ une semaine","About one week"],["Circa due mesi","Environ deux mois","About two months"],["Circa un anno","Environ un an","About a year"],["Circa un'ora","Environ une heure","About an hour"]],"e":["I ginjō, più delicati, restano freschi per circa una settimana; gli altri sake circa due.","Les ginjō, plus délicats, restent frais environ une semaine ; les autres sakés environ deux.","Delicate ginjō stays fresh for about a week; other sakes about two."],"d":["Due mesi o un anno sono tempi troppo lunghi per una bottiglia aperta. Un'ora è troppo poco: chiuso in frigo, il sake regge diversi giorni.","Deux mois ou un an, c'est trop long pour une bouteille ouverte. Une heure, c'est trop peu : rebouché au frais, le saké tient plusieurs jours.","Two months or a year is far too long for an opened bottle. An hour is too short: resealed in the fridge, sake keeps for days."]},{"id":"k19fb91eb","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Come si conservano le bottiglie di sake?","Comment conserve-t-on les bouteilles de saké ?","How should sake bottles be stored?"],"o":[["In piedi","Debout","Upright"],["Coricate","Couchées","Lying down"],["Capovolte","À l'envers","Upside down"],["Inclinate a 45°","Inclinées à 45°","Tilted at 45°"]],"e":["Le bottiglie di sake si conservano meglio in piedi.","Les bouteilles de saké se conservent mieux debout.","Sake bottles are best stored upright."],"d":["Coricare le bottiglie è un'abitudine del vino con tappo di sughero, non del sake.","Coucher les bouteilles est une habitude du vin bouché au liège, pas du saké.","Lying bottles down is a habit for cork-sealed wine, not sake."]},{"id":"k1376a2ce","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Una bottiglia di sake è rimasta aperta troppo a lungo: è più scura e sa di caramello e toffee. Quale difetto è?","Une bouteille de saké est restée ouverte trop longtemps : elle est plus foncée et sent le caramel et le caramel au beurre. Quel défaut est-ce ?","A sake bottle has been open too long: it is darker and smells of caramel and toffee. Which fault is this?"],"o":[["Ossidazione","Oxydation","Oxidation"],["Nama-hine","Nama-hine","Nama-hine"],["Luce","Goût de lumière","Light strike"],["Infezione batterica","Infection bactérienne","Bacterial infection"]],"e":["Aperta troppo a lungo + caramello, toffee e colore più scuro = ossidazione.","Ouverte trop longtemps + caramel et couleur plus foncée = oxydation.","Open too long + caramel, toffee and deeper colour = oxidation."],"d":["Il nama-hine riguarda i nama e sa di malto, carne e verdura marcia. Le altre due voci non sono i difetti del sake da conoscere a questo livello.","Le nama-hine concerne les nama et sent le malt, la viande et les légumes pourris. Les deux autres ne sont pas les défauts du saké à connaître à ce niveau.","Nama-hine affects nama and smells of malt, meat and rotting vegetables. The other two are not the sake faults covered at this level."]},{"id":"k1da5762d","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi indicano un sake «fuori condizione», cioè troppo vecchio?","Quels arômes indiquent un saké « hors d'état », c'est-à-dire trop vieux ?","Which aromas show a sake is 'out of condition', meaning too old?"],"o":[["Caramello, toffee, verdure in salamoia","Caramel, caramel au beurre, légumes saumurés","Caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables"],["Mela verde e fiori bianchi","Pomme verte et fleurs blanches","Green apple and white flowers"],["Riso cotto e yogurt","Riz cuit et yaourt","Steamed rice and yoghurt"],["Agrumi freschi","Agrumes frais","Fresh citrus"]],"e":["Una bottiglia troppo vecchia sa di caramello, toffee e salamoia, e si scurisce.","Une bouteille trop vieille sent le caramel, le caramel au beurre et la saumure, et fonce.","A bottle that is too old smells of caramel, toffee and pickles, and darkens."],"d":["Mela, fiori, riso, yogurt e agrumi sono aromi normali e graditi di un sake fresco.","Pomme, fleurs, riz, yaourt et agrumes sont des arômes normaux et appréciés d'un saké frais.","Apple, flowers, rice, yoghurt and citrus are normal, welcome aromas in fresh sake."]},{"id":"k1fca70c3","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è il nama-hine?","Qu'est-ce que le nama-hine ?","What is nama-hine?"],"o":[["Un difetto dei nama: aromi di malto, carne, verdura marcia","Un défaut des nama : arômes de malt, viande, légumes pourris","A fault in nama: malt, meat, rotting-vegetable aromas"],["Un tipo di sake frizzante","Un type de saké pétillant","A type of sparkling sake"],["La tazzina tradizionale","La coupe traditionnelle","The traditional cup"],["Una fase della preparazione del kōji","Une étape de la fabrication du kōji","A stage of kōji making"]],"e":["Il nama-hine è il difetto tipico dei sake non pastorizzati.","Le nama-hine est le défaut typique des sakés non pasteurisés.","Nama-hine is the typical fault of unpasteurised sake."],"d":["La tazzina è l'o-choko. Il nama-hine non è uno stile né una fase della produzione.","La coupe s'appelle o-choko. Le nama-hine n'est ni un style ni une étape d'élaboration.","The cup is the o-choko. Nama-hine is neither a style nor a production stage."]},{"id":"k170e24c9","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Perché gli aromi dell'ossidazione ricordano quelli del koshu?","Pourquoi les arômes d'oxydation rappellent-ils ceux du koshu ?","Why do oxidation aromas resemble those of koshu?"],"o":[["I processi che li creano sono gli stessi, ma nel koshu sono voluti","Les processus qui les créent sont les mêmes, mais dans le koshu ils sont voulus","The same processes create them, but in koshu they are wanted"],["Il koshu è sempre un sake difettoso","Le koshu est toujours un saké défectueux","Koshu is always a faulty sake"],["Il koshu si fa con riso ossidato","Le koshu se fait avec du riz oxydé","Koshu is made from oxidised rice"],["È una coincidenza senza spiegazione","C'est une coïncidence sans explication","It is an unexplained coincidence"]],"e":["Stessi processi, intenzione diversa: nel koshu quegli aromi fanno parte dello stile.","Mêmes processus, intention différente : dans le koshu, ces arômes font partie du style.","Same processes, different intention: in koshu those aromas are part of the style."],"d":["Il koshu è uno stile voluto, non un difetto, e si fa con lo stesso riso degli altri sake: è l'invecchiamento a creare quegli aromi.","Le koshu est un style recherché, pas un défaut, et il se fait avec le même riz que les autres sakés : c'est le vieillissement qui crée ces arômes.","Koshu is a deliberate style, not a fault, made from the same rice as other sakes: ageing creates those aromas."]},{"id":"k14347e1a","c":"k10","p":0,"q":["Quale sake ha più bisogno del frigorifero?","Quel saké a le plus besoin du réfrigérateur ?","Which sake most needs refrigeration?"],"o":[["Il nama-zake","Le nama-zake","Nama-zake"],["Il koshu","Le koshu","Koshu"],["Il futsū-shu pastorizzato","Le futsū-shu pasteurisé","Pasteurised futsū-shu"],["Tutti i sake allo stesso modo","Tous les sakés de la même façon","All sakes equally"]],"e":["Il nama non è pastorizzato ed è meno stabile: va tenuto sempre al freddo.","Le nama n'est pas pasteurisé et il est moins stable : il doit rester toujours au froid.","Nama is unpasteurised and less stable: it must be kept cold at all times."],"d":["Ogni sake sta meglio al fresco, ma per il nama il freddo è indispensabile; anche i ginjō ne beneficiano per proteggere gli aromi.","Tout saké préfère le frais, mais pour le nama le froid est indispensable ; les ginjō en profitent aussi pour protéger leurs arômes.","Every sake prefers cool storage, but for nama the cold is essential; ginjō also benefits to protect its aromas."]},{"id":"k16910c74","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Qual è la temperatura consigliata per servire gli stili ginjō?","Quelle est la température de service conseillée pour les styles ginjō ?","What is the recommended serving temperature for ginjō styles?"],"o":[["Fresco (6–13 °C)","Frais (6–13 °C)","Chilled (6–13 °C)"],["Caldo (40–50 °C)","Chaud (40–50 °C)","Warm (40–50 °C)"],["Molto caldo, oltre 60 °C","Très chaud, au-delà de 60 °C","Very hot, above 60 °C"],["Sotto zero","Sous zéro","Below freezing"]],"e":["I ginjō perdono aromi con il calore: si servono freschi.","Les ginjō perdent leurs arômes à la chaleur : on les sert frais.","Ginjō loses its aromas when heated: serve it chilled."],"d":["Il caldo spegnerebbe i profumi fruttati e floreali. Sotto zero il sake sarebbe troppo freddo per sentirne gli aromi.","La chaleur éteindrait les parfums fruités et floraux. Sous zéro, le saké serait trop froid pour qu'on en sente les arômes.","Heat would flatten the fruity, floral scents. Below freezing the sake would be too cold to smell."]},{"id":"k174c4a2a","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Quale fascia di temperatura corrisponde al sake servito caldo?","Quelle plage de température correspond au saké servi chaud ?","Which temperature range is warm/hot sake?"],"o":[["40–50 °C","40–50 °C","40–50 °C"],["15–18 °C","15–18 °C","15–18 °C"],["6–13 °C","6–13 °C","6–13 °C"],["70–80 °C","70–80 °C","70–80 °C"]],"e":["Il sake caldo si serve tra 40 e 50 °C.","Le saké chaud se sert entre 40 et 50 °C.","Warm/hot sake is served at 40–50 °C."],"d":["15–18 °C è la temperatura ambiente, 6–13 °C il fresco. Circa 80 °C è l'acqua del bagnomaria, non il sake.","15–18 °C, c'est l'ambiant ; 6–13 °C, le frais. Environ 80 °C, c'est l'eau du bain-marie, pas le saké.","15–18 °C is room temperature and 6–13 °C chilled. About 80 °C is the water-bath water, not the sake."]},{"id":"k17869938","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha scaldare un sake?","Quel effet a le fait de chauffer un saké ?","What effect does warming have on a sake?"],"o":[["Lo fa sembrare più intenso, più ricco e più acido","Il le fait paraître plus intense, plus riche et plus acide","It seems more intense, richer and more acidic"],["Lo rende più leggero e meno acido","Il le rend plus léger et moins acide","It becomes lighter and less acidic"],["Ne alza il grado alcolico","Il augmente son degré d'alcool","It raises its alcohol level"],["Esalta gli aromi dei ginjō","Il exalte les arômes des ginjō","It boosts ginjō aromas"]],"e":["Il calore aumenta intensità, consistenza e acidità percepite, cosa utile con il cibo.","La chaleur accroît l'intensité, la texture et l'acidité perçues, ce qui aide avec les plats.","Heat increases perceived intensity, texture and acidity, which can help with food."],"d":["Il grado non cambia, e i ginjō perdono aromi con il caldo. L'effetto è l'opposto di «più leggero».","Le degré ne change pas, et les ginjō perdent leurs arômes à la chaleur. L'effet est l'inverse de « plus léger ».","Strength does not change, and ginjō loses aromas with heat. The effect is the opposite of 'lighter'."]},{"id":"k1d1fd4f7","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Quali sake si possono servire freschi, a temperatura ambiente E caldi?","Quels sakés peuvent se servir frais, à température ambiante ET chauds ?","Which sakes can be served chilled, at room temperature AND warm?"],"o":[["Futsū-shu, junmai e honjōzō","Futsū-shu, junmai et honjōzō","Futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō"],["Ginjō e daiginjō","Ginjō et daiginjō","Ginjō and daiginjō"],["Solo il sake frizzante","Seulement le saké pétillant","Sparkling sake only"],["Junmai ginjō e junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō et junmai daiginjō","Junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō"]],"e":["Futsū-shu, junmai e honjōzō vanno bene a tutte e tre le temperature.","Futsū-shu, junmai et honjōzō conviennent aux trois températures.","Futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō suit all three temperatures."],"d":["Tutti gli stili ginjō (anche junmai ginjō e junmai daiginjō) non vanno scaldati. Il frizzante si serve solo fresco.","Tous les styles ginjō (y compris junmai ginjō et junmai daiginjō) ne se chauffent pas. Le pétillant se sert seulement frais.","No ginjō style (including junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō) should be warmed. Sparkling is served chilled only."]},{"id":"k117fc7d7","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Come si serve il sake frizzante?","Comment sert-on le saké pétillant ?","How is sparkling sake served?"],"o":[["Solo fresco","Seulement frais","Chilled only"],["Caldo, per sentire meglio le bollicine","Chaud, pour mieux sentir les bulles","Warm, to feel the bubbles better"],["A temperatura ambiente o caldo","À température ambiante ou chaud","At room temperature or warm"],["Indifferentemente a qualsiasi temperatura","Indifféremment à n'importe quelle température","At any temperature"]],"e":["Il sake frizzante si serve soltanto fresco.","Le saké pétillant se sert uniquement frais.","Sparkling sake is served chilled only."],"d":["Né ambiente né caldo sono consigliati per lo sparkling, che perderebbe freschezza e bollicine.","Ni l'ambiant ni le chaud ne conviennent au pétillant, qui perdrait fraîcheur et bulles.","Neither room temperature nor warm suits sparkling sake, which would lose freshness and bubbles."]},{"id":"k18e59add","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Come si servono in genere koshu e nigori?","Comment sert-on généralement le koshu et le nigori ?","How are koshu and nigori generally served?"],"o":[["Di solito freschi, ma alcuni anche caldi","Plutôt frais, mais certains aussi chauds","Generally chilled, though some can be served warm"],["Sempre caldi","Toujours chauds","Always warm"],["Mai freschi","Jamais frais","Never chilled"],["Solo a temperatura ambiente","Seulement à température ambiante","Only at room temperature"]],"e":["Koshu e nigori stanno meglio freschi, ma alcuni si possono servire caldi.","Koshu et nigori sont meilleurs frais, mais certains peuvent se servir chauds.","Koshu and nigori are generally best chilled, but some can be served warm."],"d":["Le opzioni con «sempre», «mai» o «solo» sono troppo rigide per questi stili così vari.","Les options avec « toujours », « jamais » ou « seulement » sont trop rigides pour des styles si variés.","Options with 'always', 'never' or 'only' are too rigid for such varied styles."]},{"id":"k14caa9ea","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Per scaldare il sake a bagnomaria, a quale temperatura deve essere l'acqua?","Pour chauffer le saké au bain-marie, à quelle température doit être l'eau ?","To warm sake in a water bath, what temperature should the water be?"],"o":[["Circa 80 °C","Environ 80 °C","About 80 °C"],["Circa 40 °C","Environ 40 °C","About 40 °C"],["Bollente, 100 °C, per 10 minuti","Bouillante, 100 °C, pendant 10 minutes","Boiling, 100 °C, for 10 minutes"],["Circa 15 °C","Environ 15 °C","About 15 °C"]],"e":["Acqua a circa 80 °C: un tokkuri piccolo si scalda in 2–4 minuti.","De l'eau à environ 80 °C : un petit tokkuri chauffe en 2 à 4 minutes.","Water at about 80 °C: a small tokkuri warms in 2–4 minutes."],"d":["40 °C è la temperatura del sake caldo, non dell'acqua. L'acqua bollente per 10 minuti lo scalderebbe troppo; 15 °C non lo scalderebbe affatto.","40 °C est la température du saké chaud, pas de l'eau. L'eau bouillante 10 minutes le chaufferait trop ; 15 °C ne le chaufferait pas.","40 °C is the temperature of warm sake, not the water. Boiling water for 10 minutes would overheat it; 15 °C would not warm it at all."]},{"id":"k1322d1c6","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Che cosa bisogna sempre usare quando si scalda il sake a bagnomaria?","Que faut-il toujours utiliser pour chauffer le saké au bain-marie ?","What should always be used when warming sake in a water bath?"],"o":[["Un termometro","Un thermomètre","A thermometer"],["Un masu di cedro","Un masu en cèdre","A cedar masu"],["Ghiaccio","Des glaçons","Ice"],["Un bicchiere da vino","Un verre à vin","A wine glass"]],"e":["Il termometro permette di restare nella fascia giusta di 40–50 °C.","Le thermomètre permet de rester dans la bonne plage de 40–50 °C.","A thermometer keeps you in the right 40–50 °C range."],"d":["Il sake si scalda nel tokkuri, non nel masu o nel bicchiere; il ghiaccio servirebbe a raffreddare.","On chauffe le saké dans le tokkuri, pas dans le masu ni le verre ; les glaçons servent à refroidir.","Sake is warmed in the tokkuri, not a masu or glass; ice is for cooling."]},{"id":"k17286660","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Quanto tempo serve circa per scaldare 180 mL di sake al microonde?","Combien de temps faut-il environ pour chauffer 180 mL de saké au micro-ondes ?","About how long does it take to warm 180 mL of sake in a microwave?"],"o":[["20–40 secondi","20–40 secondes","20–40 seconds"],["2–4 minuti","2–4 minutes","2–4 minutes"],["5 secondi","5 secondes","5 seconds"],["10 minuti","10 minutes","10 minutes"]],"e":["Bastano circa 20–40 secondi, secondo l'apparecchio e la temperatura voluta.","Il faut environ 20 à 40 secondes, selon l'appareil et la température voulue.","About 20–40 seconds, depending on the microwave and target temperature."],"d":["2–4 minuti è il tempo del bagnomaria per un tokkuri piccolo. 5 secondi sono troppo pochi, 10 minuti decisamente troppi.","2 à 4 minutes, c'est le temps du bain-marie pour un petit tokkuri. 5 secondes, c'est trop peu ; 10 minutes, beaucoup trop.","2–4 minutes is the water-bath time for a small tokkuri. 5 seconds is too short and 10 minutes far too long."]},{"id":"k1cb9c500","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un tokkuri?","Qu'est-ce qu'un tokkuri ?","What is a tokkuri?"],"o":[["La caraffa per scaldare e servire il sake","La carafe pour chauffer et servir le saké","The carafe for heating and serving sake"],["La tazzina tradizionale","La petite coupe traditionnelle","The traditional cup"],["La scatola di cedro","La boîte en cèdre","The cedar box"],["La stanza del kōji","La salle du kōji","The kōji room"]],"e":["Il tokkuri è la caraffa, di solito di ceramica, da 150–300 mL.","Le tokkuri est la carafe, souvent en céramique, de 150 à 300 mL.","The tokkuri is the carafe, usually pottery, holding 150–300 mL."],"d":["La tazzina è l'o-choko, la scatola di cedro è il masu.","La petite coupe est l'o-choko, la boîte en cèdre le masu.","The cup is the o-choko and the cedar box is the masu."]},{"id":"k15909d80","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Perché l'o-choko va riempita spesso?","Pourquoi faut-il remplir souvent l'o-choko ?","Why does an o-choko need frequent refilling?"],"o":[["È piccola: riempirla spesso riflette l'ospitalità giapponese","Elle est petite : la remplir souvent reflète l'hospitalité japonaise","It is small: frequent refilling reflects Japanese hospitality"],["Perde sake dal fondo","Elle fuit par le fond","It leaks from the base"],["Il legno assorbe il sake","Le bois absorbe le saké","The wood absorbs the sake"],["Il sake evapora subito","Le saké s'évapore aussitôt","The sake evaporates at once"]],"e":["Le tazzine piccole si svuotano in fretta: riempirle è un gesto di ospitalità.","Les petites coupes se vident vite : les remplir est un geste d'hospitalité.","Small cups empty quickly: refilling them is a gesture of hospitality."],"d":["Le o-choko più comuni sono di ceramica o vetro, non di legno; il legno è quello del masu.","Les o-choko les plus courantes sont en céramique ou en verre, pas en bois ; le bois, c'est le masu.","The most common o-choko are pottery or glass, not wood; wood is the masu."]},{"id":"k1a043805","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Perché il masu non è un recipiente ideale per il sake?","Pourquoi le masu n'est-il pas un récipient idéal pour le saké ?","Why is a masu not an ideal vessel for sake?"],"o":[["Il legno di cedro dà sapore al sake","Le bois de cèdre donne du goût au saké","The cedar wood adds flavour to the sake"],["È troppo grande","Il est trop grand","It is too large"],["È di vetro fragile","Il est en verre fragile","It is made of fragile glass"],["Scalda troppo il sake","Il chauffe trop le saké","It overheats the sake"]],"e":["Il masu è di cedro, e il legno cambia il sapore del sake.","Le masu est en cèdre, et le bois modifie le goût du saké.","The masu is cedar, and the wood changes the sake's flavour."],"d":["Il masu è una scatoletta di legno, non di vetro; un tempo serviva a misurare il riso e oggi compare in qualche cerimonia.","Le masu est une petite boîte en bois, pas en verre ; il servait autrefois à mesurer le riz et apparaît aujourd'hui lors de cérémonies.","The masu is a small wooden box, not glass; it was once used to measure rice and now appears at some ceremonies."]},{"id":"k1cfc4b71","c":"k11","p":0,"q":["Quale bicchiere è ideale per un daiginjō servito fresco?","Quel verre est idéal pour un daiginjō servi frais ?","Which glass is ideal for a chilled daiginjō?"],"o":[["Un piccolo bicchiere da vino a tulipano","Un petit verre à vin tulipe","A small tulip-shaped wine glass"],["Un grande boccale da birra","Une grande chope à bière","A large beer mug"],["Un masu di cedro","Un masu en cèdre","A cedar masu"],["Un bicchiere largo da acqua","Un grand verre à eau","A wide tumbler"]],"e":["Piccolo per mantenere la temperatura, a tulipano per esaltare gli aromi.","Petit pour garder la température, tulipe pour mettre en valeur les arômes.","Small to keep the temperature, tulip-shaped to enhance the aromas."],"d":["Un boccale grande lascerebbe scaldare il sake, il masu darebbe sapore di legno, un bicchiere largo disperderebbe gli aromi.","Une grande chope laisserait le saké se réchauffer, le masu donnerait un goût de bois, un verre large disperserait les arômes.","A big mug lets the sake warm up, a masu adds wood flavour, and a wide tumbler lets aromas escape."]},{"id":"k1efbce10","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["In un abbinamento, chi influenza di più chi?","Dans un accord, qui influence le plus qui ?","In a pairing, which affects which more?"],"o":[["Il cibo influenza la bevanda più del contrario","Le plat influence la boisson plus que l'inverse","Food affects the drink more than the reverse"],["La bevanda influenza il cibo più del contrario","La boisson influence le plat plus que l'inverse","The drink affects the food more"],["Non si influenzano mai","Ils ne s'influencent jamais","They never affect each other"],["Dipende solo dal colore","Cela dépend seulement de la couleur","It depends only on colour"]],"e":["In genere è il cibo a cambiare il gusto della bevanda più del contrario.","En général, c'est le plat qui modifie le goût de la boisson plus que l'inverse.","Generally food changes how the drink tastes more than the reverse."],"d":["Le interazioni esistono sempre, anche se di solito sono leggere; il colore non c'entra.","Les interactions existent toujours, même si elles sont souvent légères ; la couleur n'a rien à voir.","Interactions always exist, even if usually mild; colour has nothing to do with it."]},{"id":"k16df283d","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Che effetto hanno sale e acidità del cibo sulla bevanda?","Quel effet ont le sel et l'acidité du plat sur la boisson ?","What effect do salt and acidity in food have on a drink?"],"o":[["Meno amara e acida, più dolce e fruttata","Moins amère et acide, plus douce et fruitée","Less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier"],["Più amara e acida, meno fruttata","Plus amère et acide, moins fruitée","More bitter and acidic, less fruity"],["Più bruciore d'alcol","Plus de brûlure d'alcool","More alcohol burn"],["Nessun effetto","Aucun effet","No effect"]],"e":["Sale e acidità sono interazioni positive: ammorbidiscono la bevanda.","Sel et acidité sont des interactions positives : elles adoucissent la boisson.","Salt and acidity are positive interactions: they soften the drink."],"d":["Più amara e acida è l'effetto dell'umami, dello zucchero e del piccante; il bruciore d'alcol aumenta con il piccante.","Plus amère et acide, c'est l'effet de l'umami, du sucre et du piquant ; la brûlure d'alcool augmente avec le piquant.","More bitter and acidic is the effect of umami, sugar and chilli; alcohol burn rises with chilli."]},{"id":"k126a21a7","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Quale elemento del cibo rende la bevanda più amara, più acida e meno fruttata?","Quel élément du plat rend la boisson plus amère, plus acide et moins fruitée ?","Which element in food makes a drink more bitter, more acidic and less fruity?"],"o":[["Umami","Umami","Umami"],["Sale","Sel","Salt"],["Acidità","Acidité","Acidity"],["Grassezza","Gras","Fat"]],"e":["L'umami è il principale elemento «difficile» negli abbinamenti con il sake.","L'umami est le principal élément « difficile » dans les accords avec le saké.","Umami is the main 'difficult' element in sake pairings."],"d":["Sale e acidità hanno l'effetto contrario, e il sale può persino annullare l'effetto dell'umami.","Sel et acidité ont l'effet inverse, et le sel peut même annuler l'effet de l'umami.","Salt and acidity have the opposite effect, and salt can even cancel out umami."]},{"id":"k143b2daf","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Un piatto molto piccante con un sake: che cosa succede?","Un plat très épicé avec un saké : que se passe-t-il ?","A very spicy (chilli-hot) dish with a sake: what happens?"],"o":[["Aumenta il bruciore dell'alcol","La brûlure de l'alcool augmente","The alcohol burn increases"],["Il sake sembra più dolce","Le saké paraît plus doux","The sake seems sweeter"],["Il sake sembra meno acido","Le saké paraît moins acide","The sake seems less acidic"],["Il piccante scompare","Le piquant disparaît","The heat disappears"]],"e":["Il piccante agisce come l'umami e in più accentua il bruciore dell'alcol.","Le piquant agit comme l'umami et accentue en plus la brûlure de l'alcool.","Chilli acts like umami and also increases the burning effect of the alcohol."],"d":["Il piccante rende la bevanda meno dolce e più acida, non il contrario, e non sparisce.","Le piquant rend la boisson moins douce et plus acide, pas l'inverse, et il ne disparaît pas.","Chilli makes the drink less sweet and more acidic, not the reverse, and it does not vanish."]},{"id":"k1b978725","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Qual è la considerazione più importante quando si abbina il sake al cibo?","Quel est le critère le plus important pour accorder le saké avec un plat ?","What is the most important consideration when pairing sake with food?"],"o":[["Il gusto personale","Le goût personnel","Personal preference"],["Usare solo cucina giapponese","N'utiliser que la cuisine japonaise","Only using Japanese food"],["Servire sempre il sake caldo","Toujours servir le saké chaud","Always serving sake warm"],["Scegliere il sake più caro","Choisir le saké le plus cher","Choosing the most expensive sake"]],"e":["Quasi tutti i sake vanno con quasi tutti i cibi: decide il gusto personale.","Presque tous les sakés vont avec presque tous les plats : c'est le goût personnel qui décide.","Most sakes go with most foods, so personal preference decides."],"d":["Il sake va bene anche con la cucina internazionale; la temperatura e il prezzo non sono criteri di abbinamento.","Le saké va aussi avec la cuisine internationale ; la température et le prix ne sont pas des critères d'accord.","Sake also suits international food; temperature and price are not pairing criteria."]},{"id":"k18337c91","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Un dessert molto dolce: quale sake scegliere?","Un dessert très sucré : quel saké choisir ?","A very sweet dessert: which sake should you choose?"],"o":[["Un sake almeno altrettanto dolce","Un saké au moins aussi doux","A sake at least as sweet"],["Il sake più secco possibile","Le saké le plus sec possible","The driest sake possible"],["Un sake molto acido","Un saké très acide","A very acidic sake"],["Un sake caldissimo","Un saké très chaud","A very hot sake"]],"e":["I piatti dolci vogliono un sake dolce almeno quanto loro.","Les plats sucrés demandent un saké au moins aussi doux qu'eux.","Sweet dishes call for a sake at least as sweet."],"d":["Lo zucchero del piatto fa sembrare la bevanda meno dolce e più acida: un sake secco o acido risulterebbe magro e aspro.","Le sucre du plat rend la boisson moins douce et plus acide : un saké sec ou acide paraîtrait maigre et aigre.","Sugar in the dish makes a drink seem less sweet and more acidic: a dry or acidic sake would taste thin and sour."]},{"id":"k1fcb4d6e","c":"k12","p":0,"q":["Perché conviene abbinare un sashimi delicato a un sake leggero?","Pourquoi associer un sashimi délicat à un saké léger ?","Why pair delicate sashimi with a light sake?"],"o":[["Perché cibo e sake abbiano un'intensità di sapore simile","Pour que plat et saké aient une intensité de saveur proche","So food and sake have a similar flavour intensity"],["Perché il sake leggero è sempre più costoso","Parce que le saké léger est toujours plus cher","Because light sake is always more expensive"],["Perché il pesce va solo con il sake caldo","Parce que le poisson ne va qu'avec le saké chaud","Because fish only goes with warm sake"],["Perché il sake leggero è più alcolico","Parce que le saké léger est plus alcoolisé","Because light sake is stronger"]],"e":["Intensità simili evitano che uno dei due copra l'altro.","Des intensités proches évitent que l'un écrase l'autre.","Similar intensities stop one overwhelming the other."],"d":["Il prezzo, la temperatura e il grado alcolico non sono il motivo di questo consiglio.","Le prix, la température et le degré ne sont pas la raison de ce conseil.","Price, temperature and strength are not the reason for this advice."]}],"lessons":[{"c":"k01","t":["Un bicchiere di riso","Un verre de riz","A glass of rice"],"p":[["Il sake è una bevanda alcolica giapponese ottenuta dal riso. In Giappone uno dei suoi nomi ufficiali è nihon-shu, cioè «la bevanda alcolica del Giappone»: un nome che dice già quanto il sake sia legato al suo Paese. Chi lo assaggia per la prima volta spesso si aspetta qualcosa di forte come un distillato, e invece scopre una bevanda morbida, fresca e delicata.","Le saké est une boisson alcoolisée japonaise élaborée à partir de riz. Au Japon, l'un de ses noms officiels est nihon-shu, littéralement « la boisson alcoolisée du Japon » : un nom qui montre à quel point le saké est lié à son pays. Ceux qui le goûtent pour la première fois s'attendent souvent à un alcool fort, et découvrent au contraire une boisson souple, fraîche et délicate.","Sake is a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice. In Japan one of its official names is nihon-shu, which simply means 'the alcoholic drink of Japan': the name alone tells you how closely sake is tied to its homeland. First-time tasters often expect something fiery, like a spirit, and discover instead a soft, fresh and delicate drink."],["La maggior parte dei sake è limpida e incolore; alcuni hanno un leggero riflesso giallo paglierino o verdolino. Il grado alcolico tipico va dal 15 al 17%, un po' più di un vino. In bocca il sake è di solito appena dolce e poco acido, con aromi lievi che ricordano i cereali, i latticini (come lo yogurt o la panna) oppure la frutta.","La plupart des sakés sont limpides et incolores ; certains ont un léger reflet jaune pâle ou vert. Leur degré d'alcool se situe généralement entre 15 et 17 %, un peu plus qu'un vin. En bouche, le saké est le plus souvent légèrement sucré et peu acide, avec des arômes discrets qui évoquent les céréales, les produits laitiers (yaourt, crème) ou les fruits.","Most sakes are clear and colourless; a few show a faint pale yellow or green tint. A typical sake has 15–17% abv, a little more than most wines. On the palate it is usually slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with gentle flavours that recall cereal, dairy (think yoghurt or cream) or fruit."],["Attenzione a un equivoco frequente: il sake non è un distillato. Si ottiene per fermentazione, come il vino e la birra. Ricordare il profilo «tipo» (limpido, 15–17%, leggermente dolce, poco acido, aromi delicati) aiuta a capire tutti gli stili che vedremo dopo, perché molti si definiscono proprio per come si allontanano da questo punto di partenza.","Attention à une confusion fréquente : le saké n'est pas un spiritueux. Il est obtenu par fermentation, comme le vin et la bière. Retenir le profil « type » (limpide, 15–17 %, légèrement sucré, peu acide, arômes délicats) aide à comprendre tous les styles vus ensuite, car beaucoup se définissent justement par leur écart avec ce point de départ.","Beware a common mix-up: sake is not a spirit. It is made by fermentation, like wine and beer. Keeping the 'typical' profile in mind (clear, 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, delicate flavours) makes every later style easier to understand, because many styles are defined by how they differ from this starting point."]],"k":[["Sake: bevanda alcolica giapponese a base di riso; nome ufficiale nihon-shu","Saké : boisson alcoolisée japonaise à base de riz ; nom officiel nihon-shu","Sake: a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice; official name nihon-shu"],["Di solito limpido e incolore, a volte giallo pallido o verdolino","Généralement limpide et incolore, parfois jaune pâle ou vert","Usually clear and colourless, sometimes pale yellow or green"],["Tipicamente 15–17% vol., leggermente dolce, poco acido","Typiquement 15–17 % vol., légèrement sucré, peu acide","Typically 15–17% abv, slightly sweet, lightly acidic"],["Aromi delicati di cereali, latticini o frutta; è fermentato, non distillato","Arômes délicats de céréales, de produits laitiers ou de fruits ; fermenté, pas distillé","Delicate cereal, dairy or fruity flavours; fermented, not distilled"]]},{"c":"k01","t":["Quattro ingredienti, più uno facoltativo","Quatre ingrédients, plus un facultatif","Four ingredients, plus one optional extra"],"p":[["Ogni sake nasce da quattro ingredienti principali: riso bianco cotto a vapore, kōji, acqua e lievito. Esiste poi un quinto ingrediente, facoltativo: un alcol distillato ad alta gradazione. Lo vedremo spesso, perché la sua presenza o assenza conta molto nei nomi delle categorie di sake.","Tout saké naît de quatre ingrédients principaux : du riz blanc cuit à la vapeur, du kōji, de l'eau et de la levure. Il existe aussi un cinquième ingrédient, facultatif : un alcool distillé à haut degré. Nous le retrouverons souvent, car sa présence ou son absence compte beaucoup dans le nom des catégories de saké.","Every sake starts from four main ingredients: steamed white rice, kōji, water and yeast. There is also a fifth, optional ingredient: a high-strength distilled alcohol. It will come up again and again, because whether it is used or not matters a great deal in the names of sake categories."],["Il riso di solito arriva da fornitori esterni ed entra in cantina crudo, duro e polveroso: è il birraio del sake a cuocerlo a vapore, così che si ammorbidisca e possa sciogliersi nell'acqua. Il kōji invece si fa in cantina: si prende una piccola parte del riso cotto e ci si fa crescere sopra una muffa speciale. Senza kōji non si potrebbe produrre l'alcol presente in ogni sake.","Le riz vient généralement de fournisseurs et arrive à la brasserie cru, dur et poussiéreux : c'est le brasseur qui le cuit à la vapeur pour l'attendrir et lui permettre de se défaire dans l'eau. Le kōji, lui, se fabrique sur place : on prélève une petite partie du riz cuit et on y fait pousser une moisissure spéciale. Sans kōji, impossible de produire l'alcool présent dans tout saké.","Rice is usually bought from suppliers and reaches the brewery raw, hard and dusty: the brewer steams it so that it softens and can break up in water. Kōji, on the other hand, is made in the brewery: a small part of the steamed rice is taken and a special mould is grown on it. Without kōji there would be no way to make the alcohol found in every sake."],["L'acqua viene da fonti locali: quasi ogni acqua va bene, purché sia pulita. I lieviti sono microrganismi minuscoli; le cantine usano varietà precise, comprate in genere da fornitori specializzati. Un modo semplice per ricordare: il riso e l'acqua arrivano da fuori ma vengono preparati in cantina, il kōji nasce in cantina, il lievito si sceglie con cura.","L'eau provient de ressources locales : presque toutes les eaux conviennent, à condition d'être propres. Les levures sont des micro-organismes minuscules ; les brasseries utilisent des variétés précises, achetées le plus souvent auprès de fournisseurs spécialisés. Pour retenir : le riz arrive de l'extérieur mais se prépare sur place, le kōji naît à la brasserie, la levure se choisit avec soin.","Water comes from local supplies: almost any water will do, as long as it is clean. Yeasts are tiny microorganisms; breweries use specific varieties, usually bought from specialist suppliers. An easy way to remember it: rice arrives from outside but is prepared in the brewery, kōji is born in the brewery, and yeast is carefully chosen."]],"k":[["Quattro ingredienti: riso bianco cotto a vapore, kōji, acqua, lievito","Quatre ingrédients : riz blanc cuit à la vapeur, kōji, eau, levure","Four ingredients: steamed white rice, kōji, water, yeast"],["Facoltativo: alcol distillato ad alta gradazione","Facultatif : alcool distillé à haut degré","Optional: high-strength distilled alcohol"],["Kōji: muffa coltivata su una piccola parte del riso cotto; indispensabile per avere alcol","Kōji : moisissure cultivée sur une petite partie du riz cuit ; indispensable pour obtenir de l'alcool","Kōji: mould grown on a small part of the steamed rice; essential for any alcohol"],["Acqua locale e pulita; lieviti scelti, comprati da fornitori specializzati","Eau locale et propre ; levures choisies, achetées à des fournisseurs spécialisés","Local, clean water; chosen yeasts bought from specialist suppliers"]]},{"c":"k01","t":["Dall'amido allo zucchero, dallo zucchero all'alcol","De l'amidon au sucre, du sucre à l'alcool","From starch to sugar, from sugar to alcohol"],"p":[["Per fare alcol serve zucchero sciolto in acqua. Si aggiungono i lieviti: mangiano lo zucchero, lo trasformano in alcol e liberano anidride carbonica, un gas. È la fermentazione alcolica, la stessa che sta dietro al vino e alla birra.","Pour faire de l'alcool, il faut du sucre dissous dans l'eau. On ajoute les levures : elles consomment le sucre, le transforment en alcool et libèrent du dioxyde de carbone, un gaz. C'est la fermentation alcoolique, la même que pour le vin et la bière.","To make alcohol you need sugar dissolved in water. Yeast is added: it eats the sugar, turns it into alcohol and releases carbon dioxide, a gas. This is alcoholic fermentation, the same process behind wine and beer."],["Il problema è che il riso non contiene zucchero: è pieno di amido. L'amido è fatto di molecole di zucchero legate tra loro in lunghe catene, e i lieviti non riescono a mangiarlo. Servono sostanze chiamate enzimi, capaci di spezzare quei legami e liberare gli zuccheri uno per uno. Questo passaggio si chiama conversione dell'amido.","Le problème, c'est que le riz ne contient pas de sucre : il est rempli d'amidon. L'amidon est formé de molécules de sucre liées entre elles en longues chaînes, et les levures ne peuvent pas le consommer. Il faut des substances appelées enzymes, capables de couper ces liaisons et de libérer les sucres un à un. C'est la conversion de l'amidon.","The catch is that rice contains no sugar: it is full of starch. Starch is made of sugar molecules bonded together in long chains, and yeast cannot eat it. You need substances called enzymes, which can break those bonds and free the sugars one by one. This step is called starch conversion."],["Ecco perché il kōji è così importante: la muffa che cresce sul riso produce proprio questi enzimi. Quando riso cotto, kōji e acqua vengono mescolati, gli enzimi trasformano l'amido in zucchero e i lieviti trasformano lo zucchero in alcol. Niente kōji, niente zucchero; niente zucchero, niente alcol.","Voilà pourquoi le kōji est si important : la moisissure qui pousse sur le riz produit justement ces enzymes. Quand on mélange riz cuit, kōji et eau, les enzymes transforment l'amidon en sucre et les levures transforment le sucre en alcool. Pas de kōji, pas de sucre ; pas de sucre, pas d'alcool.","This is why kōji matters so much: the mould growing on the rice produces exactly these enzymes. When steamed rice, kōji and water are mixed, the enzymes turn starch into sugar and the yeast turns the sugar into alcohol. No kōji, no sugar; no sugar, no alcohol."]],"k":[["Fermentazione alcolica: zucchero + lievito → alcol + anidride carbonica","Fermentation alcoolique : sucre + levure → alcool + dioxyde de carbone","Alcoholic fermentation: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide"],["Il riso contiene amido, non zucchero; i lieviti non mangiano l'amido","Le riz contient de l'amidon, pas de sucre ; les levures ne consomment pas l'amidon","Rice contains starch, not sugar; yeast cannot eat starch"],["Conversione dell'amido: gli enzimi spezzano l'amido in zuccheri","Conversion de l'amidon : les enzymes découpent l'amidon en sucres","Starch conversion: enzymes break starch into sugars"],["Gli enzimi vengono dalla muffa del kōji","Les enzymes viennent de la moisissure du kōji","The enzymes come from the kōji mould"]]},{"c":"k02","t":["Tre tappe obbligatorie","Trois étapes obligatoires","Three steps that always happen"],"p":[["Quando riso cotto, kōji, acqua e lievito sono pronti, può cominciare la produzione vera e propria. Tre tappe ci sono sempre: fermentazione, filtrazione e imbottigliamento. Altre tre sono facoltative: aggiunta di alcol, aggiunta di acqua e pastorizzazione. Conviene imparare le due liste separatamente.","Une fois le riz cuit, le kōji, l'eau et la levure prêts, l'élaboration proprement dite peut commencer. Trois étapes ont toujours lieu : la fermentation, la filtration et la mise en bouteille. Trois autres sont facultatives : l'ajout d'alcool, l'ajout d'eau et la pasteurisation. Mieux vaut apprendre les deux listes séparément.","Once the steamed rice, kōji, water and yeast are ready, brewing proper can begin. Three steps always happen: fermentation, filtration and bottling. Three more are optional: adding alcohol, adding water and pasteurisation. It pays to learn the two lists separately."],["La fermentazione parte in piccolo: con poca quantità di ingredienti si prepara un «avviamento» che crea una popolazione di lieviti sana e attiva. Poi questo avviamento viene unito poco a poco ad altro riso, kōji e acqua, fino a formare una partita più grande: la fermentazione principale. Durante la fermentazione il liquido è bianco e torbido, colorato dal riso.","La fermentation commence petit : avec peu d'ingrédients, on prépare un « levain » qui crée une population de levures saine et active. Ce levain est ensuite mélangé peu à peu avec davantage de riz, de kōji et d'eau, jusqu'à former un lot plus important : la fermentation principale. Pendant la fermentation, le liquide est blanc et trouble, coloré par le riz.","Fermentation starts small: a little of the ingredients is used to make a starter that builds a healthy, active yeast population. The starter is then gradually mixed with more rice, kōji and water to make a larger batch: the main fermentation. While it ferments, the liquid is white and cloudy, coloured by the rice."],["Finita la fermentazione, la legge impone che ogni sake venga filtrato: si tolgono i residui solidi di riso e di solito si ottiene un liquido limpido. Poi si imbottiglia: quasi tutto il sake finisce in bottiglie di vetro di varie dimensioni.","Une fois la fermentation terminée, la loi impose de filtrer tout saké : on retire les résidus solides de riz et l'on obtient généralement un liquide limpide. Vient ensuite la mise en bouteille : presque tout le saké est conditionné en bouteilles de verre de tailles variées.","When fermentation is over, the law requires every sake to be filtered: the solid rice residue is removed, usually leaving a clear liquid. Then comes bottling: nearly all sake is packed in glass bottles of various sizes."]],"k":[["Sempre: fermentazione, filtrazione, imbottigliamento","Toujours : fermentation, filtration, mise en bouteille","Always: fermentation, filtration, bottling"],["Facoltative: aggiunta di alcol, aggiunta di acqua, pastorizzazione","Facultatives : ajout d'alcool, ajout d'eau, pasteurisation","Optional: adding alcohol, adding water, pasteurisation"],["Avviamento della fermentazione → fermentazione principale","Levain de fermentation → fermentation principale","Fermentation starter → main fermentation"],["La filtrazione è obbligatoria per legge; quasi tutto il sake va in vetro","La filtration est obligatoire ; presque tout le saké est mis en verre","Filtration is required by law; nearly all sake goes into glass bottles"]]},{"c":"k02","t":["La fermentazione parallela","La fermentation parallèle","Parallel fermentation"],"p":[["Nel sake succede una cosa particolare: mentre gli enzimi del kōji trasformano l'amido in zucchero, i lieviti stanno già mangiando quello zucchero e producendo alcol. Le due reazioni avvengono nello stesso momento e nello stesso recipiente, dall'inizio alla fine della fermentazione. Per questo si parla di «fermentazione parallela», un tratto unico della produzione del sake.","Dans le saké se produit quelque chose de particulier : pendant que les enzymes du kōji transforment l'amidon en sucre, les levures consomment déjà ce sucre et produisent de l'alcool. Les deux réactions ont lieu en même temps et dans la même cuve, du début à la fin de la fermentation. On parle donc de « fermentation parallèle », un trait propre à l'élaboration du saké.","Something special happens in sake: while the kōji enzymes are turning starch into sugar, the yeast is already eating that sugar and making alcohol. Both reactions take place at the same time, in the same vessel, from the start to the end of fermentation. This is why it is called 'parallel fermentation', a feature unique to sake brewing."],["Immagina una cucina dove un cuoco taglia il pane e un altro lo mangia subito, fetta dopo fetta: sul tagliere non si accumula mai molto pane. Allo stesso modo, nella vasca lo zucchero viene prodotto e consumato a poco a poco. Il risultato è un liquido che a fine fermentazione ha di solito circa il 20% di alcol, più di quanto il sake abbia poi in bottiglia.","Imaginez une cuisine où un cuisinier tranche le pain pendant qu'un autre le mange aussitôt, tranche après tranche : il n'y a jamais beaucoup de pain sur la planche. De la même façon, dans la cuve, le sucre est produit et consommé petit à petit. Résultat : en fin de fermentation, le liquide titre généralement environ 20 % d'alcool, plus que le saké en bouteille.","Picture a kitchen where one cook slices bread while another eats each slice straight away: there is never much bread piling up on the board. In the same way, sugar is made and used up little by little in the tank. The result is a liquid that usually reaches about 20% abv by the end of fermentation, more than sake normally has in the bottle."],["Ricorda la differenza con la birra, dove la trasformazione dell'amido in zucchero avviene prima e la fermentazione dopo, in due fasi separate. Nel sake le due cose si sovrappongono: è proprio questa sovrapposizione che merita il nome di fermentazione parallela.","Retenez la différence avec la bière, où la transformation de l'amidon en sucre se fait d'abord, puis la fermentation ensuite, en deux phases distinctes. Dans le saké, les deux se superposent : c'est précisément cette superposition qui mérite le nom de fermentation parallèle.","Note the contrast with beer, where starch is turned into sugar first and fermented afterwards, in two separate stages. In sake the two overlap: it is exactly this overlap that earns the name parallel fermentation."]],"k":[["Fermentazione parallela: lo zucchero viene prodotto e mangiato allo stesso tempo","Fermentation parallèle : le sucre est produit et consommé en même temps","Parallel fermentation: sugar is made and eaten at the same time"],["È una caratteristica unica del sake","C'est une particularité propre au saké","It is unique to sake brewing"],["A fine fermentazione: circa 20% vol.","En fin de fermentation : environ 20 % vol.","At the end of fermentation: about 20% abv"]]},{"c":"k02","t":["Tre scelte facoltative: alcol, acqua, calore","Trois choix facultatifs : alcool, eau, chaleur","Three optional choices: alcohol, water, heat"],"p":[["Prima della filtrazione il birraio può aggiungere un alcol distillato ad alta gradazione e dal gusto neutro. Non serve a rendere il sake più forte: aiuta a estrarre gli aromi rimasti intrappolati nei residui solidi di riso. I sake che non ricevono questa aggiunta portano in etichetta una parola speciale, che incontreremo presto: junmai.","Avant la filtration, le brasseur peut ajouter un alcool distillé à haut degré et au goût neutre. Il ne sert pas à rendre le saké plus fort : il aide à extraire les arômes restés piégés dans les résidus solides de riz. Les sakés qui ne reçoivent pas cet ajout portent sur l'étiquette un mot spécial, que nous verrons bientôt : junmai.","Before filtration the brewer may add a high-strength distilled alcohol with a neutral flavour. Its purpose is not to make the sake stronger: it helps to pull out flavours trapped in the solid rice residue. Sakes made without this addition carry a special word on the label, which we will meet soon: junmai."],["Quasi sempre, prima dell'imbottigliamento, si aggiunge acqua. La fermentazione lascia il sake intorno al 20% di alcol; l'acqua lo riporta al livello abituale, tra il 15 e il 17%. È per questo che il sake in bottiglia è un po' meno alcolico del liquido appena fermentato.","Presque toujours, avant la mise en bouteille, on ajoute de l'eau. La fermentation laisse le saké autour de 20 % d'alcool ; l'eau le ramène au niveau habituel, entre 15 et 17 %. C'est pourquoi le saké en bouteille est un peu moins alcoolisé que le liquide sortant de fermentation.","Water is nearly always added before bottling. Fermentation leaves the sake at around 20% abv; water brings it down to the usual 15–17%. That is why bottled sake is a little lower in alcohol than the freshly fermented liquid."],["Infine, la grande maggioranza dei sake viene trattata con il calore prima della vendita: è la pastorizzazione. Serve a impedire che si sviluppino aromi difettosi e rende il sake più stabile. I sake che saltano questo passaggio formano uno stile speciale, il nama, che va trattato con molta più attenzione.","Enfin, la grande majorité des sakés est traitée par la chaleur avant la vente : c'est la pasteurisation. Elle empêche l'apparition d'arômes défectueux et rend le saké plus stable. Les sakés qui sautent cette étape forment un style spécial, le nama, qui demande beaucoup plus de soin.","Finally, the vast majority of sake is heat-treated before it goes on sale: this is pasteurisation. It prevents faulty aromas from developing and makes the sake more stable. Sakes that skip this step form a special style, nama, which needs far more careful handling."]],"k":[["Alcol neutro aggiunto prima della filtrazione: estrae aromi dai residui di riso","Alcool neutre ajouté avant la filtration : extrait les arômes des résidus de riz","Neutral alcohol added before filtration: extracts flavours from the rice solids"],["Acqua aggiunta quasi sempre prima dell'imbottigliamento: da circa 20% a 15–17%","Eau ajoutée presque toujours avant la mise en bouteille : d'environ 20 % à 15–17 %","Water nearly always added before bottling: from about 20% down to 15–17%"],["Pastorizzazione per la grande maggioranza: evita aromi difettosi","Pasteurisation pour la grande majorité : évite les arômes défectueux","Pasteurisation for the vast majority: prevents faulty aromas"]]},{"c":"k03","t":["Levigare il riso: togliere per scegliere lo stile","Polir le riz : enlever pour choisir le style","Polishing: removing rice to choose a style"],"p":[["Il birraio del sake parte da chicchi di riso integrale, che devono passare per quattro fasi prima di diventare riso bianco cotto a vapore: levigatura, lavaggio, ammollo e cottura a vapore. La prima è la più importante per lo stile. Durante la levigatura i chicchi passano tra due superfici ruvide che, nel giro di alcune ore, consumano lentamente gli strati esterni e una parte di quelli intermedi.","Le brasseur de saké part de grains de riz brun, qui doivent passer par quatre étapes avant de devenir du riz blanc cuit à la vapeur : le polissage, le lavage, le trempage et la cuisson à la vapeur. La première est la plus importante pour le style. Pendant le polissage, les grains passent entre deux surfaces rugueuses qui, en quelques heures, usent lentement les couches extérieures et une partie des couches intermédiaires.","A sake brewer starts with grains of brown rice, which go through four stages before they become steamed white rice: polishing, washing, soaking and steaming. The first matters most for style. During polishing the grains pass between two rough surfaces that, over a few hours, slowly wear away the outer layers and some of the middle layers."],["Un chicco di riso ha tre zone. Gli strati esterni sono marroni; quelli intermedi sono bianchi; al centro c'è un nucleo bianco fatto quasi solo di amido. Gli strati esterni e intermedi contengono anche amido, ma insieme a molte altre sostanze: sono queste a dare al sake più acidità e umami, con aromi di cereali e di latticini. Gli strati esterni vengono tolti quasi sempre; la vera scelta riguarda quelli intermedi.","Un grain de riz a trois zones. Les couches extérieures sont brunes ; les couches intermédiaires sont blanches ; au centre se trouve un cœur blanc presque entièrement fait d'amidon. Les couches extérieures et intermédiaires contiennent aussi de l'amidon, mais avec beaucoup d'autres substances : ce sont elles qui donnent au saké plus d'acidité et d'umami, avec des arômes de céréales et lactés. Les couches extérieures sont presque toujours retirées ; le vrai choix porte sur les intermédiaires.","A rice grain has three zones. The outer layers are brown; the middle layers are white; at the centre is a white core that is almost pure starch. The outer and middle layers also hold starch, but together with many other components: these give sake more acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas. The outer layers are nearly always removed; the real decision concerns the middle layers."],["Se il birraio toglie solo una parte degli strati intermedi, il sake avrà più acidità e umami, con aromi di cereali e latticini. Se invece li elimina quasi tutti, lasciando soprattutto il nucleo di amido, il sake sarà di solito meno acido, con meno umami e con aromi più fruttati e floreali. Levigare di più significa quindi spostarsi verso uno stile più puro e profumato.","Si le brasseur ne retire qu'une partie des couches intermédiaires, le saké aura plus d'acidité et d'umami, avec des arômes de céréales et lactés. S'il les retire presque toutes pour ne garder que le cœur d'amidon, le saké sera généralement moins acide, avec moins d'umami et des arômes plus fruités et floraux. Polir davantage, c'est donc aller vers un style plus pur et plus parfumé.","If the brewer polishes away only some of the middle layers, the sake will have more acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas. If most or all of the middle layers go, leaving mainly the starch core, the sake will usually have less acidity and umami and more fruity, floral aromas. Polishing more means moving towards a purer, more fragrant style."]],"k":[["Quattro fasi: levigatura, lavaggio, ammollo, cottura a vapore","Quatre étapes : polissage, lavage, trempage, cuisson à la vapeur","Four stages: polishing, washing, soaking, steaming"],["Strati esterni marroni, intermedi bianchi, nucleo quasi solo amido","Couches extérieures brunes, intermédiaires blanches, cœur presque pur amidon","Outer layers brown, middle layers white, core almost pure starch"],["Poca levigatura → più acidità e umami, aromi di cereali e latticini","Peu de polissage → plus d'acidité et d'umami, arômes de céréales et lactés","Light polishing → more acidity and umami, cereal and lactic aromas"],["Molta levigatura → meno acidità e umami, più frutta e fiori","Beaucoup de polissage → moins d'acidité et d'umami, plus de fruits et de fleurs","Heavy polishing → less acidity and umami, more fruit and flowers"]]},{"c":"k03","t":["Il grado di levigatura: un numero da leggere al contrario","Le taux de polissage : un chiffre qui se lit à l'envers","The polishing ratio: a number that works backwards"],"p":[["Quanto riso bisogna togliere per avere diritto a una categoria premium è stabilito dalla legge giapponese: è il grado di levigatura. Grazie a questa regola i termini in etichetta danno un'indicazione affidabile dello stile del sake.","La quantité de riz à retirer pour avoir droit à une catégorie premium est fixée par la loi japonaise : c'est le taux de polissage. Grâce à cette règle, les termes de l'étiquette donnent une indication fiable du style du saké.","How much rice must be removed to qualify for a premium grade is set by Japanese law: this is the polishing ratio. Thanks to this rule, the label terms give a reliable guide to the style of the sake."],["Il numero si esprime in percentuale e indica quanto chicco RESTA, non quanto se ne toglie. Se la legge chiede il 60%, significa che dopo la levigatura deve rimanere il 60% o meno del chicco originale: almeno il 40% è stato tolto. Più il numero è basso, più il riso è stato levigato.","Le chiffre s'exprime en pourcentage et indique la part du grain qui RESTE, pas celle qu'on enlève. Si la loi exige 60 %, il doit rester 60 % ou moins du grain d'origine après polissage : au moins 40 % ont été retirés. Plus le chiffre est bas, plus le riz a été poli.","The figure is a percentage and shows how much of the grain REMAINS, not how much is removed. If the law requires 60%, then 60% or less of the original grain must be left after polishing: at least 40% has gone. The lower the number, the more the rice has been polished."],["Tre soglie da ricordare. 70% o meno: honjōzō e la maggior parte dei junmai. 60% o meno: ginjō e junmai ginjō. 50% o meno: daiginjō e junmai daiginjō. Il junmai può in teoria usare riso levigato tra il 100% e il 70%, ma succede molto di rado.","Trois seuils à retenir. 70 % ou moins : honjōzō et la plupart des junmai. 60 % ou moins : ginjō et junmai ginjō. 50 % ou moins : daiginjō et junmai daiginjō. Le junmai peut en théorie utiliser du riz poli entre 100 % et 70 %, mais c'est très rare.","Three thresholds to remember. 70% or less: honjōzō and most junmai. 60% or less: ginjō and junmai ginjō. 50% or less: daiginjō and junmai daiginjō. Junmai may in theory use rice with a ratio between 100% and 70%, but this is very rare."]],"k":[["Grado di levigatura: % del chicco che resta, fissata dalla legge","Taux de polissage : % du grain qui reste, fixé par la loi","Polishing ratio: % of the grain that remains, set by law"],["Numero più basso = riso più levigato","Chiffre plus bas = riz plus poli","Lower number = more polished rice"],["≤70% honjōzō e quasi tutti i junmai; ≤60% ginjō e junmai ginjō; ≤50% daiginjō e junmai daiginjō","≤70 % honjōzō et la plupart des junmai ; ≤60 % ginjō et junmai ginjō ; ≤50 % daiginjō et junmai daiginjō","≤70% honjōzō and most junmai; ≤60% ginjō and junmai ginjō; ≤50% daiginjō and junmai daiginjō"],["Junmai tra 100% e 70%: possibile ma molto raro","Junmai entre 100 % et 70 % : possible mais très rare","Junmai between 100% and 70%: allowed but very rare"]]},{"c":"k03","t":["Lavare, ammollare, cuocere a vapore","Laver, faire tremper, cuire à la vapeur","Washing, soaking and steaming"],"p":[["Dopo la levigatura i chicchi sono coperti di polvere di riso: sono proprio gli strati esterni e intermedi che il birraio voleva eliminare. Per questo il riso va lavato con cura, altrimenti quella polvere riporterebbe nel sake ciò che si è appena tolto.","Après le polissage, les grains sont couverts de poussière de riz : ce sont précisément les couches extérieures et intermédiaires que le brasseur voulait éliminer. Il faut donc laver le riz avec soin, sinon cette poussière ramènerait dans le saké ce que l'on vient d'enlever.","After polishing, the grains are covered in rice dust: exactly the outer and middle layers the brewer wanted to get rid of. That is why the rice must be washed carefully; otherwise the dust would put back into the sake what has just been removed."],["Poi vengono l'ammollo e la cottura a vapore. Insieme servono ad ammorbidire il chicco e a dargli la consistenza e l'umidità giuste, così che durante la fermentazione possa disgregarsi nell'acqua. Un riso troppo duro non si scioglierebbe; un riso troppo bagnato diventerebbe una pappa difficile da gestire.","Viennent ensuite le trempage et la cuisson à la vapeur. Ensemble, ils attendrissent le grain et lui donnent la texture et l'humidité justes pour qu'il puisse se défaire dans l'eau pendant la fermentation. Un riz trop dur ne se déferait pas ; un riz trop mouillé deviendrait une bouillie difficile à travailler.","Next come soaking and steaming. Together they soften the grain and give it the right texture and moisture so that it can break up in the water during fermentation. Rice that is too hard would not break down; rice that is too wet would turn into a mush that is hard to work with."]],"k":[["Lavaggio: toglie la polvere di riso rimasta dopo la levigatura","Lavage : retire la poussière de riz laissée par le polissage","Washing: removes the rice dust left by polishing"],["Ammollo e vapore: consistenza e umidità giuste","Trempage et vapeur : texture et humidité justes","Soaking and steaming: the right texture and moisture"],["Obiettivo: un chicco che si disgreghi nell'acqua durante la fermentazione","Objectif : un grain qui se défasse dans l'eau pendant la fermentation","Goal: a grain that breaks up in the water during fermentation"]]},{"c":"k04","t":["La stanza del kōji","La salle du kōji","The kōji room"],"p":[["Il kōji si prepara in una serie di stanze speciali della cantina, dove il birraio può controllare con grande precisione la temperatura e l'umidità. Non è un dettaglio: la muffa è viva, e cresce più o meno in fretta a seconda del caldo e dell'umido che trova. Le stanze hanno quindi zone diverse, dalla più calda e umida alla più fresca e asciutta.","Le kōji se prépare dans une série de salles spéciales de la brasserie, où le brasseur peut contrôler très précisément la température et l'humidité. Ce n'est pas un détail : la moisissure est vivante et pousse plus ou moins vite selon la chaleur et l'humidité qu'elle trouve. Les salles ont donc plusieurs zones, de la plus chaude et humide à la plus fraîche et sèche.","Kōji is made in a special series of rooms in the brewery, where the brewer can control temperature and humidity very precisely. This matters: the mould is alive, and it grows faster or slower depending on the warmth and moisture it finds. The rooms therefore have different zones, from the warmest and most humid to the coolest and driest."],["Il lavoro segue quattro fasi: raffreddare il riso cotto, spargere le spore della muffa, lasciare che la muffa cresca rapidamente all'inizio, poi controllarne e infine fermarne la crescita. In pratica il riso «viaggia» nella stanza: entra nella zona più calda per far partire la muffa ed esce verso la zona più fresca quando bisogna rallentarla.","Le travail suit quatre étapes : refroidir le riz cuit, répandre les spores de la moisissure, laisser la moisissure pousser vite au début, puis contrôler et enfin arrêter sa croissance. En pratique, le riz « voyage » dans la salle : il entre dans la zone la plus chaude pour lancer la moisissure et se déplace vers la zone la plus fraîche quand il faut la ralentir.","The work follows four stages: cool the steamed rice, spread the mould spores, let the mould grow quickly at first, then control and finally stop its growth. In practice the rice 'travels' through the room: it goes into the warmest zone to get the mould started and moves towards the coolest zone when the growth must slow down."]],"k":[["Stanze dedicate con temperatura e umidità controllate con precisione","Salles dédiées où température et humidité sont contrôlées avec précision","Dedicated rooms with precisely controlled temperature and humidity"],["Quattro fasi: raffreddare, spargere le spore, crescita iniziale, controllo e arresto","Quatre étapes : refroidir, répandre les spores, croissance initiale, contrôle et arrêt","Four stages: cool, spread spores, initial growth, control and stop"],["Caldo e umido = crescita veloce; fresco e asciutto = crescita lenta","Chaud et humide = croissance rapide ; frais et sec = croissance lente","Warm and humid = fast growth; cool and dry = slow growth"]]},{"c":"k04","t":["Le quattro fasi del kōji, una per una","Les quatre étapes du kōji, une par une","The four kōji stages, one by one"],"p":[["1. Raffreddare. Appena uscito dal vapore il riso è troppo caldo per il kōji: viene steso su stuoie e lasciato raffreddare naturalmente. 2. Spargere la muffa. Quando è abbastanza freddo, il riso passa nella parte più calda e umida della stanza, viene steso in uno strato sottile su un grande tavolo e le spore della muffa (i suoi «semi») vengono sparse sopra.","1. Refroidir. À la sortie de la vapeur, le riz est trop chaud pour le kōji : on l'étale sur des nattes et on le laisse refroidir naturellement. 2. Répandre la moisissure. Une fois assez refroidi, le riz passe dans la partie la plus chaude et la plus humide de la salle ; on l'étale en couche fine sur une grande table et on y répand les spores de la moisissure (ses « graines »).","1. Cooling. Fresh from the steamer, the rice is too hot for kōji making: it is spread on mats to cool naturally. 2. Spreading the mould. Once cool enough, the rice moves into the warmest, most humid part of the room, is spread in a thin layer on a large table, and the mould spores (its 'seeds') are scattered over it."],["3. Prima crescita. Nella zona calda e umida la muffa si sviluppa in fretta sul riso, che viene girato regolarmente a mano perché la crescita sia uniforme. 4. Controllare e fermare. Il riso viene a volte spostato su rastrelliere, nelle zone più fresche e meno umide, per rallentare la muffa e ottenerne esattamente la quantità desiderata; per fermarla del tutto si porta il riso nella parte più fresca della stanza.","3. Première croissance. Dans la zone chaude et humide, la moisissure se développe vite sur le riz, que l'on retourne régulièrement à la main pour une croissance homogène. 4. Contrôler et arrêter. Le riz est parfois transféré sur des claies, dans des zones plus fraîches et moins humides, pour ralentir la moisissure et en obtenir exactement la quantité voulue ; pour l'arrêter complètement, on le porte dans la partie la plus fraîche de la salle.","3. Initial growth. In the warm, humid zone the mould spreads quickly over the rice, which is turned regularly by hand so that the growth is even. 4. Controlling and stopping. The rice is sometimes moved onto racks in cooler, less humid zones to slow the mould and get exactly the right amount; to stop it altogether, the rice is moved to the coolest part of the room."]],"k":[["Raffreddamento naturale su stuoie","Refroidissement naturel sur des nattes","Natural cooling on mats"],["Spore sparse su uno strato sottile, nella zona più calda e umida","Spores répandues sur une couche fine, dans la zone la plus chaude et humide","Spores scattered on a thin layer, in the warmest, most humid zone"],["Crescita rapida, riso girato a mano","Croissance rapide, riz retourné à la main","Fast growth, rice turned by hand"],["Rallentare nelle zone fresche, fermare nella zona più fresca","Ralentir dans les zones fraîches, arrêter dans la zone la plus fraîche","Slow it in cooler zones, stop it in the coolest zone"]]},{"c":"k05","t":["Il lievito, vero regista degli aromi","La levure, vraie metteuse en scène des arômes","Yeast, the real flavour maker"],"p":[["In molti stili di sake il riso cotto, il kōji e l'acqua danno relativamente poco gusto. È il lievito, in quasi tutti gli stili, a contribuire con una parte importante degli aromi. Ecco perché la fermentazione è il momento in cui il birraio decide molto del carattere del sake.","Dans beaucoup de styles de saké, le riz cuit, le kōji et l'eau apportent relativement peu de goût. C'est la levure qui, dans presque tous les styles, fournit une part importante des arômes. C'est pourquoi la fermentation est le moment où le brasseur décide beaucoup du caractère du saké.","In many sake styles the steamed rice, kōji and water add relatively little flavour. In nearly all styles it is the yeast that contributes a large share of the aromas. That is why fermentation is when the brewer decides much of the sake's character."],["Come abbiamo visto, tutto comincia con un piccolo avviamento: un po' dei quattro ingredienti principali serve a far crescere una popolazione di lieviti sana. Poi l'avviamento passa in un recipiente più grande e viene mescolato con cura con altro riso cotto, kōji e acqua: è la fermentazione principale. A questo punto il birraio ha in mano due leve: il tipo di lievito e la temperatura.","Comme on l'a vu, tout commence par un petit levain : un peu des quatre ingrédients principaux sert à faire croître une population de levures saine. Le levain passe ensuite dans une cuve plus grande et se mélange avec soin à davantage de riz cuit, de kōji et d'eau : c'est la fermentation principale. Le brasseur dispose alors de deux leviers : le type de levure et la température.","As we saw, it all begins with a small starter: a little of the four main ingredients is used to grow a healthy yeast population. The starter then moves to a larger vessel and is carefully mixed with more steamed rice, kōji and water: the main fermentation. Now the brewer has two levers: the choice of yeast and the temperature."]],"k":[["Riso, kōji e acqua danno poco gusto in molti stili; il lievito ne dà molto","Riz, kōji et eau donnent peu de goût dans beaucoup de styles ; la levure en donne beaucoup","Rice, kōji and water give little flavour in many styles; yeast gives a lot"],["Avviamento → fermentazione principale in un recipiente più grande","Levain → fermentation principale dans une cuve plus grande","Starter → main fermentation in a larger vessel"],["Due leve di stile: scelta del lievito e temperatura","Deux leviers de style : choix de la levure et température","Two style levers: choice of yeast and temperature"]]},{"c":"k05","t":["Fresco e profumato, o caldo e cerealicolo","Frais et parfumé, ou chaud et céréalier","Cool and fragrant, or warm and cereal-like"],"p":[["Per ottenere gli aromi fruttati e floreali tipici degli stili ginjō servono due cose insieme: ceppi di lievito speciali e temperature di fermentazione più basse. La fermentazione fresca è più lenta e conserva profumi delicati, come di mela, pera o fiori bianchi.","Pour obtenir les arômes fruités et floraux typiques des styles ginjō, il faut deux choses à la fois : des souches de levure spéciales et des températures de fermentation plus basses. La fermentation fraîche est plus lente et préserve des parfums délicats, comme la pomme, la poire ou les fleurs blanches.","To get the fruity, floral aromas typical of ginjō styles, two things are needed together: special yeast strains and lower fermentation temperatures. A cool fermentation is slower and keeps delicate scents such as apple, pear or white flowers."],["Al contrario, temperature di fermentazione più calde portano aromi di cereali e di latticini. Se colleghiamo questo alla levigatura, il quadro diventa chiaro: riso molto levigato + lieviti speciali + fermentazione fresca danno sake fruttati e floreali; riso poco levigato + fermentazione più calda danno sake cerealicoli e lattici, con più acidità e umami.","À l'inverse, des températures de fermentation plus chaudes donnent des arômes de céréales et lactés. En reliant cela au polissage, le tableau devient clair : riz très poli + levures spéciales + fermentation fraîche donnent des sakés fruités et floraux ; riz peu poli + fermentation plus chaude donnent des sakés céréaliers et lactés, avec plus d'acidité et d'umami.","Warmer fermentation temperatures, by contrast, produce cereal and lactic aromas. Link this to polishing and the picture becomes clear: highly polished rice + special yeasts + cool fermentation give fruity, floral sakes; lightly polished rice + warmer fermentation give cereal, lactic sakes with more acidity and umami."]],"k":[["Aromi ginjō (frutta, fiori): lieviti speciali + fermentazione fresca","Arômes ginjō (fruits, fleurs) : levures spéciales + fermentation fraîche","Ginjō aromas (fruit, flowers): special yeasts + cool fermentation"],["Fermentazione più calda: aromi di cereali e latticini","Fermentation plus chaude : arômes de céréales et lactés","Warmer fermentation: cereal and lactic aromas"],["Stile = levigatura + lievito + temperatura","Style = polissage + levure + température","Style = polishing + yeast + temperature"]]},{"c":"k06","t":["Futsū-shu, il sake di tutti i giorni","Futsū-shu, le saké de tous les jours","Futsū-shu, the everyday sake"],"p":[["Il sake si divide in categorie e gradi. La divisione principale è tra sake di base e sake premium; il sake premium, a sua volta, si suddivide in diversi gradi. Il sake di base, semplice e diffuso, in giapponese si chiama futsū-shu.","Le saké se divise en catégories et en grades. La grande séparation se fait entre saké de base et saké premium ; le saké premium se subdivise à son tour en plusieurs grades. Le saké de base, simple et répandu, s'appelle en japonais futsū-shu.","Sake is divided into categories and grades. The main split is between basic and premium sake; premium sake is then divided into several grades. The simple, widespread basic sake is called futsū-shu in Japanese."],["Il futsū-shu corrisponde in pieno al ritratto del sake tipico: per lo più limpido e incolore, a volte giallo pallido o verdolino, tra il 15 e il 17% di alcol, appena dolce e poco acido, con aromi delicati di latticini e di frutta. È il punto di riferimento da cui partire per capire i gradi premium.","Le futsū-shu correspond tout à fait au portrait du saké typique : le plus souvent limpide et incolore, parfois jaune pâle ou vert, entre 15 et 17 % d'alcool, légèrement sucré et peu acide, avec des arômes délicats lactés et fruités. C'est le point de repère pour comprendre les grades premium.","Futsū-shu fits the portrait of typical sake exactly: mostly clear and colourless, sometimes pale yellow or green, 15–17% abv, slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with delicate lactic and fruity flavours. It is the reference point for understanding the premium grades."]],"k":[["Divisione principale: sake di base e sake premium","Grande division : saké de base et saké premium","Main division: basic and premium sake"],["Sake di base = futsū-shu","Saké de base = futsū-shu","Basic sake = futsū-shu"],["Futsū-shu: 15–17%, leggermente dolce, poco acido, note lattiche e fruttate delicate","Futsū-shu : 15–17 %, légèrement sucré, peu acide, notes lactées et fruitées délicates","Futsū-shu: 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, delicate lactic and fruity notes"]]},{"c":"k06","t":["Sei gradi premium, due famiglie di stile","Six grades premium, deux familles de style","Six premium grades, two style families"],"p":[["Tra i gradi premium, sei sono i più importanti. Quasi tutti hanno lo stesso grado alcolico e lo stesso colore del sake di base, ma si raggruppano in due stili ben diversi. Il primo è quello dei sake con aromi puri di fiori e frutta: la parola chiave è ginjō. Daiginjō significa letteralmente «grande ginjō» e indica i sake dagli aromi fruttati e floreali più puri.","Parmi les grades premium, six sont les plus importants. Presque tous ont le même degré et la même couleur que le saké de base, mais ils se regroupent en deux styles bien différents. Le premier réunit les sakés aux arômes purs de fleurs et de fruits : le mot clé est ginjō. Daiginjō signifie littéralement « grand ginjō » et désigne les sakés aux arômes fruités et floraux les plus purs.","Among the premium grades, six matter most. Nearly all have the same strength and colour as basic sake, but they fall into two very different styles. The first covers sakes with pure floral and fruity aromas: the key word is ginjō. Daiginjō literally means 'big ginjō' and marks the sakes with the purest fruity, floral flavours."],["Il secondo stile è quello dei sake con aromi di cereali e di latticini, che hanno di solito più acidità e più umami degli stili ginjō. Ne fanno parte il junmai e l'honjōzō. Riassumendo: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō e junmai daiginjō stanno dalla parte di frutta e fiori; junmai e honjōzō dalla parte di cereali, latticini, acidità e umami.","Le second style réunit les sakés aux arômes de céréales et lactés, qui ont en général plus d'acidité et d'umami que les styles ginjō. On y trouve le junmai et le honjōzō. En résumé : ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō et junmai daiginjō sont du côté des fruits et des fleurs ; junmai et honjōzō du côté des céréales, des notes lactées, de l'acidité et de l'umami.","The second style covers sakes with cereal and lactic aromas, which usually have more acidity and umami than the ginjō styles. Junmai and honjōzō belong here. In short: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō and junmai daiginjō sit on the fruit-and-flower side; junmai and honjōzō on the side of cereal, lactic notes, acidity and umami."]],"k":[["Sei gradi premium principali, quasi tutti con grado e colore del sake di base","Six grades premium principaux, presque tous avec le degré et la couleur du saké de base","Six main premium grades, mostly with the strength and colour of basic sake"],["Stile ginjō: aromi puri di frutta e fiori, meno acidità e umami","Style ginjō : arômes purs de fruits et de fleurs, moins d'acidité et d'umami","Ginjō style: pure fruity, floral aromas, less acidity and umami"],["Daiginjō = «grande ginjō»: gli aromi più puri","Daiginjō = « grand ginjō » : les arômes les plus purs","Daiginjō = 'big ginjō': the purest aromas"],["Junmai e honjōzō: cereali e latticini, più acidità e umami","Junmai et honjōzō : céréales et notes lactées, plus d'acidité et d'umami","Junmai and honjōzō: cereal and lactic, more acidity and umami"]]},{"c":"k06","t":["Junmai: riso puro, e la griglia completa","Junmai : riz pur, et la grille complète","Junmai: pure rice, and the full grid"],"p":[["C'è un secondo modo di dividere i sei gradi. Tre portano la parola junmai, che significa «riso puro»: indica che prima della filtrazione NON è stato aggiunto alcol distillato. Così il junmai ginjō è uno stile simile al ginjō; l'unica differenza è che il junmai ginjō non ha ricevuto alcol aggiunto. Lo stesso vale per daiginjō e junmai daiginjō, e per honjōzō (con alcol) e junmai (senza).","Il existe une deuxième façon de diviser les six grades. Trois portent le mot junmai, qui signifie « riz pur » : il indique qu'aucun alcool distillé n'a été ajouté avant la filtration. Ainsi, le junmai ginjō est un style proche du ginjō ; la seule différence est que le junmai ginjō n'a pas reçu d'alcool ajouté. Il en va de même pour daiginjō et junmai daiginjō, et pour honjōzō (avec alcool) et junmai (sans).","There is a second way to split the six grades. Three carry the word junmai, meaning 'pure rice': it shows that NO distilled alcohol was added before filtration. So junmai ginjō is a style similar to ginjō; the only difference is that junmai ginjō has had no alcohol added. The same goes for daiginjō and junmai daiginjō, and for honjōzō (with alcohol) and junmai (without)."],["Ora mettiamo tutto in una griglia a due colonne. A sinistra, senza alcol aggiunto: junmai daiginjō (≤50%), junmai ginjō (≤60%), junmai (di solito 70%). A destra, con alcol aggiunto: daiginjō (≤50%), ginjō (≤60%), honjōzō (≤70%). Le due righe in alto, fruttate e floreali, nascono da riso molto levigato, lieviti speciali e fermentazione fresca; la riga in basso, cerealicola e lattica, da riso poco levigato e fermentazione più calda.","Mettons maintenant tout dans une grille à deux colonnes. À gauche, sans alcool ajouté : junmai daiginjō (≤50 %), junmai ginjō (≤60 %), junmai (généralement 70 %). À droite, avec alcool ajouté : daiginjō (≤50 %), ginjō (≤60 %), honjōzō (≤70 %). Les deux lignes du haut, fruitées et florales, naissent d'un riz très poli, de levures spéciales et d'une fermentation fraîche ; la ligne du bas, céréalière et lactée, d'un riz peu poli et d'une fermentation plus chaude.","Now put it all in a two-column grid. Left, no added alcohol: junmai daiginjō (≤50%), junmai ginjō (≤60%), junmai (usually 70%). Right, with added alcohol: daiginjō (≤50%), ginjō (≤60%), honjōzō (≤70%). The top two rows, fruity and floral, come from highly polished rice, special yeasts and cool fermentation; the bottom row, cereal and lactic, from lightly polished rice and warmer fermentation."]],"k":[["Junmai = «riso puro»: nessun alcol distillato aggiunto","Junmai = « riz pur » : aucun alcool distillé ajouté","Junmai = 'pure rice': no distilled alcohol added"],["Coppie: junmai daiginjō/daiginjō, junmai ginjō/ginjō, junmai/honjōzō","Paires : junmai daiginjō/daiginjō, junmai ginjō/ginjō, junmai/honjōzō","Pairs: junmai daiginjō/daiginjō, junmai ginjō/ginjō, junmai/honjōzō"],["Stesso stile in ogni coppia: cambia solo l'alcol aggiunto","Même style dans chaque paire : seul l'alcool ajouté change","Same style within each pair: only the added alcohol differs"],["Ginjō: molto levigato + lieviti speciali + fresco; junmai/honjōzō: poco levigato + più caldo","Ginjō : très poli + levures spéciales + frais ; junmai/honjōzō : peu poli + plus chaud","Ginjō: highly polished + special yeasts + cool; junmai/honjōzō: lightly polished + warmer"]]},{"c":"k07","t":["Quattro parole, sette kanji","Quatre mots, sept kanji","Four words, seven kanji"],"p":[["Le etichette di sake sono scritte per lo più in giapponese, con pochissime parole in alfabeto latino. Per orientarsi basta riconoscere quattro termini chiave: junmai, honjōzō, ginjō e daiginjō. Ogni termine si scompone in suoni, e ogni suono corrisponde a un simbolo chiamato kanji.","Les étiquettes de saké sont surtout écrites en japonais, avec très peu de mots en alphabet latin. Pour s'y retrouver, il suffit de reconnaître quatre termes clés : junmai, honjōzō, ginjō et daiginjō. Chaque terme se découpe en sons, et chaque son correspond à un symbole appelé kanji.","Sake labels are mostly written in Japanese, with only a few words in the Latin alphabet. To find your way, you only need to recognise four key terms: junmai, honjōzō, ginjō and daiginjō. Each term breaks down into sounds, and each sound matches a symbol called a kanji."],["Junmai = jun 純 + mai 米. Honjōzō = hon 本 + jō 醸 + zō 造. Ginjō = gin 吟 + jō 醸. Daiginjō = dai 大 + gin 吟 + jō 醸. Contando, i kanji da imparare sono solo sette, perché gin 吟 e jō 醸 si ripetono. Un trucco: 大 (dai, grande) assomiglia a una persona a braccia aperte, «grande» come il daiginjō, il «grande ginjō».","Junmai = jun 純 + mai 米. Honjōzō = hon 本 + jō 醸 + zō 造. Ginjō = gin 吟 + jō 醸. Daiginjō = dai 大 + gin 吟 + jō 醸. Au total, il n'y a que sept kanji à apprendre, car gin 吟 et jō 醸 se répètent. Une astuce : 大 (dai, grand) ressemble à une personne aux bras ouverts, « grande » comme le daiginjō, le « grand ginjō ».","Junmai = jun 純 + mai 米. Honjōzō = hon 本 + jō 醸 + zō 造. Ginjō = gin 吟 + jō 醸. Daiginjō = dai 大 + gin 吟 + jō 醸. In total there are only seven kanji to learn, because gin 吟 and jō 醸 repeat. A memory trick: 大 (dai, big) looks like a person with arms spread wide, 'big' like daiginjō, the 'big ginjō'."]],"k":[["Etichette quasi tutte in giapponese: riconoscere 4 termini","Étiquettes presque toutes en japonais : reconnaître 4 termes","Labels mostly in Japanese: recognise 4 terms"],["純米 junmai · 本醸造 honjōzō · 吟醸 ginjō · 大吟醸 daiginjō","純米 junmai · 本醸造 honjōzō · 吟醸 ginjō · 大吟醸 daiginjō","純米 junmai · 本醸造 honjōzō · 吟醸 ginjō · 大吟醸 daiginjō"],["Solo 7 kanji: gin 吟 e jō 醸 si ripetono","Seulement 7 kanji : gin 吟 et jō 醸 se répètent","Only 7 kanji: gin 吟 and jō 醸 repeat"]]},{"c":"k08","t":["Nama e nigori","Nama et nigori","Nama and nigori"],"p":[["Esistono quattro stili speciali importanti: nama, nigori, sparkling (frizzante) e koshu. Nama indica un sake non pastorizzato. Poiché è meno stabile degli altri, la maggior parte dei nama va bevuta poco dopo l'uscita sul mercato e tenuta sempre in frigorifero. Appena messo in vendita può sembrare particolarmente vivace e fresco, ma può sviluppare in fretta aromi speziati e maltati che non piacciono a tutti.","Il existe quatre styles spéciaux importants : nama, nigori, pétillant et koshu. Nama désigne un saké non pasteurisé. Comme il est moins stable que les autres, la plupart des nama se boivent peu après leur sortie et se gardent toujours au réfrigérateur. À sa sortie, il peut sembler particulièrement vif et frais, mais il peut vite développer des arômes épicés et maltés qui ne plaisent pas à tout le monde.","There are four important speciality styles: nama, nigori, sparkling and koshu. Nama means unpasteurised sake. Because it is less stable than other sakes, most nama should be drunk soon after release and kept refrigerated at all times. On release it can taste especially lively and fresh, but it can quickly develop spicy, malty aromas that are not to everyone's taste."],["Una curiosità di pronuncia: in giapponese la «s» di nama-sake si ammorbidisce in «z», perciò di solito si scrive nama-zake. Nigori indica invece un sake filtrato in modo grossolano: è torbido perché contiene particelle di riso in sospensione. Lo stile varia molto a seconda di quanti solidi restano: alcuni nigori sono appena velati, altri densi e con pezzetti di riso.","Une curiosité de prononciation : en japonais, le « s » de nama-sake s'adoucit en « z », d'où la graphie habituelle nama-zake. Nigori désigne quant à lui un saké filtré grossièrement : il est trouble car il contient des particules de riz en suspension. Le style varie beaucoup selon la quantité de solides conservée : certains nigori sont à peine voilés, d'autres épais avec des fragments de riz.","A pronunciation note: in Japanese the 's' of nama-sake softens to a 'z', so it is usually spelled nama-zake. Nigori, on the other hand, means sake that has been roughly filtered: it is cloudy because of suspended rice particles. The style varies with how much solid matter is kept: some nigori are lightly cloudy, others thick-textured with lumps of rice."]],"k":[["Nama: non pastorizzato, meno stabile, sempre in frigo, da bere presto","Nama : non pasteurisé, moins stable, toujours au frais, à boire vite","Nama: unpasteurised, less stable, always refrigerated, drink soon"],["Nama giovane: vivace e fresco; poi può diventare speziato e maltato","Nama jeune : vif et frais ; puis il peut devenir épicé et malté","Young nama: lively and fresh; later can turn spicy and malty"],["Si scrive di solito nama-zake","S'écrit généralement nama-zake","Usually spelled nama-zake"],["Nigori: filtrazione grossolana, torbido per le particelle di riso","Nigori : filtration grossière, trouble à cause des particules de riz","Nigori: roughly filtered, cloudy from rice particles"]]},{"c":"k08","t":["Sake frizzante e koshu","Saké pétillant et koshu","Sparkling sake and koshu"],"p":[["Come in ogni bevanda frizzante, le bollicine del sake sparkling vengono dall'anidride carbonica disciolta nel liquido. Esistono diverse tecniche per scioglierla nel sake in bottiglia. Alcuni sake frizzanti sono molto leggeri di corpo e poco alcolici; altri hanno una consistenza più ricca e sono più complessi, e possono persino essere anche nigori. Esistono termini giapponesi per questi sake, ma fuori dal Giappone sono poco usati.","Comme dans toute boisson pétillante, les bulles du saké pétillant viennent du dioxyde de carbone dissous dans le liquide. Plusieurs techniques permettent de le dissoudre dans le saké en bouteille. Certains sakés pétillants sont très légers en texture et peu alcoolisés ; d'autres ont une texture plus riche, plus de complexité, et peuvent même être nigori. Il existe des termes japonais pour ces sakés, mais ils sont peu utilisés hors du Japon.","As with any sparkling drink, the bubbles in sparkling sake come from carbon dioxide dissolved in the liquid. There are various techniques for getting it into bottled sake. Some sparkling sakes are very light in texture and low in alcohol; others are richer-textured and more complex, and can even be nigori too. Japanese terms for these sakes exist but are little used outside Japan."],["Koshu è il nome dei sake invecchiati. Si possono invecchiare in recipienti diversi: vasche di stoccaggio, terracotta, bottiglie di vetro, legno (il rovere però si usa molto di rado). Alcune cantine invecchiano a temperatura ambiente, altre a basse temperature, a volte sotto zero: ne nasce una grande varietà di stili. La maggior parte dei koshu è ambrata o marrone, ricca di consistenza e dolce, con aromi intensi di frutta secca a guscio, frutta secca, perfino carne e verdure in salamoia; esistono però anche koshu più chiari e delicati.","Koshu est le nom des sakés vieillis. On peut les vieillir dans différents contenants : cuves de stockage, terre cuite, bouteilles de verre, bois (le chêne est toutefois très rarement employé). Certaines brasseries vieillissent à température ambiante, d'autres à basse température, parfois sous zéro : d'où une grande diversité de styles. La plupart des koshu sont ambrés ou bruns, riches en texture et sucrés, avec des arômes marqués de fruits à coque, de fruits secs, voire de viande et de légumes saumurés ; mais il existe aussi des koshu plus pâles et délicats.","Koshu is the name for aged sake. It can be aged in various vessels: storage tanks, terracotta, glass bottles, wood (though oak is very rarely used). Some brewers age at room temperature, others at low temperatures, sometimes below freezing: hence a wide range of styles. Most koshu is amber or brown, richly textured and sweet, with pronounced aromas of nuts, dried fruit and even meat and pickled vegetables; but some aged sakes are paler and more delicate."]],"k":[["Sparkling: bollicine di anidride carbonica disciolta; da leggero e poco alcolico a ricco e complesso","Pétillant : bulles de dioxyde de carbone dissous ; de léger et peu alcoolisé à riche et complexe","Sparkling: bubbles of dissolved carbon dioxide; from light and low-alcohol to rich and complex"],["Koshu = sake invecchiato; recipienti vari, il rovere è raro","Koshu = saké vieilli ; contenants variés, le chêne est rare","Koshu = aged sake; various vessels, oak is rare"],["Koshu tipico: ambrato/marrone, ricco, dolce, frutta secca, noci, perfino carne e salamoia","Koshu typique : ambré/brun, riche, sucré, fruits secs, noix, voire viande et saumure","Typical koshu: amber/brown, rich, sweet, nuts, dried fruit, even meat and pickles"]]},{"c":"k08","t":["Stili speciali e gradi: si possono combinare","Styles spéciaux et grades : ils se combinent","Speciality styles and grades combine"],"p":[["Un punto che confonde molti: gli stili speciali non sono una categoria a parte rispetto ai gradi. Un nama, un nigori, uno sparkling o un koshu può essere un futsū-shu oppure uno qualunque dei gradi premium. Un junmai ginjō, per esempio, potrebbe essere anche nama, nigori, frizzante, o perfino una combinazione di questi stili.","Un point qui en trouble beaucoup : les styles spéciaux ne forment pas une catégorie à part par rapport aux grades. Un nama, un nigori, un pétillant ou un koshu peut être un futsū-shu ou n'importe lequel des grades premium. Un junmai ginjō, par exemple, pourrait aussi être nama, nigori, pétillant, voire une combinaison de ces styles.","A point that confuses many: speciality styles are not a separate category from the grades. A nama, nigori, sparkling sake or koshu can be a futsū-shu or any of the premium grades. A junmai ginjō, for example, could also be nama, nigori, sparkling, or even a combination of these styles."],["Pensa al grado come a «come è stato fatto il sake» (levigatura, alcol aggiunto o no) e allo stile speciale come a «un trattamento in più»: niente pastorizzazione, filtrazione grossolana, bollicine, invecchiamento. Su un'etichetta possono quindi comparire entrambe le informazioni, per esempio un «junmai nigori nama».","Voyez le grade comme « la façon dont le saké a été fait » (polissage, alcool ajouté ou non) et le style spécial comme « un traitement en plus » : pas de pasteurisation, filtration grossière, bulles, vieillissement. Les deux informations peuvent donc figurer sur une même étiquette, par exemple un « junmai nigori nama ».","Think of the grade as 'how the sake was made' (polishing, alcohol added or not) and the speciality style as 'one extra treatment': no pasteurisation, rough filtration, bubbles, ageing. Both pieces of information can therefore appear on one label, for example a 'junmai nigori nama'."]],"k":[["Gli stili speciali si applicano al futsū-shu e a ogni grado premium","Les styles spéciaux s'appliquent au futsū-shu et à tous les grades premium","Speciality styles apply to futsū-shu and to every premium grade"],["Uno stesso sake può combinare più stili speciali","Un même saké peut combiner plusieurs styles spéciaux","One sake can combine several speciality styles"],["Grado = come è fatto; stile speciale = trattamento in più","Grade = façon de faire ; style spécial = traitement en plus","Grade = how it is made; speciality = one extra treatment"]]},{"c":"k09","t":["Prepararsi a degustare","Se préparer à déguster","Getting ready to taste"],"p":[["Per ricavare il massimo da un assaggio serve un metodo uguale per ogni campione: così le note di degustazione descrivono il sake con precisione e si possono rileggere anche a distanza di tempo. Prima ancora di versare, conviene preparare l'ambiente: nessun odore che distragga (profumi, cucina, fumo) e una superficie bianca su cui osservare l'aspetto del sake.","Pour tirer le meilleur d'une dégustation, il faut une méthode identique pour chaque échantillon : ainsi, les notes décrivent le saké avec précision et peuvent être relues plus tard. Avant même de servir, on prépare l'environnement : aucune odeur gênante (parfum, cuisine, fumée) et une surface blanche pour observer l'aspect du saké.","To get the most from a tasting you need the same method for every sample: that way your notes describe each sake accurately and are still useful when you reread them later. Before pouring, prepare the setting: no distracting smells (perfume, cooking, smoke) and a white surface for judging the sake's appearance."],["Il bicchiere giusto ha una coppa ampia che si stringe verso l'alto: concentra gli aromi e rende più facile valutare il naso. Infine, il palato deve essere pulito, senza sapori che restano in bocca come il dentifricio o il caffè, che falserebbero tutto.","Le bon verre a un calice large qui se resserre vers le haut : il concentre les arômes et facilite l'analyse du nez. Enfin, la bouche doit être propre, sans goûts persistants comme le dentifrice ou le café, qui fausseraient tout.","The right glass has a wide bowl that narrows towards the top: it concentrates the aromas and makes the nose easier to assess. Finally, your palate should be clean, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee, which would distort everything."]],"k":[["Stesso metodo per ogni campione","Même méthode pour chaque échantillon","Same method for every sample"],["Niente odori che distraggono; superficie bianca","Pas d'odeurs gênantes ; surface blanche","No distracting smells; a white surface"],["Bicchiere a coppa ampia che si stringe in alto","Verre à calice large qui se resserre en haut","Glass with a wide bowl narrowing at the top"],["Palato pulito: niente dentifricio o caffè","Bouche propre : pas de dentifrice ni de café","Clean palate: no toothpaste or coffee"]]},{"c":"k09","t":["Una griglia semplice: aspetto, naso, bocca","Une grille simple : aspect, nez, bouche","A simple grid: appearance, nose, palate"],"p":[["Aspetto: si guarda la limpidezza, da limpido a torbido (un nigori sarà torbido), e si notano eventuali bollicine e il colore. Naso: si cercano le famiglie di aromi (fruttato/floreale, cereali/chicco/frutta a guscio, latticini, altro) e si annotano l'intensità e gli eventuali difetti.","Aspect : on observe la limpidité, de limpide à trouble (un nigori sera trouble), et l'on note les éventuelles bulles et la couleur. Nez : on cherche les familles d'arômes (fruité/floral, céréales/grain/fruits à coque, lacté, autre) et l'on note l'intensité et d'éventuels défauts.","Appearance: check clarity, from clear to cloudy (a nigori will be cloudy), and note any bubbles and the colour. Nose: look for the aroma families (fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other) and note intensity and any faults."],["Bocca: si valuta l'intensità dei sapori (leggera, media, pronunciata) e le stesse famiglie del naso; poi tutto il resto: dolcezza, acidità, consistenza, umami, eventuali particelle di riso, bollicine e persistenza finale. Con questa griglia un ginjō (fruttato, delicato) e un junmai (cerealicolo, più acido e umami) si distinguono subito.","Bouche : on évalue l'intensité des saveurs (légère, moyenne, prononcée) et les mêmes familles qu'au nez ; puis le reste : douceur, acidité, texture, umami, éventuelles particules de riz, bulles et longueur finale. Avec cette grille, un ginjō (fruité, délicat) et un junmai (céréalier, plus acide et umami) se distinguent tout de suite.","Palate: judge flavour intensity (light, medium, pronounced) and the same families as on the nose; then everything else: sweetness, acidity, texture, umami, any rice particles, bubbles and the finish. With this grid a ginjō (fruity, delicate) and a junmai (cereal, more acidity and umami) stand apart at once."]],"k":[["Aspetto: limpido–torbido, bollicine, colore","Aspect : limpide–trouble, bulles, couleur","Appearance: clear–cloudy, bubbles, colour"],["Naso: fruttato/floreale, cereali/frutta a guscio, latticini, altro; intensità, difetti","Nez : fruité/floral, céréales/fruits à coque, lacté, autre ; intensité, défauts","Nose: fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other; intensity, faults"],["Bocca: intensità leggera–media–pronunciata; dolcezza, acidità, consistenza, umami, particelle, bollicine, finale","Bouche : intensité légère–moyenne–prononcée ; douceur, acidité, texture, umami, particules, bulles, finale","Palate: light–medium–pronounced; sweetness, acidity, texture, umami, particles, bubbles, finish"]]},{"c":"k10","t":["Quattro regole per conservare il sake","Quatre règles pour conserver le saké","Four rules for storing sake"],"p":[["Il sake si rovina facilmente con il caldo e la luce forte. Prima regola: tenerlo al fresco, anche per periodi brevi, idealmente in frigorifero; il freddo è fondamentale per i nama e per proteggere gli aromi fruttati dei ginjō. Seconda regola: berlo giovane. Quasi tutti i sake sono pensati per essere bevuti entro circa un anno dalla messa in vendita; dopo, perdono freschezza. I nama la perdono in pochi mesi.","Le saké s'abîme facilement à la chaleur et à la lumière forte. Première règle : le garder au frais, même peu de temps, idéalement au réfrigérateur ; le froid est essentiel pour les nama et pour protéger les arômes fruités des ginjō. Deuxième règle : le boire jeune. Presque tous les sakés sont faits pour être bus dans l'année environ qui suit leur mise en vente ; ensuite, ils perdent leur fraîcheur. Les nama la perdent en quelques mois.","Sake is easily damaged by heat and strong light. Rule one: keep it cool, even for short periods, ideally in the fridge; cold is essential for nama and for protecting the fruity aromas of ginjō. Rule two: drink it young. Most sake is meant to be drunk within about a year of going on sale; after that it loses freshness. Nama loses it within a few months."],["Terza regola: conservare la bottiglia in piedi. Quarta: evitare la luce forte, sia il sole sia l'illuminazione artificiale intensa, che possono creare aromi difettosi. Una bottiglia aperta va richiusa e messa in frigorifero: di solito dura circa due settimane, a volte di più; i ginjō, più delicati, restano freschi per circa una settimana.","Troisième règle : conserver la bouteille debout. Quatrième : éviter la lumière forte, soleil comme éclairage artificiel intense, qui peut créer des arômes défectueux. Une bouteille ouverte se rebouche et se met au réfrigérateur : elle tient en général environ deux semaines, parfois plus ; les ginjō, plus délicats, restent frais environ une semaine.","Rule three: store the bottle upright. Rule four: avoid bright light, both sunshine and strong artificial light, which can cause faulty aromas. An opened bottle should be resealed and kept in the fridge: it usually lasts about two weeks, sometimes longer; the more delicate ginjō styles stay fresh for about a week."]],"k":[["Al fresco, idealmente in frigo (soprattutto nama e ginjō)","Au frais, idéalement au réfrigérateur (surtout nama et ginjō)","Cool, ideally refrigerated (especially nama and ginjō)"],["Bere giovane: entro circa un anno; nama in pochi mesi","Boire jeune : dans l'année environ ; nama en quelques mois","Drink young: within about a year; nama within a few months"],["Bottiglia in piedi, lontano dalla luce forte","Bouteille debout, loin de la lumière forte","Bottle upright, away from bright light"],["Aperta: in frigo, circa 2 settimane; ginjō circa 1","Ouverte : au frais, environ 2 semaines ; ginjō environ 1","Opened: in the fridge, about 2 weeks; ginjō about 1"]]},{"c":"k10","t":["Riconoscere i difetti","Reconnaître les défauts","Recognising faults"],"p":[["I difetti più comuni nascono da una cattiva conservazione. Ossidazione: una bottiglia rimasta aperta troppo a lungo sviluppa aromi sgradevoli di caramello e toffee e prende un colore più scuro. Fuori condizione: una bottiglia troppo vecchia mostra aromi di caramello, toffee e verdure in salamoia, sempre con un colore più scuro. Nama-hine: i nama possono sviluppare odori sgradevoli di malto, carne e verdura marcia.","Les défauts les plus courants viennent d'une mauvaise conservation. Oxydation : une bouteille restée ouverte trop longtemps développe des arômes désagréables de caramel et de caramel au beurre et prend une couleur plus foncée. Hors d'état : une bouteille trop vieille montre des arômes de caramel, de caramel au beurre et de légumes saumurés, avec aussi une couleur plus foncée. Nama-hine : les nama peuvent développer des odeurs déplaisantes de malt, de viande et de légumes pourris.","The most common faults come from poor storage. Oxidation: a bottle left open too long develops unwelcome caramel and toffee aromas and turns deeper in colour. Out of condition: a bottle that is too old shows caramel, toffee and pickled-vegetable aromas, again with a deeper colour. Nama-hine: nama sakes can develop unpleasant smells of malt, meat and rotting vegetables."],["Curiosamente, gli aromi dell'ossidazione e del «fuori condizione» somigliano a quelli del koshu: i processi chimici sono gli stessi. La differenza è l'intenzione: nel koshu sono cercati, negli altri sake i consumatori non li vogliono. Una nota sulla salute: l'alcol, consumato con moderazione, non è considerato dannoso, ma in eccesso fa male a breve e lungo termine; meglio seguire le indicazioni ufficiali di consumo a basso rischio del proprio Paese.","Fait curieux, les arômes de l'oxydation et du « hors d'état » ressemblent à ceux du koshu : les processus chimiques sont les mêmes. La différence tient à l'intention : dans le koshu, ils sont recherchés ; dans les autres sakés, les consommateurs n'en veulent pas. Un mot sur la santé : consommé avec modération, l'alcool n'est pas considéré comme nocif, mais en excès il nuit à court et à long terme ; mieux vaut suivre les repères officiels de consommation à faible risque de son pays.","Interestingly, the aromas of oxidation and 'out of condition' resemble those of koshu: the chemical processes are the same. The difference is intention: in koshu they are wanted, in other sakes consumers do not want them. A word on health: in moderation alcohol is not regarded as harmful, but in excess it damages health in the short and long term; it is best to follow your country's official low-risk drinking guidelines."]],"k":[["Ossidazione (aperto troppo a lungo): caramello, toffee, colore più scuro","Oxydation (ouvert trop longtemps) : caramel, caramel au beurre, couleur plus foncée","Oxidation (open too long): caramel, toffee, deeper colour"],["Fuori condizione (troppo vecchio): caramello, toffee, verdure in salamoia, più scuro","Hors d'état (trop vieux) : caramel, caramel au beurre, légumes saumurés, plus foncé","Out of condition (too old): caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables, deeper colour"],["Nama-hine (nama): malto, carne, verdura marcia","Nama-hine (nama) : malt, viande, légumes pourris","Nama-hine (nama): malt, meat, rotting vegetables"],["Aromi simili al koshu, ma indesiderati negli altri sake","Arômes proches du koshu, mais indésirables dans les autres sakés","Aromas like koshu's, but unwanted in other sakes"]]},{"c":"k11","t":["Freddo, ambiente o caldo?","Frais, ambiant ou chaud ?","Chilled, room temperature or warm?"],"p":[["Il sake si può servire a molte temperature, ma non tutti gli stili sopportano il caldo. Tre fasce da ricordare: fresco 6–13 °C, ambiente 15–18 °C, caldo 40–50 °C. Scaldare un sake lo fa sembrare più intenso, più ricco di consistenza e più acido, cosa che può aiutare con il cibo. Gli stili ginjō però perdono aromi e sapori con il calore: vanno serviti freschi.","Le saké se sert à de nombreuses températures, mais tous les styles ne supportent pas la chaleur. Trois plages à retenir : frais 6–13 °C, ambiant 15–18 °C, chaud 40–50 °C. Chauffer un saké le rend plus intense, plus riche en texture et plus acide, ce qui peut aider avec les plats. Les styles ginjō, eux, perdent arômes et saveurs à la chaleur : on les sert frais.","Sake can be served at many temperatures, but not every style takes heat well. Three ranges to remember: chilled 6–13 °C (43–55 °F), room temperature 15–18 °C (59–64 °F), warm/hot 40–50 °C (104–122 °F). Warming makes a sake seem more intense, richer in texture and higher in acidity, which can help with food. Ginjō styles, however, lose their aromas and flavours when heated: serve them chilled."],["Riassunto per stile: futsū-shu, junmai e honjōzō vanno bene a tutte e tre le temperature. Ginjō: fresco; ambiente a piacere; caldo no. Sparkling: solo fresco. Koshu e nigori: in genere meglio freschi, ma alcuni si possono servire caldi. Per servire fresco basta il frigorifero: si versa dalla bottiglia refrigerata oppure si travasa in un tokkuri, alcuni dei quali hanno uno scomparto per l'acqua ghiacciata.","Résumé par style : futsū-shu, junmai et honjōzō conviennent aux trois températures. Ginjō : frais ; ambiant selon les goûts ; chaud non. Pétillant : frais uniquement. Koshu et nigori : en général meilleurs frais, mais certains se servent chauds. Pour servir frais, le réfrigérateur suffit : on verse depuis la bouteille réfrigérée ou l'on transvase dans un tokkuri, dont certains ont un compartiment pour l'eau glacée.","Summary by style: futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō suit all three temperatures. Ginjō: chilled; room temperature is personal preference; not warm. Sparkling: chilled only. Koshu and nigori: generally best chilled, but some can be served warm. To serve chilled, the fridge is enough: pour from the refrigerated bottle or decant into a tokkuri, some of which have a compartment for iced water."]],"k":[["Fresco 6–13 °C · ambiente 15–18 °C · caldo 40–50 °C","Frais 6–13 °C · ambiant 15–18 °C · chaud 40–50 °C","Chilled 6–13 °C · room 15–18 °C · warm 40–50 °C"],["Il caldo rende più intenso, più ricco e più acido","La chaleur rend plus intense, plus riche et plus acide","Warmth makes it seem more intense, richer and more acidic"],["Futsū-shu, junmai, honjōzō: tutte e tre","Futsū-shu, junmai, honjōzō : les trois","Futsū-shu, junmai, honjōzō: all three"],["Ginjō: fresco, mai caldo · sparkling: solo fresco · koshu e nigori: di solito freschi","Ginjō : frais, jamais chaud · pétillant : frais seulement · koshu et nigori : plutôt frais","Ginjō: chilled, never warm · sparkling: chilled only · koshu, nigori: usually chilled"]]},{"c":"k11","t":["Scaldare il sake a bagnomaria o al microonde","Chauffer le saké au bain-marie ou au micro-ondes","Warming sake: water bath or microwave"],"p":[["Bagnomaria: si mette il tokkuri in un recipiente pieno d'acqua scaldata a circa 80 °C. Per un tokkuri piccolo servono da due a quattro minuti, e la temperatura va sempre controllata con un termometro, per restare nella fascia giusta di 40–50 °C.","Bain-marie : on place le tokkuri dans un récipient rempli d'eau chauffée à environ 80 °C. Pour un petit tokkuri, il faut de deux à quatre minutes, et l'on vérifie toujours la température au thermomètre pour rester dans la bonne plage de 40–50 °C.","Water bath: stand the tokkuri in a container of water heated to about 80 °C (176 °F). A small tokkuri takes two to four minutes, and the temperature should always be checked with a thermometer to stay in the right 40–50 °C range."],["Microonde: si usa un contenitore adatto al microonde. Per scaldare 180 mL di sake bastano circa 20–40 secondi, a seconda dell'apparecchio e di quanto si vuole scaldare. Siccome l'acqua si scalda quasi alla stessa velocità del sake, ci si può esercitare prima scaldando dell'acqua.","Micro-ondes : on utilise un récipient adapté. Pour chauffer 180 mL de saké, il faut environ 20 à 40 secondes, selon l'appareil et l'écart de température voulu. Comme l'eau chauffe presque à la même vitesse que le saké, on peut s'entraîner d'abord avec de l'eau.","Microwave: use a microwave-safe container. Warming 180 mL of sake takes about 20–40 seconds, depending on the microwave and how much warmer you want it. Because water heats at almost the same rate as sake, you can practise with water first."]],"k":[["Bagnomaria: acqua a circa 80 °C, 2–4 minuti per un tokkuri piccolo","Bain-marie : eau à environ 80 °C, 2–4 minutes pour un petit tokkuri","Water bath: water at about 80 °C, 2–4 minutes for a small tokkuri"],["Controllare sempre con il termometro","Toujours vérifier au thermomètre","Always check with a thermometer"],["Microonde: 20–40 secondi per 180 mL, contenitore adatto","Micro-ondes : 20–40 secondes pour 180 mL, récipient adapté","Microwave: 20–40 seconds for 180 mL, microwave-safe container"],["Esercitarsi prima con l'acqua","S'entraîner d'abord avec de l'eau","Practise with water first"]]},{"c":"k11","t":["Tokkuri, o-choko, masu e bicchieri da vino","Tokkuri, o-choko, masu et verres à vin","Tokkuri, o-choko, masu and wine glasses"],"p":[["Il sake si serve in vari recipienti giapponesi tradizionali, ma anche nei bicchieri da vino. Il tokkuri è la caraffa da sake, usata per scaldarlo e servirlo: ne esistono di molte forme e materiali, i più comuni contengono 150–300 mL e sono di ceramica. L'o-choko è la tazzina tradizionale: di solito piccola, di ceramica o vetro, con fondo piatto. Essendo piccola va riempita spesso, secondo una tradizione di ospitalità giapponese.","Le saké se sert dans divers récipients japonais traditionnels, mais aussi dans des verres à vin. Le tokkuri est la carafe à saké, utilisée pour le chauffer et le servir : il en existe de nombreuses formes et matières, les plus courants contiennent 150 à 300 mL et sont en céramique. L'o-choko est la petite coupe traditionnelle : en général petite, en céramique ou en verre, à fond plat. Étant petite, on la remplit souvent, selon une tradition d'hospitalité japonaise.","Sake can be served in various traditional Japanese vessels as well as wine glasses. The tokkuri is the sake carafe, used for heating and serving: it comes in many shapes and materials, and the most common hold about 150–300 mL and are made of pottery. The o-choko is the traditional cup: usually small, pottery or glass, with a flat base. Being small, it needs frequent refilling, reflecting a tradition of Japanese hospitality."],["Il masu è una scatoletta di legno di cedro. Non è un recipiente ideale, perché il legno dà sapore al sake; un tempo serviva a misurare il riso, oggi si usa a volte nelle cerimonie. I bicchieri da vino sono invece ideali per il sake premium servito fresco o a temperatura ambiente: meglio se piccoli, così il sake resta alla temperatura giusta mentre si beve, e a tulipano, per esaltare gli aromi.","Le masu est une petite boîte en bois de cèdre. Ce n'est pas un récipient idéal, car le bois donne du goût au saké ; il servait autrefois à mesurer le riz et s'utilise parfois lors de cérémonies. Les verres à vin sont en revanche idéaux pour le saké premium servi frais ou à température ambiante : de préférence petits, pour que le saké reste à la bonne température pendant qu'on le boit, et en forme de tulipe, pour mettre en valeur les arômes.","The masu is a small box made of cedar. It is not an ideal vessel, because the wood adds flavour to the sake; historically it was used to measure rice, and today it appears occasionally at ceremonies. Wine glasses, on the other hand, are ideal for premium sake served chilled or at room temperature: preferably small, so the sake stays at the right temperature while you drink it, and tulip-shaped to enhance the aromas."]],"k":[["Tokkuri: caraffa per scaldare e servire, di solito 150–300 mL, in ceramica","Tokkuri : carafe pour chauffer et servir, souvent 150–300 mL, en céramique","Tokkuri: carafe for heating and serving, usually 150–300 mL, pottery"],["O-choko: tazzina piccola a fondo piatto; si riempie spesso (ospitalità)","O-choko : petite coupe à fond plat ; on la remplit souvent (hospitalité)","O-choko: small flat-based cup; refilled often (hospitality)"],["Masu: scatola di cedro, non ideale (il legno dà sapore); usi cerimoniali","Masu : boîte en cèdre, pas idéale (le bois donne du goût) ; usages cérémoniels","Masu: cedar box, not ideal (wood adds flavour); ceremonial use"],["Bicchieri da vino piccoli a tulipano: ideali per il premium fresco o ambiente","Petits verres à vin tulipe : idéaux pour le premium frais ou ambiant","Small tulip wine glasses: ideal for premium chilled or room temperature"]]},{"c":"k12","t":["Come il cibo cambia il sake","Comment les plats changent le saké","How food changes sake"],"p":[["Quando cibo e bevanda si incontrano in bocca, si influenzano a vicenda: è un'interazione di gusto. Un esempio estremo è il succo d'arancia bevuto subito dopo aver lavato i denti: diventa amaro e acido. Di solito le interazioni sono molto più leggere, ma esistono, e in genere è il cibo a cambiare la bevanda più di quanto la bevanda cambi il cibo.","Quand un plat et une boisson se rencontrent en bouche, ils s'influencent mutuellement : c'est une interaction de goût. Un exemple extrême : le jus d'orange bu juste après s'être brossé les dents devient amer et acide. Les interactions sont en général bien plus légères, mais elles existent, et c'est souvent le plat qui modifie la boisson plus que l'inverse.","When food and drink meet in the mouth, each changes how the other tastes: this is a taste interaction. An extreme example is orange juice straight after brushing your teeth: it tastes bitter and sour. Usually the interactions are much milder, but they do happen, and in general food affects a drink more than a drink affects food."],["Interazioni positive: sale e acidità nel cibo rendono la bevanda meno astringente, meno amara e meno acida, e la fanno sembrare più dolce e più fruttata. Interazioni negative: l'umami nel cibo rende la bevanda più astringente, amara e acida, meno dolce e meno fruttata; il sale può però annullare questo effetto. Zucchero e piccante agiscono in modo simile all'umami, e il piccante aumenta anche il bruciore dell'alcol. L'amaro nel cibo rende la bevanda più amara.","Interactions positives : le sel et l'acidité du plat rendent la boisson moins asséchante, moins amère et moins acide, et la font paraître plus douce et plus fruitée. Interactions négatives : l'umami du plat rend la boisson plus asséchante, plus amère et plus acide, moins douce et moins fruitée ; le sel peut toutefois annuler cet effet. Le sucre et le piquant agissent comme l'umami, et le piquant augmente en plus la brûlure de l'alcool. L'amertume du plat rend la boisson plus amère.","Positive interactions: salt and acidity in food make a drink seem less drying, less bitter and less acidic, and also sweeter and fruitier. Negative interactions: umami in food makes a drink seem more drying, bitter and acidic, less sweet and less fruity; salt in the food can cancel this out. Sugar and chilli heat act much like umami, and chilli also increases the burn of the alcohol. Bitterness in food makes a drink taste more bitter."]],"k":[["Il cibo cambia la bevanda più del contrario","Le plat change la boisson plus que l'inverse","Food affects a drink more than the reverse"],["Sale e acidità: bevanda meno amara e acida, più dolce e fruttata","Sel et acidité : boisson moins amère et acide, plus douce et fruitée","Salt and acid: drink less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier"],["Umami, zucchero, piccante: più amara e acida, meno dolce e fruttata; il sale aiuta contro l'umami","Umami, sucre, piquant : plus amère et acide, moins douce et fruitée ; le sel aide contre l'umami","Umami, sugar, chilli: more bitter and acidic, less sweet and fruity; salt offsets umami"],["Piccante: più bruciore d'alcol; amaro nel cibo: bevanda più amara","Piquant : plus de brûlure d'alcool ; amertume du plat : boisson plus amère","Chilli: more alcohol burn; bitter food: more bitter drink"]]},{"c":"k12","t":["Tre consigli per abbinare il sake","Trois conseils pour accorder le saké","Three tips for pairing sake"],"p":[["Il sake non si abbina solo alla cucina giapponese: si può gustare con la maggior parte dei piatti internazionali. Di solito non ha interazioni negative forti con il cibo; quando ci sono, sono legate soprattutto all'umami e allo zucchero dei piatti. Per questo bastano pochi punti chiave.","Le saké ne s'accorde pas qu'avec la cuisine japonaise : il accompagne la plupart des plats internationaux. Il n'a généralement pas d'interactions négatives fortes avec les mets ; quand il y en a, elles viennent surtout de l'umami et du sucre des plats. Quelques repères suffisent donc.","Sake does not only go with Japanese food: it can be enjoyed with most international dishes. It does not usually have strong negative interactions with food; when they happen, they are mostly linked to umami and sugar in the dish. So only a few key points are needed."],["Primo: quasi tutti i sake stanno bene con quasi tutti i cibi, quindi il gusto personale è sempre la cosa più importante. Secondo: cibo e sake dovrebbero avere un'intensità di sapore simile, perché uno non copra l'altro: un sashimi delicato con un ginjō leggero, uno stufato saporito con un junmai più pieno. Terzo: i piatti dolci vanno con un sake almeno altrettanto dolce, altrimenti il sake sembrerà magro e acido.","Premièrement : presque tous les sakés vont avec presque tous les plats, donc le goût personnel est toujours le critère le plus important. Deuxièmement : plat et saké doivent avoir une intensité de saveur proche, pour que l'un n'écrase pas l'autre : un sashimi délicat avec un ginjō léger, un ragoût savoureux avec un junmai plus ample. Troisièmement : les plats sucrés demandent un saké au moins aussi sucré, sinon le saké paraîtra maigre et acide.","First: most sakes go with most foods, so personal preference is always the most important thing. Second: food and sake should have a similar flavour intensity so that neither overwhelms the other: delicate sashimi with a light ginjō, a rich stew with a fuller junmai. Third: sweet dishes need a sake that is at least as sweet, or the sake will taste thin and sour."]],"k":[["Il sake va bene anche con la cucina internazionale","Le saké va aussi avec la cuisine internationale","Sake suits international food too"],["Il gusto personale conta più di tutto","Le goût personnel compte avant tout","Personal preference comes first"],["Stessa intensità di sapore tra piatto e sake","Même intensité de saveur entre plat et saké","Match flavour intensity"],["Piatto dolce → sake almeno altrettanto dolce","Plat sucré → saké au moins aussi sucré","Sweet dish → sake at least as sweet"]]}],"flash":[{"c":"k01","f":["Nihon-shu","Nihon-shu","Nihon-shu"],"b":["Nome ufficiale del sake: «bevanda alcolica del Giappone».","Nom officiel du saké : « boisson alcoolisée du Japon ».","Official name for sake: 'Japanese alcoholic drink'."]},{"c":"k01","f":["Sake tipico: grado alcolico","Saké typique : degré d'alcool","Typical sake: alcohol level"],"b":["15–17% vol.","15–17 % vol.","15–17% abv"]},{"c":"k01","f":["Profilo del sake tipico","Profil du saké typique","Typical sake profile"],"b":["Limpido, incolore, leggermente dolce, poco acido; aromi di cereali, latticini o frutta.","Limpide, incolore, légèrement sucré, peu acide ; arômes de céréales, laitiers ou fruités.","Clear, colourless, slightly sweet, lightly acidic; cereal, lactic or fruity notes."]},{"c":"k01","f":["I quattro ingredienti principali","Les quatre ingrédients principaux","The four main ingredients"],"b":["Riso bianco cotto a vapore, kōji, acqua, lievito.","Riz blanc cuit à la vapeur, kōji, eau, levure.","Steamed white rice, kōji, water, yeast."]},{"c":"k01","f":["Ingrediente facoltativo","Ingrédient facultatif","Optional ingredient"],"b":["Alcol distillato ad alta gradazione, dal gusto neutro.","Alcool distillé à haut degré, au goût neutre.","High-strength distilled alcohol with a neutral flavour."]},{"c":"k01","f":["Kōji","Kōji","Kōji"],"b":["Riso cotto a vapore con una muffa speciale che produce enzimi.","Riz cuit à la vapeur couvert d'une moisissure spéciale qui produit des enzymes.","Steamed rice grown with a special mould that makes enzymes."]},{"c":"k01","f":["Conversione dell'amido","Conversion de l'amidon","Starch conversion"],"b":["Gli enzimi spezzano l'amido in zuccheri che il lievito può mangiare.","Les enzymes découpent l'amidon en sucres que la levure peut consommer.","Enzymes break starch into sugars yeast can eat."]},{"c":"k01","f":["Fermentazione alcolica","Fermentation alcoolique","Alcoholic fermentation"],"b":["Zucchero + lievito → alcol + anidride carbonica.","Sucre + levure → alcool + dioxyde de carbone.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Tappe sempre presenti","Étapes toujours présentes","Steps that always happen"],"b":["Fermentazione, filtrazione, imbottigliamento.","Fermentation, filtration, mise en bouteille.","Fermentation, filtration, bottling."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Tappe facoltative","Étapes facultatives","Optional steps"],"b":["Aggiunta di alcol, aggiunta di acqua, pastorizzazione.","Ajout d'alcool, ajout d'eau, pasteurisation.","Adding alcohol, adding water, pasteurisation."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Fermentazione parallela","Fermentation parallèle","Parallel fermentation"],"b":["Zucchero prodotto dagli enzimi e mangiato dal lievito allo stesso tempo; unica del sake.","Sucre produit par les enzymes et consommé par la levure en même temps ; propre au saké.","Enzymes make sugar while yeast eats it, at the same time; unique to sake."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Alcol a fine fermentazione","Alcool en fin de fermentation","Alcohol at end of fermentation"],"b":["Circa 20% vol.","Environ 20 % vol.","About 20% abv."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Perché si aggiunge alcol neutro?","Pourquoi ajouter de l'alcool neutre ?","Why add neutral alcohol?"],"b":["Prima della filtrazione, per estrarre aromi dai solidi di riso.","Avant la filtration, pour extraire les arômes des solides de riz.","Before filtration, to extract flavours from the rice solids."]},{"c":"k02","f":["Pastorizzazione","Pasteurisation","Pasteurisation"],"b":["Trattamento con il calore della maggior parte dei sake: evita aromi difettosi.","Traitement thermique de la plupart des sakés : évite les arômes défectueux.","Heat treatment of most sake: prevents faulty aromas."]},{"c":"k03","f":["Dal riso integrale al riso cotto","Du riz brun au riz cuit","Brown rice to steamed rice"],"b":["Levigatura → lavaggio → ammollo → cottura a vapore.","Polissage → lavage → trempage → cuisson à la vapeur.","Polishing → washing → soaking → steaming."]},{"c":"k03","f":["Le tre zone del chicco","Les trois zones du grain","The three zones of a grain"],"b":["Esterni marroni, intermedi bianchi, nucleo quasi solo amido.","Extérieures brunes, intermédiaires blanches, cœur presque pur amidon.","Brown outer, white middle, almost pure starch core."]},{"c":"k03","f":["Levigatura leggera dà…","Un polissage léger donne…","Light polishing gives…"],"b":["Più acidità e umami, aromi di cereali e latticini.","Plus d'acidité et d'umami, arômes de céréales et lactés.","More acidity and umami, cereal and lactic aromas."]},{"c":"k03","f":["Levigatura spinta dà…","Un polissage poussé donne…","Heavy polishing gives…"],"b":["Meno acidità e umami, aromi fruttati e floreali.","Moins d'acidité et d'umami, arômes fruités et floraux.","Less acidity and umami, fruity and floral aromas."]},{"c":"k03","f":["Grado di levigatura","Taux de polissage","Polishing ratio"],"b":["Percentuale del chicco che RESTA dopo la levigatura; fissata dalla legge.","Pourcentage du grain qui RESTE après polissage ; fixé par la loi.","Percentage of the grain that REMAINS after polishing; set by law."]},{"c":"k03","f":["70% o meno","70 % ou moins","70% or less"],"b":["Honjōzō e la maggior parte dei junmai.","Honjōzō et la plupart des junmai.","Honjōzō and most junmai."]},{"c":"k03","f":["60% o meno","60 % ou moins","60% or less"],"b":["Ginjō e junmai ginjō.","Ginjō et junmai ginjō.","Ginjō and junmai ginjō."]},{"c":"k03","f":["50% o meno","50 % ou moins","50% or less"],"b":["Daiginjō e junmai daiginjō.","Daiginjō et junmai daiginjō.","Daiginjō and junmai daiginjō."]},{"c":"k04","f":["Le quattro fasi del kōji","Les quatre étapes du kōji","The four kōji stages"],"b":["Raffreddare, spargere le spore, prima crescita, controllo e arresto.","Refroidir, répandre les spores, première croissance, contrôle et arrêt.","Cool, spread spores, initial growth, control and stop."]},{"c":"k04","f":["Dove parte la muffa?","Où démarre la moisissure ?","Where does the mould start?"],"b":["Nella zona più calda e umida della stanza del kōji.","Dans la zone la plus chaude et humide de la salle du kōji.","In the warmest, most humid part of the kōji room."]},{"c":"k04","f":["Come si ferma la muffa?","Comment arrête-t-on la moisissure ?","How is the mould stopped?"],"b":["Portando il riso nella zona più fresca della stanza.","En portant le riz dans la zone la plus fraîche de la salle.","By moving the rice to the coolest part of the room."]},{"c":"k05","f":["Aromi ginjō: come si ottengono?","Arômes ginjō : comment les obtenir ?","Ginjō aromas: how?"],"b":["Lieviti speciali + fermentazione a temperatura bassa.","Levures spéciales + fermentation à basse température.","Special yeast strains + cool fermentation."]},{"c":"k05","f":["Fermentazione più calda","Fermentation plus chaude","Warmer fermentation"],"b":["Aromi di cereali e latticini.","Arômes de céréales et lactés.","Cereal and lactic aromas."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu","Futsū-shu"],"b":["Sake di base: 15–17%, leggermente dolce, poco acido, note lattiche e fruttate.","Saké de base : 15–17 %, légèrement sucré, peu acide, notes lactées et fruitées.","Basic sake: 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, lactic and fruity notes."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Ginjō","Ginjō","Ginjō"],"b":["Parola chiave dello stile con aromi puri di fiori e frutta.","Mot clé du style aux arômes purs de fleurs et de fruits.","Key word for the style with pure floral, fruity aromas."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Daiginjō","Daiginjō","Daiginjō"],"b":["«Grande ginjō»: aromi fruttati e floreali più puri; riso ≤50%; alcol aggiunto.","« Grand ginjō » : arômes fruités et floraux les plus purs ; riz ≤50 % ; alcool ajouté.","'Big ginjō': purest fruity, floral aromas; rice ≤50%; alcohol added."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Junmai","Junmai","Junmai"],"b":["«Riso puro»: nessun alcol distillato aggiunto prima della filtrazione.","« Riz pur » : aucun alcool distillé ajouté avant la filtration.","'Pure rice': no distilled alcohol added before filtration."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Honjōzō","Honjōzō","Honjōzō"],"b":["Riso ≤70%, alcol aggiunto; cereali e latticini, più acidità e umami.","Riz ≤70 %, alcool ajouté ; céréales et notes lactées, plus d'acidité et d'umami.","Rice ≤70%, alcohol added; cereal and lactic, more acidity and umami."]},{"c":"k06","f":["Ginjō vs junmai ginjō","Ginjō vs junmai ginjō","Ginjō vs junmai ginjō"],"b":["Stesso stile e stessa levigatura (≤60%); il junmai ginjō non ha alcol aggiunto.","Même style et même polissage (≤60 %) ; le junmai ginjō n'a pas d'alcool ajouté.","Same style and polishing (≤60%); junmai ginjō has no added alcohol."]},{"c":"k07","f":["純米","純米","純米"],"b":["Junmai (jun + mai).","Junmai (jun + mai).","Junmai (jun + mai)."]},{"c":"k07","f":["本醸造","本醸造","本醸造"],"b":["Honjōzō (hon + jō + zō).","Honjōzō (hon + jō + zō).","Honjōzō (hon + jō + zō)."]},{"c":"k07","f":["吟醸","吟醸","吟醸"],"b":["Ginjō (gin + jō).","Ginjō (gin + jō).","Ginjō (gin + jō)."]},{"c":"k07","f":["大吟醸","大吟醸","大吟醸"],"b":["Daiginjō (dai + gin + jō); 大 = grande.","Daiginjō (dai + gin + jō) ; 大 = grand.","Daiginjō (dai + gin + jō); 大 = big."]},{"c":"k08","f":["Nama / nama-zake","Nama / nama-zake","Nama / nama-zake"],"b":["Non pastorizzato: sempre in frigo, da bere presto; vivace, poi speziato e maltato.","Non pasteurisé : toujours au frais, à boire vite ; vif, puis épicé et malté.","Unpasteurised: always chilled, drink soon; lively, later spicy and malty."]},{"c":"k08","f":["Nigori","Nigori","Nigori"],"b":["Filtrato in modo grossolano: torbido per le particelle di riso.","Filtré grossièrement : trouble à cause des particules de riz.","Roughly filtered: cloudy from suspended rice particles."]},{"c":"k08","f":["Sake frizzante","Saké pétillant","Sparkling sake"],"b":["Bollicine di anidride carbonica disciolta; da leggero a ricco, a volte nigori.","Bulles de dioxyde de carbone dissous ; de léger à riche, parfois nigori.","Bubbles of dissolved CO2; light to rich, sometimes nigori."]},{"c":"k08","f":["Koshu","Koshu","Koshu"],"b":["Sake invecchiato: spesso ambrato, dolce, frutta secca, noci; il rovere è raro.","Saké vieilli : souvent ambré, sucré, fruits secs, noix ; le chêne est rare.","Aged sake: often amber, sweet, dried fruit, nuts; oak is rare."]},{"c":"k09","f":["Preparare una degustazione","Préparer une dégustation","Preparing a tasting"],"b":["Niente odori, superficie bianca, bicchiere che si stringe in alto, palato pulito.","Pas d'odeurs, surface blanche, verre qui se resserre, bouche propre.","No smells, white surface, glass narrowing at top, clean palate."]},{"c":"k09","f":["Famiglie di aromi del sake","Familles d'arômes du saké","Sake aroma families"],"b":["Fruttato/floreale, cereali/frutta a guscio, latticini, altro.","Fruité/floral, céréales/fruits à coque, lacté, autre.","Fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other."]},{"c":"k10","f":["Conservare il sake","Conserver le saké","Storing sake"],"b":["Fresco, giovane (circa 1 anno), in piedi, lontano dalla luce forte.","Frais, jeune (environ 1 an), debout, loin de la lumière forte.","Cool, young (about 1 year), upright, away from bright light."]},{"c":"k10","f":["Bottiglia aperta","Bouteille ouverte","Opened bottle"],"b":["Richiusa in frigo: circa 2 settimane; ginjō circa 1.","Rebouchée au frais : environ 2 semaines ; ginjō environ 1.","Resealed in the fridge: about 2 weeks; ginjō about 1."]},{"c":"k10","f":["Ossidazione","Oxydation","Oxidation"],"b":["Aperto troppo a lungo: caramello, toffee, colore più scuro.","Ouvert trop longtemps : caramel, caramel au beurre, plus foncé.","Open too long: caramel, toffee, deeper colour."]},{"c":"k10","f":["Fuori condizione","Hors d'état","Out of condition"],"b":["Troppo vecchio: caramello, toffee, verdure in salamoia, più scuro.","Trop vieux : caramel, caramel au beurre, légumes saumurés, plus foncé.","Too old: caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables, deeper colour."]},{"c":"k10","f":["Nama-hine","Nama-hine","Nama-hine"],"b":["Difetto dei nama: malto, carne, verdura marcia.","Défaut des nama : malt, viande, légumes pourris.","Fault in nama: malt, meat, rotting vegetables."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Tre temperature di servizio","Trois températures de service","Three serving temperatures"],"b":["Fresco 6–13 °C · ambiente 15–18 °C · caldo 40–50 °C.","Frais 6–13 °C · ambiant 15–18 °C · chaud 40–50 °C.","Chilled 6–13 °C · room 15–18 °C · warm 40–50 °C."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Ginjō: a che temperatura?","Ginjō : à quelle température ?","Ginjō: what temperature?"],"b":["Fresco; ambiente a piacere; mai caldo.","Frais ; ambiant selon les goûts ; jamais chaud.","Chilled; room temperature by preference; never warm."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Bagnomaria","Bain-marie","Water bath"],"b":["Acqua a circa 80 °C, 2–4 minuti per un tokkuri piccolo; usare il termometro.","Eau à environ 80 °C, 2–4 minutes pour un petit tokkuri ; thermomètre.","Water about 80 °C, 2–4 min for a small tokkuri; use a thermometer."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Microonde","Micro-ondes","Microwave"],"b":["20–40 secondi per 180 mL, in un contenitore adatto.","20–40 secondes pour 180 mL, dans un récipient adapté.","20–40 seconds for 180 mL, in a suitable container."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Tokkuri","Tokkuri","Tokkuri"],"b":["Caraffa per scaldare e servire; di solito 150–300 mL, in ceramica.","Carafe pour chauffer et servir ; souvent 150–300 mL, en céramique.","Carafe for heating and serving; usually 150–300 mL, pottery."]},{"c":"k11","f":["O-choko","O-choko","O-choko"],"b":["Tazzina tradizionale, piccola, a fondo piatto; si riempie spesso.","Petite coupe traditionnelle à fond plat ; on la remplit souvent.","Small traditional flat-based cup; refilled often."]},{"c":"k11","f":["Masu","Masu","Masu"],"b":["Scatoletta di cedro: il legno dà sapore, non ideale; usi cerimoniali.","Petite boîte en cèdre : le bois donne du goût, pas idéale ; cérémonies.","Cedar box: wood adds flavour, not ideal; ceremonial use."]},{"c":"k12","f":["Sale e acidità nel cibo","Sel et acidité dans le plat","Salt and acid in food"],"b":["Bevanda meno amara e acida, più dolce e fruttata.","Boisson moins amère et acide, plus douce et fruitée.","Drink less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier."]},{"c":"k12","f":["Umami nel cibo","Umami dans le plat","Umami in food"],"b":["Bevanda più amara, astringente e acida, meno dolce e fruttata.","Boisson plus amère, asséchante et acide, moins douce et fruitée.","Drink more bitter, drying and acidic, less sweet and fruity."]},{"c":"k12","f":["Tre regole di abbinamento","Trois règles d'accord","Three pairing rules"],"b":["Gusto personale; intensità simile; piatto dolce → sake almeno altrettanto dolce.","Goût personnel ; intensité proche ; plat sucré → saké au moins aussi doux.","Personal preference; similar intensity; sweet dish → sake at least as sweet."]}],"ui":{"tab_study":["Sake 1","Saké 1","Sake 1"],"l2Title":["Esame Sake 1","Examen Saké 1","Sake 1 exam"],"l2Intro":["Lezioni, quiz e flashcard su riso, kōji, categorie di sake e servizio.","Leçons, quiz et flashcards sur le riz, le kōji, les catégories de saké et le service.","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on rice, kōji, sake grades and service."],"l2FlD":["Ripassa termini giapponesi, categorie e stili","Révisez termes japonais, catégories et styles","Review Japanese terms, grades and styles"],"l2RevT":["Tutto Sake 1","Tout Saké 1","All of Sake 1"],"l2RevI":["Lezioni, flashcard ed errori: solo il programma di Sake 1.","Leçons, flashcards et erreurs : uniquement le programme Saké 1.","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Sake 1 syllabus."],"l2PlayT":["Giochi di Sake 1","Jeux Saké 1","Sake 1 games"],"l2PlayI":["Giochi brevi sulle domande e sui termini di Sake 1.","Des jeux courts sur les questions et les termes de Saké 1.","Short games on Sake 1 questions and terms."],"obHi":["Ciao! Sono la tua capra del sake 🍶","Bonjour ! Je suis votre chèvre du saké 🍶","Hi! I'm your sake goat 🍶"],"obHiP":["Ti preparo un percorso su misura per passare l'esame Sake 1. Bastano 5 domande veloci.","Je vous prépare un parcours sur mesure pour réussir l'examen Saké 1. Il suffit de 5 questions rapides.","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Sake 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions."]}};
window.TWG_ESX=Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX||{es:{},ar:{}},{});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.es,{"A glass of rice":"Un vaso de arroz","Sake is a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice. In Japan one of its official names is nihon-shu, which simply means 'the alcoholic drink of Japan': the name alone tells you how closely sake is tied to its homeland. First-time tasters often expect something fiery, like a spirit, and discover instead a soft, fresh and delicate drink.":"El sake es una bebida alcohólica japonesa elaborada con arroz. En Japón uno de sus nombres oficiales es nihon-shu, es decir, «la bebida alcohólica de Japón»: el propio nombre muestra lo unido que está el sake a su país. Quien lo prueba por primera vez suele esperar algo fuerte, como un destilado, y descubre en cambio una bebida suave, fresca y delicada.","Most sakes are clear and colourless; a few show a faint pale yellow or green tint. A typical sake has 15–17% abv, a little more than most wines. On the palate it is usually slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with gentle flavours that recall cereal, dairy (think yoghurt or cream) or fruit.":"La mayoría de los sakes son transparentes e incoloros; algunos tienen un ligero tono amarillo pálido o verdoso. Su graduación típica va del 15 al 17 %, algo más que un vino. En boca suele ser ligeramente dulce y poco ácido, con sabores suaves que recuerdan a cereales, lácteos (como yogur o nata) o fruta.","Beware a common mix-up: sake is not a spirit. It is made by fermentation, like wine and beer. Keeping the 'typical' profile in mind (clear, 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, delicate flavours) makes every later style easier to understand, because many styles are defined by how they differ from this starting point.":"Cuidado con una confusión frecuente: el sake no es un destilado. Se obtiene por fermentación, como el vino y la cerveza. Tener presente el perfil «típico» (transparente, 15–17 %, ligeramente dulce, poco ácido, sabores delicados) ayuda a entender todos los estilos que veremos, porque muchos se definen precisamente por cómo se alejan de este punto de partida.","Sake: a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice; official name nihon-shu":"Sake: bebida alcohólica japonesa a base de arroz; nombre oficial nihon-shu","Usually clear and colourless, sometimes pale yellow or green":"Normalmente transparente e incoloro, a veces amarillo pálido o verdoso","Typically 15–17% abv, slightly sweet, lightly acidic":"Típicamente 15–17 % vol., ligeramente dulce, poco ácido","Delicate cereal, dairy or fruity flavours; fermented, not distilled":"Sabores delicados a cereales, lácteos o fruta; fermentado, no destilado","Four ingredients, plus one optional extra":"Cuatro ingredientes, más uno opcional","Every sake starts from four main ingredients: steamed white rice, kōji, water and yeast. There is also a fifth, optional ingredient: a high-strength distilled alcohol. It will come up again and again, because whether it is used or not matters a great deal in the names of sake categories.":"Todo sake parte de cuatro ingredientes principales: arroz blanco al vapor, kōji, agua y levadura. Existe además un quinto ingrediente, opcional: un alcohol destilado de alta graduación. Aparecerá a menudo, porque usarlo o no cuenta mucho en los nombres de las categorías de sake.","Rice is usually bought from suppliers and reaches the brewery raw, hard and dusty: the brewer steams it so that it softens and can break up in water. Kōji, on the other hand, is made in the brewery: a small part of the steamed rice is taken and a special mould is grown on it. Without kōji there would be no way to make the alcohol found in every sake.":"El arroz suele comprarse a proveedores y llega a la bodega crudo, duro y polvoriento: el elaborador lo cuece al vapor para que se ablande y pueda deshacerse en el agua. El kōji, en cambio, se hace en la propia bodega: se toma una pequeña parte del arroz al vapor y se hace crecer sobre él un moho especial. Sin kōji no se podría producir el alcohol que contiene todo sake.","Water comes from local supplies: almost any water will do, as long as it is clean. Yeasts are tiny microorganisms; breweries use specific varieties, usually bought from specialist suppliers. An easy way to remember it: rice arrives from outside but is prepared in the brewery, kōji is born in the brewery, and yeast is carefully chosen.":"El agua procede de fuentes locales: casi cualquier agua sirve, siempre que esté limpia. Las levaduras son microorganismos diminutos; las bodegas usan variedades concretas, normalmente compradas a proveedores especializados. Una forma sencilla de recordarlo: el arroz llega de fuera pero se prepara en la bodega, el kōji nace en la bodega y la levadura se elige con cuidado.","Four ingredients: steamed white rice, kōji, water, yeast":"Cuatro ingredientes: arroz blanco al vapor, kōji, agua, levadura","Optional: high-strength distilled alcohol":"Opcional: alcohol destilado de alta graduación","Kōji: mould grown on a small part of the steamed rice; essential for any alcohol":"Kōji: moho cultivado sobre una pequeña parte del arroz al vapor; imprescindible para obtener alcohol","Local, clean water; chosen yeasts bought from specialist suppliers":"Agua local y limpia; levaduras elegidas, compradas a proveedores especializados","From starch to sugar, from sugar to alcohol":"Del almidón al azúcar, del azúcar al alcohol","To make alcohol you need sugar dissolved in water. Yeast is added: it eats the sugar, turns it into alcohol and releases carbon dioxide, a gas. This is alcoholic fermentation, the same process behind wine and beer.":"Para hacer alcohol hace falta azúcar disuelto en agua. Se añaden las levaduras: se comen el azúcar, lo transforman en alcohol y liberan dióxido de carbono, un gas. Es la fermentación alcohólica, la misma que da el vino y la cerveza.","The catch is that rice contains no sugar: it is full of starch. Starch is made of sugar molecules bonded together in long chains, and yeast cannot eat it. You need substances called enzymes, which can break those bonds and free the sugars one by one. This step is called starch conversion.":"El problema es que el arroz no contiene azúcar: está lleno de almidón. El almidón está formado por moléculas de azúcar unidas en largas cadenas, y las levaduras no pueden comérselo. Hacen falta unas sustancias llamadas enzimas, capaces de romper esos enlaces y liberar los azúcares uno a uno. Este paso se llama conversión del almidón.","This is why kōji matters so much: the mould growing on the rice produces exactly these enzymes. When steamed rice, kōji and water are mixed, the enzymes turn starch into sugar and the yeast turns the sugar into alcohol. No kōji, no sugar; no sugar, no alcohol.":"Por eso el kōji es tan importante: el moho que crece sobre el arroz produce precisamente esas enzimas. Al mezclar arroz al vapor, kōji y agua, las enzimas convierten el almidón en azúcar y las levaduras convierten el azúcar en alcohol. Sin kōji no hay azúcar; sin azúcar no hay alcohol.","Alcoholic fermentation: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide":"Fermentación alcohólica: azúcar + levadura → alcohol + dióxido de carbono","Rice contains starch, not sugar; yeast cannot eat starch":"El arroz contiene almidón, no azúcar; las levaduras no comen almidón","Starch conversion: enzymes break starch into sugars":"Conversión del almidón: las enzimas rompen el almidón en azúcares","The enzymes come from the kōji mould":"Las enzimas proceden del moho del kōji","Three steps that always happen":"Tres pasos que siempre se dan","Once the steamed rice, kōji, water and yeast are ready, brewing proper can begin. Three steps always happen: fermentation, filtration and bottling. Three more are optional: adding alcohol, adding water and pasteurisation. It pays to learn the two lists separately.":"Cuando el arroz al vapor, el kōji, el agua y la levadura están listos, empieza la elaboración propiamente dicha. Tres pasos se dan siempre: fermentación, filtración y embotellado. Otros tres son opcionales: añadir alcohol, añadir agua y pasteurizar. Conviene aprender las dos listas por separado.","Fermentation starts small: a little of the ingredients is used to make a starter that builds a healthy, active yeast population. The starter is then gradually mixed with more rice, kōji and water to make a larger batch: the main fermentation. While it ferments, the liquid is white and cloudy, coloured by the rice.":"La fermentación empieza a pequeña escala: con poca cantidad de ingredientes se prepara un «iniciador» que crea una población de levaduras sana y activa. Después se mezcla poco a poco con más arroz, kōji y agua hasta formar una partida mayor: la fermentación principal. Mientras fermenta, el líquido es blanco y turbio, teñido por el arroz.","When fermentation is over, the law requires every sake to be filtered: the solid rice residue is removed, usually leaving a clear liquid. Then comes bottling: nearly all sake is packed in glass bottles of various sizes.":"Terminada la fermentación, la ley obliga a filtrar todo sake: se retiran los restos sólidos de arroz y normalmente se obtiene un líquido transparente. Después se embotella: casi todo el sake se envasa en botellas de vidrio de distintos tamaños.","Always: fermentation, filtration, bottling":"Siempre: fermentación, filtración, embotellado","Optional: adding alcohol, adding water, pasteurisation":"Opcionales: añadir alcohol, añadir agua, pasteurizar","Fermentation starter → main fermentation":"Iniciador de fermentación → fermentación principal","Filtration is required by law; nearly all sake goes into glass bottles":"La filtración es obligatoria por ley; casi todo el sake va en vidrio","Parallel fermentation":"La fermentación paralela","Something special happens in sake: while the kōji enzymes are turning starch into sugar, the yeast is already eating that sugar and making alcohol. Both reactions take place at the same time, in the same vessel, from the start to the end of fermentation. This is why it is called 'parallel fermentation', a feature unique to sake brewing.":"En el sake ocurre algo especial: mientras las enzimas del kōji convierten el almidón en azúcar, las levaduras ya se están comiendo ese azúcar y produciendo alcohol. Las dos reacciones suceden a la vez y en el mismo depósito, desde el principio hasta el final de la fermentación. Por eso se habla de «fermentación paralela», un rasgo exclusivo de la elaboración del sake.","Picture a kitchen where one cook slices bread while another eats each slice straight away: there is never much bread piling up on the board. In the same way, sugar is made and used up little by little in the tank. The result is a liquid that usually reaches about 20% abv by the end of fermentation, more than sake normally has in the bottle.":"Imagina una cocina donde un cocinero corta pan y otro se lo come al momento, rebanada a rebanada: nunca se acumula mucho pan en la tabla. Del mismo modo, en el depósito el azúcar se produce y se consume poco a poco. El resultado es un líquido que al final de la fermentación suele tener alrededor del 20 % de alcohol, más de lo que el sake tiene luego en la botella.","Note the contrast with beer, where starch is turned into sugar first and fermented afterwards, in two separate stages. In sake the two overlap: it is exactly this overlap that earns the name parallel fermentation.":"Recuerda la diferencia con la cerveza, donde el almidón se convierte en azúcar primero y se fermenta después, en dos fases separadas. En el sake ambas cosas se solapan: es justamente ese solapamiento lo que recibe el nombre de fermentación paralela.","Parallel fermentation: sugar is made and eaten at the same time":"Fermentación paralela: el azúcar se produce y se consume a la vez","It is unique to sake brewing":"Es exclusiva de la elaboración del sake","At the end of fermentation: about 20% abv":"Al final de la fermentación: alrededor del 20 % vol.","Three optional choices: alcohol, water, heat":"Tres opciones: alcohol, agua, calor","Before filtration the brewer may add a high-strength distilled alcohol with a neutral flavour. Its purpose is not to make the sake stronger: it helps to pull out flavours trapped in the solid rice residue. Sakes made without this addition carry a special word on the label, which we will meet soon: junmai.":"Antes de la filtración el elaborador puede añadir un alcohol destilado de alta graduación y sabor neutro. No sirve para hacer el sake más fuerte: ayuda a extraer los aromas atrapados en los restos sólidos de arroz. Los sakes sin esta adición llevan en la etiqueta una palabra especial que veremos pronto: junmai.","Water is nearly always added before bottling. Fermentation leaves the sake at around 20% abv; water brings it down to the usual 15–17%. That is why bottled sake is a little lower in alcohol than the freshly fermented liquid.":"Casi siempre se añade agua antes de embotellar. La fermentación deja el sake en torno al 20 % de alcohol; el agua lo baja al nivel habitual, entre el 15 y el 17 %. Por eso el sake embotellado tiene algo menos de alcohol que el líquido recién fermentado.","Finally, the vast majority of sake is heat-treated before it goes on sale: this is pasteurisation. It prevents faulty aromas from developing and makes the sake more stable. Sakes that skip this step form a special style, nama, which needs far more careful handling.":"Por último, la gran mayoría de los sakes recibe un tratamiento térmico antes de venderse: la pasteurización. Evita que se desarrollen aromas defectuosos y hace el sake más estable. Los sakes que se saltan este paso forman un estilo especial, el nama, que exige mucho más cuidado.","Neutral alcohol added before filtration: extracts flavours from the rice solids":"Alcohol neutro añadido antes de filtrar: extrae aromas de los restos de arroz","Water nearly always added before bottling: from about 20% down to 15–17%":"Agua añadida casi siempre antes de embotellar: de un 20 % a un 15–17 %","Pasteurisation for the vast majority: prevents faulty aromas":"Pasteurización en la gran mayoría: evita aromas defectuosos","What is sake made from?":"¿Con qué materia prima se elabora el sake?","Rice":"Arroz","Malted barley":"Cebada malteada","Sweet potatoes":"Batatas","White grapes":"Uva blanca","Sake is a Japanese alcoholic drink made from rice.":"El sake es una bebida alcohólica japonesa hecha con arroz.","Malted barley is the base of beer and grapes of wine. Sweet potatoes are used for other drinks, not sake.":"La cebada malteada es la base de la cerveza y la uva la del vino. Las batatas se usan para otras bebidas, no para el sake.","What does nihon-shu, one of sake's official names, literally mean?":"¿Qué significa literalmente nihon-shu, uno de los nombres oficiales del sake?","Japanese alcoholic drink":"Bebida alcohólica de Japón","Fine rice wine":"Vino de arroz selecto","Pure rice":"Arroz puro","Big sake":"Gran sake","Nihon-shu means 'Japanese alcoholic drink': the name ties sake to its country.":"Nihon-shu quiere decir «bebida alcohólica japonesa»: el nombre une el sake a su país.","'Pure rice' is the meaning of junmai, a label term. 'Big' recalls the dai in daiginjō. No official name means 'fine rice wine'.":"«Arroz puro» es el significado de junmai, un término de etiqueta. «Gran» recuerda al dai de daiginjō. Ningún nombre oficial significa «vino de arroz selecto».","What is the typical alcohol level of a bottled sake?":"¿Cuál es la graduación típica de un sake embotellado?","15–17% abv":"15–17 % vol.","4–6% abv":"4–6 % vol.","9–11% abv":"9–11 % vol.","38–40% abv":"38–40 % vol.","Most sakes are between 15 and 17% abv.":"La mayoría de los sakes tienen entre un 15 y un 17 % de alcohol.","4–6% is the level of many beers and 38–40% that of a spirit. 9–11% is too low for a typical sake, although some sparkling sakes are light.":"El 4–6 % es lo de muchas cervezas y el 38–40 % lo de un destilado. El 9–11 % es demasiado bajo para un sake típico, aunque algunos sakes espumosos son ligeros.","Which description fits a typical sake?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a un sake típico?","Clear and colourless, slightly sweet, lightly acidic":"Transparente e incoloro, ligeramente dulce, poco ácido","Amber, very bitter, fizzy":"Ámbar, muy amargo, con burbujas","Cloudy, dry, very tannic":"Turbio, seco, muy tánico","Ruby red, tart, fruity":"Rojo rubí, ácido, afrutado","Typical sake is clear and colourless, slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with delicate flavours.":"El sake típico es transparente e incoloro, ligeramente dulce y poco ácido, con sabores delicados.","Cloudy describes nigori and amber is often koshu: these are speciality styles, not typical sake. Sake is never red or tannic, and marked bitterness belongs to beer rather than sake.":"Turbio es el nigori y ámbar suele ser el koshu: son estilos especiales, no el sake típico. El sake no es rojo ni tiene taninos, y el amargor marcado es más propio de la cerveza.","Which of these is NOT one of the four main ingredients of sake?":"¿Cuál de estos NO es uno de los cuatro ingredientes principales del sake?","High-strength distilled alcohol":"Alcohol destilado de alta graduación","Kōji":"Kōji","Water":"Agua","Yeast":"Levadura","Distilled alcohol is an optional extra, not one of the four main ingredients.":"El alcohol destilado es un ingrediente opcional, no uno de los cuatro principales.","Steamed white rice, kōji, water and yeast are in every sake. Distilled alcohol is added only in some cases, before filtration.":"Arroz blanco al vapor, kōji, agua y levadura están en todo sake. El alcohol destilado solo se añade en algunos casos, antes de filtrar.","In what state does rice usually arrive at a sake brewery?":"¿En qué estado llega normalmente el arroz a una bodega de sake?","Raw, hard and dusty":"Crudo, duro y polvoriento","Already steamed":"Ya cocido al vapor","Already turned into kōji":"Ya convertido en kōji","Ground into flour":"Molido en harina","Rice is bought raw; steaming is done in the brewery.":"El arroz se compra crudo; la cocción al vapor se hace en la bodega.","Kōji is made in the brewery from steamed rice. Rice is not ground into flour: it is polished, washed, soaked and steamed.":"El kōji se hace en la bodega a partir del arroz al vapor. El arroz no se muele en harina: se pule, se lava, se remoja y se cuece al vapor.","Why is the rice steamed?":"¿Por qué se cuece el arroz al vapor?","To soften it so it can break up in the water":"Para ablandarlo y que se deshaga en el agua","To turn its starch into alcohol":"Para convertir el almidón en alcohol","To give it an amber colour":"Para darle un color ámbar","To remove the outer layers":"Para eliminar las capas exteriores","Steam softens the hard rice, which can then break up in the water during fermentation.":"El vapor ablanda el arroz duro, que luego se deshace en el agua durante la fermentación.","The outer layers are removed by polishing, not steaming. Starch becomes sugar thanks to kōji enzymes, then alcohol thanks to yeast. Steaming does not colour the rice.":"Las capas exteriores se quitan al pulir, no con el vapor. El almidón se vuelve azúcar gracias a las enzimas del kōji y alcohol gracias a las levaduras. El vapor no colorea el arroz.","What is kōji?":"¿Qué es el kōji?","Steamed rice on which a special mould has been grown":"Arroz al vapor sobre el que se ha cultivado un moho especial","A selected yeast bought from a supplier":"Una levadura seleccionada comprada a un proveedor","A neutral alcohol added before filtration":"Un alcohol neutro añadido antes de filtrar","The rice dust removed during polishing":"El polvo de arroz retirado al pulir","Kōji is steamed rice covered in a special mould that produces enzymes.":"El kōji es arroz al vapor cubierto de un moho especial que produce enzimas.","Yeast is a separate ingredient that turns sugar into alcohol. Neutral alcohol is the optional ingredient. Polishing dust is washed off and not used.":"La levadura es otro ingrediente, que convierte el azúcar en alcohol. El alcohol neutro es el ingrediente opcional. El polvo de pulido se lava y no se usa.","How much of the rice is used to make kōji?":"¿Qué parte del arroz se usa para hacer el kōji?","A small proportion of the steamed rice":"Una pequeña parte del arroz al vapor","All of the steamed rice":"Todo el arroz al vapor","Only the brown outer layers":"Solo las capas exteriores marrones","Unpolished raw rice":"El arroz crudo sin pulir","Only a small proportion of the steamed rice is taken to grow the mould on.":"Solo se toma una pequeña parte del arroz al vapor para cultivar el moho.","The rest of the steamed rice is the starch source in fermentation. Kōji is made from polished, steamed rice, not raw rice or the outer layers.":"El resto del arroz al vapor sirve de fuente de almidón en la fermentación. El kōji se hace con arroz pulido y cocido, no con arroz crudo ni con las capas exteriores.","What water do sake breweries usually use?":"¿Qué agua usan normalmente las bodegas de sake?","Local water: almost any, as long as it is clean":"Agua local: casi cualquiera, siempre que esté limpia","Only desalinated seawater":"Solo agua de mar desalinizada","Only factory-bought distilled water":"Solo agua destilada comprada en fábrica","Water imported from a single Japanese spring":"Agua importada de un único manantial de Japón","Local supplies are used; almost any water works if it is clean.":"Se usa agua del lugar; casi cualquier agua sirve si está limpia.","There is no rule requiring distilled water, seawater or a single spring. The simple rule to remember: local, clean water.":"No existe obligación de usar agua destilada, de mar o de un solo manantial. La regla sencilla: agua local y limpia.","Where do the yeasts used for sake usually come from?":"¿De dónde suelen proceder las levaduras usadas para el sake?","From specialist suppliers selling specific varieties":"De proveedores especializados que venden variedades concretas","From the kōji mould":"Del moho del kōji","From the husk of brown rice":"De la cáscara del arroz integral","From the added distilled alcohol":"Del alcohol destilado añadido","Breweries buy specific yeast varieties from specialist suppliers.":"Las bodegas compran variedades concretas de levadura a proveedores especializados.","The kōji mould produces enzymes; it is not the yeast. Distilled alcohol contains no live yeast, and yeasts are not taken from the rice.":"El moho del kōji produce enzimas; no es la levadura. El alcohol destilado no contiene levaduras vivas, y las levaduras no se sacan del arroz.","During alcoholic fermentation, yeast turns sugar into…":"Durante la fermentación alcohólica, la levadura convierte el azúcar en…","alcohol and carbon dioxide":"alcohol y dióxido de carbono","starch and water":"almidón y agua","enzymes and oxygen":"enzimas y oxígeno","kōji and alcohol":"kōji y alcohol","Yeast eats sugar and makes alcohol, releasing carbon dioxide.":"La levadura se come el azúcar y produce alcohol, liberando dióxido de carbono.","Starch is the starting point, not the product. Enzymes come from kōji, which is made before fermentation: yeast does not make them from sugar.":"El almidón es el punto de partida, no el resultado. Las enzimas vienen del kōji, que se prepara antes de fermentar: la levadura no las fabrica a partir del azúcar.","Why could yeast alone not turn rice into alcohol?":"¿Por qué la levadura sola no podría convertir el arroz en alcohol?","Because rice contains starch and yeast cannot eat starch":"Porque el arroz contiene almidón y la levadura no puede comérselo","Because rice contains too much sugar":"Porque el arroz contiene demasiado azúcar","Because yeast needs grapes":"Porque la levadura necesita uva","Because rice is too acidic":"Porque el arroz es demasiado ácido","Rice has no sugar, only starch: without kōji enzymes the yeast has nothing to eat.":"El arroz no tiene azúcar sino almidón: sin las enzimas del kōji la levadura no tiene qué comer.","Rice contains no sugar, so it cannot have too much. Yeast does not need grapes: sugar dissolved in water is enough. Acidity is not the issue.":"El arroz no contiene azúcar, así que no puede tener demasiado. La levadura no necesita uva: le basta azúcar disuelto en agua. La acidez no es el problema.","What do enzymes do during starch conversion?":"¿Qué hacen las enzimas durante la conversión del almidón?","They break starch chains into individual sugars":"Rompen las cadenas de almidón en azúcares sueltos","They turn alcohol back into sugar":"Convierten el alcohol en azúcar","They join sugars together into starch":"Unen los azúcares en almidón","They remove the carbon dioxide":"Eliminan el dióxido de carbono","Enzymes unlock the bonds between the sugar molecules in starch, freeing sugars the yeast can eat.":"Las enzimas rompen los enlaces entre las moléculas de azúcar del almidón y liberan azúcares que la levadura puede comer.","Joining sugars into starch is the opposite of what is needed. Enzymes do not act on alcohol or carbon dioxide, which are made by the yeast.":"Unir azúcares en almidón es lo contrario de lo que se necesita. Las enzimas no actúan sobre el alcohol ni sobre el dióxido de carbono, que produce la levadura.","Where do the enzymes that turn rice starch into sugar come from?":"¿De dónde vienen las enzimas que convierten el almidón del arroz en azúcar?","From the mould grown to make kōji":"Del moho cultivado para hacer el kōji","From the yeast":"De la levadura","From the spring water":"Del agua del manantial","From the distilled alcohol":"Del alcohol destilado","The kōji mould produces the enzymes: that is why kōji is essential.":"El moho del kōji produce las enzimas: por eso el kōji es imprescindible.","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol but cannot break down starch. Water and distilled alcohol bring no enzymes for conversion.":"La levadura convierte azúcar en alcohol pero no sabe descomponer el almidón. Ni el agua ni el alcohol destilado aportan enzimas para la conversión.","Which three steps ALWAYS happen when sake is made?":"¿Cuáles son los tres pasos que se dan SIEMPRE al elaborar sake?","Fermentation, filtration, bottling":"Fermentación, filtración, embotellado","Fermentation, pasteurisation, adding water":"Fermentación, pasteurización, añadir agua","Adding alcohol, filtration, ageing":"Añadir alcohol, filtración, envejecimiento","Distillation, filtration, bottling":"Destilación, filtración, embotellado","Fermentation, filtration and bottling happen for every sake.":"Fermentación, filtración y embotellado se dan en todo sake.","Pasteurisation, adding water and adding alcohol are optional. Sake is not distilled, and ageing applies only to one speciality style, koshu.":"Pasteurizar, añadir agua y añadir alcohol son opcionales. El sake no se destila, y el envejecimiento solo afecta a un estilo especial, el koshu.","Which of these steps is OPTIONAL?":"¿Cuál de estos pasos es OPCIONAL?","Pasteurisation":"Pasteurización","Filtration":"Filtración","Fermentation":"Fermentación","Bottling":"Embotellado","Pasteurisation is very common but not compulsory: sakes that skip it are called nama.":"La pasteurización es muy habitual pero no obligatoria: los sakes que se la saltan se llaman nama.","Filtration, fermentation and bottling always happen; filtration is even required by law.":"Filtración, fermentación y embotellado se dan siempre; la filtración incluso la exige la ley.","What is the fermentation starter for?":"¿Para qué sirve el iniciador de la fermentación?","To build a healthy, active yeast population":"Para crear una población de levaduras sana y activa","To remove the rice solids":"Para retirar los restos sólidos de arroz","To lower the alcohol level":"Para bajar la graduación","To pasteurise the sake":"Para pasteurizar el sake","A little of the ingredients is used to multiply the yeast; the starter then goes into the main fermentation.":"Con poca cantidad de ingredientes se multiplican las levaduras y después el iniciador pasa a la fermentación principal.","Solids are removed by filtration, alcohol is lowered with water, and pasteurisation is a heat treatment: all later steps.":"Los restos se quitan al filtrar, la graduación se baja con agua y la pasteurización es un tratamiento térmico: todos son pasos posteriores.","What is meant by 'parallel fermentation' in sake?":"¿Qué se entiende por «fermentación paralela» en el sake?","Enzymes make sugar while yeast turns it into alcohol":"Las enzimas producen azúcar mientras la levadura lo convierte en alcohol","Two tanks ferment the same sake side by side":"Dos depósitos fermentan el mismo sake uno junto al otro","Rice and grapes are fermented together":"Se fermentan juntos arroz y uva","The sake ferments a second time in the bottle":"El sake fermenta por segunda vez en la botella","Starch conversion and alcoholic fermentation happen at the same time: this is unique to sake.":"La conversión del almidón y la fermentación alcohólica suceden a la vez: es exclusivo del sake.","'Parallel' refers to the two simultaneous reactions, not two tanks. There are no grapes in sake, and a second fermentation in bottle is not what the term means.":"«Paralela» se refiere a las dos reacciones simultáneas, no a dos depósitos. En el sake no hay uva, y una segunda fermentación en botella no es lo que significa el término.","How much alcohol does sake usually have at the end of fermentation?":"¿Cuánto alcohol suele tener el sake al final de la fermentación?","About 20% abv":"Alrededor del 20 % vol.","About 5% abv":"Alrededor del 5 % vol.","About 12% abv":"Alrededor del 12 % vol.","About 40% abv":"Alrededor del 40 % vol.","At the end of fermentation sake is usually around 20%; water then brings it down to 15–17%.":"Al final de la fermentación el sake suele rondar el 20 %; luego el agua lo baja al 15–17 %.","5% is beer strength and 12% light-wine strength. 40% is spirit strength, impossible to reach by fermentation alone.":"El 5 % es graduación de cerveza y el 12 % de vino ligero. El 40 % es de destilado, imposible de alcanzar solo fermentando.","Why is the fermenting liquid white and cloudy?":"¿Por qué el líquido en fermentación es blanco y turbio?","Because of the rice in the tank":"Por el arroz que hay en el depósito","Because of the added distilled alcohol":"Por el alcohol destilado añadido","Because milk is added to the recipe":"Por la leche añadida a la receta","Because of pasteurisation":"Por la pasteurización","The white colour comes from the rice: the solids are removed later by filtration.":"El color blanco viene del arroz: los restos sólidos se retiran después al filtrar.","Neutral alcohol is clear. No milk is added to sake: 'lactic' aromas come from fermentation. Pasteurisation happens later, on filtered sake.":"El alcohol neutro es transparente. Al sake no se le añade leche: los aromas «lácticos» vienen de la fermentación. La pasteurización se hace después, sobre el sake ya filtrado.","What does the law say about filtering sake?":"¿Qué dice la ley sobre la filtración del sake?","Every sake must be filtered":"Todo sake debe filtrarse","Filtration is banned for premium sakes":"La filtración está prohibida en los sakes premium","Only export sake is filtered":"Solo se filtra el sake de exportación","The law says nothing about it":"La ley no dice nada","By law, all sake must be filtered after fermentation.":"Por ley, todo sake debe filtrarse tras la fermentación.","Even cloudy nigori is filtered, just roughly. No rule exempts premium sake or applies only to exports.":"Incluso el nigori, turbio, se filtra, aunque de forma grosera. Ninguna regla exime a los premium ni afecta solo a la exportación.","What does filtration remove?":"¿Qué elimina la filtración?","The rice solids":"Los restos sólidos de arroz","Excess alcohol":"El exceso de alcohol","The carbon dioxide":"El dióxido de carbono","The sweetness":"El dulzor","Filtering separates out the rice solids and usually leaves a clear liquid.":"Al filtrar se separan los sólidos de arroz y se suele obtener un líquido transparente.","Alcohol is lowered by adding water, not by filtering. Filtration removes neither gas nor sweetness.":"El alcohol se baja añadiendo agua, no filtrando. La filtración no quita ni gas ni dulzor.","What container is nearly all sake packed in?":"¿En qué envase se embotella casi todo el sake?","Glass bottles":"Botellas de vidrio","Cans":"Latas","Wooden casks":"Barriles de madera","Cartons":"Briks de cartón","Nearly all sake goes into glass bottles of various sizes.":"Casi todo el sake va en botellas de vidrio de distintos tamaños.","Cans and cartons exist but are rare. Wood, and oak especially, is very rarely used, even for ageing.":"Latas y briks existen, pero son raros. La madera, sobre todo el roble, se usa muy poco, incluso para envejecer.","Why does a brewer add neutral distilled alcohol before filtration?":"¿Por qué un elaborador añade alcohol destilado neutro antes de filtrar?","To extract flavours trapped in the rice solids":"Para extraer los aromas atrapados en los sólidos de arroz","To turn the sake into a spirit":"Para convertir el sake en un destilado","To restart fermentation":"Para reiniciar la fermentación","To give the sake colour":"Para dar color al sake","The neutral alcohol helps draw out flavours left in the solids.":"El alcohol neutro ayuda a sacar los aromas que quedan en los restos sólidos.","Sake stays a fermented drink and is later diluted with water. The alcohol does not restart fermentation and adds no colour: it is neutral.":"El sake sigue siendo una bebida fermentada y luego se diluye con agua. El alcohol no reinicia la fermentación ni da color: es neutro.","At what point is distilled alcohol added, when it is used?":"¿En qué momento se añade el alcohol destilado, cuando se usa?","Before filtration":"Antes de la filtración","Before steaming the rice":"Antes de cocer el arroz","After bottling":"Después del embotellado","While making kōji":"Durante la elaboración del kōji","It is added at the end of fermentation, before filtering, while the rice solids are still present.":"Se añade al final de la fermentación, antes de filtrar, cuando aún están los sólidos de arroz.","Its job is to extract flavour from the solids: after filtration or bottling there are none left. It has no role in kōji or steaming.":"Su función es extraer aromas de los sólidos: tras filtrar o embotellar ya no los hay. No interviene en el kōji ni en la cocción.","Why is water nearly always added to sake before bottling?":"¿Por qué casi siempre se añade agua al sake antes de embotellar?","To lower the alcohol from about 20% to 15–17%":"Para bajar el alcohol de un 20 % a un 15–17 %","To make it cloudy":"Para enturbiarlo","To pasteurise it":"Para pasteurizarlo","To make it sparkling":"Para hacerlo espumoso","Water takes sake from its end-of-fermentation strength (about 20%) to the usual 15–17%.":"El agua lleva el sake de la graduación de final de fermentación (un 20 %) a la habitual (15–17 %).","Cloudiness comes from rice solids left in nigori, bubbles from carbon dioxide and pasteurisation from heat: water does none of these.":"La turbidez viene de los sólidos que deja el nigori, las burbujas del dióxido de carbono y la pasteurización del calor: el agua no hace nada de eso.","What is pasteurisation of sake?":"¿Qué es la pasteurización del sake?","A heat treatment before the sake goes on sale":"Un tratamiento térmico antes de la venta","Ageing in cedar casks":"Un envejecimiento en barricas de cedro","An addition of sugar":"Una adición de azúcar","A second filtration through charcoal":"Una segunda filtración con carbón","Pasteurising means heating the sake before it is sold.":"Pasteurizar es calentar el sake antes de ponerlo a la venta.","Pasteurisation has nothing to do with wood, sugar or charcoal: it is purely about heat.":"La pasteurización no tiene nada que ver con madera, azúcar o carbón: es solo cuestión de calor.","What does pasteurisation achieve?":"¿Qué consigue la pasteurización?","It prevents faulty aromas from developing":"Evita que se desarrollen aromas defectuosos","It raises the alcohol level":"Aumenta la graduación","It adds fruity and floral aromas":"Aporta aromas de fruta y flores","It makes the sake cloudy":"Enturbia el sake","Heat stabilises the sake and stops faulty aromas from appearing.":"El calor estabiliza el sake y evita que aparezcan aromas defectuosos.","Fruity, floral aromas come from highly polished rice, special yeasts and cool fermentation. Pasteurisation changes neither strength nor clarity.":"Los aromas de fruta y flores vienen de arroz muy pulido, levaduras especiales y fermentación fresca. La pasteurización no cambia la graduación ni la transparencia.","A sake has just finished fermenting: which order of the next steps is correct?":"Un sake acaba de fermentar: ¿qué orden de los pasos siguientes es correcto?","Optional alcohol → filtration → water → bottling":"Alcohol opcional → filtración → agua → embotellado","Filtration → alcohol → bottling → water":"Filtración → alcohol → embotellado → agua","Bottling → filtration → alcohol → water":"Embotellado → filtración → alcohol → agua","Water → bottling → alcohol → filtration":"Agua → embotellado → alcohol → filtración","Alcohol comes before filtration (it needs the solids) and water before bottling.":"El alcohol va antes de filtrar (necesita los sólidos) y el agua antes de embotellar.","Adding alcohol after filtration would be pointless: there would be no solids left to extract flavour from. Water adjusts the strength before the sake is bottled.":"Añadir alcohol tras filtrar no tendría sentido: ya no habría sólidos de los que extraer aromas. El agua ajusta la graduación antes de embotellar.","Nihon-shu":"Nihon-shu","Official name for sake: 'Japanese alcoholic drink'.":"Nombre oficial del sake: «bebida alcohólica de Japón».","Typical sake: alcohol level":"Sake típico: graduación","Typical sake profile":"Perfil del sake típico","Clear, colourless, slightly sweet, lightly acidic; cereal, lactic or fruity notes.":"Transparente, incoloro, ligeramente dulce, poco ácido; notas de cereal, lácteas o frutales.","The four main ingredients":"Los cuatro ingredientes principales","Steamed white rice, kōji, water, yeast.":"Arroz blanco al vapor, kōji, agua, levadura.","Optional ingredient":"Ingrediente opcional","High-strength distilled alcohol with a neutral flavour.":"Alcohol destilado de alta graduación y sabor neutro.","Steamed rice grown with a special mould that makes enzymes.":"Arroz al vapor con un moho especial que produce enzimas.","Starch conversion":"Conversión del almidón","Enzymes break starch into sugars yeast can eat.":"Las enzimas rompen el almidón en azúcares que la levadura puede comer.","Alcoholic fermentation":"Fermentación alcohólica","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"Azúcar + levadura → alcohol + dióxido de carbono.","Steps that always happen":"Pasos que siempre se dan","Fermentation, filtration, bottling.":"Fermentación, filtración, embotellado.","Optional steps":"Pasos opcionales","Adding alcohol, adding water, pasteurisation.":"Añadir alcohol, añadir agua, pasteurizar.","Enzymes make sugar while yeast eats it, at the same time; unique to sake.":"Las enzimas producen azúcar mientras la levadura lo consume; exclusiva del sake.","Alcohol at end of fermentation":"Alcohol al final de la fermentación","About 20% abv.":"Alrededor del 20 % vol.","Why add neutral alcohol?":"¿Por qué añadir alcohol neutro?","Before filtration, to extract flavours from the rice solids.":"Antes de filtrar, para extraer aromas de los sólidos de arroz.","Heat treatment of most sake: prevents faulty aromas.":"Tratamiento térmico de casi todo el sake: evita aromas defectuosos.","Polishing: removing rice to choose a style":"Pulir el arroz: quitar para elegir el estilo","A sake brewer starts with grains of brown rice, which go through four stages before they become steamed white rice: polishing, washing, soaking and steaming. The first matters most for style. During polishing the grains pass between two rough surfaces that, over a few hours, slowly wear away the outer layers and some of the middle layers.":"El elaborador de sake parte de granos de arroz integral, que pasan por cuatro fases antes de convertirse en arroz blanco al vapor: pulido, lavado, remojo y cocción al vapor. La primera es la más importante para el estilo. Durante el pulido los granos pasan entre dos superficies rugosas que, en unas horas, desgastan poco a poco las capas exteriores y parte de las intermedias.","A rice grain has three zones. The outer layers are brown; the middle layers are white; at the centre is a white core that is almost pure starch. The outer and middle layers also hold starch, but together with many other components: these give sake more acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas. The outer layers are nearly always removed; the real decision concerns the middle layers.":"Un grano de arroz tiene tres zonas. Las capas exteriores son marrones; las intermedias, blancas; en el centro hay un núcleo blanco que es casi puro almidón. Las capas exteriores e intermedias también tienen almidón, pero junto a muchas otras sustancias: son ellas las que dan al sake más acidez y umami, con aromas de cereal y lácteos. Las capas exteriores se quitan casi siempre; la verdadera decisión es sobre las intermedias.","If the brewer polishes away only some of the middle layers, the sake will have more acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas. If most or all of the middle layers go, leaving mainly the starch core, the sake will usually have less acidity and umami and more fruity, floral aromas. Polishing more means moving towards a purer, more fragrant style.":"Si el elaborador quita solo parte de las capas intermedias, el sake tendrá más acidez y umami, con aromas de cereal y lácteos. Si las elimina casi todas y deja sobre todo el núcleo de almidón, el sake tendrá normalmente menos acidez y umami y aromas más frutales y florales. Pulir más significa ir hacia un estilo más puro y perfumado.","Four stages: polishing, washing, soaking, steaming":"Cuatro fases: pulido, lavado, remojo, cocción al vapor","Outer layers brown, middle layers white, core almost pure starch":"Capas exteriores marrones, intermedias blancas, núcleo casi puro almidón","Light polishing → more acidity and umami, cereal and lactic aromas":"Poco pulido → más acidez y umami, aromas de cereal y lácteos","Heavy polishing → less acidity and umami, more fruit and flowers":"Mucho pulido → menos acidez y umami, más fruta y flores","The polishing ratio: a number that works backwards":"El grado de pulido: un número que se lee al revés","How much rice must be removed to qualify for a premium grade is set by Japanese law: this is the polishing ratio. Thanks to this rule, the label terms give a reliable guide to the style of the sake.":"Cuánto arroz hay que quitar para tener derecho a una categoría premium lo fija la ley japonesa: es el grado de pulido. Gracias a esta regla, los términos de la etiqueta indican de forma fiable el estilo del sake.","The figure is a percentage and shows how much of the grain REMAINS, not how much is removed. If the law requires 60%, then 60% or less of the original grain must be left after polishing: at least 40% has gone. The lower the number, the more the rice has been polished.":"La cifra se expresa en porcentaje e indica cuánto grano QUEDA, no cuánto se quita. Si la ley exige un 60 %, tras el pulido debe quedar un 60 % o menos del grano original: se ha quitado al menos un 40 %. Cuanto más bajo el número, más pulido está el arroz.","Three thresholds to remember. 70% or less: honjōzō and most junmai. 60% or less: ginjō and junmai ginjō. 50% or less: daiginjō and junmai daiginjō. Junmai may in theory use rice with a ratio between 100% and 70%, but this is very rare.":"Tres umbrales que recordar. 70 % o menos: honjōzō y la mayoría de los junmai. 60 % o menos: ginjō y junmai ginjō. 50 % o menos: daiginjō y junmai daiginjō. En teoría el junmai puede usar arroz pulido entre el 100 % y el 70 %, pero es muy raro.","Polishing ratio: % of the grain that remains, set by law":"Grado de pulido: % del grano que queda, fijado por ley","Lower number = more polished rice":"Número más bajo = arroz más pulido","≤70% honjōzō and most junmai; ≤60% ginjō and junmai ginjō; ≤50% daiginjō and junmai daiginjō":"≤70 % honjōzō y casi todos los junmai; ≤60 % ginjō y junmai ginjō; ≤50 % daiginjō y junmai daiginjō","Junmai between 100% and 70%: allowed but very rare":"Junmai entre 100 % y 70 %: posible pero muy raro","Washing, soaking and steaming":"Lavar, remojar y cocer al vapor","After polishing, the grains are covered in rice dust: exactly the outer and middle layers the brewer wanted to get rid of. That is why the rice must be washed carefully; otherwise the dust would put back into the sake what has just been removed.":"Tras el pulido los granos están cubiertos de polvo de arroz: justo las capas exteriores e intermedias que el elaborador quería eliminar. Por eso el arroz se lava con cuidado; si no, ese polvo devolvería al sake lo que se acaba de quitar.","Next come soaking and steaming. Together they soften the grain and give it the right texture and moisture so that it can break up in the water during fermentation. Rice that is too hard would not break down; rice that is too wet would turn into a mush that is hard to work with.":"Después vienen el remojo y la cocción al vapor. Juntos ablandan el grano y le dan la textura y la humedad justas para que se deshaga en el agua durante la fermentación. Un arroz demasiado duro no se desharía; uno demasiado mojado se convertiría en una papilla difícil de manejar.","Washing: removes the rice dust left by polishing":"Lavado: quita el polvo de arroz que deja el pulido","Soaking and steaming: the right texture and moisture":"Remojo y vapor: textura y humedad adecuadas","Goal: a grain that breaks up in the water during fermentation":"Objetivo: un grano que se deshaga en el agua al fermentar","The kōji room":"La sala del kōji","Kōji is made in a special series of rooms in the brewery, where the brewer can control temperature and humidity very precisely. This matters: the mould is alive, and it grows faster or slower depending on the warmth and moisture it finds. The rooms therefore have different zones, from the warmest and most humid to the coolest and driest.":"El kōji se elabora en una serie de salas especiales de la bodega, donde el elaborador puede controlar con mucha precisión la temperatura y la humedad. No es un detalle: el moho está vivo y crece más o menos rápido según el calor y la humedad que encuentra. Por eso las salas tienen zonas distintas, de la más cálida y húmeda a la más fresca y seca.","The work follows four stages: cool the steamed rice, spread the mould spores, let the mould grow quickly at first, then control and finally stop its growth. In practice the rice 'travels' through the room: it goes into the warmest zone to get the mould started and moves towards the coolest zone when the growth must slow down.":"El trabajo sigue cuatro fases: enfriar el arroz al vapor, esparcir las esporas del moho, dejar que el moho crezca rápido al principio y después controlar y, por último, detener su crecimiento. En la práctica el arroz «viaja» por la sala: entra en la zona más cálida para arrancar el moho y se desplaza hacia la más fresca cuando hay que frenarlo.","Dedicated rooms with precisely controlled temperature and humidity":"Salas dedicadas con temperatura y humedad controladas con precisión","Four stages: cool, spread spores, initial growth, control and stop":"Cuatro fases: enfriar, esparcir esporas, crecimiento inicial, control y parada","Warm and humid = fast growth; cool and dry = slow growth":"Cálido y húmedo = crecimiento rápido; fresco y seco = crecimiento lento","The four kōji stages, one by one":"Las cuatro fases del kōji, una a una","1. Cooling. Fresh from the steamer, the rice is too hot for kōji making: it is spread on mats to cool naturally. 2. Spreading the mould. Once cool enough, the rice moves into the warmest, most humid part of the room, is spread in a thin layer on a large table, and the mould spores (its 'seeds') are scattered over it.":"1. Enfriar. Recién salido del vapor, el arroz está demasiado caliente para el kōji: se extiende sobre esteras y se deja enfriar de forma natural. 2. Esparcir el moho. Cuando está lo bastante frío, el arroz pasa a la parte más cálida y húmeda de la sala, se extiende en una capa fina sobre una gran mesa y se esparcen encima las esporas del moho (sus «semillas»).","3. Initial growth. In the warm, humid zone the mould spreads quickly over the rice, which is turned regularly by hand so that the growth is even. 4. Controlling and stopping. The rice is sometimes moved onto racks in cooler, less humid zones to slow the mould and get exactly the right amount; to stop it altogether, the rice is moved to the coolest part of the room.":"3. Primer crecimiento. En la zona cálida y húmeda el moho se extiende rápido sobre el arroz, que se voltea a mano con regularidad para que crezca de forma uniforme. 4. Controlar y detener. A veces el arroz se pasa a estantes en zonas más frescas y menos húmedas para frenar el moho y conseguir exactamente la cantidad deseada; para detenerlo del todo se lleva a la parte más fresca de la sala.","Natural cooling on mats":"Enfriado natural sobre esteras","Spores scattered on a thin layer, in the warmest, most humid zone":"Esporas sobre una capa fina, en la zona más cálida y húmeda","Fast growth, rice turned by hand":"Crecimiento rápido, arroz volteado a mano","Slow it in cooler zones, stop it in the coolest zone":"Frenar en zonas frescas, detener en la zona más fresca","Yeast, the real flavour maker":"La levadura, verdadera creadora de aromas","In many sake styles the steamed rice, kōji and water add relatively little flavour. In nearly all styles it is the yeast that contributes a large share of the aromas. That is why fermentation is when the brewer decides much of the sake's character.":"En muchos estilos de sake el arroz al vapor, el kōji y el agua aportan relativamente poco sabor. En casi todos los estilos es la levadura la que aporta una parte importante de los aromas. Por eso la fermentación es el momento en que el elaborador decide buena parte del carácter del sake.","As we saw, it all begins with a small starter: a little of the four main ingredients is used to grow a healthy yeast population. The starter then moves to a larger vessel and is carefully mixed with more steamed rice, kōji and water: the main fermentation. Now the brewer has two levers: the choice of yeast and the temperature.":"Como vimos, todo empieza con un pequeño iniciador: un poco de los cuatro ingredientes principales sirve para criar una población de levaduras sana. Después pasa a un recipiente mayor y se mezcla con cuidado con más arroz al vapor, kōji y agua: la fermentación principal. Entonces el elaborador tiene dos palancas: el tipo de levadura y la temperatura.","Rice, kōji and water give little flavour in many styles; yeast gives a lot":"Arroz, kōji y agua aportan poco sabor en muchos estilos; la levadura mucho","Starter → main fermentation in a larger vessel":"Iniciador → fermentación principal en un recipiente mayor","Two style levers: choice of yeast and temperature":"Dos palancas de estilo: elección de levadura y temperatura","Cool and fragrant, or warm and cereal-like":"Fresco y perfumado, o cálido y cereal","To get the fruity, floral aromas typical of ginjō styles, two things are needed together: special yeast strains and lower fermentation temperatures. A cool fermentation is slower and keeps delicate scents such as apple, pear or white flowers.":"Para lograr los aromas frutales y florales típicos de los estilos ginjō hacen falta dos cosas a la vez: cepas de levadura especiales y temperaturas de fermentación más bajas. La fermentación fresca es más lenta y conserva perfumes delicados, como manzana, pera o flores blancas.","Warmer fermentation temperatures, by contrast, produce cereal and lactic aromas. Link this to polishing and the picture becomes clear: highly polished rice + special yeasts + cool fermentation give fruity, floral sakes; lightly polished rice + warmer fermentation give cereal, lactic sakes with more acidity and umami.":"En cambio, temperaturas de fermentación más cálidas dan aromas de cereal y lácteos. Si lo unimos al pulido, el cuadro queda claro: arroz muy pulido + levaduras especiales + fermentación fresca dan sakes frutales y florales; arroz poco pulido + fermentación más cálida dan sakes de cereal y lácteos, con más acidez y umami.","Ginjō aromas (fruit, flowers): special yeasts + cool fermentation":"Aromas ginjō (fruta, flores): levaduras especiales + fermentación fresca","Warmer fermentation: cereal and lactic aromas":"Fermentación más cálida: aromas de cereal y lácteos","Style = polishing + yeast + temperature":"Estilo = pulido + levadura + temperatura","Which four stages turn brown rice into steamed white rice?":"¿Cuáles son las cuatro fases que convierten el arroz integral en arroz blanco al vapor?","Polishing, washing, soaking, steaming":"Pulido, lavado, remojo, cocción al vapor","Malting, milling, mashing, boiling":"Malteado, molienda, maceración, cocción","Washing, drying, roasting, grinding":"Lavado, secado, tostado, molienda","Soaking, germination, drying, polishing":"Remojo, germinación, secado, pulido","Brown rice is polished, washed, soaked and steamed.":"El arroz integral se pule, se lava, se remoja y se cuece al vapor.","Malting, milling and mashing belong to beer. Sake rice is neither germinated nor roasted.":"Malteado, molienda y maceración pertenecen a la cerveza. El arroz del sake no se germina ni se tuesta.","How is rice polished?":"¿Cómo se pule el arroz?","Grains pass between two rough surfaces for a few hours":"Los granos pasan unas horas entre dos superficies rugosas","Grains are dissolved in boiling water":"Los granos se disuelven en agua hirviendo","A mould eats away the outer layers":"Un moho se come las capas exteriores","Grains are roasted until the husk falls off":"Los granos se tuestan hasta que cae la cáscara","Two rough surfaces slowly wear away the outer and some middle layers over a few hours.":"Dos superficies rugosas desgastan poco a poco, en unas horas, las capas exteriores y parte de las intermedias.","The mould comes later, on steamed rice, to make kōji. The rice is neither dissolved nor roasted.":"El moho interviene después, sobre el arroz cocido, para hacer el kōji. El arroz no se disuelve ni se tuesta.","What colour are the middle layers of a rice grain?":"¿De qué color son las capas intermedias del grano de arroz?","White":"Blancas","Brown":"Marrones","Green":"Verdes","Black":"Negras","The outer layers are brown; the middle layers and core are white.":"Las capas exteriores son marrones; las intermedias y el núcleo, blancos.","Brown is the colour of the outer layers, which are nearly always removed. Neither green nor black describes any part of the grain.":"El marrón es el color de las capas exteriores, que casi siempre se quitan. Ni el verde ni el negro describen ninguna parte del grano.","What is the core of a rice grain made of, almost entirely?":"¿De qué está hecho casi por completo el núcleo del grano de arroz?","Starch":"Almidón","Sugar":"Azúcar","Fats and proteins":"Grasas y proteínas","The core is almost pure starch: that is why heavy polishing gives purer sakes.":"El núcleo es casi almidón puro: por eso pulir mucho da sakes más puros.","Rice contains no sugar, and the 'other components' that give acidity and umami sit mainly in the outer and middle layers.":"El arroz no contiene azúcar, y las «otras sustancias» que dan acidez y umami están sobre todo en las capas exteriores e intermedias.","What do the outer and middle layers of the grain bring to sake?":"¿Qué aportan al sake las capas exteriores e intermedias del grano?","More acidity and umami, with cereal and lactic aromas":"Más acidez y umami, con aromas de cereal y lácteos","Pure fruity and floral aromas":"Aromas puros de fruta y flores","Natural bubbles":"Burbujas naturales","An amber colour and dried-fruit aromas":"Un color ámbar y aromas de fruta seca","Besides starch they contain other components that give acidity, umami and cereal, lactic notes.":"Además de almidón contienen otras sustancias que aportan acidez, umami y notas de cereal y lácteas.","Fruit and flowers come when these layers are almost entirely removed. Amber and dried fruit belong to aged koshu; bubbles come from carbon dioxide.":"La fruta y las flores aparecen cuando estas capas se quitan casi del todo. Ámbar y fruta seca son propios del koshu envejecido; las burbujas vienen del dióxido de carbono.","A brewer removes almost all the middle layers, leaving mainly the core. What style will usually result?":"Un elaborador elimina casi todas las capas intermedias y deja sobre todo el núcleo. ¿Qué estilo obtendrá normalmente?","Less acidity and umami, more fruity and floral aromas":"Menos acidez y umami, más aromas frutales y florales","More acidity and umami, cereal aromas":"Más acidez y umami, aromas de cereal","A cloudy sake with rice fragments":"Un sake turbio con trocitos de arroz","A stronger sake, above 25% abv":"Un sake más alcohólico, por encima del 25 %","Keeping almost pure starch removes the components behind acidity and umami, so fruit and flowers take over.":"Al dejar casi solo almidón se pierden las sustancias que dan acidez y umami, y dominan la fruta y las flores.","More acidity and cereal notes come from light polishing. Cloudiness depends on rough filtration, not polishing, which does not change the final strength either.":"Más acidez y notas de cereal vienen de un pulido ligero. La turbidez depende de una filtración grosera, no del pulido, que tampoco cambia la graduación final.","Who sets the minimum polishing for the premium grades?":"¿Quién fija el pulido mínimo de las categorías premium?","Japanese law":"La ley japonesa","Each brewery, freely":"Cada bodega, libremente","The rice suppliers":"Los proveedores de arroz","The importers in each country":"Los importadores de cada país","The polishing ratio required for each premium grade is defined in Japanese law.":"El grado de pulido exigido para cada categoría premium lo fija la ley japonesa.","Precisely because it is law rather than free choice, the label terms are a reliable guide to style.":"Precisamente porque es ley y no elección libre, los términos de la etiqueta son una guía fiable del estilo.","A label says 'polishing ratio 60%'. What does this mean?":"En una etiqueta pone «grado de pulido 60 %». ¿Qué significa?","60% of the grain remains: 40% has been removed":"Queda el 60 % del grano: se ha quitado el 40 %","60% of the grain has been removed":"Se ha quitado el 60 % del grano","The sake contains 60% rice and 40% water":"El sake contiene un 60 % de arroz y un 40 % de agua","60% of the rice became kōji":"El 60 % del arroz se ha convertido en kōji","The polishing ratio shows the part of the grain left after polishing.":"El grado de pulido indica la parte del grano que queda tras el pulido.","This is the most common mistake: the number shows what remains, not what is removed. It has nothing to do with water or the amount of kōji.":"Es el error más habitual: el número no indica lo que se quita, sino lo que queda. No tiene nada que ver con el agua ni con la cantidad de kōji.","Which rice has been polished the MOST?":"¿Qué arroz se ha pulido MÁS?","Polishing ratio 45%":"Grado de pulido 45 %","Polishing ratio 60%":"Grado de pulido 60 %","Polishing ratio 70%":"Grado de pulido 70 %","Polishing ratio 90%":"Grado de pulido 90 %","At 45% the least grain remains: this is the most polished rice.":"Con un 45 % es donde menos grano queda: es el arroz más pulido.","The higher the number, the more grain remains and the less polishing: 90% is the least polished of the four.":"Cuanto más alto el número, más grano queda y menos pulido está: el 90 % es el menos pulido de los cuatro.","What is the maximum polishing ratio allowed for daiginjō and junmai daiginjō?":"¿Cuál es el grado de pulido máximo permitido para daiginjō y junmai daiginjō?","50%":"50 %","60%":"60 %","70%":"70 %","80%":"80 %","For daiginjō, 50% or less of the grain must remain.":"En los daiginjō debe quedar un 50 % del grano o menos.","60% is the limit for ginjō and junmai ginjō, 70% for honjōzō and most junmai. 80% matches no premium grade.":"El 60 % es el límite de ginjō y junmai ginjō, el 70 % el de honjōzō y la mayoría de los junmai. El 80 % no corresponde a ninguna categoría premium.","Which grade requires a polishing ratio of 60% or less?":"¿Qué categoría exige un grado de pulido del 60 % o menos?","Junmai ginjō":"Junmai ginjō","Honjōzō":"Honjōzō","Futsū-shu":"Futsū-shu","Junmai daiginjō":"Junmai daiginjō","Ginjō and junmai ginjō: 60% or less.":"Ginjō y junmai ginjō: 60 % o menos.","Honjōzō stops at 70% and junmai daiginjō goes down to 50%. Futsū-shu is basic sake with no premium threshold.":"El honjōzō se queda en el 70 % y el junmai daiginjō baja al 50 %. El futsū-shu es el sake básico, sin umbral premium.","What is true of the polishing ratio for junmai?":"¿Qué ocurre con el grado de pulido del junmai?","Usually 70%; rice up to 100% may be used, but this is very rare":"Normalmente 70 %; se puede usar arroz hasta el 100 %, pero es muy raro","It must always be 50% or less":"Siempre debe ser del 50 % o menos","It may never go below 70%":"Está prohibido bajar del 70 %","Junmai does not use polished rice":"El junmai no usa arroz pulido","Junmai is usually made with rice polished to 70%; 100–70% is allowed but very rare.":"El junmai se suele hacer con arroz pulido al 70 %; entre el 100 % y el 70 % se permite pero es muy raro.","50% applies to daiginjō. A junmai may be polished further than 70% (junmai ginjō is also junmai), so there is no ban on going lower.":"El 50 % es para los daiginjō. Un junmai puede pulirse más del 70 % (los junmai ginjō también son junmai), así que no hay prohibición de bajar.","Why must rice be washed after polishing?":"¿Por qué hay que lavar el arroz tras el pulido?","To remove the dust from the layers just polished away":"Para quitar el polvo de las capas que se acaban de eliminar","To give the rice a floral aroma":"Para dar al arroz un aroma floral","To start fermentation":"Para iniciar la fermentación","To remove the starch from the core":"Para quitar el almidón del núcleo","The dust is made of the outer and middle layers the brewer wanted to remove.":"El polvo está hecho de las capas exteriores e intermedias que el elaborador quería quitar.","The starch in the core is exactly what is needed to make alcohol, so it stays. Washing adds no aroma and does not start fermentation.":"El almidón del núcleo es justo lo que se necesita para hacer alcohol, así que no se quita. El lavado no aporta aromas ni inicia la fermentación.","What are soaking and steaming for?":"¿Para qué sirven el remojo y la cocción al vapor?","To give the grain the right texture and moisture to break up during fermentation":"A dar al grano la textura y humedad justas para deshacerse al fermentar","To polish the grain more deeply":"A pulir el grano más a fondo","To turn the starch into sugar":"A convertir el almidón en azúcar","To sterilise the finished sake":"A esterilizar el sake terminado","Soaking and steaming soften the grain and give it the right moisture.":"El remojo y el vapor ablandan el grano y le dan la humedad adecuada.","Starch becomes sugar thanks to kōji enzymes. Polishing comes first, and pasteurising the finished sake is a different step.":"El almidón se convierte en azúcar gracias a las enzimas del kōji. El pulido va antes, y la pasteurización del sake terminado es otro paso.","What does the kōji room allow the brewer to control?":"¿Qué permite controlar la sala del kōji?","Temperature and humidity, very precisely":"La temperatura y la humedad, con mucha precisión","Carbon dioxide pressure":"La presión del dióxido de carbono","The alcohol level of the sake":"La graduación del sake","Light and noise":"La luz y el ruido","Kōji rooms let the brewer fine-tune warmth and humidity, which drive mould growth.":"Las salas del kōji permiten ajustar con precisión calor y humedad, que deciden el crecimiento del moho.","There is no alcohol or fermentation gas yet in kōji making: it is just about growing a mould under the right conditions.":"En el kōji todavía no hay alcohol ni gas de fermentación: solo se trata de cultivar un moho en las condiciones adecuadas.","What is the FIRST stage of making kōji?":"¿Cuál es la PRIMERA fase de la elaboración del kōji?","Cooling the steamed rice":"Enfriar el arroz al vapor","Spreading the mould spores":"Esparcir las esporas del moho","Turning the rice by hand":"Voltear el arroz a mano","Moving the rice to the coolest zone":"Llevar el arroz a la zona más fresca","Fresh from the steamer the rice is too hot: it must be cooled first.":"Recién salido del vapor el arroz está demasiado caliente: primero hay que enfriarlo.","Spreading spores is stage two, turning the rice belongs to stage three, and moving it to the coolest zone stops growth at the end.":"Esparcir las esporas es la segunda fase, voltear el arroz forma parte de la tercera y llevarlo a la zona más fresca detiene el crecimiento al final.","How is the rice for kōji cooled?":"¿Cómo se enfría el arroz destinado al kōji?","Spread on mats, it cools naturally":"Extendido sobre esteras, se enfría de forma natural","Plunged into iced water":"Sumergido en agua helada","Put in a freezer":"Metido en un congelador","Mixed with distilled alcohol":"Mezclado con alcohol destilado","The rice is spread on mats and left to cool by itself.":"El arroz se extiende sobre esteras y se deja enfriar solo.","Iced water would make it too wet and a freezer too cold for the mould. Distilled alcohol has nothing to do with kōji.":"El agua helada lo mojaría demasiado y el congelador lo dejaría demasiado frío para el moho. El alcohol destilado no tiene nada que ver con el kōji.","In which part of the room are the mould spores spread?":"¿En qué zona de la sala se esparcen las esporas del moho?","The warmest, most humid part":"En la zona más cálida y húmeda","The coolest, driest part":"En la zona más fresca y seca","Outdoors, in the sun":"Al aire libre, al sol","In the fermentation tank":"En el depósito de fermentación","Warmth and humidity get the mould growing quickly.":"El calor y la humedad hacen arrancar rápido el moho.","The coolest zone is used at the end, to stop growth. Kōji is made in its own rooms, not outdoors or in the tank.":"La zona más fresca se usa al final, para detener el crecimiento. El kōji se hace en sus salas, no al aire libre ni en el depósito.","Why is the rice turned regularly by hand during the initial mould growth?":"¿Por qué se voltea el arroz a mano con regularidad durante el primer crecimiento del moho?","So that the mould grows evenly":"Para que el moho crezca de forma uniforme","To remove the mould":"Para quitar el moho","To cool it below freezing":"Para enfriarlo bajo cero","To add the yeast":"Para añadir la levadura","Turning spreads warmth and moisture so the growth is even.":"Voltear el arroz reparte calor y humedad y hace el crecimiento uniforme.","The mould is wanted, not removed. Yeast comes in at fermentation, and kōji is never taken below freezing.":"El moho se busca, no se quita. La levadura entra en la fermentación, y en el kōji no se baja de cero.","How is mould growth slowed and then stopped?":"¿Cómo se frena y luego se detiene el crecimiento del moho?","By moving the rice to cooler zones, finally the coolest":"Llevando el arroz a zonas más frescas, hasta la más fresca","By adding lots of hot water":"Añadiendo mucha agua caliente","By steaming the rice again":"Volviendo a cocer el arroz al vapor","By putting the rice in the dark":"Poniendo el arroz a oscuras","Less warmth and humidity slow the mould; the coolest zone stops it.":"Menos calor y humedad frenan el moho; la zona más fresca lo detiene.","Hot water and steam would add warmth and moisture, the opposite of what is needed. Light is not the lever: temperature and humidity are.":"El agua caliente y el vapor aumentarían calor y humedad, justo lo contrario. La luz no es la palanca: lo son la temperatura y la humedad.","Why does the brewer slow the mould instead of letting it grow freely?":"¿Por qué el elaborador frena el moho en lugar de dejarlo crecer libremente?","To get exactly the right amount of mould":"Para obtener exactamente la cantidad de moho deseada","Because mould is a fault":"Porque el moho es un defecto","To make the sake sparkling":"Para hacer el sake espumoso","To raise the polishing ratio":"Para subir el grado de pulido","The goal is measured growth: neither too much nor too little mould.":"El objetivo es un crecimiento medido: ni demasiado ni demasiado poco moho.","The kōji mould is essential, not a fault. Bubbles and the polishing ratio do not depend on this stage.":"El moho del kōji es imprescindible, no un defecto. Las burbujas y el grado de pulido no dependen de esta fase.","In nearly all sake styles, which ingredient contributes most to the aromas?":"En casi todos los estilos de sake, ¿qué ingrediente aporta más a los aromas?","Distilled alcohol":"El alcohol destilado","Yeast contributes a large share of the aromas in nearly all styles.":"La levadura aporta buena parte de los aromas en casi todos los estilos.","In many styles rice, kōji and water give relatively little flavour. Added alcohol is neutral: it helps extract flavour but brings none of its own.":"En muchos estilos arroz, kōji y agua dan relativamente poco sabor. El alcohol añadido es neutro: ayuda a extraer aromas, pero no aporta los suyos.","What is needed for the fruity, floral aromas typical of ginjō styles?":"¿Qué hace falta para los aromas frutales y florales típicos de los estilos ginjō?","Special yeast strains and lower fermentation temperatures":"Levaduras especiales y temperaturas de fermentación más bajas","Any yeast and higher temperatures":"Cualquier levadura y temperaturas más altas","Lots of water and a long pasteurisation":"Mucha agua y una pasteurización larga","Ageing in oak":"Envejecimiento en roble","Ginjō aromas require special yeast strains and a cool fermentation.":"Los aromas ginjō exigen cepas de levadura especiales y una fermentación fresca.","Warm temperatures give cereal and lactic aromas. Water and pasteurisation do not create fruity scents, and oak is very rarely used in sake.":"Las temperaturas cálidas dan aromas de cereal y lácteos. El agua y la pasteurización no crean perfumes frutales, y el roble apenas se usa en el sake.","What aromas does a warmer fermentation tend to give?":"¿Qué aromas tiende a dar una fermentación más cálida?","Cereal and lactic":"Cereal y lácteos","White flowers and delicate fruit":"Flores blancas y fruta delicada","Dried fruit and meat":"Fruta seca y carne","Caramel and toffee":"Caramelo y toffee","More warmth in fermentation = cereal and lactic aromas.":"Más calor en la fermentación = aromas de cereal y lácteos.","Flowers and delicate fruit come from cool fermentation. Dried fruit and meat belong to koshu; caramel and toffee often signal an oxidised or old sake.":"Flores y fruta delicada vienen de la fermentación fresca. La fruta seca y la carne son propias del koshu; caramelo y toffee suelen indicar un sake oxidado o viejo.","Which combination usually produces a fruity, floral sake with little acidity and umami?":"¿Qué combinación suele dar un sake frutal y floral, con poca acidez y umami?","Highly polished rice, special yeasts, cool fermentation":"Arroz muy pulido, levaduras especiales, fermentación fresca","Lightly polished rice, warm fermentation":"Arroz poco pulido, fermentación cálida","Lightly polished rice, special yeasts, ageing":"Arroz poco pulido, levaduras especiales, envejecimiento","Highly polished rice, warm fermentation, no filtration":"Arroz muy pulido, fermentación cálida, sin filtrar","These are the three factors of the ginjō style: heavy polishing, special yeasts, low temperature.":"Son los tres factores del estilo ginjō: pulido intenso, levaduras especiales, temperatura baja.","Lightly polished rice and warm fermentation give cereal, lactic notes with more acidity and umami. Filtration is required by law anyway.":"Arroz poco pulido y fermentación cálida dan notas de cereal y lácteas, con más acidez y umami. La filtración es obligatoria por ley en cualquier caso.","During fermentation, which two levers does the brewer use to steer style?":"Durante la fermentación, ¿qué dos palancas usa el elaborador para orientar el estilo?","Choice of yeast and temperature":"La elección de la levadura y la temperatura","Choice of bottle and light":"La elección de la botella y la luz","Type of wood and time in cask":"El tipo de madera y el tiempo en barrica","Amount of added sugar and gas":"La cantidad de azúcar añadido y el gas","Yeast and fermentation temperature change the aroma profile a great deal.":"La levadura y la temperatura de fermentación cambian mucho el perfil aromático.","Bottle and light concern storage, not fermentation. Wood is rare in sake, and sugar is not added to steer the style.":"La botella y la luz tienen que ver con la conservación, no con la fermentación. La madera es rara en el sake, y no se añade azúcar para orientar el estilo.","Brown rice to steamed rice":"Del arroz integral al arroz al vapor","Polishing → washing → soaking → steaming.":"Pulido → lavado → remojo → cocción al vapor.","The three zones of a grain":"Las tres zonas del grano","Brown outer, white middle, almost pure starch core.":"Exteriores marrones, intermedias blancas, núcleo casi puro almidón.","Light polishing gives…":"Un pulido ligero da…","More acidity and umami, cereal and lactic aromas.":"Más acidez y umami, aromas de cereal y lácteos.","Heavy polishing gives…":"Un pulido intenso da…","Less acidity and umami, fruity and floral aromas.":"Menos acidez y umami, aromas frutales y florales.","Polishing ratio":"Grado de pulido","Percentage of the grain that REMAINS after polishing; set by law.":"Porcentaje del grano que QUEDA tras el pulido; fijado por ley.","70% or less":"70 % o menos","Honjōzō and most junmai.":"Honjōzō y la mayoría de los junmai.","60% or less":"60 % o menos","Ginjō and junmai ginjō.":"Ginjō y junmai ginjō.","50% or less":"50 % o menos","Daiginjō and junmai daiginjō.":"Daiginjō y junmai daiginjō.","The four kōji stages":"Las cuatro fases del kōji","Cool, spread spores, initial growth, control and stop.":"Enfriar, esparcir esporas, primer crecimiento, control y parada.","Where does the mould start?":"¿Dónde arranca el moho?","In the warmest, most humid part of the kōji room.":"En la zona más cálida y húmeda de la sala del kōji.","How is the mould stopped?":"¿Cómo se detiene el moho?","By moving the rice to the coolest part of the room.":"Llevando el arroz a la zona más fresca de la sala.","Ginjō aromas: how?":"Aromas ginjō: ¿cómo?","Special yeast strains + cool fermentation.":"Levaduras especiales + fermentación a baja temperatura.","Warmer fermentation":"Fermentación más cálida","Cereal and lactic aromas.":"Aromas de cereal y lácteos.","Futsū-shu, the everyday sake":"Futsū-shu, el sake de cada día","Sake is divided into categories and grades. The main split is between basic and premium sake; premium sake is then divided into several grades. The simple, widespread basic sake is called futsū-shu in Japanese.":"El sake se divide en categorías y grados. La gran división es entre sake básico y sake premium; el premium, a su vez, se divide en varios grados. El sake básico, sencillo y muy extendido, se llama en japonés futsū-shu.","Futsū-shu fits the portrait of typical sake exactly: mostly clear and colourless, sometimes pale yellow or green, 15–17% abv, slightly sweet and lightly acidic, with delicate lactic and fruity flavours. It is the reference point for understanding the premium grades.":"El futsū-shu encaja de lleno en el retrato del sake típico: casi siempre transparente e incoloro, a veces amarillo pálido o verdoso, con un 15–17 % de alcohol, ligeramente dulce y poco ácido, con sabores delicados lácteos y frutales. Es el punto de referencia para entender los grados premium.","Main division: basic and premium sake":"División principal: sake básico y sake premium","Basic sake = futsū-shu":"Sake básico = futsū-shu","Futsū-shu: 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, delicate lactic and fruity notes":"Futsū-shu: 15–17 %, ligeramente dulce, poco ácido, notas lácteas y frutales delicadas","Six premium grades, two style families":"Seis grados premium, dos familias de estilo","Among the premium grades, six matter most. Nearly all have the same strength and colour as basic sake, but they fall into two very different styles. The first covers sakes with pure floral and fruity aromas: the key word is ginjō. Daiginjō literally means 'big ginjō' and marks the sakes with the purest fruity, floral flavours.":"Entre los grados premium, seis son los más importantes. Casi todos tienen la misma graduación y el mismo color que el sake básico, pero se agrupan en dos estilos muy distintos. El primero reúne los sakes con aromas puros de flores y fruta: la palabra clave es ginjō. Daiginjō significa literalmente «gran ginjō» y señala los sakes con los aromas frutales y florales más puros.","The second style covers sakes with cereal and lactic aromas, which usually have more acidity and umami than the ginjō styles. Junmai and honjōzō belong here. In short: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō and junmai daiginjō sit on the fruit-and-flower side; junmai and honjōzō on the side of cereal, lactic notes, acidity and umami.":"El segundo estilo reúne los sakes con aromas de cereal y lácteos, que suelen tener más acidez y umami que los estilos ginjō. Aquí están el junmai y el honjōzō. En resumen: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō y junmai daiginjō están del lado de la fruta y las flores; junmai y honjōzō, del lado del cereal, lo lácteo, la acidez y el umami.","Six main premium grades, mostly with the strength and colour of basic sake":"Seis grados premium principales, casi todos con la graduación y el color del básico","Ginjō style: pure fruity, floral aromas, less acidity and umami":"Estilo ginjō: aromas puros de fruta y flores, menos acidez y umami","Daiginjō = 'big ginjō': the purest aromas":"Daiginjō = «gran ginjō»: los aromas más puros","Junmai and honjōzō: cereal and lactic, more acidity and umami":"Junmai y honjōzō: cereal y lácteos, más acidez y umami","Junmai: pure rice, and the full grid":"Junmai: arroz puro, y la cuadrícula completa","There is a second way to split the six grades. Three carry the word junmai, meaning 'pure rice': it shows that NO distilled alcohol was added before filtration. So junmai ginjō is a style similar to ginjō; the only difference is that junmai ginjō has had no alcohol added. The same goes for daiginjō and junmai daiginjō, and for honjōzō (with alcohol) and junmai (without).":"Hay una segunda forma de dividir los seis grados. Tres llevan la palabra junmai, que significa «arroz puro»: indica que antes de filtrar NO se ha añadido alcohol destilado. Así, el junmai ginjō es un estilo parecido al ginjō; la única diferencia es que el junmai ginjō no ha recibido alcohol añadido. Lo mismo vale para daiginjō y junmai daiginjō, y para honjōzō (con alcohol) y junmai (sin él).","Now put it all in a two-column grid. Left, no added alcohol: junmai daiginjō (≤50%), junmai ginjō (≤60%), junmai (usually 70%). Right, with added alcohol: daiginjō (≤50%), ginjō (≤60%), honjōzō (≤70%). The top two rows, fruity and floral, come from highly polished rice, special yeasts and cool fermentation; the bottom row, cereal and lactic, from lightly polished rice and warmer fermentation.":"Pongámoslo todo en una cuadrícula de dos columnas. A la izquierda, sin alcohol añadido: junmai daiginjō (≤50 %), junmai ginjō (≤60 %), junmai (normalmente 70 %). A la derecha, con alcohol añadido: daiginjō (≤50 %), ginjō (≤60 %), honjōzō (≤70 %). Las dos filas de arriba, frutales y florales, nacen de arroz muy pulido, levaduras especiales y fermentación fresca; la fila de abajo, de cereal y láctea, de arroz poco pulido y fermentación más cálida.","Junmai = 'pure rice': no distilled alcohol added":"Junmai = «arroz puro»: sin alcohol destilado añadido","Pairs: junmai daiginjō/daiginjō, junmai ginjō/ginjō, junmai/honjōzō":"Parejas: junmai daiginjō/daiginjō, junmai ginjō/ginjō, junmai/honjōzō","Same style within each pair: only the added alcohol differs":"Mismo estilo en cada pareja: solo cambia el alcohol añadido","Ginjō: highly polished + special yeasts + cool; junmai/honjōzō: lightly polished + warmer":"Ginjō: muy pulido + levaduras especiales + fresco; junmai/honjōzō: poco pulido + más cálido","Four words, seven kanji":"Cuatro palabras, siete kanji","Sake labels are mostly written in Japanese, with only a few words in the Latin alphabet. To find your way, you only need to recognise four key terms: junmai, honjōzō, ginjō and daiginjō. Each term breaks down into sounds, and each sound matches a symbol called a kanji.":"Las etiquetas de sake están escritas sobre todo en japonés, con muy pocas palabras en alfabeto latino. Para orientarse basta con reconocer cuatro términos clave: junmai, honjōzō, ginjō y daiginjō. Cada término se divide en sonidos, y cada sonido corresponde a un símbolo llamado kanji.","Junmai = jun 純 + mai 米. Honjōzō = hon 本 + jō 醸 + zō 造. Ginjō = gin 吟 + jō 醸. Daiginjō = dai 大 + gin 吟 + jō 醸. In total there are only seven kanji to learn, because gin 吟 and jō 醸 repeat. A memory trick: 大 (dai, big) looks like a person with arms spread wide, 'big' like daiginjō, the 'big ginjō'.":"Junmai = jun 純 + mai 米. Honjōzō = hon 本 + jō 醸 + zō 造. Ginjō = gin 吟 + jō 醸. Daiginjō = dai 大 + gin 吟 + jō 醸. En total solo hay siete kanji que aprender, porque gin 吟 y jō 醸 se repiten. Un truco: 大 (dai, grande) parece una persona con los brazos abiertos, «grande» como el daiginjō, el «gran ginjō».","Labels mostly in Japanese: recognise 4 terms":"Etiquetas casi todas en japonés: reconocer 4 términos","純米 junmai · 本醸造 honjōzō · 吟醸 ginjō · 大吟醸 daiginjō":"純米 junmai · 本醸造 honjōzō · 吟醸 ginjō · 大吟醸 daiginjō","Only 7 kanji: gin 吟 and jō 醸 repeat":"Solo 7 kanji: gin 吟 y jō 醸 se repiten","Nama and nigori":"Nama y nigori","There are four important speciality styles: nama, nigori, sparkling and koshu. Nama means unpasteurised sake. Because it is less stable than other sakes, most nama should be drunk soon after release and kept refrigerated at all times. On release it can taste especially lively and fresh, but it can quickly develop spicy, malty aromas that are not to everyone's taste.":"Hay cuatro estilos especiales importantes: nama, nigori, espumoso y koshu. Nama significa sake sin pasteurizar. Como es menos estable que los demás, la mayoría de los nama deben beberse poco después de salir al mercado y guardarse siempre en el frigorífico. Al salir puede resultar especialmente vivo y fresco, pero puede desarrollar pronto aromas especiados y malteados que no gustan a todo el mundo.","A pronunciation note: in Japanese the 's' of nama-sake softens to a 'z', so it is usually spelled nama-zake. Nigori, on the other hand, means sake that has been roughly filtered: it is cloudy because of suspended rice particles. The style varies with how much solid matter is kept: some nigori are lightly cloudy, others thick-textured with lumps of rice.":"Una curiosidad de pronunciación: en japonés la «s» de nama-sake se suaviza en «z», por eso suele escribirse nama-zake. Nigori, en cambio, es un sake filtrado de forma grosera: está turbio porque contiene partículas de arroz en suspensión. El estilo cambia mucho según cuántos sólidos se dejan: algunos nigori están apenas velados y otros son densos, con trocitos de arroz.","Nama: unpasteurised, less stable, always refrigerated, drink soon":"Nama: sin pasteurizar, menos estable, siempre en frío, beber pronto","Young nama: lively and fresh; later can turn spicy and malty":"Nama joven: vivo y fresco; después puede volverse especiado y malteado","Usually spelled nama-zake":"Suele escribirse nama-zake","Nigori: roughly filtered, cloudy from rice particles":"Nigori: filtrado grosero, turbio por las partículas de arroz","Sparkling sake and koshu":"Sake espumoso y koshu","As with any sparkling drink, the bubbles in sparkling sake come from carbon dioxide dissolved in the liquid. There are various techniques for getting it into bottled sake. Some sparkling sakes are very light in texture and low in alcohol; others are richer-textured and more complex, and can even be nigori too. Japanese terms for these sakes exist but are little used outside Japan.":"Como en toda bebida con burbujas, las del sake espumoso vienen del dióxido de carbono disuelto en el líquido. Hay distintas técnicas para disolverlo en el sake embotellado. Algunos sakes espumosos son muy ligeros de textura y de poco alcohol; otros tienen una textura más rica y más complejidad, e incluso pueden ser también nigori. Existen términos japoneses para ellos, pero fuera de Japón se usan poco.","Koshu is the name for aged sake. It can be aged in various vessels: storage tanks, terracotta, glass bottles, wood (though oak is very rarely used). Some brewers age at room temperature, others at low temperatures, sometimes below freezing: hence a wide range of styles. Most koshu is amber or brown, richly textured and sweet, with pronounced aromas of nuts, dried fruit and even meat and pickled vegetables; but some aged sakes are paler and more delicate.":"Koshu es el nombre de los sakes envejecidos. Pueden envejecer en distintos recipientes: depósitos, terracota, botellas de vidrio, madera (aunque el roble se usa muy poco). Algunas bodegas envejecen a temperatura ambiente y otras a baja temperatura, a veces bajo cero: de ahí una gran variedad de estilos. La mayoría de los koshu son ámbar o marrones, de textura rica y dulces, con aromas marcados de frutos secos, fruta pasa e incluso carne y verduras encurtidas; pero también hay koshu más pálidos y delicados.","Sparkling: bubbles of dissolved carbon dioxide; from light and low-alcohol to rich and complex":"Espumoso: burbujas de dióxido de carbono disuelto; de ligero y poco alcohólico a rico y complejo","Koshu = aged sake; various vessels, oak is rare":"Koshu = sake envejecido; recipientes variados, el roble es raro","Typical koshu: amber/brown, rich, sweet, nuts, dried fruit, even meat and pickles":"Koshu típico: ámbar/marrón, rico, dulce, frutos secos, pasas, incluso carne y encurtidos","Speciality styles and grades combine":"Estilos especiales y grados: se combinan","A point that confuses many: speciality styles are not a separate category from the grades. A nama, nigori, sparkling sake or koshu can be a futsū-shu or any of the premium grades. A junmai ginjō, for example, could also be nama, nigori, sparkling, or even a combination of these styles.":"Un punto que confunde a muchos: los estilos especiales no son una categoría aparte de los grados. Un nama, un nigori, un espumoso o un koshu puede ser un futsū-shu o cualquiera de los grados premium. Un junmai ginjō, por ejemplo, podría ser también nama, nigori, espumoso o incluso una combinación de estos estilos.","Think of the grade as 'how the sake was made' (polishing, alcohol added or not) and the speciality style as 'one extra treatment': no pasteurisation, rough filtration, bubbles, ageing. Both pieces of information can therefore appear on one label, for example a 'junmai nigori nama'.":"Piensa en el grado como «cómo se hizo el sake» (pulido, alcohol añadido o no) y en el estilo especial como «un tratamiento más»: sin pasteurizar, filtrado grosero, burbujas, envejecimiento. Por eso en una etiqueta pueden aparecer las dos cosas, por ejemplo un «junmai nigori nama».","Speciality styles apply to futsū-shu and to every premium grade":"Los estilos especiales se aplican al futsū-shu y a cualquier grado premium","One sake can combine several speciality styles":"Un mismo sake puede combinar varios estilos especiales","Grade = how it is made; speciality = one extra treatment":"Grado = cómo se hace; estilo especial = tratamiento extra","What is basic sake called in Japanese?":"¿Cómo se llama en japonés el sake básico?","Junmai":"Junmai","Koshu":"Koshu","Daiginjō":"Daiginjō","Futsū-shu is the name for simple, basic sake.":"Futsū-shu es el nombre del sake básico y sencillo.","Junmai and daiginjō are premium grades; koshu is the speciality style for aged sake.":"Junmai y daiginjō son grados premium; koshu es el estilo especial de los sakes envejecidos.","What is the main division of sake categories?":"¿Cuál es la gran división de las categorías de sake?","Basic sake and premium sake":"Sake básico y sake premium","White sake and red sake":"Sake blanco y sake tinto","Dry sake and sweet sake":"Sake seco y sake dulce","Japanese and foreign sake":"Sake japonés y sake extranjero","First comes basic (futsū-shu) versus premium, then premium splits into grades.":"Primero se distingue entre básico (futsū-shu) y premium, y luego el premium se divide en grados.","Sake is not red. Sweetness and origin are not the main basis of the categories.":"El sake no es tinto. El dulzor y el origen no son el criterio principal de las categorías.","What do nearly all premium sakes share with basic sake?":"¿Qué tienen en común casi todos los sakes premium con el básico?","The same alcohol level and colour":"La misma graduación y el mismo color","The same polishing ratio":"El mismo grado de pulido","The same fruity aromas":"Los mismos aromas frutales","The same price":"El mismo precio","Most premium sakes have similar strength and colour to futsū-shu; aromas and style change.":"La mayoría de los premium tiene graduación y color parecidos al futsū-shu; cambian los aromas y el estilo.","Polishing is exactly what sets the premium grades apart. Aromas differ between the two style families.":"El pulido es justo lo que distingue los grados premium. Los aromas varían entre las dos familias de estilo.","Which label word indicates the style with pure floral and fruity aromas?":"¿Qué palabra indica en la etiqueta el estilo de aromas puros de flores y fruta?","Ginjō":"Ginjō","Nama":"Nama","Ginjō is the key word for the fruity, floral style.":"Ginjō es la palabra clave del estilo frutal y floral.","Honjōzō belongs to the cereal, lactic style. Nama only means unpasteurised, and futsū-shu is basic sake.":"El honjōzō pertenece al estilo de cereal y lácteo. Nama solo indica que no está pasteurizado, y futsū-shu es el sake básico.","What does daiginjō literally mean?":"¿Qué significa literalmente daiginjō?","Big ginjō":"Gran ginjō","Aged sake":"Sake envejecido","Raw sake":"Sake crudo","Dai means 'big': daiginjō is the 'big ginjō', with the purest aromas.":"Dai significa «grande»: daiginjō es el «gran ginjō», con los aromas más puros.","'Pure rice' is junmai and 'aged sake' is koshu. Nama (unpasteurised) is sometimes described as 'raw', but that is not daiginjō.":"«Arroz puro» es junmai y «sake envejecido» es koshu. Al nama (sin pasteurizar) a veces se le llama «crudo», pero no es daiginjō.","Which sakes usually have cereal and lactic aromas with more acidity and umami?":"¿Qué sakes suelen tener aromas de cereal y lácteos, con más acidez y umami?","Junmai and honjōzō":"Junmai y honjōzō","Ginjō and daiginjō":"Ginjō y daiginjō","Junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō":"Junmai ginjō y junmai daiginjō","Daiginjō and junmai daiginjō":"Daiginjō y junmai daiginjō","Junmai and honjōzō make up the cereal, lactic family.":"Junmai y honjōzō forman la familia de cereal y láctea.","All the other options contain the word ginjō: they belong to the fruity, floral style with less acidity and umami.":"Todas las demás opciones contienen la palabra ginjō: pertenecen al estilo frutal y floral, con menos acidez y umami.","What does junmai mean?":"¿Qué significa junmai?","Pure rice: no distilled alcohol added":"Arroz puro: sin alcohol destilado añadido","Rice polished to 50%":"Arroz pulido al 50 %","Unfiltered sake":"Sake sin filtrar","Unpasteurised sake":"Sake sin pasteurizar","Junmai means 'pure rice': no distilled alcohol was added before filtration.":"Junmai significa «arroz puro»: antes de filtrar no se añadió alcohol destilado.","50% is the daiginjō threshold. All sake is filtered by law; unpasteurised sake is called nama.":"El 50 % es el umbral de los daiginjō. Todo sake se filtra por ley; el sake sin pasteurizar se llama nama.","What is the ONLY difference between a ginjō and a junmai ginjō?":"¿Cuál es la ÚNICA diferencia entre un ginjō y un junmai ginjō?","The junmai ginjō has no added distilled alcohol":"El junmai ginjō no lleva alcohol destilado añadido","The junmai ginjō is polished to 70%":"El junmai ginjō está pulido al 70 %","The junmai ginjō is cloudy":"El junmai ginjō es turbio","The junmai ginjō is aged":"El junmai ginjō está envejecido","The style is similar; only the added alcohol differs, absent in junmai ginjō.":"El estilo es parecido; solo cambia el alcohol añadido, ausente en el junmai ginjō.","Both require rice polished to 60% or less. Cloudiness (nigori) and ageing (koshu) are speciality styles, not the difference between these grades.":"Ambos exigen arroz pulido al 60 % o menos. La turbidez (nigori) y el envejecimiento (koshu) son estilos especiales, no la diferencia entre estos dos grados.","A sake is polished to 65% and had distilled alcohol added before filtration. Which grade can it carry?":"Un sake está pulido al 65 % y recibió alcohol destilado antes de filtrar. ¿Qué grado puede llevar?","With added alcohol and polishing of 70% or less (but above 60%), the grade is honjōzō.":"Con alcohol añadido y pulido del 70 % o menos (pero por encima del 60 %), el grado es honjōzō.","Ginjō would need 60% or less. Junmai and junmai ginjō rule out added alcohol.":"Para el ginjō haría falta un 60 % o menos. Junmai y junmai ginjō excluyen el alcohol añadido.","A sake is polished to 45% with no added alcohol. What is the highest grade it can carry?":"Un sake está pulido al 45 % y sin alcohol añadido. ¿Qué grado más alto puede llevar?","Rice at 50% or less and no added alcohol: junmai daiginjō.":"Arroz al 50 % o menos y sin alcohol añadido: junmai daiginjō.","Daiginjō and honjōzō mean added alcohol. Junmai ginjō would be possible, but it is not the highest grade for rice at 45%.":"Daiginjō y honjōzō indican alcohol añadido. Junmai ginjō sería posible, pero no es el grado más alto para un arroz al 45 %.","How many of the six main premium grades contain the word junmai?":"¿Cuántos de los seis grados premium principales contienen la palabra junmai?","Three":"Tres","Two":"Dos","Four":"Cuatro","Six":"Seis","Junmai, junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō: three grades with no added alcohol.":"Junmai, junmai ginjō y junmai daiginjō: tres grados sin alcohol añadido.","The other three (honjōzō, ginjō, daiginjō) have distilled alcohol added before filtration.":"Los otros tres (honjōzō, ginjō, daiginjō) llevan alcohol destilado añadido antes de filtrar.","A customer wants a premium sake with pure fruity, floral aromas, made from rice only with no added alcohol. What do you suggest?":"Un cliente busca un sake premium de aromas puros de fruta y flores, hecho solo con arroz y sin alcohol añadido. ¿Qué le propones?","Junmai ginjō or junmai daiginjō":"Junmai ginjō o junmai daiginjō","Ginjō or daiginjō":"Ginjō o daiginjō","Ginjō = fruit and flowers; junmai = no added alcohol: both words are needed.":"Ginjō = fruta y flores; junmai = sin alcohol añadido: hacen falta las dos palabras.","Ginjō and daiginjō without junmai have added alcohol. Honjōzō has added alcohol and a cereal style; futsū-shu is not premium.":"Ginjō y daiginjō sin junmai llevan alcohol añadido. El honjōzō lleva alcohol añadido y estilo de cereal; el futsū-shu no es premium.","Which combination of factors gives the junmai and honjōzō style?":"¿Qué combinación de factores da el estilo de junmai y honjōzō?","Lightly polished rice and warmer fermentation":"Arroz poco pulido y fermentación más cálida","Highly polished rice and cool fermentation":"Arroz muy pulido y fermentación fresca","Long ageing and rough filtration":"Envejecimiento largo y filtrado grosero","No pasteurisation and carbon dioxide":"Sin pasteurizar y con dióxido de carbono","Light polishing and warmer temperature give cereal, lactic notes, acidity and umami.":"Poco pulido y temperatura más alta dan cereal, notas lácteas, acidez y umami.","Highly polished rice and cool fermentation are the ginjō recipe. The other options describe speciality styles (koshu, nigori, nama, sparkling).":"Arroz muy pulido y fermentación fresca son la receta ginjō. Las demás opciones describen estilos especiales (koshu, nigori, nama, espumoso).","How many kanji must you learn to recognise the four key label terms?":"¿Cuántos kanji hay que aprender para reconocer los cuatro términos clave de la etiqueta?","Seven":"Siete","Nine":"Nueve","Twelve":"Doce","There are seven, because gin 吟 and jō 醸 appear in more than one term.":"Son siete, porque gin 吟 y jō 醸 aparecen en varios términos.","Counting every sound including repeats gives nine; removing the duplicate gin and jō leaves seven different symbols.":"Contando todos los sonidos con repeticiones salen nueve; quitando los duplicados de gin y jō quedan siete símbolos distintos.","Which term is written 純米?":"¿Qué término se escribe 純米?","純 (jun) + 米 (mai) = junmai, 'pure rice'.":"純 (jun) + 米 (mai) = junmai, «arroz puro».","Ginjō is 吟醸, honjōzō is 本醸造, daiginjō is 大吟醸.":"Ginjō es 吟醸, honjōzō es 本醸造, daiginjō es 大吟醸.","A label shows 大吟醸. Which grade is it?":"En una etiqueta aparece 大吟醸. ¿De qué grado se trata?","大 (dai) + 吟 (gin) + 醸 (jō) = daiginjō.":"大 (dai) + 吟 (gin) + 醸 (jō) = daiginjō.","Ginjō would be just 吟醸, without 大. Junmai is 純米 and honjōzō 本醸造.":"El ginjō sería solo 吟醸, sin 大. Junmai es 純米 y honjōzō 本醸造.","Which kanji appears in both ginjō and honjōzō?":"¿Qué kanji aparece tanto en ginjō como en honjōzō?","醸 (jō)":"醸 (jō)","吟 (gin)":"吟 (gin)","米 (mai)":"米 (mai)","大 (dai)":"大 (dai)","The sound jō, 醸, is in ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) and daiginjō (大吟醸).":"El sonido jō, 醸, está en ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) y daiginjō (大吟醸).","吟 (gin) is in ginjō and daiginjō but not honjōzō. 米 is only in junmai and 大 only in daiginjō.":"吟 (gin) está en ginjō y daiginjō pero no en honjōzō. 米 solo está en junmai y 大 solo en daiginjō.","A label shows 純米吟醸. What does it indicate?":"Una etiqueta muestra 純米吟醸. ¿Qué indica?","Junmai ginjō: fruity style, no added alcohol":"Junmai ginjō: estilo frutal, sin alcohol añadido","Honjōzō: cereal style, with added alcohol":"Honjōzō: estilo de cereal, con alcohol añadido","Daiginjō: with added alcohol, rice at 50%":"Daiginjō: con alcohol añadido, arroz al 50 %","Futsū-shu: basic sake":"Futsū-shu: sake básico","純米 (junmai) + 吟醸 (ginjō): fruity and floral, with no added distilled alcohol.":"純米 (junmai) + 吟醸 (ginjō): frutal y floral, sin alcohol destilado añadido.","There is no 本醸造 (honjōzō) and no 大 (dai). Futsū-shu does not carry these premium terms.":"No aparece 本醸造 (honjōzō) ni 大 (dai). El futsū-shu no lleva estos términos premium.","What does the term nama indicate?":"¿Qué indica el término nama?","An unpasteurised sake":"Un sake sin pasteurizar","A cloudy sake":"Un sake turbio","An aged sake":"Un sake envejecido","A sake with no added alcohol":"Un sake sin alcohol añadido","Nama means the sake has skipped pasteurisation.":"Nama significa que el sake no se ha pasteurizado.","Cloudy is nigori, aged is koshu, no added alcohol is junmai.":"Turbio es nigori, envejecido es koshu y sin alcohol añadido es junmai.","How should a nama-zake be stored?":"¿Cómo hay que conservar un nama-zake?","Always refrigerated, drunk soon after release":"Siempre en el frigorífico, para beber poco después de salir","At room temperature for a few years":"A temperatura ambiente durante unos años","Lying down, in sunlight":"Tumbado, a la luz del sol","In an oak cask":"En una barrica de roble","Without pasteurisation nama is less stable: constant cold and quick drinking.":"Sin pasteurizar, el nama es menos estable: frío constante y consumo rápido.","Heat and time spoil it, and strong light harms any sake. Sake bottles are stored upright, and oak has nothing to do with it.":"El calor y el tiempo lo estropean, y la luz fuerte daña cualquier sake. Las botellas de sake se guardan de pie, y el roble no tiene nada que ver.","What aromas can a nama quickly develop?":"¿Qué aromas puede desarrollar pronto un nama?","Spicy and malty":"Especiados y malteados","White flowers and pear":"Flores blancas y pera","Citrus and mint":"Cítricos y menta","Vanilla and coconut":"Vainilla y coco","On release it is fresh and lively, but it can soon turn spicy and malty.":"Al salir es fresco y vivo, pero puede volverse pronto especiado y malteado.","Flowers and pear are ginjō notes, not linked to nama. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, which is hardly used for sake.":"Flores y pera son notas ginjō, no ligadas al nama. Vainilla y coco vienen del roble, que apenas se usa en el sake.","Why is a nigori cloudy?":"¿Por qué un nigori es turbio?","It is roughly filtered and contains rice particles":"Se filtra de forma grosera y contiene partículas de arroz","It has never been filtered":"Nunca se ha filtrado","Milk is added to it":"Se le añade leche","It is aged in terracotta":"Se envejece en terracota","Rough filtration leaves suspended rice particles in the sake.":"El filtrado grosero deja partículas de arroz en suspensión en el sake.","Filtration is legally required: nigori is filtered, just lightly. No milk is used, and terracotta relates to some koshu.":"La filtración es obligatoria por ley: el nigori se filtra, pero poco. No se usa leche, y la terracota tiene que ver con algunos koshu.","Which statement about nigori is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el nigori es correcta?","It can be lightly cloudy or thick with rice fragments":"Puede estar apenas velado o ser denso con trocitos de arroz","It always turns clear after a few days":"Siempre se vuelve transparente a los pocos días","It is always sparkling":"Siempre es espumoso","It is always a futsū-shu":"Siempre es un futsū-shu","The style varies with how much solid matter is kept: from slightly cloudy to very thick.":"El estilo varía según los sólidos que se dejan: de ligeramente turbio a muy denso.","A nigori can be sparkling, but need not be. Speciality styles combine with any grade, not just futsū-shu.":"Un nigori puede ser espumoso, pero no tiene por qué. Los estilos especiales se combinan con cualquier grado, no solo con el futsū-shu.","Where do the bubbles in sparkling sake come from?":"¿De dónde vienen las burbujas del sake espumoso?","Carbon dioxide dissolved in the liquid":"Del dióxido de carbono disuelto en el líquido","Oxygen from the air":"Del oxígeno del aire","The added distilled alcohol":"Del alcohol destilado añadido","The rice particles":"De las partículas de arroz","As in any sparkling drink, they are dissolved carbon dioxide.":"Como en toda bebida con burbujas, son dióxido de carbono disuelto.","Oxygen spoils sake rather than making it fizzy. Rice particles make it cloudy (nigori), not sparkling.":"El oxígeno estropea el sake en vez de darle burbujas. Las partículas de arroz lo enturbian (nigori), no lo hacen espumoso.","Which description of sparkling sake is correct?":"¿Qué descripción del sake espumoso es correcta?","It ranges from light and low-alcohol to rich and complex, and can be nigori":"Va de ligero y poco alcohólico a rico y complejo, y puede ser nigori","It is always 20% abv":"Siempre tiene un 20 % de alcohol","It is made with a single technique":"Se hace con una única técnica","It can never be cloudy":"Nunca puede ser turbio","Styles vary: some light and low in alcohol, others richer, even cloudy.":"Los estilos son variados: algunos ligeros y de poco alcohol, otros más ricos, incluso turbios.","Several techniques exist for dissolving carbon dioxide. Many sparkling sakes are lighter, not 20%, and some are also nigori.":"Hay varias técnicas para disolver el dióxido de carbono. Muchos espumosos son más ligeros, no del 20 %, y algunos son también nigori.","What is a koshu?":"¿Qué es un koshu?","A sparkling sake":"Un sake espumoso","A basic sake":"Un sake básico","Koshu is the name for aged sakes.":"Koshu es el nombre de los sakes envejecidos.","Sparkling, unpasteurised (nama) and basic (futsū-shu) are other categories.":"Espumoso, sin pasteurizar (nama) y básico (futsū-shu) son otras categorías.","Which vessel is VERY RARELY used to age sake?":"¿Qué recipiente se usa MUY POCO para envejecer el sake?","The oak cask":"La barrica de roble","The storage tank":"El depósito","The glass bottle":"La botella de vidrio","Terracotta":"La terracota","Wood can be used, but oak is very rare for sake.":"Se puede usar madera, pero el roble es muy raro en el sake.","Tanks, glass and terracotta are all used for ageing koshu.":"Depósitos, vidrio y terracota se usan todos para envejecer el koshu.","What is a typical koshu like?":"¿Cómo suele ser un koshu?","Amber or brown, rich, sweet, with dried fruit and nut notes":"Ámbar o marrón, rico, dulce, con notas de fruta seca y nueces","Colourless, very light, with green apple notes":"Incoloro, muy ligero, con notas de manzana verde","Cloudy, with rice fragments":"Turbio, con trocitos de arroz","Sparkling and low in alcohol":"Espumoso y de poco alcohol","Most koshu is amber or brown, rich, sweet and highly aromatic.":"La mayoría de los koshu son ámbar o marrones, ricos, dulces y muy aromáticos.","Paler, more delicate koshu exist, but they are not the norm. Cloudy suggests nigori and fizzy suggests sparkling sake.":"Hay koshu más pálidos y delicados, pero no son lo habitual. Turbio indica nigori y con burbujas, espumoso.","Why do koshu vary so much?":"¿Por qué los koshu son tan distintos entre sí?","They are aged in different vessels and at different temperatures, even below freezing":"Se envejecen en recipientes y a temperaturas distintas, incluso bajo cero","They are made from different grape varieties":"Se hacen con variedades de uva distintas","They are distilled several times":"Se destilan varias veces","They contain different amounts of hops":"Contienen cantidades distintas de lúpulo","Vessels (tanks, terracotta, glass, wood) and temperatures (room or low) create many styles.":"Recipientes (depósitos, terracota, vidrio, madera) y temperaturas (ambiente o bajas) crean muchos estilos.","Sake is made from rice, not grapes or hops, and is not distilled.":"El sake se hace con arroz, no con uva ni lúpulo, y no se destila.","Can a junmai ginjō also be nama and nigori?":"¿Un junmai ginjō puede ser también nama y nigori?","Yes: speciality styles combine with any grade":"Sí: los estilos especiales se combinan con cualquier grado","No: speciality styles apply only to futsū-shu":"No: los estilos especiales solo valen para el futsū-shu","No: a sake can have only one speciality style":"No: un sake solo puede tener un estilo especial","Only if it is also aged":"Solo si además está envejecido","A premium sake can be nama, nigori, sparkling or koshu, even combining several.":"Un sake premium puede ser nama, nigori, espumoso o koshu, incluso combinando varios.","Speciality styles are not reserved for futsū-shu and do not exclude each other; ageing is not a condition.":"Los estilos especiales no están reservados al futsū-shu ni se excluyen entre sí; envejecer no es una condición.","Basic sake: 15–17%, slightly sweet, lightly acidic, lactic and fruity notes.":"Sake básico: 15–17 %, ligeramente dulce, poco ácido, notas lácteas y frutales.","Key word for the style with pure floral, fruity aromas.":"Palabra clave del estilo de aromas puros de flores y fruta.","'Big ginjō': purest fruity, floral aromas; rice ≤50%; alcohol added.":"«Gran ginjō»: aromas frutales y florales más puros; arroz ≤50 %; alcohol añadido.","'Pure rice': no distilled alcohol added before filtration.":"«Arroz puro»: sin alcohol destilado añadido antes de filtrar.","Rice ≤70%, alcohol added; cereal and lactic, more acidity and umami.":"Arroz ≤70 %, alcohol añadido; cereal y lácteos, más acidez y umami.","Ginjō vs junmai ginjō":"Ginjō vs junmai ginjō","Same style and polishing (≤60%); junmai ginjō has no added alcohol.":"Mismo estilo y pulido (≤60 %); el junmai ginjō no lleva alcohol añadido.","純米":"純米","Junmai (jun + mai).":"Junmai (jun + mai).","本醸造":"本醸造","Honjōzō (hon + jō + zō).":"Honjōzō (hon + jō + zō).","吟醸":"吟醸","Ginjō (gin + jō).":"Ginjō (gin + jō).","大吟醸":"大吟醸","Daiginjō (dai + gin + jō); 大 = big.":"Daiginjō (dai + gin + jō); 大 = grande.","Nama / nama-zake":"Nama / nama-zake","Unpasteurised: always chilled, drink soon; lively, later spicy and malty.":"Sin pasteurizar: siempre en frío, beber pronto; vivo, luego especiado y malteado.","Nigori":"Nigori","Roughly filtered: cloudy from suspended rice particles.":"Filtrado grosero: turbio por las partículas de arroz.","Sparkling sake":"Sake espumoso","Bubbles of dissolved CO2; light to rich, sometimes nigori.":"Burbujas de CO2 disuelto; de ligero a rico, a veces nigori.","Aged sake: often amber, sweet, dried fruit, nuts; oak is rare.":"Sake envejecido: a menudo ámbar, dulce, fruta seca, nueces; el roble es raro.","Getting ready to taste":"Prepararse para catar","To get the most from a tasting you need the same method for every sample: that way your notes describe each sake accurately and are still useful when you reread them later. Before pouring, prepare the setting: no distracting smells (perfume, cooking, smoke) and a white surface for judging the sake's appearance.":"Para sacar el máximo partido a una cata hace falta el mismo método con cada muestra: así las notas describen el sake con precisión y sirven cuando se releen más adelante. Antes de servir conviene preparar el entorno: ningún olor que distraiga (perfume, cocina, humo) y una superficie blanca para observar el aspecto del sake.","The right glass has a wide bowl that narrows towards the top: it concentrates the aromas and makes the nose easier to assess. Finally, your palate should be clean, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee, which would distort everything.":"La copa adecuada tiene un cáliz amplio que se estrecha hacia arriba: concentra los aromas y facilita valorar la nariz. Por último, la boca debe estar limpia, sin sabores persistentes como pasta de dientes o café, que lo falsearían todo.","Same method for every sample":"Mismo método con cada muestra","No distracting smells; a white surface":"Sin olores que distraigan; superficie blanca","Glass with a wide bowl narrowing at the top":"Copa de cáliz amplio que se estrecha arriba","Clean palate: no toothpaste or coffee":"Boca limpia: sin pasta de dientes ni café","A simple grid: appearance, nose, palate":"Una cuadrícula sencilla: aspecto, nariz, boca","Appearance: check clarity, from clear to cloudy (a nigori will be cloudy), and note any bubbles and the colour. Nose: look for the aroma families (fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other) and note intensity and any faults.":"Aspecto: se mira la limpidez, de transparente a turbio (un nigori estará turbio), y se anotan las posibles burbujas y el color. Nariz: se buscan las familias de aromas (frutal/floral, cereal/grano/fruto seco, lácteo, otros) y se anotan la intensidad y los posibles defectos.","Palate: judge flavour intensity (light, medium, pronounced) and the same families as on the nose; then everything else: sweetness, acidity, texture, umami, any rice particles, bubbles and the finish. With this grid a ginjō (fruity, delicate) and a junmai (cereal, more acidity and umami) stand apart at once.":"Boca: se valora la intensidad de sabores (ligera, media, pronunciada) y las mismas familias que en nariz; después el resto: dulzor, acidez, textura, umami, posibles partículas de arroz, burbujas y final. Con esta cuadrícula un ginjō (frutal, delicado) y un junmai (cereal, más acidez y umami) se distinguen enseguida.","Appearance: clear–cloudy, bubbles, colour":"Aspecto: transparente–turbio, burbujas, color","Nose: fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other; intensity, faults":"Nariz: frutal/floral, cereal/fruto seco, lácteo, otros; intensidad, defectos","Palate: light–medium–pronounced; sweetness, acidity, texture, umami, particles, bubbles, finish":"Boca: ligera–media–pronunciada; dulzor, acidez, textura, umami, partículas, burbujas, final","Four rules for storing sake":"Cuatro reglas para conservar el sake","Sake is easily damaged by heat and strong light. Rule one: keep it cool, even for short periods, ideally in the fridge; cold is essential for nama and for protecting the fruity aromas of ginjō. Rule two: drink it young. Most sake is meant to be drunk within about a year of going on sale; after that it loses freshness. Nama loses it within a few months.":"El sake se estropea fácilmente con el calor y la luz fuerte. Primera regla: guardarlo en fresco, aunque sea poco tiempo, idealmente en el frigorífico; el frío es clave para los nama y para proteger los aromas frutales de los ginjō. Segunda regla: beberlo joven. Casi todo el sake está pensado para beberse en el año siguiente a su salida al mercado; después pierde frescura. Los nama la pierden en pocos meses.","Rule three: store the bottle upright. Rule four: avoid bright light, both sunshine and strong artificial light, which can cause faulty aromas. An opened bottle should be resealed and kept in the fridge: it usually lasts about two weeks, sometimes longer; the more delicate ginjō styles stay fresh for about a week.":"Tercera regla: guardar la botella de pie. Cuarta: evitar la luz fuerte, tanto el sol como la luz artificial intensa, que pueden crear aromas defectuosos. Una botella abierta se cierra y se mete en el frigorífico: suele durar unas dos semanas, a veces más; los ginjō, más delicados, se mantienen frescos alrededor de una semana.","Cool, ideally refrigerated (especially nama and ginjō)":"En fresco, idealmente en frigorífico (sobre todo nama y ginjō)","Drink young: within about a year; nama within a few months":"Beber joven: en un año aprox.; nama en pocos meses","Bottle upright, away from bright light":"Botella de pie, lejos de la luz fuerte","Opened: in the fridge, about 2 weeks; ginjō about 1":"Abierta: en frío, unas 2 semanas; ginjō 1 aprox.","Recognising faults":"Reconocer los defectos","The most common faults come from poor storage. Oxidation: a bottle left open too long develops unwelcome caramel and toffee aromas and turns deeper in colour. Out of condition: a bottle that is too old shows caramel, toffee and pickled-vegetable aromas, again with a deeper colour. Nama-hine: nama sakes can develop unpleasant smells of malt, meat and rotting vegetables.":"Los defectos más comunes vienen de una mala conservación. Oxidación: una botella abierta demasiado tiempo desarrolla aromas desagradables de caramelo y toffee y toma un color más oscuro. Fuera de condición: una botella demasiado vieja muestra aromas de caramelo, toffee y verduras encurtidas, también con un color más oscuro. Nama-hine: los nama pueden desarrollar olores desagradables a malta, carne y verdura podrida.","Interestingly, the aromas of oxidation and 'out of condition' resemble those of koshu: the chemical processes are the same. The difference is intention: in koshu they are wanted, in other sakes consumers do not want them. A word on health: in moderation alcohol is not regarded as harmful, but in excess it damages health in the short and long term; it is best to follow your country's official low-risk drinking guidelines.":"Curiosamente, los aromas de la oxidación y del «fuera de condición» se parecen a los del koshu: los procesos químicos son los mismos. La diferencia está en la intención: en el koshu se buscan, en los demás sakes los consumidores no los quieren. Una nota sobre salud: con moderación, el alcohol no se considera dañino, pero en exceso perjudica a corto y largo plazo; lo mejor es seguir las pautas oficiales de consumo de bajo riesgo de cada país.","Oxidation (open too long): caramel, toffee, deeper colour":"Oxidación (abierto demasiado tiempo): caramelo, toffee, color más oscuro","Out of condition (too old): caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables, deeper colour":"Fuera de condición (demasiado viejo): caramelo, toffee, encurtidos, más oscuro","Nama-hine (nama): malt, meat, rotting vegetables":"Nama-hine (nama): malta, carne, verdura podrida","Aromas like koshu's, but unwanted in other sakes":"Aromas parecidos al koshu, pero no deseados en otros sakes","Chilled, room temperature or warm?":"¿Frío, ambiente o caliente?","Sake can be served at many temperatures, but not every style takes heat well. Three ranges to remember: chilled 6–13 °C (43–55 °F), room temperature 15–18 °C (59–64 °F), warm/hot 40–50 °C (104–122 °F). Warming makes a sake seem more intense, richer in texture and higher in acidity, which can help with food. Ginjō styles, however, lose their aromas and flavours when heated: serve them chilled.":"El sake se puede servir a muchas temperaturas, pero no todos los estilos aguantan el calor. Tres franjas que recordar: frío 6–13 °C, ambiente 15–18 °C, caliente 40–50 °C. Calentar un sake lo hace parecer más intenso, de textura más rica y más ácido, lo que puede ayudar con la comida. Los estilos ginjō, en cambio, pierden aromas y sabores con el calor: se sirven fríos.","Summary by style: futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō suit all three temperatures. Ginjō: chilled; room temperature is personal preference; not warm. Sparkling: chilled only. Koshu and nigori: generally best chilled, but some can be served warm. To serve chilled, the fridge is enough: pour from the refrigerated bottle or decant into a tokkuri, some of which have a compartment for iced water.":"Resumen por estilo: futsū-shu, junmai y honjōzō van bien a las tres temperaturas. Ginjō: frío; ambiente a gusto de cada cual; caliente no. Espumoso: solo frío. Koshu y nigori: en general mejor fríos, pero algunos se pueden servir calientes. Para servir frío basta el frigorífico: se sirve de la botella refrigerada o se pasa a un tokkuri, algunos de los cuales tienen un compartimento para agua helada.","Chilled 6–13 °C · room 15–18 °C · warm 40–50 °C":"Frío 6–13 °C · ambiente 15–18 °C · caliente 40–50 °C","Warmth makes it seem more intense, richer and more acidic":"El calor lo hace más intenso, más rico y más ácido","Futsū-shu, junmai, honjōzō: all three":"Futsū-shu, junmai, honjōzō: las tres","Ginjō: chilled, never warm · sparkling: chilled only · koshu, nigori: usually chilled":"Ginjō: frío, nunca caliente · espumoso: solo frío · koshu y nigori: normalmente fríos","Warming sake: water bath or microwave":"Calentar el sake al baño maría o en el microondas","Water bath: stand the tokkuri in a container of water heated to about 80 °C (176 °F). A small tokkuri takes two to four minutes, and the temperature should always be checked with a thermometer to stay in the right 40–50 °C range.":"Baño maría: se pone el tokkuri en un recipiente lleno de agua calentada a unos 80 °C. Para un tokkuri pequeño hacen falta de dos a cuatro minutos, y siempre hay que comprobar la temperatura con un termómetro para quedarse en la franja de 40–50 °C.","Microwave: use a microwave-safe container. Warming 180 mL of sake takes about 20–40 seconds, depending on the microwave and how much warmer you want it. Because water heats at almost the same rate as sake, you can practise with water first.":"Microondas: se usa un recipiente apto. Para calentar 180 mL de sake bastan unos 20–40 segundos, según el aparato y cuánto se quiera calentar. Como el agua se calienta casi a la misma velocidad que el sake, se puede practicar antes con agua.","Water bath: water at about 80 °C, 2–4 minutes for a small tokkuri":"Baño maría: agua a unos 80 °C, 2–4 minutos para un tokkuri pequeño","Always check with a thermometer":"Comprobar siempre con termómetro","Microwave: 20–40 seconds for 180 mL, microwave-safe container":"Microondas: 20–40 segundos para 180 mL, recipiente apto","Practise with water first":"Practicar antes con agua","Tokkuri, o-choko, masu and wine glasses":"Tokkuri, o-choko, masu y copas de vino","Sake can be served in various traditional Japanese vessels as well as wine glasses. The tokkuri is the sake carafe, used for heating and serving: it comes in many shapes and materials, and the most common hold about 150–300 mL and are made of pottery. The o-choko is the traditional cup: usually small, pottery or glass, with a flat base. Being small, it needs frequent refilling, reflecting a tradition of Japanese hospitality.":"El sake se sirve en distintos recipientes japoneses tradicionales y también en copas de vino. El tokkuri es la jarra de sake, usada para calentarlo y servirlo: los hay de muchas formas y materiales, y los más comunes tienen 150–300 mL y son de cerámica. El o-choko es la taza tradicional: normalmente pequeña, de cerámica o vidrio, con base plana. Al ser pequeña hay que rellenarla a menudo, reflejo de una tradición de hospitalidad japonesa.","The masu is a small box made of cedar. It is not an ideal vessel, because the wood adds flavour to the sake; historically it was used to measure rice, and today it appears occasionally at ceremonies. Wine glasses, on the other hand, are ideal for premium sake served chilled or at room temperature: preferably small, so the sake stays at the right temperature while you drink it, and tulip-shaped to enhance the aromas.":"El masu es una cajita de madera de cedro. No es un recipiente ideal, porque la madera da sabor al sake; antiguamente servía para medir el arroz y hoy se usa a veces en ceremonias. Las copas de vino, en cambio, son ideales para el sake premium servido frío o a temperatura ambiente: mejor pequeñas, para que el sake se mantenga a la temperatura justa mientras se bebe, y en forma de tulipán, para realzar los aromas.","Tokkuri: carafe for heating and serving, usually 150–300 mL, pottery":"Tokkuri: jarra para calentar y servir, normalmente 150–300 mL, de cerámica","O-choko: small flat-based cup; refilled often (hospitality)":"O-choko: taza pequeña de base plana; se rellena a menudo (hospitalidad)","Masu: cedar box, not ideal (wood adds flavour); ceremonial use":"Masu: caja de cedro, no ideal (la madera da sabor); uso ceremonial","Small tulip wine glasses: ideal for premium chilled or room temperature":"Copas de vino pequeñas de tulipán: ideales para premium frío o ambiente","How food changes sake":"Cómo cambia la comida el sake","When food and drink meet in the mouth, each changes how the other tastes: this is a taste interaction. An extreme example is orange juice straight after brushing your teeth: it tastes bitter and sour. Usually the interactions are much milder, but they do happen, and in general food affects a drink more than a drink affects food.":"Cuando comida y bebida se encuentran en la boca, se influyen mutuamente: es una interacción de sabor. Un ejemplo extremo es el zumo de naranja justo después de lavarse los dientes: sabe amargo y ácido. Normalmente las interacciones son mucho más suaves, pero existen, y en general la comida cambia la bebida más que la bebida la comida.","Positive interactions: salt and acidity in food make a drink seem less drying, less bitter and less acidic, and also sweeter and fruitier. Negative interactions: umami in food makes a drink seem more drying, bitter and acidic, less sweet and less fruity; salt in the food can cancel this out. Sugar and chilli heat act much like umami, and chilli also increases the burn of the alcohol. Bitterness in food makes a drink taste more bitter.":"Interacciones positivas: la sal y la acidez de la comida hacen que la bebida parezca menos secante, menos amarga y menos ácida, y además más dulce y frutal. Interacciones negativas: el umami de la comida la hace más secante, amarga y ácida, menos dulce y menos frutal; la sal puede anular este efecto. El azúcar y el picante actúan como el umami, y el picante aumenta además el ardor del alcohol. El amargor de la comida hace la bebida más amarga.","Food affects a drink more than the reverse":"La comida cambia la bebida más que al revés","Salt and acid: drink less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier":"Sal y acidez: bebida menos amarga y ácida, más dulce y frutal","Umami, sugar, chilli: more bitter and acidic, less sweet and fruity; salt offsets umami":"Umami, azúcar, picante: más amarga y ácida, menos dulce y frutal; la sal compensa el umami","Chilli: more alcohol burn; bitter food: more bitter drink":"Picante: más ardor de alcohol; comida amarga: bebida más amarga","Three tips for pairing sake":"Tres consejos para maridar el sake","Sake does not only go with Japanese food: it can be enjoyed with most international dishes. It does not usually have strong negative interactions with food; when they happen, they are mostly linked to umami and sugar in the dish. So only a few key points are needed.":"El sake no solo marida con la cocina japonesa: se puede disfrutar con la mayoría de los platos internacionales. Normalmente no tiene interacciones negativas fuertes con la comida; cuando las hay, se deben sobre todo al umami y al azúcar de los platos. Por eso bastan unos pocos puntos clave.","First: most sakes go with most foods, so personal preference is always the most important thing. Second: food and sake should have a similar flavour intensity so that neither overwhelms the other: delicate sashimi with a light ginjō, a rich stew with a fuller junmai. Third: sweet dishes need a sake that is at least as sweet, or the sake will taste thin and sour.":"Primero: casi todos los sakes van bien con casi todas las comidas, así que el gusto personal es siempre lo más importante. Segundo: comida y sake deben tener una intensidad de sabor parecida para que uno no tape al otro: un sashimi delicado con un ginjō ligero, un guiso sabroso con un junmai más amplio. Tercero: los platos dulces piden un sake al menos igual de dulce; si no, el sake parecerá flaco y ácido.","Sake suits international food too":"El sake también va con la cocina internacional","Personal preference comes first":"El gusto personal es lo primero","Match flavour intensity":"Misma intensidad de sabor entre plato y sake","Sweet dish → sake at least as sweet":"Plato dulce → sake al menos igual de dulce","Which glass is best for tasting sake?":"¿Qué copa es la más adecuada para catar sake?","A wide bowl that narrows towards the top":"Cáliz amplio que se estrecha hacia arriba","A straight, narrow flute":"Copa recta y estrecha, tipo flauta","A wide, shallow, open coupe":"Copa ancha y baja, abierta arriba","A cedar wood box":"Una caja de madera de cedro","A shape that narrows at the top concentrates the aromas.":"La forma que se estrecha arriba concentra los aromas.","An open coupe lets aromas escape. A cedar masu adds wood flavour and is unsuitable for tasting.":"Una copa abierta dispersa los aromas. El masu de cedro aporta sabor a madera y no sirve para catar.","Why is a white surface needed when tasting?":"¿Por qué hace falta una superficie blanca al catar?","To assess the sake's appearance":"Para valorar el aspecto del sake","To cool the glass":"Para enfriar la copa","To absorb smells":"Para absorber los olores","To warm the sake":"Para calentar el sake","Clarity, colour and bubbles show up best against white.":"Sobre blanco se ven mejor limpidez, color y burbujas.","The surface changes neither temperature nor smells: it is only for looking.":"La superficie no cambia la temperatura ni los olores: solo sirve para mirar.","What is assessed under 'appearance' when tasting?":"¿Qué se valora en la fase de «aspecto» de la cata?","Clarity (clear–cloudy), bubbles, colour":"Limpidez (transparente–turbio), burbujas, color","Sweetness and acidity":"Dulzor y acidez","Umami and finish":"Umami y final","Aroma families":"Familias de aromas","Appearance covers what you see: clarity, bubbles and colour.":"El aspecto es lo que se ve: limpidez, burbujas y color.","Sweetness, acidity, umami and finish are judged on the palate; aroma families on the nose (and palate).":"Dulzor, acidez, umami y final se valoran en boca; las familias de aromas en nariz (y en boca).","Which of these aroma families is NOT part of the sake tasting grid?":"¿Cuál de estas familias de aromas NO forma parte de la cuadrícula del sake?","Oak and vanilla":"Roble y vainilla","Fruity/floral":"Frutal/floral","Cereal/grain/nut":"Cereal/grano/fruto seco","Lactic/dairy":"Lácteo","The grid uses fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy and 'other'; oak is not one of the families.":"La cuadrícula usa frutal/floral, cereal/fruto seco, lácteo y «otros»; el roble no es una de las familias.","Oak is hardly used for sake, so it has no family of its own; the other three options are grid families.":"El roble apenas se usa en el sake, así que no tiene familia propia; las otras tres opciones son familias de la cuadrícula.","Before a tasting, what should you avoid just beforehand?":"Antes de una cata, ¿qué conviene evitar justo antes?","Brushing your teeth or drinking coffee":"Lavarse los dientes o tomar café","Drinking a glass of water":"Beber un vaso de agua","Switching on a light":"Encender una luz","Sitting at a white table":"Sentarse a una mesa blanca","Toothpaste and coffee leave lingering flavours that distort tasting.":"La pasta de dientes y el café dejan sabores que falsean la cata.","Water leaves no taste, light helps you see, and a white table is actually recommended.":"El agua no deja sabor, la luz ayuda a ver y la mesa blanca es justo lo recomendable.","What are the four rules for storing sake?":"¿Cuáles son las cuatro reglas para conservar el sake?","Keep cool, drink young, store upright, avoid bright light":"En fresco, beber joven, botella de pie, lejos de la luz fuerte","Keep warm, age it, lie it down, keep in light":"En calor, envejecer, botella tumbada, a la luz","Keep cool, age it, lie it down, keep dark":"En fresco, envejecer, botella tumbada, a oscuras","Room temperature, drink young, lie it down, keep in light":"Temperatura ambiente, beber joven, botella tumbada, a la luz","Cool, young, upright, away from bright light.":"Fresco, joven, de pie, lejos de la luz fuerte.","Sake is not stored lying down and, apart from koshu, is not made for ageing; heat and bright light spoil it.":"El sake no se guarda tumbado y, salvo el koshu, no está hecho para envejecer; el calor y la luz fuerte lo estropean.","Within what time should most sake be drunk after going on sale?":"¿En cuánto tiempo debería beberse la mayoría de los sakes tras salir a la venta?","About a year":"Alrededor de un año","About a week":"Alrededor de una semana","About five years":"Alrededor de cinco años","There is no limit":"No hay límite","Most sake should be drunk within about a year, after which it loses freshness.":"Casi todo el sake debe beberse en un año aproximadamente; después pierde frescura.","A week is how long an opened ginjō lasts. Nama lasts only a few months; only koshu is meant for ageing.":"Una semana es lo que dura un ginjō abierto. Los nama duran solo unos meses; solo el koshu está pensado para envejecer.","How long does a ginjō usually stay fresh once opened, in the fridge?":"¿Cuánto se mantiene fresco normalmente un ginjō abierto, en el frigorífico?","About one week":"Alrededor de una semana","About two months":"Alrededor de dos meses","About an hour":"Alrededor de una hora","Delicate ginjō stays fresh for about a week; other sakes about two.":"Los ginjō, más delicados, se mantienen frescos una semana; los demás sakes unas dos.","Two months or a year is far too long for an opened bottle. An hour is too short: resealed in the fridge, sake keeps for days.":"Dos meses o un año es demasiado para una botella abierta. Una hora es muy poco: cerrado en frío, el sake aguanta varios días.","How should sake bottles be stored?":"¿Cómo se guardan las botellas de sake?","Upright":"De pie","Lying down":"Tumbadas","Upside down":"Boca abajo","Tilted at 45°":"Inclinadas a 45°","Sake bottles are best stored upright.":"Las botellas de sake se conservan mejor de pie.","Lying bottles down is a habit for cork-sealed wine, not sake.":"Tumbar las botellas es costumbre del vino con corcho, no del sake.","A sake bottle has been open too long: it is darker and smells of caramel and toffee. Which fault is this?":"Una botella de sake lleva demasiado tiempo abierta: está más oscura y huele a caramelo y toffee. ¿Qué defecto es?","Oxidation":"Oxidación","Nama-hine":"Nama-hine","Light strike":"Luz","Bacterial infection":"Infección bacteriana","Open too long + caramel, toffee and deeper colour = oxidation.":"Abierta demasiado tiempo + caramelo, toffee y color más oscuro = oxidación.","Nama-hine affects nama and smells of malt, meat and rotting vegetables. The other two are not the sake faults covered at this level.":"El nama-hine afecta a los nama y huele a malta, carne y verdura podrida. Los otros dos no son los defectos del sake de este nivel.","Which aromas show a sake is 'out of condition', meaning too old?":"¿Qué aromas indican que un sake está «fuera de condición», es decir, demasiado viejo?","Caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables":"Caramelo, toffee, verduras encurtidas","Green apple and white flowers":"Manzana verde y flores blancas","Steamed rice and yoghurt":"Arroz cocido y yogur","Fresh citrus":"Cítricos frescos","A bottle that is too old smells of caramel, toffee and pickles, and darkens.":"Una botella demasiado vieja huele a caramelo, toffee y encurtidos, y se oscurece.","Apple, flowers, rice, yoghurt and citrus are normal, welcome aromas in fresh sake.":"Manzana, flores, arroz, yogur y cítricos son aromas normales y apreciados en un sake fresco.","What is nama-hine?":"¿Qué es el nama-hine?","A fault in nama: malt, meat, rotting-vegetable aromas":"Un defecto de los nama: aromas a malta, carne, verdura podrida","A type of sparkling sake":"Un tipo de sake espumoso","The traditional cup":"La taza tradicional","A stage of kōji making":"Una fase de la elaboración del kōji","Nama-hine is the typical fault of unpasteurised sake.":"El nama-hine es el defecto típico de los sakes sin pasteurizar.","The cup is the o-choko. Nama-hine is neither a style nor a production stage.":"La taza es el o-choko. El nama-hine no es un estilo ni una fase de elaboración.","Why do oxidation aromas resemble those of koshu?":"¿Por qué los aromas de oxidación recuerdan a los del koshu?","The same processes create them, but in koshu they are wanted":"Los procesos que los crean son los mismos, pero en el koshu se buscan","Koshu is always a faulty sake":"El koshu siempre es un sake defectuoso","Koshu is made from oxidised rice":"El koshu se hace con arroz oxidado","It is an unexplained coincidence":"Es una coincidencia sin explicación","Same processes, different intention: in koshu those aromas are part of the style.":"Mismos procesos, distinta intención: en el koshu esos aromas forman parte del estilo.","Koshu is a deliberate style, not a fault, made from the same rice as other sakes: ageing creates those aromas.":"El koshu es un estilo buscado, no un defecto, y se hace con el mismo arroz que los demás: es el envejecimiento el que crea esos aromas.","Which sake most needs refrigeration?":"¿Qué sake necesita más el frigorífico?","Nama-zake":"El nama-zake","Pasteurised futsū-shu":"El futsū-shu pasteurizado","All sakes equally":"Todos los sakes por igual","Nama is unpasteurised and less stable: it must be kept cold at all times.":"El nama no está pasteurizado y es menos estable: hay que tenerlo siempre en frío.","Every sake prefers cool storage, but for nama the cold is essential; ginjō also benefits to protect its aromas.":"Todo sake está mejor en fresco, pero para el nama el frío es imprescindible; los ginjō también lo agradecen para proteger sus aromas.","What is the recommended serving temperature for ginjō styles?":"¿Cuál es la temperatura de servicio recomendada para los estilos ginjō?","Chilled (6–13 °C)":"Frío (6–13 °C)","Warm (40–50 °C)":"Caliente (40–50 °C)","Very hot, above 60 °C":"Muy caliente, más de 60 °C","Below freezing":"Bajo cero","Ginjō loses its aromas when heated: serve it chilled.":"Los ginjō pierden aromas con el calor: se sirven fríos.","Heat would flatten the fruity, floral scents. Below freezing the sake would be too cold to smell.":"El calor apagaría los perfumes frutales y florales. Bajo cero estaría demasiado frío para percibir sus aromas.","Which temperature range is warm/hot sake?":"¿Qué franja de temperatura corresponde al sake caliente?","40–50 °C":"40–50 °C","15–18 °C":"15–18 °C","6–13 °C":"6–13 °C","70–80 °C":"70–80 °C","Warm/hot sake is served at 40–50 °C.":"El sake caliente se sirve entre 40 y 50 °C.","15–18 °C is room temperature and 6–13 °C chilled. About 80 °C is the water-bath water, not the sake.":"15–18 °C es temperatura ambiente y 6–13 °C frío. Unos 80 °C es el agua del baño maría, no el sake.","What effect does warming have on a sake?":"¿Qué efecto tiene calentar un sake?","It seems more intense, richer and more acidic":"Lo hace parecer más intenso, más rico y más ácido","It becomes lighter and less acidic":"Lo vuelve más ligero y menos ácido","It raises its alcohol level":"Sube su graduación","It boosts ginjō aromas":"Realza los aromas de los ginjō","Heat increases perceived intensity, texture and acidity, which can help with food.":"El calor aumenta la intensidad, la textura y la acidez percibidas, algo útil con la comida.","Strength does not change, and ginjō loses aromas with heat. The effect is the opposite of 'lighter'.":"La graduación no cambia, y los ginjō pierden aromas con el calor. El efecto es lo contrario de «más ligero».","Which sakes can be served chilled, at room temperature AND warm?":"¿Qué sakes se pueden servir fríos, a temperatura ambiente Y calientes?","Futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō":"Futsū-shu, junmai y honjōzō","Sparkling sake only":"Solo el sake espumoso","Futsū-shu, junmai and honjōzō suit all three temperatures.":"Futsū-shu, junmai y honjōzō van bien a las tres temperaturas.","No ginjō style (including junmai ginjō and junmai daiginjō) should be warmed. Sparkling is served chilled only.":"Ningún estilo ginjō (ni junmai ginjō ni junmai daiginjō) debe calentarse. El espumoso se sirve solo frío.","How is sparkling sake served?":"¿Cómo se sirve el sake espumoso?","Chilled only":"Solo frío","Warm, to feel the bubbles better":"Caliente, para notar mejor las burbujas","At room temperature or warm":"A temperatura ambiente o caliente","At any temperature":"A cualquier temperatura","Sparkling sake is served chilled only.":"El sake espumoso se sirve solo frío.","Neither room temperature nor warm suits sparkling sake, which would lose freshness and bubbles.":"Ni el ambiente ni el calor convienen al espumoso, que perdería frescura y burbujas.","How are koshu and nigori generally served?":"¿Cómo se sirven en general el koshu y el nigori?","Generally chilled, though some can be served warm":"Normalmente fríos, aunque algunos también calientes","Always warm":"Siempre calientes","Never chilled":"Nunca fríos","Only at room temperature":"Solo a temperatura ambiente","Koshu and nigori are generally best chilled, but some can be served warm.":"El koshu y el nigori están mejor fríos, pero algunos pueden servirse calientes.","Options with 'always', 'never' or 'only' are too rigid for such varied styles.":"Las opciones con «siempre», «nunca» o «solo» son demasiado rígidas para estilos tan variados.","To warm sake in a water bath, what temperature should the water be?":"Para calentar el sake al baño maría, ¿a qué temperatura debe estar el agua?","About 80 °C":"Unos 80 °C","About 40 °C":"Unos 40 °C","Boiling, 100 °C, for 10 minutes":"Hirviendo, 100 °C, durante 10 minutos","About 15 °C":"Unos 15 °C","Water at about 80 °C: a small tokkuri warms in 2–4 minutes.":"Agua a unos 80 °C: un tokkuri pequeño se calienta en 2–4 minutos.","40 °C is the temperature of warm sake, not the water. Boiling water for 10 minutes would overheat it; 15 °C would not warm it at all.":"40 °C es la temperatura del sake caliente, no del agua. El agua hirviendo 10 minutos lo calentaría demasiado; a 15 °C no se calentaría.","What should always be used when warming sake in a water bath?":"¿Qué hay que usar siempre al calentar sake al baño maría?","A thermometer":"Un termómetro","A cedar masu":"Un masu de cedro","Ice":"Hielo","A wine glass":"Una copa de vino","A thermometer keeps you in the right 40–50 °C range.":"El termómetro permite quedarse en la franja de 40–50 °C.","Sake is warmed in the tokkuri, not a masu or glass; ice is for cooling.":"El sake se calienta en el tokkuri, no en el masu ni en la copa; el hielo sirve para enfriar.","About how long does it take to warm 180 mL of sake in a microwave?":"¿Cuánto tiempo hace falta aproximadamente para calentar 180 mL de sake en el microondas?","20–40 seconds":"20–40 segundos","2–4 minutes":"2–4 minutos","5 seconds":"5 segundos","10 minutes":"10 minutos","About 20–40 seconds, depending on the microwave and target temperature.":"Bastan unos 20–40 segundos, según el aparato y la temperatura deseada.","2–4 minutes is the water-bath time for a small tokkuri. 5 seconds is too short and 10 minutes far too long.":"2–4 minutos es el tiempo del baño maría para un tokkuri pequeño. 5 segundos es muy poco y 10 minutos demasiado.","What is a tokkuri?":"¿Qué es un tokkuri?","The carafe for heating and serving sake":"La jarra para calentar y servir el sake","The cedar box":"La caja de cedro","The tokkuri is the carafe, usually pottery, holding 150–300 mL.":"El tokkuri es la jarra, normalmente de cerámica, de 150–300 mL.","The cup is the o-choko and the cedar box is the masu.":"La taza es el o-choko y la caja de cedro es el masu.","Why does an o-choko need frequent refilling?":"¿Por qué hay que rellenar a menudo el o-choko?","It is small: frequent refilling reflects Japanese hospitality":"Es pequeña: rellenarla a menudo refleja la hospitalidad japonesa","It leaks from the base":"Pierde sake por el fondo","The wood absorbs the sake":"La madera absorbe el sake","The sake evaporates at once":"El sake se evapora enseguida","Small cups empty quickly: refilling them is a gesture of hospitality.":"Las tazas pequeñas se vacían rápido: rellenarlas es un gesto de hospitalidad.","The most common o-choko are pottery or glass, not wood; wood is the masu.":"Los o-choko más comunes son de cerámica o vidrio, no de madera; la madera es del masu.","Why is a masu not an ideal vessel for sake?":"¿Por qué el masu no es un recipiente ideal para el sake?","The cedar wood adds flavour to the sake":"La madera de cedro da sabor al sake","It is too large":"Es demasiado grande","It is made of fragile glass":"Es de vidrio frágil","It overheats the sake":"Calienta demasiado el sake","The masu is cedar, and the wood changes the sake's flavour.":"El masu es de cedro, y la madera cambia el sabor del sake.","The masu is a small wooden box, not glass; it was once used to measure rice and now appears at some ceremonies.":"El masu es una cajita de madera, no de vidrio; antes servía para medir el arroz y hoy aparece en algunas ceremonias.","Which glass is ideal for a chilled daiginjō?":"¿Qué copa es ideal para un daiginjō servido frío?","A small tulip-shaped wine glass":"Una copa de vino pequeña en forma de tulipán","A large beer mug":"Una jarra grande de cerveza","A wide tumbler":"Un vaso ancho de agua","Small to keep the temperature, tulip-shaped to enhance the aromas.":"Pequeña para mantener la temperatura y de tulipán para realzar los aromas.","A big mug lets the sake warm up, a masu adds wood flavour, and a wide tumbler lets aromas escape.":"Una jarra grande dejaría que el sake se calentara, el masu daría sabor a madera y un vaso ancho dispersaría los aromas.","In a pairing, which affects which more?":"En un maridaje, ¿quién influye más en quién?","Food affects the drink more than the reverse":"La comida influye en la bebida más que al revés","The drink affects the food more":"La bebida influye en la comida más que al revés","They never affect each other":"Nunca se influyen","It depends only on colour":"Depende solo del color","Generally food changes how the drink tastes more than the reverse.":"En general es la comida la que cambia el sabor de la bebida más que al revés.","Interactions always exist, even if usually mild; colour has nothing to do with it.":"Las interacciones siempre existen, aunque suelen ser suaves; el color no tiene nada que ver.","What effect do salt and acidity in food have on a drink?":"¿Qué efecto tienen la sal y la acidez de la comida en la bebida?","Less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier":"Menos amarga y ácida, más dulce y frutal","More bitter and acidic, less fruity":"Más amarga y ácida, menos frutal","More alcohol burn":"Más ardor de alcohol","No effect":"Ningún efecto","Salt and acidity are positive interactions: they soften the drink.":"La sal y la acidez son interacciones positivas: suavizan la bebida.","More bitter and acidic is the effect of umami, sugar and chilli; alcohol burn rises with chilli.":"Más amarga y ácida es el efecto del umami, el azúcar y el picante; el ardor del alcohol aumenta con el picante.","Which element in food makes a drink more bitter, more acidic and less fruity?":"¿Qué elemento de la comida hace la bebida más amarga, más ácida y menos frutal?","Umami":"Umami","Salt":"Sal","Acidity":"Acidez","Fat":"Grasa","Umami is the main 'difficult' element in sake pairings.":"El umami es el principal elemento «difícil» en los maridajes con sake.","Salt and acidity have the opposite effect, and salt can even cancel out umami.":"La sal y la acidez tienen el efecto contrario, y la sal puede incluso anular el umami.","A very spicy (chilli-hot) dish with a sake: what happens?":"Un plato muy picante con un sake: ¿qué pasa?","The alcohol burn increases":"Aumenta el ardor del alcohol","The sake seems sweeter":"El sake parece más dulce","The sake seems less acidic":"El sake parece menos ácido","The heat disappears":"El picante desaparece","Chilli acts like umami and also increases the burning effect of the alcohol.":"El picante actúa como el umami y además acentúa el ardor del alcohol.","Chilli makes the drink less sweet and more acidic, not the reverse, and it does not vanish.":"El picante hace la bebida menos dulce y más ácida, no al revés, y no desaparece.","What is the most important consideration when pairing sake with food?":"¿Qué es lo más importante al maridar sake con comida?","Personal preference":"El gusto personal","Only using Japanese food":"Usar solo cocina japonesa","Always serving sake warm":"Servir siempre el sake caliente","Choosing the most expensive sake":"Elegir el sake más caro","Most sakes go with most foods, so personal preference decides.":"Casi todos los sakes van con casi todo: decide el gusto personal.","Sake also suits international food; temperature and price are not pairing criteria.":"El sake también va con la cocina internacional; la temperatura y el precio no son criterios de maridaje.","A very sweet dessert: which sake should you choose?":"Un postre muy dulce: ¿qué sake elegir?","A sake at least as sweet":"Un sake al menos igual de dulce","The driest sake possible":"El sake más seco posible","A very acidic sake":"Un sake muy ácido","A very hot sake":"Un sake muy caliente","Sweet dishes call for a sake at least as sweet.":"Los platos dulces piden un sake al menos igual de dulce.","Sugar in the dish makes a drink seem less sweet and more acidic: a dry or acidic sake would taste thin and sour.":"El azúcar del plato hace que la bebida parezca menos dulce y más ácida: un sake seco o ácido resultaría flaco y agrio.","Why pair delicate sashimi with a light sake?":"¿Por qué maridar un sashimi delicado con un sake ligero?","So food and sake have a similar flavour intensity":"Para que comida y sake tengan una intensidad de sabor parecida","Because light sake is always more expensive":"Porque el sake ligero siempre es más caro","Because fish only goes with warm sake":"Porque el pescado solo va con sake caliente","Because light sake is stronger":"Porque el sake ligero tiene más alcohol","Similar intensities stop one overwhelming the other.":"Intensidades parecidas evitan que uno tape al otro.","Price, temperature and strength are not the reason for this advice.":"El precio, la temperatura y la graduación no son la razón de este consejo.","Which production step is legally controlled for junmai?":"¿Qué paso de elaboración controla la ley en el junmai?","No addition of distilled alcohol":"Ninguna adición de alcohol destilado","No pasteurisation":"Ninguna pasteurización","Compulsory ageing":"Un envejecimiento obligatorio","Rough filtration":"Un filtrado grosero","By law, junmai may not have high-strength distilled alcohol added.":"Por ley, el junmai no puede llevar alcohol destilado de alta graduación.","No pasteurisation defines nama, ageing defines koshu, and rough filtration defines nigori.":"No pasteurizar define el nama, envejecer el koshu y el filtrado grosero el nigori.","Which production step defines koshu?":"¿Qué paso de elaboración define el koshu?","Maturation (ageing)":"El envejecimiento","Adding carbon dioxide":"La adición de dióxido de carbono","Polishing to 50%":"Un pulido al 50 %","Koshu is aged sake: maturation is the step that defines it.":"El koshu es el sake envejecido: lo define la maduración.","No pasteurisation = nama; carbon dioxide = sparkling; 50% polishing = daiginjō.":"Sin pasteurizar = nama; dióxido de carbono = espumoso; pulido al 50 % = daiginjō.","What is the maximum polishing ratio for honjōzō?":"¿Cuál es el grado de pulido máximo para un honjōzō?","100%":"100 %","For honjōzō, 70% or less of the grain must remain.":"En el honjōzō debe quedar un 70 % del grano o menos.","50% and 60% are the daiginjō and ginjō limits. 100% is allowed only for junmai, and even there it is rare.":"El 50 % y el 60 % son los límites de daiginjō y ginjō. El 100 % solo se admite en el junmai, y aun así es raro.","Which of these sakes has no added distilled alcohol at all?":"¿Cuál de estos sakes no lleva nada de alcohol destilado añadido?","The word junmai guarantees no added distilled alcohol.":"La palabra junmai garantiza que no hay alcohol destilado añadido.","Daiginjō, ginjō and honjōzō without the word junmai are sakes with alcohol added before filtration.":"Daiginjō, ginjō y honjōzō sin la palabra junmai son sakes con alcohol añadido antes de filtrar.","What does 純米 mean?":"¿Qué significa 純米?","Junmai (pure rice)":"Junmai (arroz puro)","純米 reads junmai and means 'pure rice'.":"純米 se lee junmai y significa «arroz puro».","Ginjō is written 吟醸. Nama and koshu are not among the four kanji terms at this level.":"Ginjō se escribe 吟醸. Nama y koshu no están entre los cuatro términos en kanji de este nivel.","A label shows 本醸造. What do you know about this sake?":"En una etiqueta aparece 本醸造. ¿Qué sabes de este sake?","It is honjōzō: added alcohol, rice ≤70%, cereal style":"Es un honjōzō: alcohol añadido, arroz ≤70 %, estilo de cereal","It is junmai: no added alcohol":"Es un junmai: sin alcohol añadido","It is daiginjō: rice ≤50%":"Es un daiginjō: arroz ≤50 %","It is an unpasteurised sake":"Es un sake sin pasteurizar","本醸造 = honjōzō: added alcohol, polished to 70% or less, cereal and lactic notes.":"本醸造 = honjōzō: alcohol añadido, pulido al 70 % o menos, notas de cereal y lácteas.","Junmai is 純米 and daiginjō 大吟醸. Unpasteurised sake is called nama.":"Junmai es 純米 y daiginjō 大吟醸. El sake sin pasteurizar se llama nama.","In which term does the kanji 米 (mai) appear?":"¿En qué término aparece el kanji 米 (mai)?","米 is the 'mai' in junmai (純米).":"米 es el «mai» de junmai (純米).","Ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) and daiginjō (大吟醸) do not contain 米.":"Ginjō (吟醸), honjōzō (本醸造) y daiginjō (大吟醸) no contienen 米.","Why is it useful to recognise the kanji of the four key terms?":"¿Por qué es útil reconocer los kanji de los cuatro términos clave?","Labels are mostly in Japanese, with few words in the Latin alphabet":"Las etiquetas están casi todas en japonés, con pocas palabras en alfabeto latino","The kanji show the sake's price":"Los kanji indican el precio del sake","The kanji show the production year":"Los kanji indican el año de producción","The law bans the Latin alphabet":"La ley prohíbe el alfabeto latino","Recognising a few kanji lets you read the grade even on an all-Japanese label.":"Reconocer unos pocos kanji permite entender el grado incluso en una etiqueta toda en japonés.","These kanji show the grade, not price or year; the Latin alphabet is not banned, just little used.":"Estos kanji indican el grado, no el precio ni el año; el alfabeto latino no está prohibido, solo se usa poco.","Preparing a tasting":"Preparar una cata","No smells, white surface, glass narrowing at top, clean palate.":"Sin olores, superficie blanca, copa que se estrecha, boca limpia.","Sake aroma families":"Familias de aromas del sake","Fruity/floral, cereal/grain/nut, lactic/dairy, other.":"Frutal/floral, cereal/fruto seco, lácteo, otros.","Storing sake":"Conservar el sake","Cool, young (about 1 year), upright, away from bright light.":"Fresco, joven (1 año aprox.), de pie, lejos de la luz fuerte.","Opened bottle":"Botella abierta","Resealed in the fridge: about 2 weeks; ginjō about 1.":"Cerrada en frío: unas 2 semanas; ginjō 1 aprox.","Open too long: caramel, toffee, deeper colour.":"Abierto demasiado: caramelo, toffee, color más oscuro.","Out of condition":"Fuera de condición","Too old: caramel, toffee, pickled vegetables, deeper colour.":"Demasiado viejo: caramelo, toffee, encurtidos, más oscuro.","Fault in nama: malt, meat, rotting vegetables.":"Defecto de los nama: malta, carne, verdura podrida.","Three serving temperatures":"Tres temperaturas de servicio","Chilled 6–13 °C · room 15–18 °C · warm 40–50 °C.":"Frío 6–13 °C · ambiente 15–18 °C · caliente 40–50 °C.","Ginjō: what temperature?":"Ginjō: ¿a qué temperatura?","Chilled; room temperature by preference; never warm.":"Frío; ambiente a gusto; nunca caliente.","Water bath":"Baño maría","Water about 80 °C, 2–4 min for a small tokkuri; use a thermometer.":"Agua a unos 80 °C, 2–4 min para un tokkuri pequeño; con termómetro.","Microwave":"Microondas","20–40 seconds for 180 mL, in a suitable container.":"20–40 segundos para 180 mL, en un recipiente apto.","Tokkuri":"Tokkuri","Carafe for heating and serving; usually 150–300 mL, pottery.":"Jarra para calentar y servir; normalmente 150–300 mL, cerámica.","O-choko":"O-choko","Small traditional flat-based cup; refilled often.":"Taza tradicional pequeña, de base plana; se rellena a menudo.","Masu":"Masu","Cedar box: wood adds flavour, not ideal; ceremonial use.":"Cajita de cedro: la madera da sabor, no ideal; uso ceremonial.","Salt and acid in food":"Sal y acidez en la comida","Drink less bitter and acidic, sweeter and fruitier.":"Bebida menos amarga y ácida, más dulce y frutal.","Umami in food":"Umami en la comida","Drink more bitter, drying and acidic, less sweet and fruity.":"Bebida más amarga, secante y ácida, menos dulce y frutal.","Three pairing rules":"Tres reglas de maridaje","Personal preference; similar intensity; sweet dish → sake at least as sweet.":"Gusto personal; intensidad parecida; plato dulce → sake al menos igual de dulce.","What sake is":"Qué es el sake","The brewing steps":"Los pasos de la elaboración","From brown rice to steamed rice":"Del arroz integral al arroz al vapor","Making kōji":"Cómo se hace el kōji","Fermentation and style":"Fermentación y estilo","Basic and premium sake":"Sake básico y sake premium","Reading a Japanese label":"Leer una etiqueta japonesa","Speciality styles":"Los estilos especiales","Tasting sake":"Catar el sake","Storage and faults":"Conservación y defectos","Serving sake":"Servir el sake","Sake and food":"Sake y comida","Ingredients and brewing":"Ingredientes y elaboración","Categories and styles":"Categorías y estilos","Tasting, storage and service":"Catar, conservar, servir","Sake 1":"Sake 1","Sake 1 exam":"Examen Sake 1","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on rice, kōji, sake grades and service.":"Lecciones, tests y tarjetas sobre arroz, kōji, categorías de sake y servicio.","Review Japanese terms, grades and styles":"Repasa términos japoneses, categorías y estilos","All of Sake 1":"Todo Sake 1","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Sake 1 syllabus.":"Lecciones, tarjetas y errores: solo el programa de Sake 1.","Sake 1 games":"Juegos de Sake 1","Short games on Sake 1 questions and terms.":"Juegos cortos sobre preguntas y términos de Sake 1.","Hi! I'm your sake goat 🍶":"¡Hola! Soy tu cabra del sake 🍶","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Sake 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"Te preparo un recorrido a medida para aprobar el examen Sake 1. Bastan 5 preguntas rápidas."});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.ar,{"Picture a kitchen where one cook slices bread while another eats each slice straight away: there is never much bread piling up on the board. In the same way, sugar is made and used up little by little in the tank. The result is a liquid that usually reaches about 20% abv by the end of fermentation, more than sake normally has in the bottle.":"Imaginá una cocina donde un cocinero corta pan y otro se lo come al momento, rebanada a rebanada: nunca se acumula mucho pan en la tabla. Del mismo modo, en el depósito el azúcar se produce y se consume poco a poco. El resultado es un líquido que al final de la fermentación suele tener alrededor del 20 % de alcohol, más de lo que el sake tiene luego en la botella.","Note the contrast with beer, where starch is turned into sugar first and fermented afterwards, in two separate stages. In sake the two overlap: it is exactly this overlap that earns the name parallel fermentation.":"Recordá la diferencia con la cerveza, donde el almidón se convierte en azúcar primero y se fermenta después, en dos fases separadas. En el sake ambas cosas se solapan: es justamente ese solapamiento lo que recibe el nombre de fermentación paralela.","The second style covers sakes with cereal and lactic aromas, which usually have more acidity and umami than the ginjō styles. Junmai and honjōzō belong here. In short: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō and junmai daiginjō sit on the fruit-and-flower side; junmai and honjōzō on the side of cereal, lactic notes, acidity and umami.":"El segundo estilo reúne los sakes con aromas de cereal y lácteos, que suelen tener más acidez y umami que los estilos ginjō. Acá están el junmai y el honjōzō. En resumen: ginjō, junmai ginjō, daiginjō y junmai daiginjō están del lado de la fruta y las flores; junmai y honjōzō, del lado del cereal, lo lácteo, la acidez y el umami.","There is a second way to split the six grades. Three carry the word junmai, meaning 'pure rice': it shows that NO distilled alcohol was added before filtration. So junmai ginjō is a style similar to ginjō; the only difference is that junmai ginjō has had no alcohol added. The same goes for daiginjō and junmai daiginjō, and for honjōzō (with alcohol) and junmai (without).":"Hay una segunda forma de dividir los seis grados. Tres llevan la palabra junmai, que significa «arroz puro»: indicá que antes de filtrar NO se ha añadido alcohol destilado. Así, el junmai ginjō es un estilo parecido al ginjō; la única diferencia es que el junmai ginjō no ha recibido alcohol añadido. Lo mismo vale para daiginjō y junmai daiginjō, y para honjōzō (con alcohol) y junmai (sin él).","Think of the grade as 'how the sake was made' (polishing, alcohol added or not) and the speciality style as 'one extra treatment': no pasteurisation, rough filtration, bubbles, ageing. Both pieces of information can therefore appear on one label, for example a 'junmai nigori nama'.":"Pensá en el grado como «cómo se hizo el sake» (pulido, alcohol añadido o no) y en el estilo especial como «un tratamiento más»: sin pasteurizar, filtrado grosero, burbujas, envejecimiento. Por eso en una etiqueta pueden aparecer las dos cosas, por ejemplo un «junmai nigori nama».","When food and drink meet in the mouth, each changes how the other tastes: this is a taste interaction. An extreme example is orange juice straight after brushing your teeth: it tastes bitter and sour. Usually the interactions are much milder, but they do happen, and in general food affects a drink more than a drink affects food.":"Cuando comida y bebida se encuentran en la boca, se influyen mutuamente: es una interacción de sabor. Un ejemplo extremo es el jugo de naranja justo después de lavarse los dientes: sabe amargo y ácido. Normalmente las interacciones son mucho más suaves, pero existen, y en general la comida cambia la bebida más que la bebida la comida.","It raises its alcohol level":"Subí su graduación","A label shows 本醸造. What do you know about this sake?":"En una etiqueta aparece 本醸造. ¿Qué sabés de este sake?","Review Japanese terms, grades and styles":"Repasá términos japoneses, categorías y estilos"});
